t of Genital integrity.<br /> <br /> I Still tend to dislike Plans to &quot;Burn down the establishment!!!&quot; without a plan of WHAT precisely you will replace it with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T05:08:23-07:00","id":980194,"title":"","content":"I am Spanish, and here the media is anti-Christian. A Catholic Spanish watching movies about Spanish Civil War is like the Captain America reading &quot;Russia Today&quot;. I am very angry when I read the fantasy version of the Inquisition (for example Castilla from &quot;7th Sea&quot;). Why do you talk about Torquemada but you say nothing about Asia Bibi and Pakistan anti-blasfemy law? I don't spend 30 euros to feel like Peter Parker reading J.J. Jameson's articles about Spiderman, or &quot;Friends of humanity&quot; propaganda about mutans. In my homebrew fiction the &quot;mugless&quot; hates-fear againts spellcasters and powerless humans againts mutants and metahumans is a allegory about comunist workers againt businessmen. <br /> <br /> And it is curious, because now USA is the new American Empire, and they are suffering their own black legend created by enemy propaganda. I hope they understand how we feel with anti-Spanish and anti-Catholic misinformation. <br /> <br /> Please, we need the right balance between self-criticism and self-esteem, both are necesary, but too much may hurt you. USA isn't worse than Russia or China, and Catholic Spanish empire wasn't worse than our rival powers. America isn't the evil empire.To accept a lot of things have to be improved or corrected doesn't mean the others to be better option to be the supreme power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 10-02-2016, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T05:48:22-07:00","id":980204,"title":"","content":"For me, I'm not conservative. I'm fiscally liberal and socially moderate. But I really don't like my own generation's brand of political correctness and we'll just leave it at that because I don't want to break any rules.<br /> <br /> \u200bI do support the right to bear arms (a traditionally conservative value) and the right to free speech and free expression (Hence my dislike of PC culture/identity politics), but other than that, I generally lean to the left.<br /> <br /> \u200bHowever, I do believe that everyone has the right to believe in and express their own ideologies, regardless of whether or not I personally agree with it, and this goes for both sides of the political spectrum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:52:18-07:00","id":980262,"title":"","content":"The key is to respect the human dignity, the base of the human rights. Without human dignity you can't defend freedom, tolerance and citizens' rights. People shouldn't understand State isn't Robin Hood stealing to rich men to give them to the poors, but the king John Lackland collecting taxes. The anticapitalism doesn't want to distribute the wealth but monopolize it. They want to replace the businessmen with their own oligarchy of party bosses and their entourage of privileged friends. A good example is the Spanish movie and teleseries industry. We don't want to see Spanish movies, because they are boring propaganda, but it is paid with subsidies. But we want to watch Spanish teleseries, because TV channels don't get subsidies, they risk their own money and they have produce series to be liked by the public. Do you remember the marvel civil war? It is a good example of Keynes vs Hayek economy. State wants to controll the power to protect the people,(or they tell us that), but liberals don't want be controlled by state because we don't trust goverments with too much power.<br /> <br /> In my fantasy settings, divine and arcane spellcasters are a allegory about state vs businessmen. The clerics are like state, they says they want to protect the powerless people againts the powerful ones but you have to obey their rules, and the wizards are like rich businessmen, feared and envied by the masses, but they say their powers is by their effort and talent. In my works the hate againts the wizards by muggles, or againts mutants by powerless humans is a metaphor about the anticapitalism hate. A great power is a great responsability, but not always the powerful is the villain of the story and the weak isn't the innocent victim. Don't trust too much who promises defend people againts most powerfuls. Maybe the rebel is a new tyrant worse than the last one. <br /> <br /> And please, I don't want any more the stupy clich\u00e9 about Christians believers hating Sciencie. We aren't like that crazy Carrie's mother (that Stephen King's character with telekinetic powers). Our teology allows us to reconcile Reason and Faith, we haven't to reject one of them. Lots of great scientifics were believers. The father of Big Bang theory, George Lemaitre, was a priest, the creater of scientify method, FRAY Rogerd Bacon was a Franciscan friar. Ren\u00e9 Descartes, creator of Racionalist philosphy, was believer. And what do you know about Troffin Lysenko's pseudo-ciencie in Soviet Union? By his fault genetic studies and evolution theories were forbidden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 10-03-2016, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T15:02:32-07:00","id":980438,"title":"","content":"Conservative gamer, here.<br /> <br /> Definitely have some liberal views as well, but I tend to side more towards conservative. It really hasn't affected my games in any negative way, and I play with mostly liberal gamers. So no problems there.<br /> <br /> However, I've noticed an increasingly hostile attitude towards conservative views by game developers, forum moderators, etc. Which is fine, since it's their playground, and I know if I don't like it, I can leave. <br /> <br /> But I'll be honest: sometimes it bothers me. In a way that any extremist of any political or religious ideology can bother me, I guess. Not sure how to explain it.<br /> <br /> So I do my best educate myself on pretty much one thing: Are you a nice fucking person that treats others with respect and doesn't push your views into someone else's mouth? Awesome. I'll buy your product.<br /> <br /> Are you a raging dick hemorrhoid that shoves your views into people like a bully in secondary school? No thanks. Keep your shit. <br /> <br /> It's saving me quite a bit of money in the long run!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T16:29:49-07:00","id":980467,"title":"","content":"So. I was reading the 7th Sea 2nd edition corebook and got to the section on the Rilasciare - the anarchist secret society that players can join.<br /> <br /> My first impression of them? &quot;Wow, okay, I know you shouldn't just blindly follow tradition instead of thinking for yourself, but really guys? What a bunch of *#(@).&quot;<br /> <br /> So, yes. I identify as &quot;inclined to conservatism.&quot; To what extent I haven't quite narrowed down yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T18:26:04-07:00","id":980507,"title":"","content":"On some things, very conservative (fiscal issues, social spending, 2nd Amendment, national defense/foreign policy) and on others, very liberal (abortion, the environment, LBTGQ rights). I absolutely despise any sort of political correctness; it's simply the tool of the weak to silence those they disagree with rather than constructively engaging them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5853-krb","name":"KRB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:29:02-07:00","id":980524,"title":"","content":"I am a Constitutional Conservative. I do not always vote Republican, but I do not see myself voting for any candidates of the other parties in this election. I despise Clinton, yet I have reservations about Trump. I suspect he may be a Clinton plant to ensure she is elected. Trump's behavior during this election cycle does not match his behavior over the last 20 years. He has come off as impulsive and crass, when he has been deliberate and calculating in private and public since the 80's. Pay attention, whenever Hillary has bad press, a scandal becomes known, or Trump pulls ahead in the polls, Trump commits an obvious and unnecessary blunder that benefits Hillary. I cannot vote for Gary Johnson because he has no idea what is going on in the world, see his Aleppo comments for example. I disagree with Jill Stein on every single issue. I have voted in every election since I turned 18, I will be 38 tomorrow, and I intend to vote this year as well. I will be voting for Trump because I agree with ALL of his policies yet I am not sure he is genuine. A while back I did joke around about writing in Elmo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1090-tobias","name":"Tobias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1090_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:34:02-07:00","id":980529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KRB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980507#post980507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On some things, very conservative (fiscal issues, social spending, 2nd Amendment, national defense/foreign policy) and on others, very liberal (abortion, the environment, LBTGQ rights). I absolutely despise any sort of political correctness; it's simply the tool of the weak to silence those they disagree with rather than constructively engaging them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think disparaging your political opposition as &quot;weak&quot; is terribly called for, and certainly not a great way to start a dialogue with those you disagree with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:43:00-07:00","id":980534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980529#post980529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think disparaging your political opposition as &quot;weak&quot; is terribly called for, and certainly not a great way to start a dialogue with those you disagree with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't care for it regardless of which side of the political aisle it comes from, and both sides use it far too much. It's not so much as political opposition as intellectual opposition to anyone who shuts down conversations and thought that way. It's impossible to have any sort of dialogue with people who immediately disregard other opinions by yelling &quot;you're Un-Christian if you _____&quot; or &quot;you're a (fill in the blank)ist pig&quot; rather than thinking and discussing. <br /> <br /> However, you are right in that I should not have used the word &quot;weak,&quot; and for that, I apologize. I should have said &quot;narrow-minded.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5853-krb","name":"KRB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T21:58:53-07:00","id":980582,"title":"","content":"I'm quite conservative, well I have some pretty big problems with the Republican Party, but we conservatives are a diverse lot and there are plenty of things that we differ in opinion on. I was a big time Ron Paul supporter back when he ran.<br /> <br /> It's a bit strange because most of the people I have role played with over the years have been conservative leaning to some degree, but it seems like online role playing communities are way more left leaning. <br /> <br /> Anyway, nice to encounter some other conservatives here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:01:31-07:00","id":980801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980582#post980582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a bit strange because most of the people I have role played with over the years have been conservative leaning to some degree, but it seems like online role playing communities are way more left leaning.<br /> <br /> Anyway, nice to encounter some other conservatives here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much my experience, until I moved from my hometown. And I agree with you on the online role-playing communities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:02:09-07:00","id":980962,"title":"","content":"The online communities are more left leaning because most of the first world is left leaning compared to American political standards. The US political landscape is heavily skewed towards the right. By American standards I'm solidly politically liberal, but in most of Europe I'd bee seen as a right-leaning centrist.<br /> <br /> On top of that, younger demographic cohorts are generally more left leaning on average, and the Gen Xer and Millenials are no exceptions. Most online communities are dominated by younger cohorts.<br /> <br /> So online communities feeling left leaning shouldn't really be surprising... they generally are unless they're aimed specifically at right leaning demographics or sub-groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:09:38-07:00","id":980970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980962#post980962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The online communities are more left leaning because most of the first world is left leaning compared to American political standards. The US political landscape is heavily skewed towards the right. By American standards I'm solidly politically liberal, but in most of Europe I'd bee seen as a right-leaning centrist.<br /> <br /> On top of that, younger demographic cohorts are generally more left leaning on average, and the Gen Xer and Millenials are no exceptions. Most online communities are dominated by younger cohorts.<br /> <br /> So online communities feeling left leaning shouldn't really be surprising... they generally are unless they're aimed specifically at right leaning demographics or sub-groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact: I was once hardcore attacked for calling myself a liberal in a chat full of Europeans, because the American left barely counts to their mindset. What a world!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:21:02-07:00","id":980977,"title":"","content":"&quot;So online communities feeling left leaning shouldn't really be surprising&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:25:19-07:00","id":980980,"title":"","content":"I'm an US liberal myself, but play a lot with conservative gamers. Miniature games and d20 games are a trend I have seen with conservative gamers. I'm not sure if this trend holds true outside of my limited experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:30:29-07:00","id":980981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980980#post980980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm an US liberal myself, but play a lot with conservative gamers. Miniature games and d20 games are a trend I have seen with conservative gamers. I'm not sure if this trend holds true outside of my limited experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a weird association with narrativist/storygames on the left and crunchy or OSR games on the right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:39:34-07:00","id":980990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980970#post980970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fun fact: I was once hardcore attacked for calling myself a liberal in a chat full of Europeans, because the American left barely counts to their mindset. What a world!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry to hear that. That said, I must admit that american left sounds like an oximoron to most europeans, myself included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:02:53-07:00","id":981006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tobias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980524#post980524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I despise Clinton, yet I have reservations about Trump. I suspect he may be a Clinton plant to ensure she is elected. Trump's behavior during this election cycle does not match his behavior over the last 20 years. He has come off as impulsive and crass, when he has been deliberate and calculating in private and public since the 80's. Pay attention, whenever Hillary has bad press, a scandal becomes known, or Trump pulls ahead in the polls, Trump commits an obvious and unnecessary blunder that benefits Hillary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Trump started out as a Plant. I grew up in an area where <a href=\"http://www.politico.com/magazine/story/2015/09/trumps-war-with-palm-beach-213122\" target=\"_blank\">Trump has a lot of business dealings</a>, so a lot of his actions fit his character. ( I don't remember him being particularly racist, but sexist fits his character.)<br /> <br /> However, I never expected Trump to want the presidency - too much oversight and no money in it. I think he was trying to pull a Palin (lose the election but rebuild his brand) and didn't expect to get the nomination. So now he is trying to throw the election because he doesn't want to be president, yet doesn't want to quit.<br /> <br /> /I hope I am not derailing the topic with Trump talk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 10-03-2016, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:21:57-07:00","id":981019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tobias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980524#post980524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I despise Clinton, yet I have reservations about Trump. I suspect he may be a Clinton plant to ensure she is elected. Trump's behavior during this election cycle does not match his behavior over the last 20 years. He has come off as impulsive and crass, when he has been deliberate and calculating in private and public since the 80's. Pay attention, whenever Hillary has bad press, a scandal becomes known, or Trump pulls ahead in the polls, Trump commits an obvious and unnecessary blunder that benefits Hillary.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a theory I've heard bandied about that I just cannot make any sense of. Exactly how would it even be possible for Trump to be a plant for Clinton? Like, how does that plan even work? He's supposed to ensure Clinton's election by... winning a majority of the Republican vote? How else is he supposed to have done that except by presenting himself as a candidate that mobilizes conservative sentiments, and once he's done that how is he supposed to then deliberately stop himself from winning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 10-03-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:38:12-07:00","id":981028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981019#post981019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a theory I've heard bandied about that I just cannot make any sense of. Exactly how would it even be possible for Trump to be a plant for Clinton? Like, how does that plan even work? He's supposed to ensure Clinton's election by... winning a majority of the Republican vote? How else is he supposed to have done that except by presenting himself as a candidate that mobilizes conservative sentiments, and once he's done that how is he supposed to then deliberately stop himself from winning?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is that his behavior and statements and gaffes are meant to be so offensive, ignorant, or blatant that they guarantee people vote for the opposition.<br /> <br /> 'Vote for me for class president, I'll give everyone extra homework and make sure no one can bring their phones to class.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:47:16-07:00","id":981033,"title":"","content":"I think people assume far too much competence on the part of politicians to facilitate something like that. Or maybe not enough? There's too many moving parts for that kind of farce to be worthwhile, and it seems like a weird way to export blame for his primacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:00:13-07:00","id":981046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981028#post981028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea is that his behavior and statements and gaffes are meant to be so offensive, ignorant, or blatant that they guarantee people vote for the opposition.<br /> <br /> 'Vote for me for class president, I'll give everyone extra homework and make sure no one can bring their phones to class.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that idea is predicated on those same gaffes propelling him to the top of the Republican ticket. That's either some Xanatos gambit levels of precognitive intrigue or a damning indictment of the Republican party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:14:53-07:00","id":981057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981033#post981033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people assume far too much competence on the part of politicians to facilitate something like that. Or maybe not enough? There's too many moving parts for that kind of farce to be worthwhile, and it seems like a weird way to export blame for his primacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something people from all sides have always done. If something doesn't seem possible blame a 'false flag' operation or conspiracy or some other problem. It often stems from problems with perception or institution or both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981046#post981046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that idea is predicated on those same gaffes propelling him to the top of the Republican ticket. That's either some Xanatos gambit levels of precognitive intrigue or a damning indictment of the Republican party.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit, it is strange to see an accusation like that in the same paragraph as an endorsement for their vote.<br /> <br /> But more than anything, I think, people are angry right now and they're feeling they're not being heard. And they're not. Our system isn't really built about letting the individual get their way except out of loopholes, and the way we form our social organizations means we're going to have a skewed view of the world at large. 'I feel this way, as do all of my friends, I don't know anyone who feels another way, so they must be in the minority.' Then having this not be reflected in nation-wide decisions made by people who are supposed to be following the favored and best interests of their constituency, it's pretty jarring. And everyone's stuck in this situation, doesn't matter which side you're on.<br /> <br /> It forces a lot of factionalism and it's natural to blame 'the other side,' in a two-party system. I'm not saying how anyone here is doing it, but it does seem like a lot of people are voting less about 'I support this candidate,' than, 'I absolutely don't want that candidate in the White House.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T16:53:38-07:00","id":981104,"title":"","content":"Let's please not turn this into a Donald Trump thread. I already get way too much Donald Trump debates almost everywhere else. I would like to have a discussion about conservatism in gaming without all of the Trump baggage. As a staunch conservative who feels that Trump is scummy and untrustworthy, I already feel like the election puts me between a rock and a hard place and Trump tangents tend to dominate discussions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:02:38-07:00","id":981111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981057#post981057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our system isn't really built about letting the individual get their way except out of loopholes, and the way we form our social organizations means we're going to have a skewed view of the world at large.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't help that the Founding Fathers didn't actually trust the general public to be a well educated electorate and focused on putting in checks to make sure the political players (even before they solidified into a two party system which wasn't the original intent of most of them) could put their thumbs on the scales (ex: the Electoral College being who actually elects the President instead of direct elections) instead of working to ensure a well educated electorate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:34:48-07:00","id":981164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981111#post981111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't help that the Founding Fathers didn't actually trust the general public to be a well educated electorate and focused on putting in checks to make sure the political players (even before they solidified into a two party system which wasn't the original intent of most of them) could put their thumbs on the scales (ex: the Electoral College being who actually elects the President instead of direct elections) instead of working to ensure a well educated electorate.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that conspiracies do exist. They may not have been the Illuminati, but 'Big Tobacco,' Enron, various banks and other people have shown they've been willing to lie, cheat or steal when it comes to money, even at the cost of other peoples lives. It's easy to dismiss someone who doesn't want to believe such-and-such could happen and, instead, it must be a ploy, because it's happened before.<br /> <br /> I find the whole thing interesting, and I feel for conservatives and liberals both. We're all more or less in the same boat, even people in other countries.<br /> <br /> Sorry, Sergeant Brother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:37:24-07:00","id":981166,"title":"","content":"Probably because the notion of checks on the political players seemed more feasible to them than an educated electorate.<br /> <br /> I know conservatism incorporates a wide variety of perspectives, but I'm curious about conservative perspectives on ideas of direct democracy or concepts like elite theory. Is there a profound belief that the electorate is ignorant and incapable of handling democracy? How does that interact with feelings about federalism or the actions of the military?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T06:32:58-07:00","id":981409,"title":"","content":"I'm curious about something myself: Why do conservatives see political correctness as a way to silence and dismiss them from the conversation? I've always thought of political correctness as a combination of common courtesy and empowering marginalized groups to speak up when they feel like they're actively being dismissed. It honestly baffles me how &quot;PC culture&quot; is considered this awful thing used to shackle and censor when I see it being used as the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> And I don't want to put words in anybody's mouth, but usually when I see people complaining about political correctness they're just complaining that they aren't allowed to openly be an asshole without getting called out on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:27:49-07:00","id":981426,"title":"","content":"Liberal and conservative have got two axis, moral values (freedom and tolerance vs family and self-control) and economy (Keynes vs Hayek, Estatism vs minarchism). Putin is conservative moral but estatist economy, and George Soros is liberal morality but capitalist economy. You can be A-B, A'-B', A'-B or A-B'. <br /> <br /> I don't trust who ask state has to controll economy to protect workers againts capitalist corporations, really you are giving all the economy power to a only corporatocrazy linked to politicals.<br /> <br /> * I am Spanish, and you can't imagine how is the main media here. Spain is the most self-critical in the world. No people despise theirself so much. Here we can't show our flag but for sport games. Here the patriotism, the love of fatherland is not well seen by the liberals. Be careful, because North-American can follow the same ways if you don't stop enemy propaganda. We need the right balance between self-criticism and self-estemm, both are necesay but both too much may prekudice you.<br /> <br /> * I hate the stereotype or clich\u00e9 from lots of fantasy and sci-fi fiction about religious zealots who hate all they can't understand, like the church from &quot;Fading Suns&quot; or the witch hunters from Warhammer 40.000.<br /> <br /> I was very offended when I read the backcovers from some sourcebooks of 7th Sea rpg<br /> <br /> The invisible college.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;Knowledge is deadly. Ten years ago, the Church was the leading light in Th\u00e9an research. Now its natural philosophers are dead or in hiding, driven underground by the might of the Inquisition. But the flame of knowledge cannot be extinguished: the Invisible College carries on in secret, seeking to know the mind of Theus through the world he created. The Invisible College sourcebook details the secret cells of Th\u00e9ah\u2019s infant scientific community, a timeline of recent inventions and discoveries, and their ultimate goals&quot;.<br /> <br /> Los vagos.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lora\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;a terrifying Inquisition drags innocent citizens from their homes&quot;<br /> <br /> WTF?! And now by its fault a lot of stupy gamers think Catholic Inquisition from real world dragged innocent citizens from their homes. Almost nobody knows in the 30's years &quot;los rojos&quot; (the red ones, red is the symbol of communist party) killed in only a month more people than Inquisition in all History. There was a true genocide againts Catholics, and now it isn't the time to be told time after time about religious fanatism.<br /> <br /> I say it again: I don't spend my money to buy expensive rpg books to after feeling like Peter Parker reading J.J.Jameson's articles about Spiderman. If you are talking me about Torquemada then shut up and move your buttom to ask freedom for Asia Bibi. <br /> <br /> * Have you thought anytime a campaign a communist invasion like the movie &quot;Red Dawn&quot; or videogame &quot;Homefront: the revolucion&quot;? I am sick lots of cyberpunk stories (for example OCP from Robocop's movies) where the evil empire are the multinacional corporations. Not all businessmen are like Harry Osborn or Lex Luthor! </span></span></span><br /> <br /> * In the real life Catholic Church doesn't allow magic, but there is a good reason: The supernatural effects are caused by two sources, God, or Hell forces. You can't use &quot;good magic&quot; because really you are calling the &quot;dark side of the force&quot;. Miracles aren't magic, you can ask a favor or gift, but God decides to give it or no. The paranormal effects in the fantasy worlds are different, because the natural laws are different and that allows no-sentient pokemons with superpowers or monster mindless plants walking to hunt. That is like a comic of superheroes, no starting in the ocultism. Gamer storytellers should notice about that when the inquisition, crusaders, witch hunters or fantasy equivalent are added in a story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:30:55-07:00","id":981427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981409#post981409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about something myself: Why do conservatives see political correctness as a way to silence and dismiss them from the conversation? I've always thought of political correctness as a combination of common courtesy and empowering marginalized groups to speak up when they feel like they're actively being dismissed. It honestly baffles me how &quot;PC culture&quot; is considered this awful thing used to shackle and censor when I see it being used as the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> And I don't want to put words in anybody's mouth, but usually when I see people complaining about political correctness they're just complaining that they aren't allowed to openly be an asshole without getting called out on it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For me, it really depends on the subject at hand. Like, the topic of political correctness is so broad, that it would have to depend on the issue we're discussing. <br /> <br /> For example, having &quot;Black writers write Black superhero comics because only they can 'get' Black people&quot; is something I strongly disagree with. I know you didn't say this, but I'm simply giving an example based on what I've heard.<br /> <br /> To me, being PC is typically fine. I just don't like extreme forms of it. Extreme left, is just as bad to me, as the extreme right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:33:14-07:00","id":981429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981409#post981409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about something myself: Why do conservatives see political correctness as a way to silence and dismiss them from the conversation? I've always thought of political correctness as a combination of common courtesy and empowering marginalized groups to speak up when they feel like they're actively being dismissed. It honestly baffles me how &quot;PC culture&quot; is considered this awful thing used to shackle and censor when I see it being used as the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> And I don't want to put words in anybody's mouth, but usually when I see people complaining about political correctness they're just complaining that they aren't allowed to openly be an asshole without getting called out on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To those of us who are right-leaning moderates (a dying breed, to be sure, but not dead yet!), &quot;PC Culture&quot; has directly led to things like &quot;Safe Spaces&quot; and &quot;Trigger Warnings&quot; being completely hijacked into something that they're not intended to be. For the former, it has created this idea that you're allowed to run from topics which make you uncomfortable, but in actuality a &quot;Safe Space&quot; should be a location where topics of any stripe can be discussed by speakers of any agenda without threat of ridicule or censorship. A place where, as you said, marginalized groups can voice their opinions without fear. The second is similar in that those who suffer from PTSD <i>ought</i> to be informed that a topic of discussion may be sensitive to them in particular because no one believes that they ought to suffer needlessly when it could be prevented, but it's been taken over by people who seek to use it to shut down conversations because they find them &quot;offensive.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981427#post981427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, being PC is typically fine. I just don't like extreme forms of it. Extreme left, is just as bad to me, as the extreme right.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tl;dr version of what I said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","user":"Frishman","date":". 10-04-2016, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:34:27-07:00","id":981430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981409#post981409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about something myself: Why do conservatives see political correctness as a way to silence and dismiss them from the conversation? I've always thought of political correctness as a combination of common courtesy and empowering marginalized groups to speak up when they feel like they're actively being dismissed. It honestly baffles me how &quot;PC culture&quot; is considered this awful thing used to shackle and censor when I see it being used as the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> And I don't want to put words in anybody's mouth, but usually when I see people complaining about political correctness they're just complaining that they aren't allowed to openly be an asshole without getting called out on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bLike most concept, Political Correctness is a tool and tools that can be abused. <br /> <br /> From what I have heard my conservatives friends and family, too many people hide behind Political Correctness to get away with unacceptable behavior. An individual may be rude and when called out about it, they complain about how the person called them out. <br /> <br /> They also feel that some people/organizations make too much of a fuss on word choice, instead of fixing the actually issue. For example, colleges need to increase the enrollment of females in sciences and engineering. The College's answer is to change language/show photos of woman in ads. They don't see how this actually solves anything and feel the college is just pandering to seem like they are doing something. <br /> <br /> Also, you have to realize that media calls out the worse incidents of PC and people fighting against PC. So you are going to conservative articles about colleges banning pronouns from their recruitment literature and liberal articles about racists ranting about PC. Your average person (no matter which side) is much more reasonable than the media portrays. <br /> <br /> /Okay. Liberal me is going to stop posting in this thread now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:38:36-07:00","id":981435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981430#post981430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">/Okay. Liberal me is going to stop posting in this thread now.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you actually brought up a good point; our views of the other side <i>are</i> typically colored by the media portrayal of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:38:53-07:00","id":981436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981430#post981430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bLike most concept, Political Correctness is a tool and tools that can be abused.<br /> <br /> From what I have heard my conservatives friends and family, too many people hide behind Political Correctness to get away with unacceptable behavior. An individual may be rude and when called out about it, they complain about how the person called them out.<br /> <br /> They also feel that some people/organizations make too much of a fuss on word choice, instead of fixing the actually issue. For example, colleges need to increase the enrollment of females in sciences and engineering. The College's answer is to change language/show photos of woman in ads. They don't see how this actually solves anything and feel the college is just pandering to seem like they are doing something.<br /> <br /> Also, you have to realize that media calls out the worse incidents of PC and people fighting against PC. So you are going to conservative articles about colleges banning pronouns from their recruitment literature and liberal articles about racists ranting about PC. Your average person (no matter which side) is much more reasonable than the media portrays.<br /> <br /> /Okay. Liberal me is going to stop posting in this thread now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very well said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:53:28-07:00","id":981442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981435#post981435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you actually brought up a good point; our views of the other side <i>are</i> typically colored by the media portrayal of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. This is what the media does:<br /> <br /> Republican #1: Abortion is murder!<br /> Republican #2: We need to get this freeloaders off of welfare!<br /> <br /> Liberal: Don't these idiots realize that there would be less abortion if we help out poor mothers? Republicans are stupid.<br /> <br /> Me: You do realize these two people don't even know each other and the media just cut these quotes out of context?<br /> <br /> Individuals get a skewed and schizophrenic view of the other party because the Media cherry picks quotes. One person may believe Abortion is wrong but could believe in helping young mothers. Another person doesn't give a shit about abortion. They just don't want their tax dollars to be spent on people who don't work. However, in aggregate, it makes the opposite party look like idiots.<br /> <br /> (I'm sure the conservatives could pick out liberal insanity better than I)<br /> <br /> /Apparently I am a liar. lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:18:17-07:00","id":981452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981442#post981442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Individuals get a skewed and schizophrenic view of the other party because the Media cherry picks quotes. One person may believe Abortion is wrong but could believe in helping young mothers. Another person doesn't give a shit about abortion. They just don't want their tax dollars to be spent on people who don't work. However, in aggregate, it makes the opposite party look like idiots.<br /> <br /> (I'm sure the conservatives could pick out liberal insanity better than I)<br /> <br /> /Apparently I am a liar. lol</div> </div> </div> </div>The best liberal insanity I've ever seen in recent years is the simultaneous cry from the left both for interculturalism and against cultural appropriation, with the net result being &quot;You need to respect and acknowledge all cultures, but you shouldn't allow them to ever mix, ever, for any reason. They should remain isolated pockets of cultural identity forever.&quot; Which, for the record, is not how interculturalism works and accomplishes the exact opposite of desegregation, which I'm told is called &quot;segregation,&quot; which I'm told is bad. By liberals.<br /> <br /> Now, my best friend is a Democrat who is a staunch opponent of the concept of cultural appropriation, so I'm well aware that it's silly to assume that all liberals hold these views simultaneously, but it's very much not apparent from the media's portrayal of the issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T10:40:19-07:00","id":981515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981427#post981427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For me, it really depends on the subject at hand. Like, the topic of political correctness is so broad, that it would have to depend on the issue we're discussing.<br /> <br /> For example, having &quot;Black writers write Black superhero comics because only they can 'get' Black people&quot; is something I strongly disagree with. I know you didn't say this, but I'm simply giving an example based on what I've heard.<br /> <br /> To me, being PC is typically fine. I just don't like extreme forms of it. Extreme left, is just as bad to me, as the extreme right.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> \u200bI believe in common sense decency towards others, but when I complain about Political Correctness, I'm talking about the extreme version of it. And I am a liberal, but extremism from any angle is usually bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:39:43-07:00","id":981566,"title":"","content":"We don't need to be politically correct, but to respect the human dignity.<br /> <br /> And we are a cosmopolitan society, not &quot;multicultural&quot;. Our society is open to different arts and folklores, and this allows different urban tribes, but we don't need to reject our roots. Multiculturalism is when we are asked to respect all cultures but really they mean we are the only ones who have to be ashamed about our past. Here in Spain multiculturalism has a different meaning: &quot;Spanish people has to be proud because Muslims invaded us, but to be ashamed because Spain is too Catholic&quot;. Have you readen anything about the corvent burnings in Spain? That wan't four fool men but a failed genocide. I don't need History lessons about McCarthy's with-hunt but about Stalin's great purge, Ucranian Holodomor, Mao's cultural revolution, the 1793-94 French Terror by Robespierre and jacobines, or the brutal genocide of la Vend\u00e9e shortly after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:43:28-07:00","id":981619,"title":"","content":"I think we're giving a bit too much of the blame to the media on some of this.<br /> <br /> The US political parties are very guilty of encouraging the wave of polarization and tribalism in the US political landscape. To keep the two party system in power, they need to convince frequently disparate groups together in a single coalition by convincing them that there's some common philosophic link between causes that don't inherently have one (as mentioned the issue of abortion vs. the issue of the social safety net concept).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:05:14-07:00","id":981644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981426#post981426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WTF?! And now by its fault a lot of stupy gamers think Catholic Inquisition from real world dragged innocent citizens from their homes. Almost nobody knows in the 30's years &quot;los rojos&quot; (the red ones, red is the symbol of communist party) killed in only a month more people than Inquisition in all History. There was a true genocide againts Catholics, and now it isn't the time to be told time after time about religious fanatism.<br /> <br /> I say it again: I don't spend my money to buy expensive rpg books to after feeling like Peter Parker reading J.J.Jameson's articles about Spiderman. If you are talking me about Torquemada then shut up and move your buttom to ask freedom for Asia Bibi.<br /> <br /> * Have you thought anytime a campaign a communist invasion like the movie &quot;Red Dawn&quot; or videogame &quot;Homefront: the revolucion&quot;? I am sick lots of cyberpunk stories (for example OCP from Robocop's movies) where the evil empire are the multinacional corporations. Not all businessmen are like Harry Osborn or Lex Luthor! [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> <br /> * In the real life Catholic Church doesn't allow magic, but there is a good reason: The supernatural effects are caused by two sources, God, or Hell forces. You can't use &quot;good magic&quot; because really you are calling the &quot;dark side of the force&quot;. Miracles aren't magic, you can ask a favor or gift, but God decides to give it or no. The paranormal effects in the fantasy worlds are different, because the natural laws are different and that allows no-sentient pokemons with superpowers or monster mindless plants walking to hunt. That is like a comic of superheroes, no starting in the ocultism. Gamer storytellers should notice about that when the inquisition, crusaders, witch hunters or fantasy equivalent are added in a story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, oh dear...<br /> <br /> Inquisitors were well-known for targeting innocent people, particularly vulnerable people like widows, and then <i>stealing their possessions after murdering them</i> for their own usage. People quickly happened upon the idea that you could guarantee your inheritance by turning in your old mother, or crushing a business partner by casting aspersions, or hey, that woman dares hold a business in her own right - let's accuse her of being a heretic/witch!<br /> <br /> And I hate to break it to you - but virtually everyone the Inquisition targeted was innocent. Everyone. <i><b>EVERYONE</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Even if you accept that SOME inquisitors SOMEWHERE believed they were actually doing the work of god, not one single person they killed deserved to die by any real standard beyond that of a myopic Medieval idiot. The Inquisition was definitive, substantial religious <i>persecution of the innocent</i>. Series that cast the Inquisition as the good guys and their victims as deserving have to go to the extreme of making the other side as evil as possible, and really it just ends up sounding like casting Jews as rat-faced, disease-carrying parasites so as to make the fucking Nazis sound good, and when you start talking about making Nazis sound good you get into a realllly awkward place that I don't think you or any sane person wants to go. Speaking of, you know who else the Inquisition killed? <i>Jews. </i>I'm not joking.<br /> <br /> And you don't need to go to modern times to find criticisms, either - there are contemporary rants against the Inquisition by priests who personally witnessed their abuses first hand.<br /> <br /> And before you get into the numbers of people killed, let me point out two things:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>This was long before the explosion of population we saw as a result of the Industrial Revolution. There were far, far fewer people then.</li> <li>This was before massive state control and industrial means of killing.</li> </ol>I'm not defending Stalinism - far from it, Stalinism is a horrible, horrible thing - but you can't go &quot;WELL STALIN IS THE WORST THING EVER SO NOTHING ELSE MEANS ANYTHING!&quot; Stalinist/Spanish Revolutionary massacres were a horrible thing. The Inquisition is <i>also</i> a horrible thing. We can talk about one without bringing up the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-04-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:37:05-07:00","id":981663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981409#post981409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about something myself: Why do conservatives see political correctness as a way to silence and dismiss them from the conversation? I've always thought of political correctness as a combination of common courtesy and empowering marginalized groups to speak up when they feel like they're actively being dismissed. It honestly baffles me how &quot;PC culture&quot; is considered this awful thing used to shackle and censor when I see it being used as the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> And I don't want to put words in anybody's mouth, but usually when I see people complaining about political correctness they're just complaining that they aren't allowed to openly be an asshole without getting called out on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't what people are saying when they say they oppose political correctness. <br /> <br /> Rather, there is a certain tendency of people on the left to villainize anyone who offers any opposition to their beliefs. Political correctness is at it's heart extreme intolerance. PC people won't say that they are intolerant of ideas other than their own, they will merely say that they strongly oppose truly evil things such as racism, sexism, homophobia, and so on. Then they present every issue in such a way as to portray anyone who disagrees with them as one of the afore mentioned heretics. Then the ends justify the means in crushing dissent. This attitude goes far beyond merely being vociferous and judgmental and very often extends into the realm of threats, doxxing, censorship, getting people fired, getting people expelled, and even actual violence. People who criticize PC don't merely object to getting called out on so called &quot;asshole behavior&quot; but object to people literally trying to terrorize them and destroy their lives and livelihood just for expressing dissent against people in power. <br /> <br /> I work in such an odious environment (a college) and must frequently nod and smile at beliefs I find objectionable for fear of losing my job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:16:16-07:00","id":981689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981663#post981663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't what people are saying when they say they oppose political correctness. <br /> <br /> Rather, there is a certain tendency of people on the left to villainize anyone who offers any opposition to their beliefs. Political correctness is at it's heart extreme intolerance. PC people won't say that they are intolerant of ideas other than their own, they will merely say that they strongly oppose truly evil things such as racism, sexism, homophobia, and so on. Then they present every issue in such a way as to portray anyone who disagrees with them as one of the afore mentioned heretics. Then the ends justify the means in crushing dissent. This attitude goes far beyond merely being vociferous and judgmental and very often extends into the realm of threats, doxxing, censorship, getting people fired, getting people expelled, and even actual violence. People who criticize PC don't merely object to getting called out on so called &quot;asshole behavior&quot; but object to people literally trying to terrorize them and destroy their lives and livelihood just for expressing dissent against people in power. <br /> <br /> I work in such an odious environment (a college) and must frequently nod and smile at beliefs I find objectionable for fear of losing my job.</div> </div> </div> </div>The counterpoint is when people act like I need to respect &quot;people like you and your loved ones are sick/sinful/don't exist/whatever&quot; as a valid political viewpoint instead out rightly calling that outright hate. I'm tired of having to debate my own right to exist.<br /> <br /> Also, I've been threatened and doxxed for having the gall to say nonbinary people exist. This isn't an issue with &quot;PC people,&quot; it's with radical assholes on the internet of all stripes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:18:01-07:00","id":981690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981619#post981619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we're giving a bit too much of the blame to the media on some of this.<br /> <br /> The US political parties are very guilty of encouraging the wave of polarization and tribalism in the US political landscape. To keep the two party system in power, they need to convince frequently disparate groups together in a single coalition by convincing them that there's some common philosophic link between causes that don't inherently have one (as mentioned the issue of abortion vs. the issue of the social safety net concept).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a result of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duverger%27s_law\" target=\"_blank\">Duverger's Law</a> forcing us into a two-party system. Political parties arise in any Republic as it makes it easier for people with a common cause to rally together and share resources and to create a &quot;manifesto&quot; of sorts as to what they want the government to do. Because of America's &quot;first-past-the-post&quot; system, mathematically we're stuck in a two-party system which forces disparate causes that would be different political parties in countries that conduct preferential voting into rallying together to form large conglomerates for the purpose of gaining greater access to resources.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I think I just channeled a disgruntled political scientist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981689#post981689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I've been threatened and doxxed for having the gall to say nonbinary people exist. This isn't an issue with &quot;PC people,&quot; it's with radical assholes on the internet of all stripes.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that, we can agree, and let me for one say that I am deeply sorry that radical assholes on the internet did that to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","user":"Frishman","date":". 10-04-2016, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:00:12-07:00","id":981711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981663#post981663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather, there is a certain tendency of people on the left to villainize anyone who offers any opposition to their beliefs. Political correctness is at it's heart extreme intolerance. PC people won't say that they are intolerant of ideas other than their own, they will merely say that they strongly oppose truly evil things such as racism, sexism, homophobia, and so on. Then they present every issue in such a way as to portray anyone who disagrees with them as one of the afore mentioned heretics. Then the ends justify the means in crushing dissent. This attitude goes far beyond merely being vociferous and judgmental and very often extends into the realm of threats, doxxing, censorship, getting people fired, getting people expelled, and even actual violence. People who criticize PC don't merely object to getting called out on so called &quot;asshole behavior&quot; but object to people literally trying to terrorize them and destroy their lives and livelihood just for expressing dissent against people in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've pretty much just described the alt-right playbook. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:06:17-07:00","id":981714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981711#post981711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've pretty much just described the alt-right playbook. </div> </div> </div> </div>That is completely absurd. What universities does the alt-right control? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981689#post981689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The counterpoint is when people act like I need to respect &amp;quot;people like you and your loved ones are sick/sinful/don't exist/whatever&amp;quot; as a valid political viewpoint instead out rightly calling that outright hate. I'm tired of having to debate my own right to exist.<br /> <br /> Also, I've been threatened and doxxed for having the gall to say nonbinary people exist. This isn't an issue with &amp;quot;PC people,&amp;quot; it's with radical assholes on the internet of all stripes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anybody who uses dozing and against people they don't like is an asshole who I would completely condemn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:23:20-07:00","id":981724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981714#post981714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is completely absurd. What universities does the alt-right control? </div> </div> </div> </div>Hillsdale comes to mind. U of Dallas too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:28:28-07:00","id":981728,"title":"","content":"Well this was a nice thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:40:09-07:00","id":981739,"title":"","content":"I started this thread and I'm happy so watch it flourish. However, I'm not sure how I can express my opinions without being censored. It's not only a problem here, but a internet-wide issue: Facebook and Twitter are biased against conservatives, and most media outlets (Huffington Post, Buzzfeed etc.) are openly against conservatives. If you guys are interested, I have two interesting sources of news and commentary:<br /> <br /> The Imaginative Conservative: <a href=\"http://www.theimaginativeconservative.org/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.theimaginativeconservative.org/</a><br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> The National Review: <a href=\"http://www.nationalreview.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nationalreview.com/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:50:43-07:00","id":981749,"title":"","content":"I feel ya. When I jumped in, i had hopes that we could have a space where we could have polite discourse on the gamut of conservative views while fielding respectful questions about our beliefs.<br /> <br /> But apparently conservatives don't get &quot;Safe Spaces&quot; :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:04:03-07:00","id":981756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981739#post981739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started this thread and I'm happy so watch it flourish. However, I'm not sure how I can express my opinions without being censored. It's not only a problem here, but a internet-wide issue: Facebook and Twitter are biased against conservatives, and most media outlets (Huffington Post, Buzzfeed etc.) are openly against conservatives. If you guys are interested, I have two interesting sources of news and commentary:<br /> <br /> The Imaginative Conservative: <a href=\"http://www.theimaginativeconservative.org/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.theimaginativeconservative.org/</a><br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> The National Review: <a href=\"http://www.nationalreview.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nationalreview.com/</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Receiving criticism for your opinion is not censorship. Please understand what Freedom of Speech is; the entire spirit of that amendment is so that the government has to be open to criticism, and cannot shut down dissenting opinion. When a group of people on the internet criticize you, when you feel like you're being ignored, or that your opinion is unpopular, that is not censorship.<br /> <br /> Hell, even if Onyx Path sent its moderators to ban you from their forums, that is not censorship because they have a right to maintain their environments in a way that they feel is safe and productive for their customers. You're completely free to go to tumblr, twitter, youtube, facebook, what have you, and voice whatever message you like. The government is not going to come in and black bag you, because you are not being censored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-04-2016, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:04:50-07:00","id":981757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981749#post981749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel ya. When I jumped in, i had hopes that we could have a space where we could have polite discourse on the gamut of conservative views while fielding respectful questions about our beliefs.<br /> <br /> But apparently conservatives don't get &quot;Safe Spaces&quot; :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope you're not against Safe Spaces as part of PC culture, then, that would make you a hypocrite wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> I'm aware you made the comparison yourself, but you said Safe Spaces, in quotes, with a tongue emoticon, if you weren't trying to convey sarcasm, you kind of did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:13:59-07:00","id":981766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981663#post981663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't what people are saying when they say they oppose political correctness.<br /> <br /> Rather, there is a certain tendency of people on the left to villainize anyone who offers any opposition to their beliefs. Political correctness is at it's heart extreme intolerance. PC people won't say that they are intolerant of ideas other than their own, they will merely say that they strongly oppose truly evil things such as racism, sexism, homophobia, and so on. Then they present every issue in such a way as to portray anyone who disagrees with them as one of the afore mentioned heretics. Then the ends justify the means in crushing dissent. This attitude goes far beyond merely being vociferous and judgmental and very often extends into the realm of threats, doxxing, censorship, getting people fired, getting people expelled, and even actual violence. People who criticize PC don't merely object to getting called out on so called &quot;asshole behavior&quot; but object to people literally trying to terrorize them and destroy their lives and livelihood just for expressing dissent against people in power.<br /> <br /> I work in such an odious environment (a college) and must frequently nod and smile at beliefs I find objectionable for fear of losing my job.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've worked moderation and support for a certain famous MOBA with just about the most toxic community you can possibly imagine. In one thread a pair of guys started talking about their sex lives (I assume they were long distance friends) they then started talking graphically about it, I'm not going to get into specifics because I'm pretty sure doing so would be against this board's rules. We have a policy against mature content, first offense is a seven day suspension. I did the disciplinary action. The next morning I found out that people higher up had received an email complaint over the suspension. I was told that a couple of guys being guys is not worth a seven day suspension, that I should have only deleted the comments, and then they told my managers to fire me and remove me from all conversations before I was even spoken to. I was also a contractor, so they could legally fire me for no reason, and I do not get to file for unemployment while I look for a new job.<br /> <br /> Not exactly unique to the left or PC culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:20:19-07:00","id":981773,"title":"","content":"Please read earlier discussions within this thread itself in regards to his we view safe spaces. I believe you'll find it on page 3. <br /> <br /> And kindly disengage from the pedagogy. We've heard all of it before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:11:26-07:00","id":981809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981773#post981773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please read earlier discussions within this thread itself in regards to his we view safe spaces. I believe you'll find it on page 3.<br /> <br /> And kindly disengage from the pedagogy. We've heard all of it before.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981429#post981429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;PC Culture&quot; has directly led to things like &quot;Safe Spaces&quot; and &quot;Trigger Warnings&quot; being completely hijacked into something that they're not intended to be. For the former, it has created this idea that you're allowed to run from topics which make you uncomfortable, but in actuality a &quot;Safe Space&quot; should be a location where topics of any stripe can be discussed by speakers of any agenda without threat of ridicule or censorship.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not is it though? Safe Spaces were originally a concept developed for victims, in other words the victims of violence, rape, other forms of abuse, etc. In another thread I actually did exactly what you proclaim safe spaces to be - the concept that you propose in a way to make it seem desirable. When people attacked people with conservative views and called them idiots without actually criticizing their arguments, I asked them to stop. And yet I still had other people from this thread decrying it as 'an echo chamber'. The irony of deriding another thread for that, before retreating back to a thread literally named after their own views and accusing anyone with differing viewpoints of pedantry is not lost on me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:23:39-07:00","id":981817,"title":"","content":"Wasn't me, though. I have literally no idea what you're talking about. Meanwhile, you came into this thread without reading the previous posts and began lecturing people who don't have any of this context. If that is what you would care to do, I shall depart and leave you to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:29:23-07:00","id":981822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981817#post981817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't me, though. I have literally no idea what you're talking about. Meanwhile, you came into this thread without reading the previous posts and began lecturing people who don't have any of this context. If that is what you would care to do, I shall depart and leave you to it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except I did read the previous posts?<br /> <br /> And the point that it 'wasn't you' isn't exactly material, considering you're in a thread for conservative view points, someone criticized your comment, and your immediate response is &quot;I don't have to listen to this, if only we had SAFE SPACES, am I right guys?&quot; <br /> <br /> Apparently oblivious that that is exactly what this is currently attempting to be, and not the kind you proposed where everyone gets to discuss their ideas. Well I mean, certainly you can, if you don't take attitude with someone accusing your character before trying to duck out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-04-2016, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:35:08-07:00","id":981827,"title":"","content":"Welp. I'm glad all of us conservative gamers were able to hang around for a bit. <br /> <br /> You know, that brings up a question: Is there a forum that specifically has conservative gamers? The only other table top forum I know of is rpg.net, and...well...no thanks. lol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:43:52-07:00","id":981836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981827#post981827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welp. I'm glad all of us conservative gamers were able to hang around for a bit.<br /> <br /> You know, that brings up a question: Is there a forum that specifically has conservative gamers? The only other table top forum I know of is rpg.net, and...well...no thanks. lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, actually there is therpgsite.com which is run by a conservative and is, I would say, politically middle of the road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T19:42:21-07:00","id":981915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981836#post981836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, actually there is therpgsite.com which is run by a conservative and is, I would say, politically middle of the road.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect. I'll check it out. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T20:18:03-07:00","id":981926,"title":"","content":"Honestly thinking about my place on the political spectrum never ceases to amuse me.<br /> <br /> When I was younger I used to be fairly liberal. These days I'm definitely centrist and, in fact, learn conservative on a number of issues. It's not so much that my opinions or views on issues have changed over the years, but rather that the political spectrum itself has moved quite a bit. Ideas that used to be radically liberal are now viewed as merely somewhat liberal whereas ideas that were once middle-of-the-road are often viewed as conservative or even regressive.<br /> <br /> I'm still not entirely comfortable with the thought of labeling myself conservative though - unfortunately there are a lot of very nasty groups of people (xenophobes, radical-fundamentalist Christians, white supremacists, and such) who often flock towards certain conservative individuals, movements and ideologies and it makes me uncomfortable to imagine myself associating with them.<br /> <br /> Certainly the far left has its share of radicals and loons, but they tend to be more annoying and aggravating than anything else. In contrast I often find the people on the far right fringe to be downright frightening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T22:35:35-07:00","id":981971,"title":"","content":"Is gaming culture actually as liberal as the original post implied? And when we talk about conservative gaming sites, what do we mean? I've certainly found niches on the Internet where my own Canadian centrism (i.e, flaming socialist by US standards) seems to line up with average group belief, but they always appeared out-numbered by the places dominated by what is now collectively dubbed the alt-right. To use the recently mentioned therpgsite.com as the example, it's the baby of the TheRPGPundit and my experience was the usual stock &quot;anti-PC culture&quot; stuff that's commonly used to excuse bigotry. Are there conservative gaming sites that don't end up catering to the unsavory elements of conservatism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T22:42:54-07:00","id":981974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981644#post981644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, oh dear...<br /> <br /> Inquisitors were well-known for targeting innocent people, particularly vulnerable people like widows, and then <i>stealing their possessions after murdering them</i> for their own usage. People quickly happened upon the idea that you could guarantee your inheritance by turning in your old mother, or crushing a business partner by casting aspersions, or hey, that woman dares hold a business in her own right - let's accuse her of being a heretic/witch!<br /> <br /> And I hate to break it to you - but virtually everyone the Inquisition targeted was innocent. Everyone. <i><b>EVERYONE</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Even if you accept that SOME inquisitors SOMEWHERE believed they were actually doing the work of god, not one single person they killed deserved to die by any real standard beyond that of a myopic Medieval idiot. The Inquisition was definitive, substantial religious <i>persecution of the innocent</i>. Series that cast the Inquisition as the good guys and their victims as deserving have to go to the extreme of making the other side as evil as possible, and really it just ends up sounding like casting Jews as rat-faced, disease-carrying parasites so as to make the fucking Nazis sound good, and when you start talking about making Nazis sound good you get into a realllly awkward place that I don't think you or any sane person wants to go. Speaking of, you know who else the Inquisition killed? <i>Jews. </i>I'm not joking.<br /> <br /> And you don't need to go to modern times to find criticisms, either - there are contemporary rants against the Inquisition by priests who personally witnessed their abuses first hand.<br /> <br /> And before you get into the numbers of people killed, let me point out two things:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>This was long before the explosion of population we saw as a result of the Industrial Revolution. There were far, far fewer people then.</li> <li>This was before massive state control and industrial means of killing.</li> </ol>I'm not defending Stalinism - far from it, Stalinism is a horrible, horrible thing - but you can't go &quot;WELL STALIN IS THE WORST THING EVER SO NOTHING ELSE MEANS ANYTHING!&quot; Stalinist/Spanish Revolutionary massacres were a horrible thing. The Inquisition is <i>also</i> a horrible thing. We can talk about one without bringing up the other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Catholic Inquisition wasn't worse than Protestant Wich-hunt, only we lost the propaganda war. The black anti-Catholic legend lied or exaggerated a lot of things. For example the iron maiden wasn't used in the middle age, the chastity belts are also other historical legend. The &quot;Droit du seigneur&quot; is another myth, or at least if it happened it wasn't allowed by laws. What do you know about the medieval &quot;peace and truce of God&quot;? The dark age wasn't so dark. Why not to talk about Irish slaves? Yes, Irish slaves in Northeamerica suffered more than black people, but we don't see movies about Irish slaves.<br /> <br /> And now USA is suffering her own black legend to be presented like the new evil empire, but the world isn't better with Russia or China like supreme power. North-american like the new American empire is following the same steps of Spanish nation. We aren't forgiven to be Christians.<br /> <br /> If you don't like Russia Today news, I don't like those shits like Garth Ernnis' Preacher comics. Self-criticism doesn't mean self-deprecating. We don't need lessons from people who knows nothing about Spanish anti-Catholic failed genocide in the 30's, the reasons of the Mexican Cristero war, or the Pakistani anti-blasphemy law what has condemme some Christians with false acusations.<br /> <br /> Do you remember when Kamala Khan, the new Miss Marvel with Pakistani origin, asked freedom for Asia Bibi? Me neither.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 10-05-2016, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T00:03:48-07:00","id":981992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981974#post981974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Catholic Inquisition wasn't worse than Protestant Wich-hunt, only we lost the propaganda war. The black anti-Catholic legend lied or exaggerated a lot of things. For example the iron maiden wasn't used in the middle age, the chastity belts are also other historical legend. The &amp;quot;Droit du seigneur&amp;quot; is another myth, or at least if it happened it wasn't allowed by laws. What do you know about the medieval &amp;quot;peace and truce of God&amp;quot;? The dark age wasn't so dark. Why not to talk about Irish slaves? Yes, Irish slaves in Northeamerica suffered more than black people, but we don't see movies about Irish slaves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You'll notice that I never referred to the iron maiden, chastity belts, or scientific development during the medieval period. Protestant witch hunts are a different but also bad thing. Nice try deflecting, but I never mentioned any of those things.<br /> <br /> And I'll notice you never answered my points. Any of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T00:30:23-07:00","id":981996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981971#post981971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is gaming culture actually as liberal as the original post implied?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly.<br /> <br /> Gaming culture, as part of the wider modern geek culture, is one that's facing a lot of push (and blow back for it) from the left as its rise to more mainstream status as caused a large number of minority individuals to feel it is the right time to start pushing back at a lot of the regressive elements in the geek community. Conservative members are put in a difficult spot by this because the left and the regressive forces are both frequently too heavy handed with making the narrative a binary choice of &quot;with us&quot; or &quot;against us.&quot; While I don't personally think there's a lot of middle ground on the topics at hand, I don't think the most vocal left in the gamer world is doing itself a favor by alienating the conservatives that would at worst simple stay out of it by calling such individuals inherently siding for the regressive attitudes by not actively pushing against them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981974#post981974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Catholic Inquisition wasn't worse than Protestant Wich-hunt, only we lost the propaganda war. The black anti-Catholic legend lied or exaggerated a lot of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Black Legend is shit. The exaggerations of the Spanish Inquisition and the myths about it don't do anyone justice. But that includes the not giving its victims historical justice either.<br /> <br /> The Spanish Inquisition tortured and killed people; esp. already oppressed minorities since most of their targets were forced converts from Judaism and Islam. That's not myth, that's truth. They kept records of it. I don't really care about trying to rank historical atrocities. But don't deny them either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why not to talk about Irish slaves? </div> </div> </div>Because it's a neo-nazi myth. Don't complain about people not knowing their Spanish history while falling for myths that exaggerated the factually horrible actions of the Inquisition to ludicrous levels, and then dive head first into revisionist racist myths that are more preposterous than any of the Black Legend.<br /> <br /> 1) The harsh treatment of the Irish in the colonies and early USA are talked about in education, and discussions of racism in US history.<br /> <br /> 2) The indentured servitude of people now considered white was not limited to the Irish, and the Irish Slaves myth is mostly based on a single massive push of Irish people into indentured servitude after an English civil war.<br /> <br /> 3) Comparing indentured servitude to chattel slavery should be at best a bad offensive joke. Indentured servants were in the eyes of the law full humans with the protections provided therein. Their status rarely lasted more than seven years, and it was not hereditary. Chattel slaves were property deny any rights as human beings, were so for life, and their status was hereditary and forced upon their children.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you remember when Kamala Khan, the new Miss Marvel with Pakistani origin, asked freedom for Asia Bibi? Me neither. </div> </div> </div>If comic book authors spent a page on every ridiculous human rights violation around the world... they'd just be newspapers about human rights violations.<br /> <br /> Kamala Khan is an American character of Pakistani decent. Her focus as a fictional character is not on cleaning up Pakistan's insane human rights violations, and there's no reason for her to know about Asia Bibi over the hundreds of other Christians the Pakistani government persecutes every year for their faith, or the thousands of women of any faith the same government persecutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 10-05-2016, 03:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T01:04:21-07:00","id":982005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist#post979988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, any conservative gamers around? The Ron Paul / Gary Johnson crowd is also very welcome!</div> </div> </div> </div>Conservative and proud!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980015#post980015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm Pro Life.(With exceptions for rape, incest, and worst-case scenarios.) Don't want the kid? Plenty of people looking to adopt.</div> </div> </div> </div>While i am like you in not believing in abortion other than in certain cases, i don't see it as making me 'pro-life'. Just anti-abortion. Heck over on another site, we have a semi-political thread where someone mentioned a pair of adults suffering downs syndrome in iirc Australia are wondering if they should have kids thinking it might also have downs, or worse.. I can understand the logic some use in saying maybe those parents who have debilitating genetic conditions might not want to bring a kid into the world with it (or worse)&lt; but i can also see the emotional argument, in that there are plenty examples of good families who have strugled but still raised a good kid (or 4) who did have genetic conditions, and so that shouldn't automatically be an excluding reason...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980015#post980015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm Pro Gun Control. Assault rifles are for the battlefield, not the suburbs.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you call an assault rifle? A 306? An AR-15? A Bereeta 9mm? All are single shot weapons.. <br /> As for me, i am pro gun/2nd amendment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980015#post980015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm Pro Death Penalty. You kill, you deserve to be killed; not as a &quot;deterrent&quot;, but to make damn sure you don't kill again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am also pro-death penalty, but i hate it that we have appeal after appeal after hit hit the appelate court, from the appeal that they appealed last time, stringing out the time someone serves to 20+ years. I have long felt, that the LEVEL of proof before someone can be SENTENCED to death, needs to be a hell of a lot more stringent than we have seen in the past (case and point 30+ Clemencies for death row inmates in the past year or so cause of DNA evidence clearing them).. HOWEVER if they do get sentenced, they should get 1 appeal, and after that is exhausted, they should have said sentence carried out within 5 years at the most. I also feel there should be some more crimes that should get someone the death penalty.<br /> Drug dealing, especially all those who 'cut the drugs' with stuff that is causing all these overdoses, imo should qualify. So to should child rape/sex slave and human trafficking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980015#post980015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm... respectfully ambivalent about Marriage Equality.(I know what the Bible says, but the First Amendment says we shouldn't make laws based on religion, so while I wouldn't vote for it, I also wouldn't vote against.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You wanna get married. GO for it. Just don't expect or demand i support/accept it. That's my mantra towards the whole LGBTQ marriage angle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980015#post980015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As a Multi-ethnic American, I try to see both sides of any race issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, there are 3 actual 'genetic' races. Negroid, Mongolid and Caucasian. All else are Ethnicities..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980015#post980015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think America has SOME responsibility to act as the World's police, but only because no one else seems to want to step up. I sometimes think if we had just let the Soviets HAVE Afghanistan back during the Cold War, it would be THEM dealing with Islamic Extremists, and not us. Seems like every time we step in to help, the people we help turn around and attack us later, usually with the guns WE gave them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Just cause we can, doesn't mean we should.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980182#post980182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Still tend to dislike Plans to &quot;Burn down the establishment!!!&quot; without a plan of WHAT precisely you will replace it with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the best officers i worked for in the mil often had the mantra of &quot;Don't just say something is wrong. Come up with a plan to fix it&quot;..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KRB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980507#post980507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On some things, very conservative (fiscal issues, social spending, 2nd Amendment, national defense/foreign policy) and on others, very liberal (abortion, the environment, LBTGQ rights). I absolutely despise any sort of political correctness; it's simply the tool of the weak to silence those they disagree with rather than constructively engaging them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well said on that latter line (and that's all i will say on it).. As for the fiscal issues, i have always felt that if WE the people need to keep within a budget, SO SHOULD governments. If they are needing to borrow, even AFTER raking in all the tax revenue they do, to pay for all the damn projects and such they have, then CUT THE HELL back on what you are spending.<br /> Also imo if you Can't balance your OWN BUDGET, and are borrowing, you shouldn't be giving out monies to other countries...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=980970#post980970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fun fact: I was once hardcore attacked for calling myself a liberal in a chat full of Europeans, because the American left barely counts to their mindset. What a world!</div> </div> </div> </div>Had that happen before a few years back. Had one adnd related site, where an OT thread asking for advice on where someone was thinking of moving to (his firm had an opening in 5 foreign countries) and i mentioned what i felt i was politically (since that was one of the question lines he had asked for), and someone said &quot;With what i know of you from other postings, you seem more XYZ&quot;.. and that was in THEIR countries terminology..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981111#post981111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't help that the Founding Fathers didn't actually trust the general public to be a well educated electorate and focused on putting in checks to make sure the political players (even before they solidified into a two party system which wasn't the original intent of most of them) could put their thumbs on the scales (ex: the Electoral College being who actually elects the President instead of direct elections) instead of working to ensure a well educated electorate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just that, but the founders were more 'Citizen workers than purely statesmen'. Compare that to nowdays and politicians seem to see it as a lifestyle, where if you ain't in it for 20+ years, you are inexperienced etc...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981409#post981409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about something myself: Why do conservatives see political correctness as a way to silence and dismiss them from the conversation? I've always thought of political correctness as a combination of common courtesy and empowering marginalized groups to speak up when they feel like they're actively being dismissed. It honestly baffles me how &quot;PC culture&quot; is considered this awful thing used to shackle and censor when I see it being used as the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> And I don't want to put words in anybody's mouth, but usually when I see people complaining about political correctness they're just complaining that they aren't allowed to openly be an asshole without getting called out on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe because of HOW its put into place/enforced. Courtesy goes both ways, but often in the areas we see the most cries of PC from, its often one side discusses, the other side gets shouted down/ignored. Such as on a # of college campuses, you can have 'free speech zones&quot;, but if you speak out in a pro-conservative manner, you get smacked for 'race/hate speech, even if you are NOT saying a damn thing about race.. <br /> <br /> Cont next post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T01:27:02-07:00","id":982009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981429#post981429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To those of us who are right-leaning moderates (a dying breed, to be sure, but not dead yet!), &quot;PC Culture&quot; has directly led to things like &quot;Safe Spaces&quot; and &quot;Trigger Warnings&quot; being completely hijacked into something that they're not intended to be. For the former, it has created this idea that you're allowed to run from topics which make you uncomfortable, but in actuality a &quot;Safe Space&quot; should be a location where topics of any stripe can be discussed by speakers of any agenda without threat of ridicule or censorship. A place where, as you said, marginalized groups can voice their opinions without fear. The second is similar in that those who suffer from PTSD <i>ought</i> to be informed that a topic of discussion may be sensitive to them in particular because no one believes that they ought to suffer needlessly when it could be prevented, but it's been taken over by people who seek to use it to shut down conversations because they find them &quot;offensive.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly frish. What should have been 'treat us with respect, and we treat you with respect' seems to have (to my pov) turned out to, you need to tolerate US and our ideas but we don't need to even recognize yours, let alone tolerate them.<br /> It seems we are so quick to shut down conversations, so we don't offend, even if its say ME saying &quot;THAT might offend Ms Marple&quot;, and you not being allowed to say it cause someone 'claims its offensive, so we gotta not allow it, even IF Ms Marple doesn't feel its offensive herself.. Case and point, one of my Communication shops had several gal workers (inc the leading chief), and they were often the MORE sexual joke telling people in said shops. BUT we guys were often admonished to NOT tell a sexual joke, just in case it might offend one of the gals...?!??!?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981442#post981442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Me: You do realize these two people don't even know each other and the media just cut these quotes out of context?<br /> <br /> Individuals get a skewed and schizophrenic view of the other party because the Media cherry picks quotes.<br /> <br /> /Apparently I am a liar. lol</div> </div> </div> </div>And its (IMO) not just the cherry picking of quotes, its often the cherry picking of which PART of a quote, that is t<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981663#post981663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't what people are saying when they say they oppose political correctness.<br /> <br /> Rather, there is a certain tendency of people on the left to villainize anyone who offers any opposition to their beliefs. Political correctness is at it's heart extreme intolerance.he issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well said Sarge... I've often been labeled a racist, or xenophobe, cause i dislike ILLEGAL immigration but have no issue with legal immigration. Even though i keep mentioning to those who cry that at me, that its NOT just those 'south of the border', but all that come here illegally.. Whether its someone who entered on a fake 'school visa', snuck across the rio grande, or came here on a tourist visa and just decided to never return...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981739#post981739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started this thread and I'm happy so watch it flourish. However, I'm not sure how I can express my opinions without being censored. It's not only a problem here, but a internet-wide issue: Facebook and Twitter are biased against conservatives, and most media outlets (Huffington Post, Buzzfeed etc.) are openly against conservatives</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not just the web that's like that.. I have seen a # of reports and heard many stories of conservatives in hollywood having to hide their political outlook, cause when they get found out as BEING conservative, all of a sudden, jobs shrink up. Acting gigs disappear and the like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981756#post981756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Receiving criticism for your opinion is not censorship. Please understand what Freedom of Speech is; the entire spirit of that amendment is so that the government has to be open to criticism, and cannot shut down dissenting opinion. When a group of people on the internet criticize you, when you feel like you're being ignored, or that your opinion is unpopular, that is not censorship.<br /> <br /> Hell, even if Onyx Path sent its moderators to ban you from their forums, that is not censorship because they have a right to maintain their environments in a way that they feel is safe and productive for their customers. You're completely free to go to tumblr, twitter, youtube, facebook, what have you, and voice whatever message you like. The government is not going to come in and black bag you, because you are not being censored.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is in a way censorship though, if (as i found out on one older gaming site) they only censor ONE SIDE of any arguments that cropped up, and not the other..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981827#post981827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, that brings up a question: Is there a forum that specifically has conservative gamers? The only other table top forum I know of is rpg.net, and...well...no thanks. lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends. Besides this site, there is classicbattletech.com for classic battletech fans. dragonsfoot.org and planetadnd.com for those of us who are ADND gamers. Swrpgnetwork's holonet and rancor's pit for us old school D6 west end games star wars fans..<br /> <br /> Now whether they are more conservative vs liberal i couldn't say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T05:35:28-07:00","id":982075,"title":"","content":"Do you like Garth Ennis' Preacher comics? Do you see the TV serie? And do you know a Pakistani Christian lost his arms because he didn't want to convert to islam? Do you know about priest in Chinese prisons because they aren't members of the patriotic church, created and controlled by the goverment? Have you heart about bombs in Nigerian church during the mass? What do you know about riots in Odissha (India) againt naive Christians? Who are you to give me lessons about History and intolerance in the current age? <br /> <br /> The horrible things we have been told about Catholic Inquisition are, lies, exaggerations or there were attenuanting circumstances. (And the Catholic Inquisition had got a rules about torture. Secular power for ordinary crimes was worse. ) It wasn't a bloodbath like we see in the media and fiction. Bloodbath is the revolutionary forces (communist dictatorships or terrorist groups), but the anti-comunism has a bad image in the media.I don't forgive this double standard. <br /> <br /> <br /> * Kamala Khan, the character from Marvel Comics, was created to fight againts islamophopia, but they didn't notice giving her a Pakistani origin was a mistake because Christians and Hindu minorities suffer a hard intolerance. Sometimes infidel girls are kidnnaped to be forced to convert to Islam and marry Muslim men. A young boy was burnt alive only because two unknown men asked him and he replied he was Christian. (and because my English isn't enough good to tell more things I read from fides.org new).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T09:36:20-07:00","id":982173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982005#post982005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but if you speak out in a pro-conservative manner, you get smacked for 'race/hate speech, even if you are NOT saying a damn thing about race..</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this particular nugget is that a lot of people say things that are not intended to be bigoted, but are incidentally problematic. Since there's no malice intended, when they get called out for the statement being problematic, they get defensive instead of open to dialog about what was wrong with what they said, and dialog devolves into arguments and depending on the space in question on side gets shut down.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, there's also all sorts of topics that people that call themselves conservative have labeled as &quot;conservative&quot; or &quot;liberal&quot; positions that have nothing to do with liberal or conservative values. My stance on abortion is extremely traditional (it predates Jesus) and conservative... and it pro-abortion based on my faith. But I'm pro-abortion so it's liberalism regardless of why I am.<br /> <br /> I'll give two examples of things that seem completely innocent of bigotry, and then go into why they're problems:<br /> <br /> First is a simple one because most people agree that this is a bit creepy. There's a rather large number of women - esp. older women - that seem to think that it's completely cool to touch another person's hair to see how it feels.<br /> <br /> Beyond the creepy body space invasion aspect of that, it's also a racist issue in the US. Why? The vast majority of those women are white, and the vast majority of the people who have to deal with their hair being touched like that are black women that have decided to not treat their hair to make it look more &quot;white.&quot; Again, there's nothing malicious in the intent, it's patently clear it's curiosity. But the effect for the black women that have to deal with this is to feel othered, because their natural hair isn't just accepted as being normal but it's something &quot;exotic&quot; that people feel they have the right to experience at the cost of that black women's personal comfort. It also (again with no intent from creeper personal space invading hair touchers) reinforces a constant struggle within the American black female community regarding physical presentation. They are pressured by society to look more &quot;normal&quot; by white standards by doing things like straightening their hair because it can directly impact things like job interviews. So every time someone makes a big deal out of their natural hair, it's just reinforcing the idea that they're doing something wrong just because they have very naturally curly hair.<br /> <br /> Second is a bit more complicated because it extends into more layers of society, but I'm going to paraphrase an actual conversation.<br /> <br /> Worker: Why'd my vacation time request get denied?<br /> Manager: Because two other employees already have one of those days off, and we can't schedule more than two people out at once.<br /> Worker: But they knew I wanted to take my vacation this week, why can't you talk them out of it?<br /> <br /> Seems like normal employer grousing, but completely anti-Semitic. Why? Because that &quot;one day off,&quot; was Yom Kippur, and the idea that someone's fellow coworkers were trying to screw them out of a vacation week by spending their own vacation time just to go to one of the most important days of service in their faith is on it's face bigoted even if nobody said it out loud. Those two workers didn't get a say in what day Yom Kippur was that year.<br /> <br /> And what goes deeper there, is that the manager didn't actually care about &quot;essential religious holiday&quot; vs. &quot;vacation,&quot; but simply who got on the schedule first. The next year one of those employees didn't get to go to Rosh Hashanah services because the worker paraphrased above got their request for a vacation in first.<br /> <br /> It's an annoying thing Jews in the US have to constantly juggle when working in Christian majority businesses; esp. ones that give major Christian holidays off for the company. The Christians don't have to worry about dividing up their vacation days to hit major holidays, and don't bother to recognize that their Jewish coworkers don't get that benefit and give them first choice at vacation days to make sure they can express their faith as a personal choice that means less actual vacation time. I've had years where I didn't have a vacation at all, just going to services because that's how it worked out timing wise that year.<br /> <br /> So yeah, things can be bigoted without directly bringing up the topic of that form of bigotry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982075#post982075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you like Garth Ennis' Preacher comics? Do you see the TV serie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does this matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And do you know a Pakistani Christian lost his arms because he didn't want to convert to islam? Do you know about priest in Chinese prisons because they aren't members of the patriotic church, created and controlled by the goverment? Have you heart about bombs in Nigerian church during the mass? What do you know about riots in Odissha (India) againt naive Christians? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who are you to give me lessons about History and intolerance in the current age? </div> </div> </div>Who are you to give the rest of us lectures about it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The horrible things we have been told about Catholic Inquisition are, lies, exaggerations or there were attenuanting circumstances. </div> </div> </div>I don't accept &quot;circumstances&quot; as an excuse for torture and executions of people for religious reasons. The Spanish monarchy in conjunction with the Papacy systemically persecuted Jews and Muslims, and once those that refused to convert all fled, they continued to persecuted those that accepted forced conversions to the point of execution for daring to do things like not have chimney smoke on Saturdays.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I don't care about trying to &quot;rank&quot; historical atrocities. The Spanish Inquisition deserves a place as a black mark against Spain and the Catholic Church; regardless of the exaggerations largely perpetuated by the Church after the fact because they were pissed off at Ferdinand for allowing it to go as far as it did.<br /> <br /> There's nothing good that comes out of trying to wail about double standards. Correct facts when appropriate yes, but trying to say, &quot;this genocide was worse than that genocide,&quot; is a pointless game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kamala Khan, the character from Marvel Comics, was created to fight againts islamophopia, but they didn't notice giving her a Pakistani origin was a mistake because Christians and Hindu minorities suffer a hard intolerance. </div> </div> </div>Bullshit.<br /> <br /> An American Muslim is not morally culpable for the actions of a government in a country she never lived in, or a bunch of religious fanatics she rejects as valid expressions of her faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:27:22-07:00","id":982224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982075#post982075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you like Garth Ennis' Preacher comics? Do you see the TV serie? And do you know a Pakistani Christian lost his arms because he didn't want to convert to islam? Do you know about priest in Chinese prisons because they aren't members of the patriotic church, created and controlled by the goverment? Have you heart about bombs in Nigerian church during the mass? What do you know about riots in Odissha (India) againt naive Christians? Who are you to give me lessons about History and intolerance in the current age?<br /> <br /> The horrible things we have been told about Catholic Inquisition are, lies, exaggerations or there were attenuanting circumstances. (And the Catholic Inquisition had got a rules about torture. Secular power for ordinary crimes was worse. ) It wasn't a bloodbath like we see in the media and fiction. Bloodbath is the revolutionary forces (communist dictatorships or terrorist groups), but the anti-comunism has a bad image in the media.I don't forgive this double standard.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Kamala Khan, the character from Marvel Comics, was created to fight againts islamophopia, but they didn't notice giving her a Pakistani origin was a mistake because Christians and Hindu minorities suffer a hard intolerance. Sometimes infidel girls are kidnnaped to be forced to convert to Islam and marry Muslim men. A young boy was burnt alive only because two unknown men asked him and he replied he was Christian. (and because my English isn't enough good to tell more things I read from fides.org new).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Name me one thing I <i>actually</i> said that was a lie, and stop trying to distract from the issue by bringing up completely unrelated tragedies. Am I supposed to list and rank every single terrible thing that has ever happened in the history of the human race?<br /> <br /> Though really, after the Irish slaves bit, you're running low on credibility juice to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T12:01:16-07:00","id":982249,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">It seems like folks in this thread could use a reminder of rule 2. &quot;<b>Respect the conversation.</b> Don\u2019t try to incite others to break the rules, or distract from the subject at hand. This includes threadcrapping, the posting of short messages or images which add nothing to a thread and serve only to express a user\u2019s displeasure with it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981749#post981749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel ya. When I jumped in, i had hopes that we could have a space where we could have polite discourse on the gamut of conservative views while fielding respectful questions about our beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">This absolutely is what the topic was meant to be for. If anyone doesn't want to participate in such discussion, please just stay out of the thread. Coming in here just to express disagreement with conservative political views and pick fights is not respecting the conversation.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T12:22:09-07:00","id":982259,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty profoundly liberal (for an American, anyway) and while I have no problem debating various actual aspects of <i>government</i> with folks on the right, the insistence on being anti-LGBTQ that you see so much here among our conservatives makes it hard to keep my temper in check. I'd be more than happy to hear folks out here and get a conversation flowing, but so often the talk can't get anywhere near that far in.<br /> <br /> Respect me and mine, don't try to argue my own right to exist away, and then we can talk about everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T12:23:37-07:00","id":982260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982173#post982173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this particular nugget is that a lot of people say things that are not intended to be bigoted, but are incidentally problematic. Since there's no malice intended, when they get called out for the statement being problematic, they get defensive instead of open to dialog about what was wrong with what they said, and dialog devolves into arguments and depending on the space in question on side gets shut down.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true.. Sometimes what you say may not be seen by you (or many others) as bigoted/racist/insensitive etc, but someone finds it problematic. However where i see an issue is when there are others who 'feel it MIGHT be offensive' to target group ZYX, and thus pre-emptively shuts it down, even though members OF that target group, DON'T find it offensive.. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982173#post982173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> First is a simple one because most people agree that this is a bit creepy. There's a rather large number of women - esp. older women - that seem to think that it's completely cool to touch another person's hair to see how it feels.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never understood the whole facination with touching someone else's hair.. Especially if you have not asked to do so.. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982173#post982173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second is a bit more complicated because it extends into more layers of society, but I'm going to paraphrase an actual conversation.<br /> <br /> Worker: Why'd my vacation time request get denied?<br /> Manager: Because two other employees already have one of those days off, and we can't schedule more than two people out at once.<br /> Worker: But they knew I wanted to take my vacation this week, why can't you talk them out of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, on that whole 'vacation days issue', i have experienced instances where cause I am single, and have no kids, my vacation which was already approved got canx, all cause someone married (or single parent) wanted a vacation, and so THEY got it, and i got bumped.. Now i have NO ISSUE with that bumping, for an actual family emergency (such as the one time in England, i had a 4 day weekend leave approved to go up to scotland for a weekend boardgame con, and one of my co-workers needed to go back stateside cause his sister was in hospital after a nasty auto accident)..<br /> BUT what i do get graited over is where (in a large segment of society it seems), it seems OK to dick over single folk in Favor of married/with kids folk, all cause those 'single folk don't really need vacations, while those with kids do...<br /> Or like in the military.. X holiday is considered mostly to be kept open FOR members with families to get leave approved for, if you are single, good luck getting approved for that period.. and if you DO luck out and get it, but a few weeks later someone married (or with kids), puts in for that same time frame (Or just overlapping), you will get bumped out.<br /> Where as Y holiday is the opposite, being seen as more for the single folk, BUT even so, if a married member has leave in for that time frame before you, HE (or she) gets it.. you won't bump them out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T12:41:28-07:00","id":982270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982173#post982173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a rather large number of women - esp. older women - that seem to think that it's completely cool to touch another person's hair to see how it feels.<br /> <br /> Beyond the creepy body space invasion aspect of that...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know the American situation well and this isn't really a comment on that specific case, but I think body privacy varies a lot by culture, it's one area I find where it is difficult to know how to act. In some places putting your hand on somebody's shoulder is grossly invasive and in others making no casual body contact makes people think you are rejecting them or putting them beneath you. Difficult to know what to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T12:52:15-07:00","id":982277,"title":"","content":"I'm a socialist, progun control, pro free abortions, pro tax, pro big government (big daddy, not big brother), pro legalization of weed, pro sex work, pro minium income, pro universal healthcare, pro free education, anti war, pro immigration, pro multicultralism, MRA.<br /> <br /> So naturally everyone assumes I'm rightwing, because being an MRA who has come to question PC culture, trumps every other quality/belief according to some people.<br /> <br /> I will say as a life long lefty, some of the kindest, best people I have known, like shirts off they're back kind of people have been conservatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:02:22-07:00","id":982284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982009#post982009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Its not just the web that's like that.. I have seen a # of reports and heard many stories of conservatives in hollywood having to hide their political outlook, cause when they get found out as BEING conservative, all of a sudden, jobs shrink up. Acting gigs disappear and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't be a conservative, they say (not explicitly)... but you can always be a commie, or a &quot;democratic socialist&quot;. Those godless ideologies caused the deaths of hundreds of millions, but right now they're the good guys, sure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:02:33-07:00","id":982285,"title":"","content":"* Garth Ennis' Preacher comics is a good example of anti-Christian culture. That is the reason I dislike it so much. People think reading Code di Vinci or Preacher comics they know enough about real Christianism, but they are wrong. The real Christianism is a group of Copts in Egypt they aren't allowed to rebuild their church, or Christians from Taybe, a little town in Palestine, they were attacked by a mob of Muslims of Deir Jarir to avange because a Christian was the boylover of a Muslim girl (she may be killed by her family in another honor crime).<br /> <br /> * We need self-criticism to admit in our past some things we can't be proud happened, but too much self-criticism may hurt you, because it can be used by enemies to trample, demoralice you. Self-criticism doesn't mean to hate himself for things happened before you were born. Sometimes you have to say there are another things more priority to be denounced. Open your eyes, McCarthy wasn't a monster, and Che Guevara wasn't a hero. You must to contrast all the points of view to avoid be cheated by propaganda war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:05:44-07:00","id":982287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982284#post982284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can't be a conservative, they say (not explicitly)... but you can always be a commie, or a &quot;democratic socialist&quot;. Those godless ideologies caused the deaths of hundreds of millions, but right now they're the good guys, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing wrong with being godless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:13:01-07:00","id":982297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982287#post982287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing wrong with being godless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was an atheist for most of my life (until a decade ago), and most atheists I know are sensible, honest people. However, belief systems (even secular ones, &quot;ideologies&quot;) can be judged, and I don't think atheism, or the veneration of man as some sort of (false) god enables human flourishing.<br /> <br /> We need more than cold science: we need the experience of the sacred, and the idea of the existence of eternal truths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:13:27-07:00","id":982298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982259#post982259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty profoundly liberal (for an American, anyway) and while I have no problem debating various actual aspects of <i>government</i> with folks on the right, the insistence on being anti-LGBTQ that you see so much here among our conservatives makes it hard to keep my temper in check. I'd be more than happy to hear folks out here and get a conversation flowing, but so often the talk can't get anywhere near that far in.<br /> <br /> Respect me and mine, don't try to argue my own right to exist away, and then we can talk about everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div> If it makes you feel any better, I'm very pro LGBTQ, but my sincre belief that Dominance and Submission are legit and innate sexual orientations means that feeling isn't always recipericated. I'm okay with that, I still support the LGBTQ community (ect). I've always supported gay marriage since I first heard about as child.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:16:56-07:00","id":982299,"title":"","content":"Liberals seem to forget there are conservative gays and lesbians, and even conservative transgender people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:24:35-07:00","id":982306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982284#post982284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can't be a conservative, they say (not explicitly)... but you can always be a commie, or a &quot;democratic socialist&quot;. Those godless ideologies caused the deaths of hundreds of millions, but right now they're the good guys, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bPlease, by all means do show some citations where democratic socialism has caused the deaths of hundreds of millions of people. If you are going to make claims please back them up with some facts. Unbridled authoritarianism led to the the deaths of many millions of people, the underlying political/economic systems (whether they be communism, capitalism or any 'ism' in between) were not the root cause of those deaths. This lack of nuanced critical thinking is the primary source of leftist criticism of conservative ideology. Conservatives aren't the only people guilty of this kind thought process, the same applies to people on the left who claim capitalism by itself is the cause of suffering and death, rather than the specific actions of particularly greedy capitalists with no regard for the value of other people's lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 10-05-2016, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:28:33-07:00","id":982309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982297#post982297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need more than cold science: we need the experience of the sacred, and the idea of the existence of eternal truths.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly does &quot;experience of the sacred&quot; mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":".  Second line irrelevant 10-05-2016, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:49:37-07:00","id":982322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982306#post982306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bPlease, by all means do show some citations where democratic socialism has caused the deaths of hundreds of millions of people. If you are going to make claims please back them up with some facts. Unbridled authoritarianism led to the the deaths of many millions of people, the underlying political/economic systems (whether they be communism, capitalism or any 'ism' in between) were not the root cause of those deaths. This lack of nuanced critical thinking is the primary source of leftist criticism of conservative ideology. Conservatives aren't the only people guilty of this kind thought process, the same applies to people on the left who claim capitalism by itself is the cause of suffering and death, rather than the specific actions of particularly greedy capitalists with no regard for the value of other people's lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just check Venezuela right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T14:05:59-07:00","id":982333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982309#post982309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly does &quot;experience of the sacred&quot; mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to explain - it's something you experience, or you don't; it's what most faithful experience during ritual and service, or even by themselves, during prayer. <br /> <br /> Have your ever visited a old cathedral, or attended traditional religious service? Recently, one of my PhD professors passed, and the religious service was conduced within a somber 18th century baroque chamber. All the formalities were upheld, before her exequies proper, and all those present could understand they were not experiencing a common day to day life occurrence, but something with greater meaning. And that's, maybe, the core to the experience of the sacred: the understanding that human life (and death) are more than simple facts. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982309#post982309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does science not offer eternal (albeit not related to our lives mostly) truths?</div> </div> </div> </div>Science offers a kind of truth, but it's devoid of human meaning, or morals. Of course (as a Catholic) I accept evolution, and I know the best way to understand natural processes is through science. Bad thing American protestants are still creationists. <br /> <br /> Science, however, only describes (it answers &quot;what&quot; kind of questions) nature; spirituality exists to answers the &quot;why&quot; questions, related to human anxieties and doubts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T14:15:20-07:00","id":982341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div cla