st</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bCitations. I asked for citations. I don't see &quot;hundreds of millions&quot; of people dying from democratic socialism. I do see a country on the verge of economic and political collapse from a completely mismanaged economy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't manage economy. Socialism means economic planing, and economic planing means it's impossible to have precification (for that, you need the market). Precification, itself, is necessary for the proper distribution of goods and services. It means that any socialist experience is doomed to cause famine and general scarcity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T14:30:40-07:00","id":982353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982345#post982345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science answers the &quot;how&quot;, religion attempts to answer the &quot;why&quot;. For me personally, one does a better job than the other. YMMV</div> </div> </div> </div>You're trying to equate different tools, tools with utterly different purposes. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T14:43:08-07:00","id":982361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982353#post982353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're trying to equate different tools, tools with utterly different purposes. </div> </div> </div> </div>Darksider is comparing the efficacy of different tools at fulfilling their (different) purposes. Like saying a hammer makes a better driver of nails than copsticks make eating utensils.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-05-2016, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T14:57:22-07:00","id":982372,"title":"","content":"Dang, and here the only reason I came back to this thread was because Charlaquin quoted me and I thought I might be in trouble. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982361#post982361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Darksider is comparing the efficacy of different tools at fulfilling their (different) purposes. Like saying a hammer makes a better driver of nails than copsticks make eating utensils.</div> </div> </div> </div>That all depends on how good you are at using the tools. I know plenty of people who can't drive nails with any kind of hammer. My wife, on the other hand, can eat Jello with chopsticks. Just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T14:59:42-07:00","id":982376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982260#post982260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However where i see an issue is when there are others who 'feel it MIGHT be offensive' to target group ZYX, and thus pre-emptively shuts it down, even though members OF that target group, DON'T find it offensive..</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. People playing the white knight is very annoying. But it still deserves to be discussed before conclusion.<br /> <br /> Why is that person responding that way? Maybe they have a relative, close friend, etc. that does actually find it offensive but doesn't feel comfortable speaking out, so that people speaking for others is doing so vaguely to avoid outing the person they're speaking for. Dismissing them before learning why they're speaking out against something that doesn't seem to directly impact them, isn't really that different from getting defensive when someone is directly offended.<br /> <br /> As well, demographics aren't monolithic. Just because your friends in group X are cool with something, doesn't mean it's cool in general use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982270#post982270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know the American situation well and this isn't really a comment on that specific case, but I think body privacy varies a lot by culture, it's one area I find where it is difficult to know how to act. In some places putting your hand on somebody's shoulder is grossly invasive and in others making no casual body contact makes people think you are rejecting them or putting them beneath you. Difficult to know what to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case, it's a fairly large violation of mainstream body privacy norms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982285#post982285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Garth Ennis' Preacher comics is a good example of anti-Christian culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>So? People are allowed to produce art you find anti-Christian. That has nothing to do with the persecution of Christians (or Christian persecutions of other people).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:09:16-07:00","id":982383,"title":"","content":"Economy absolutely can be managed as we do this every single day in the US. Socialism does not simply mean &quot;economic planning&quot;, it means shared ownership. As for scarcity, I can easily make the argument that capitalism creates artificial scarcity and we can see in the US the results of the artificial scarcity caused by capitalism. So if both systems are causing scarcity how do we fix the problem and what do we replace the current inefficient systems with? Those seem to me to be the questions that need answering, and dogmatically clinging to the labels &quot;conservative&quot; and &quot;liberal&quot; we are picking sides like this is a sporting contest and we are rooting for a particular team. It prevents people from looking at solutions proffered by &quot;the other side&quot; because it means their particular team isn't &quot;winning&quot;. The difference in attitudes between the time of my grandparents (WW2) and now is that people are more interested in climbing over other people than giving them a hand up. We've become a society of self interested, self absorbed narcissists who believe if it isn't a problem for me then it isn't a problem. As Carlin said &quot;it's bullshit and it's bad for you&quot;. <br /> <br /> \u200bIf the solution offered is &quot;well poor people need to work longer and harder&quot; then where does the spirituality figure in? Where is the value in human existence, where does the opportunity to further grow and develop enter into the equation? When do they get to live their lives instead of working to make someone else wealthier while they settle for whatever crumbs are allowed to trickle down their way?<br /> <br /> When do people who are exhausted from working their second and third jobs get to expand their educational development, and how do they afford an (overpriced) education when they are making choices about whether to pay rent, their utilities, or buy enough food so as not to starve (and that won't cause them health issues down the road)? I look at people now and wonder how they can afford the higher education that will afford a better quality of life, I was able to work two jobs and graduate college in the 90's without a mountain of debt and that just can't be done today with the cost of tuition, even at the state school levels.<br /> <br /> Once these issues are addressed you will have a better, fairer, more stable society. And I for one don't give a fuck what system gets us there as long as we get there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:11:28-07:00","id":982384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982361#post982361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Darksider is comparing the efficacy of different tools at fulfilling their (different) purposes. Like saying a hammer makes a better driver of nails than copsticks make eating utensils.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bPsshht, forks are obviously the better eating utensil than chopsticks regardless of how many billions of people disagree with me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:28:59-07:00","id":982395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_con