ith it.<br /> <br /> I've know very peaceful commies and social democracts, and capitals that push for none stop violence. None of these are inheriant to the idealogy. Nothing in capitalism says,you have invade others countries and nothing in communism say you have to mass murder people. Its the personalities invovled and the interrptations.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then you can't dismiss everyone you disagree with as murderers, and what's the point of political debate without that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:32:38-07:00","id":982428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982333#post982333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science offers a kind of truth, but it's devoid of human meaning, or morals. Of course (as a Catholic) I accept evolution, and I know the best way to understand natural processes is through science. Bad thing American protestants are still creationists.<br /> <br /> Science, however, only describes (it answers &quot;what&quot; kind of questions) nature; spirituality exists to answers the &quot;why&quot; questions, related to human anxieties and doubts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for answering, I realised shortly afterwards that it was obvious what you meant in that case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982333#post982333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have your ever visited a old cathedral, or attended traditional religious service?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes to both, I am an atheist (only in the strictest philosophical sense an agnostic) but was raised in a heavily traditional Catholic environment with the local church dating to the mid-1800s, from what you wrote after this you're getting at something like the experience of ritual. Hard to put into words, but I think I know what you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:54:03-07:00","id":982440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982422#post982422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then you can't dismiss everyone you disagree with as murderers, and what's the point of political debate without that?</div> </div> </div> </div>She has a point, you know. If I can't dismiss all liberals as whiny, Lenin-loving, atheist cowards then what's the point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982428#post982428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for answering, I realised shortly afterwards that it was obvious what you meant in that case.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes to both, I am an atheist (only in the strictest philosophical sense an agnostic) but was raised in a heavily traditional Catholic environment with the local church dating to the mid-1800s, from what you wrote after this you're getting at something like the experience of ritual. Hard to put into words, but I think I know what you mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. I know what you mean by the &quot;feeling of ritual,&quot; but there's a similar but distinct feeling you can have when standing in an old church. A sort of deep, light tranquility. Hard to describe. I've had the pleasure of visiting the oldest church in North America, in Santa Fe, New Mexico. Other than my wife and the priest there was no one else in the building, and the <i>intensity</i> of that feeling brought me to actual tears. I've been in places that are older, that are more historically relevant, and not had anything close to that kind of experience.<br /> <br /> In the end, though, it doesn't really matter if you &quot;get&quot; spirituality or not. These things are actual graces, but not sanctifying grace. Accepting the former leads to the latter, but they come in other, more subtle means that most people acknowledge and accept anyway regardless of their conscious communion with God.<br /> <br /> In short, personally, I don't think an omnibenevolent God is sending people to Hell just because they don't actively worship Him. I acknowledge that I'm something of a heretic in that, but the way I see it how could someone who created us and loves us not forgive us for anything other than outright conscious rejection of Him? I don't mean, &quot;I don't believe,&quot; I mean, &quot;I'm a completely unrepentant sociopath who holds no love in my heart for anything other than myself.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","user":"Frishman","date":". 10-05-2016, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:59:44-07:00","id":982442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982440#post982440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon