itle":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T18:17:04-07:00","id":982471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982462#post982462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, hard to know, I grew up with people who felt it strongly, so it isn't totally alien to me, but I'm pretty sure I only sort of get it, I do want to visit that church in Santa Fe now though, looks lovely.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Jaunt over to California and you can visit the oldest Spanish Mission in the state, I lived doen the street from it for years. Very cool place!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T18:32:54-07:00","id":982476,"title":"","content":"Two of the most amazingly spiritual places I have ever been to were the Hagia Sophia in Istanbul and Saint Peter's Basilica in the Vatican. Those are truly amazing places and I highly recommend visiting either or both if you ever have the opportunity. They don't make them like that anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T21:36:29-07:00","id":982544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982376#post982376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So? People are allowed to produce art you find anti-Christian. That has nothing to do with the persecution of Christians (or Christian persecutions of other people).</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you understand? There is a lot of things you don't know, you ignore. For example: 6th Juny 2000. A nun, sor Maria Laura Mainetti is phone by a teen girl who asks her help because she says she is pregnant. They agree in a meeting in the night, alone. The nun doesn't know it's is a trap. She was killed by three teen girls with 19 stabs, odium fidei. Oregon, 1st Octobre 2015, mass shooting by Chris Harper-Mercer, He asked his victims about religion and after he shooted them. 10th June 2016. Christina Grimme, singer, is killed by Kevin James Loibl. Police found in his mobile and computer &quot;a strong anti-Christian component&quot;. Maybe other &quot;odium fidei&quot; crime? Have you thought about the idea an anti-Christian mass shooting in a church in Sunday? How would react the society about anti-Christian media? If you read Open Doors' reports about persecutions againts Christians, you will find a different reality. And when I think about those blackafrican Nigerian Christians killed by Boko Haram or the victims of the genocide in Sourth Sudan (reported by Steven Spierbel!!) to be fogorten because ourWest society is too busy watching bullshits like code di vinci, I get angry. <br /> <br /> Maybe we start to talk about Christians not like potential menace but like real victims of hate and intolerance. In this current age there are more Christians victims by persecutions in another parts in the world than in the Roman empire. Now it isn't the right time to say Christian zealots are potential menace for freedom. We could see in the next years a second Cristero war in Mexico. In Spain there are some graffis in the walls of the churchs with the text &quot;\u00a1ARDER\u00c9IS COMO EN EL 36!&quot; ( = you will burn like in the 1936 year, when Spanish comunisht burn covents).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 10-06-2016, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T23:40:17-07:00","id":982575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982544#post982544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you understand?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what you're trying to say no.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why you're ranting about the persecutions of Christians in modern times. Nobody here is denying that it happens.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why you think ranting about a comic book that ended in 2000 as if it was some cultural touchstone that was rallying people to persecute Christians.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why you're solely focused on the religious persecution of Christians and apparently don't care at all about the religious based persecutions of all people.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why you think you are the sole &quot;truth teller&quot; here as if you should be treated with some sort of deferential authority; esp. when you've demonstrated that you are completely willing to present wholly discredited myths as facts.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why you consistently try to make hyperbolic statements about how much worse various groups have it now than they did in the past; esp. considering the sheer differences in population to account for. And it does not help when you're comparing Christianity before it gained significant political power, to the modern Christianity that has to deal with centuries of its own bad actions pissing off pretty much every other major world religion including secularists.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why you think being a member of the world's largest religion gives you any sort of special insight into being a member of a persecuted religion.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why you seem to want to play oppression olympics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a lot of things you don't know, you ignore. </div> </div> </div>If I say something factually incorrect? Correct me. Otherwise do not presume to know what I do or do not know, or what I ignore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would react the society about anti-Christian media? </div> </div> </div>I would hope that most Christians would acknowledge their religions extremely checkered history as giving a huge number of groups valid beefs with the Christian faith, and that they need outlets to express those feelings. I would hope most Christians that seek peace and harmony with their fellow man would see such sentiments, listen to what people are actually saying, and work to repair what those that came before them broken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe we start to talk about Christians not like potential menace but like real victims of hate and intolerance. </div> </div> </div>The two aren't mutually exclusive. Christians are victims of hate and intolerance. Christians are also perpetrators of hate and intolerance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T23:59:34-07:00","id":982585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982376#post982376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. People playing the white knight is very annoying. But it still deserves to be discussed before conclusion.<br /> <br /> Why is that person responding that way? Maybe they have a relative, close friend, etc. that does actually find it offensive but doesn't feel comfortable speaking out, so that people speaking for others is doing so vaguely to avoid outing the person they're speaking for. Dismissing them before learning why they're speaking out against something that doesn't seem to directly impact them, isn't really that different from getting defensive when someone is directly offended.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it is different. If something affects them directly, then speaking out SHOULD be done. However speaking out against something that doesn't affect you, just cause YOU think it might offend someone else, and therefore shutting it down, does neither side a good service, as no one communicates...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982443#post982443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a godless atheist right winger <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Funnily enough, almost all of my friends are Christians, a good number of them are even fundamentalist Christians are we still get along pretty well despite that.</div> </div> </div> </div>where as i am a humble, agnostic right leaning conservative, who proudly votes for the lord Cthulu!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T04:16:38-07:00","id":982637,"title":"","content":"I am talking about I am conservative gamer (and geek-fanboy), and I hate the anti-Christian clich\u00e9s and stereotypes in the media, in the fiction (the fanatic one, the hypocrite, the repressed, the naive idealistic or the retrograde). We aren't like the fool Carrie's mother (Stephen King's character), nor the ordo malleus, ordo xenos and ordo hereticus from warhammer 40.000 (&quot;All xenos have to die&quot;), or the Temple Avesti from Fading Suns rpg, or the inquisition of the Vaticine Church (7th Sea rpg). I don't like either comics American Jesus, Bible Reloaded, Jesus hates zombies, Battlepope, Chronicles of Wornwood nor Popetwon cartoon. I don't want to endure another movie like Agora (2009 year, Rache Weiss as main character). I hate that Buffy vampire slayer episode &quot;Gingerbread&quot; (7th from third season) when parents become crazy and started a witch-hunt). And why not more comunists like main antagonist in the movies and television?<br /> <br /> I don't want to spend my money with a geek-fiction work where I find a author trying to give me lessons about intolerance and fanaticism, when that author knows nothing about the hard reality for Christians in another parts of the world. (let's see news from Open Doors fundation web). I hate when I read a book where a nun character appears and my mind says &quot;she will be lover with the main male character&quot; and I guess, or I can predict that priest character will lose the faith or will betray the main characters, or will not find answers when somebody starts a misotheist speech.<br /> <br /> I ask again: have you thought about a mass shoot in a Christian church in a near future, and how would the society would react? We could suffer a XXI century equivalent to Fredric Wetham's &quot;Seduction of the innocent&quot;. Not only for videogames, heavy metal musi and adult-fantasy movies, also it may give a bad image for some RPG titles. White Wolf's fans to be showed in the TV news like potential psico-killers nerds (there is violence between hooligans, but nobody worries about that).<br /> <br /> * I don't dislike really Kamala Khan, the caracter from marvel comics. She wasn't her fault. Marvel wanted to create a Muslim character with good intentions to help stopping islamophobia, but when I remember their Pakistani origin, I can't avoid to link it about when I read a Christian Pakistani couple, she was pregnant, they were burned alive in a brick oven by a Muslim mob because they are accused by unconfirmed rumors about to offend Muslims feelings. This is the real reality about Christians, and you will not discover if you only read fiction and new written by people who hates our Christians roots. Why have we to respect Muslims while at the same time hostility againts Christianity is showed unceremoniosly? That is a example of the double standar of certain entertainment industry. (Once I imagine Loki, the supervillain of marvel comics, transforming all male characters of the 99 (Muslims superheroes by other company) into women, and teletransporting them to the centre of Saud Arabia to make them suffer machismo ( = male chauvinism).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 10-06-2016, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T08:59:42-07:00","id":982723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982637#post982637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ask again: have you thought about a mass shoot in a Christian church in a near future, and how would the society would react? We could suffer a XXI century equivalent to Fredric Wetham's &quot;Seduction of the innocent&quot;. Not only for videogames, heavy metal musi and adult-fantasy movies, also it may give a bad image for some RPG titles. White Wolf's fans to be showed in the TV news like potential psico-killers nerds (there is violence between hooligans, but nobody worries about that).</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a shooting in a church last year that killed 9 people. I don't see any of that happening. We long ago dismissed video games as a cause of violence, and RPG or heavy metal music even further back.<br /> <br /> There have been moves to downplay the glorification of guns in movies, but I don't see pogroms getting fired up over it. Gun control is another hornets nest unrelated to religion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-06-2016, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T09:42:10-07:00","id":982747,"title":"","content":"Yes, Charleston church, by Dylan Roof, a hate crime by a racist, but do remember also in the same year, the Chapel Hill shooting, three Muslims killed by an atheist, Craig Stephen Hicks. What if a new Craig Stephen Hicks is responsable of a new Charleton church shooting? It may be a shock for society and some parents would start to protest: &quot;our children are tough to hate our Christian roots!!&quot; <br /> <br /> Also I should tell a thing: Here in Spain in the year 1994 a man was killed by Javier Rosado, who had created his own homebrew RPG &quot;Razas&quot; (races). In that time Dungeons and Dragons was only a children cartoon, the first years of RPGs in Spain (and Games Workshop miniatures, before the boom of Blizzard's videogames) and the newspapers talked about that like &quot;el crimen del rol&quot; (= the game of the roleplaying-game). That gave a bad reputation for Spanish gamers. You should understand my own experencies here were different, and my point of view. Here in Spain in February 2013 there was a bomb in the Almuena catedral, without personal damages, by an anarchist group, &quot;Mateo Morral&quot; (the name of an anarchist who threw a bomb in the wending of Spanish kings).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:05:22-07:00","id":982765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982637#post982637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am talking about I am conservative gamer (and geek-fanboy), and I hate the anti-Christian clich\u00e9s and stereotypes in the media, in the fiction (the fanatic one, the hypocrite, the repressed, the naive idealistic or the retrograde). We aren't like the fool Carrie's mother (Stephen King's character), nor the ordo malleus, ordo xenos and ordo hereticus from warhammer 40.000 (&quot;All xenos have to die&quot;), or the Temple Avesti from Fading Suns rpg, or the inquisition of the Vaticine Church (7th Sea rpg). I don't like either comics American Jesus, Bible Reloaded, Jesus hates zombies, Battlepope, Chronicles of Wornwood nor Popetwon cartoon. I don't want to endure another movie like Agora (2009 year, Rache Weiss as main character). I hate that Buffy vampire slayer episode &quot;Gingerbread&quot; (7th from third season) when parents become crazy and started a witch-hunt). And why not more comunists like main antagonist in the movies and television?</div> </div> </div> </div>Several of those examples are deliberately farcical (Warhammer, Battlepope, etc), which is a long way from being some kind of anti-Christian blood libel. Others are critical of abuse and persecution, not specifically Christianity (Carrie, Buffy, etc). I won't deny that sometimes attacking organized religion can be low hanging fruit, but its not exactly punching down. It also ignores the preponderance of positive portrayals of Christianity. If you're looking for evil communists as antagonists and can't find them, I contend you aren't looking hard enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I ask again: have you thought about a mass shoot in a Christian church in a near future, and how would the society would react? We could suffer a XXI century equivalent to Fredric Wetham's &quot;Seduction of the innocent&quot;. Not only for videogames, heavy metal musi and adult-fantasy movies, also it may give a bad image for some RPG titles. White Wolf's fans to be showed in the TV news like potential psico-killers nerds (there is violence between hooligans, but nobody worries about that). </div> </div> </div>Have you ever heard of the &quot;Satanic Panic&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * I don't dislike really Kamala Khan, the caracter from marvel comics. She wasn't her fault. Marvel wanted to create a Muslim character with good intentions to help stopping islamophobia, but when I remember their Pakistani origin, I can't avoid to link it about when I read a Christian Pakistani couple, she was pregnant, they were burned alive in a brick oven by a Muslim mob because they are accused by unconfirmed rumors about to offend Muslims feelings. This is the real reality about Christians, and you will not discover if you only read fiction and new written by people who hates our Christians roots. Why have we to respect Muslims while at the same time hostility againts Christianity is showed unceremoniosly? That is a example of the double standar of certain entertainment industry. (Once I imagine Loki, the supervillain of marvel comics, transforming all male characters of the 99 (Muslims superheroes by other company) into women, and teletransporting them to the centre of Saud Arabia to make them suffer machismo ( = male chauvinism). </div> </div> </div>Again, I fail to see how a character written as Muslim-American, meant to grapple with the peculiar circumstance of being Muslim-American, is culpable for actions in a country she's never been to by people who'm she has no connection to other than a spurious accusation of guilt by association.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T11:16:32-07:00","id":982809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982009#post982009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is in a way censorship though, if (as i found out on one older gaming site) they only censor ONE SIDE of any arguments that cropped up, and not the other..</div> </div> </div> </div>That's still not censorship. First, your advocacy assumes that both (or in this case all) reasoning is equally valid, when that's not the case. Society recognizes that a privately owned message board is not always the place to decide those issues, therefor the board holders get to make rules for what actions and dialog may be exchanged within their own properties. If you tried to hold a protest or other public event after getting all the proper permits, then the government is obligated to allow and protect you in sharing that belief, but being ignored is not censorship, neither is being told you're not wanted as part of that specific community.<br /> <br /> You should not be fired from your job unless you are using those beliefs or ideas to harass, you shouldn't be denied in such a way that has a real effect on your life. Taking up a hobby and then facing the reality that many of the other people in that hobby have juxtaposing beliefs, resulting in all their posts getting liked while your views are criticized is not censorship nor does it prohibit you from speaking your piece in other public areas, or for meeting other people for that matter. Having your posts deleted and your accounts banned on another community site is dickish, but that's still not censorship. You may have noticed that no one is deleting your posts or banning your account here, another avenue for the topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982297#post982297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> I was an atheist for most of my life (until a decade ago), and most atheists I know are sensible, honest people. However, belief systems (even secular ones, &quot;ideologies&quot;) can be judged, and I don't think atheism, or the veneration of man as some sort of (false) god enables human flourishing. <br /> <br /> We need more than cold science: we need the experience of the sacred, and the idea of the existence of eternal truths.</div> </div> </div> </div>In most cases I am an advocate for people having religion or some form of spirituality, though I'm more an advocate for personal 'hand-crafted' spiritualities that take to heart humanist principles, I don't think this is at odds with what many people want Christianity to be, in spite of all the problematic passages in their holy text. <br /> <br /> That said, I can't agree with this assertion. Stalin's Russia may have been godless, but saying &quot;None of the crimes they committed would have happened if it weren't for Atheism, if only they believed in Christ.&quot; doesn't really fit. You yourself say it is the ideologies that are judged. Well, atheism is not really an ideology. It is simply the lack of belief in a god or divine presence. The major religions of the world, however, are ideologies, and have had a direct hand in people making evil decisions. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982299#post982299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liberals seem to forget there are conservative gays and lesbians, and even conservative transgender people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transgender people have an awful hard time forgetting every time Caitlyn Jenner says something that makes all of us cringe. That being said, how does that matter? There are also black conservatives who support policies that overwhelmingly penalize minorities. There are women with views on rape that are just as regressive as some in the Man-O-Sphere. It does not lend authority or credibility to the arguments either group proposes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982306#post982306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, by all means do show some citations where democratic socialism has caused the deaths of hundreds of millions of people. If you are going to make claims please back them up with some facts. Unbridled authoritarianism led to the the deaths of many millions of people, the underlying political/economic systems (whether they be communism, capitalism or any 'ism' in between) were not the root cause of those deaths. This lack of nuanced critical thinking is the primary source of leftist criticism of conservative ideology. Conservatives aren't the only people guilty of this kind thought process, the same applies to people on the left who claim capitalism by itself is the cause of suffering and death, rather than the specific actions of particularly greedy capitalists with no regard for the value of other people's lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Capitalism as it is practiced in the United States often comes with the legal responsibility to maximize profits. I'm not going to take this to the extreme you presented, but I do think they're on the right path when you consider that capitalism doesn't necessarily put the health of society as its greatest objective. Capitalism proposes that the best thing for society is to maximize profits and to create competition so that society continues growing by leaps and bounds. We'll see how that works out I suppose when human beings become more and more obsolete in the face of machines. I don't believe capitalism on the whole is responsible for the success we've achieved, and believe that a properly implemented social system could have hit the same milestones at roughly the same points, especially when you consider how many great people have either been lost to poverty, or have biographies where they were very nearly prevented from growing at all, simply because they had the misfortune of being born into a system that favors money and profit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T11:56:01-07:00","id":982829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982809#post982809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I can't agree with this assertion. Stalin's Russia may have been godless, but saying &quot;None of the crimes they committed would have happened if it weren't for Atheism, if only they believed in Christ.&quot; doesn't really fit. You yourself say it is the ideologies that are judged. Well, atheism is not really an ideology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd further add as a supporting statement that the real problem with Stalin's communism (and Hitler's Fascism and Pol Pot's murderness) were that these were <i>state religions,</i> and fundamentally culturally anti-progressive and <i>culturally conservative,</i> destroying anyone who didn't toe the line of the all-powerful state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T11:59:37-07:00","id":982830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981429#post981429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second is similar in that those who suffer from PTSD <i>ought</i> to be informed that a topic of discussion may be sensitive to them in particular because no one believes that they ought to suffer needlessly when it could be prevented, but it's been taken over by people who seek to use it to shut down conversations because they find them &quot;offensive.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This does not strike me as a typical conservative understanding of what trigger warnings constitute. Not knocking you by saying that, mind! Just that it's surprising.<br /> <br /> It's one of those issues where I feel like people often talk past one another to the strawman way over there, y'know? What you're describing is what I'm actually seeing when I see trigger warnings used, but people seem to insist in every case that it's the part where people are shutting something down because they find them offensive.<br /> <br /> Universities are probably the perfect example. The practice of trigger warning usage is for PTSD things and really just to give people a heads up that content will be explored in a given class, with the potential (not always) of alternative material being offered for the aforementioned PTSD grouping.<br /> <br /> But when you read about it in the media, it's always people spending 99% of the conversation on those people using it to shut down conversations, or some theoretical notion of disallowing the teaching of topics due to potentially triggering content (Which does not seem to actually be an idea discussed by any faculty at any university ever?)<br /> <br /> It's really weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:12:26-07:00","id":982839,"title":"","content":"So...I got a question that hopefully doesn't start a flame war. What do you guys think about Fox News?<br /> <br /> I've watched a fair bit of Fox News living in Texas (It's all the Doctor's offices show on TV). One thing I noticed is that when they have debates with a liberal and a conservative, they don't actually debate. They play parts.<br /> <br /> The Liberal usually have a complex explanation of the liberal side of the argument (which actually a decent representative of the liberal PoV). The Conservative doesn't even bother to argue their point with the liberal, but instead just spews easily repeatable sound bites. I actually started using this technique for my Socially manipulative NPCs and sometimes in real life (give people easily digestible and repeatable phrases)<br /> <br /> Is this what you guys see too? Or is this point of view filtered though my liberal bias?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:34:24-07:00","id":982854,"title":"","content":"Please, the true capitalism isn't like the big business corporations from cyberpunk fiction. Businessmen doesn't mean oligarchy. The free market is the opposite of oligopolies. I can accept businessmen can be in the fiction villains like Norman Osborn or Lex Luthor, but I hate when the anticapitalist radical groups never are the antagonist. Everybody knows about McCarthy's witch-hunt, but not about project Venona, or Stalin's chistka (purge), the equivalent like Catholic Inquisition executing almost Vatican leadership. I want more communists like antagonists like in the videogame &quot;Homefront: the revolution&quot;. <br /> <br /> And I hate &quot;V of Vendetta&quot;. Anarchy is a nerd child suffering school bullying, a potential Steve Jobs or Bill Gates with broken self-estreem, with broken wings, without social skills because he would rather to be alone. Anarchy is a group of narcos calling at the door of a Mexican family and telling: &quot;I like your wife, your daughter has to go to the shower because she will the next&quot; (and this happened). I don't like estatism, when the state has too control, but total anarchy isn't the right answer. Anarchy only can work when everybody are saints.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> &quot;It is hard to imagine a more stupid or more dangerous way of making decisions than by putting those decisions in the hands of people who pay no price for being wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thomas Sowell Read","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:36:15-07:00","id":982857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982829#post982829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd further add as a supporting statement that the real problem with Stalin's communism (and Hitler's Fascism and Pol Pot's murderness) were that these were <i>state religions,</i> and fundamentally culturally anti-progressive and <i>culturally conservative,</i> destroying anyone who didn't toe the line of the all-powerful state.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't use Hitler as an example because he was Christian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:38:33-07:00","id":982859,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Nevermind that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 10-06-2016, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:51:19-07:00","id":982867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982809#post982809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's still not censorship. First, your advocacy assumes that both (or in this case all) reasoning is equally valid, when that's not the case. Society recognizes that a privately owned message board is not always the place to decide those issues, therefor the board holders get to make rules for what actions and dialog may be exchanged within their own properties. If you tried to hold a protest or other public event after getting all the proper permits, then the government is obligated to allow and protect you in sharing that belief, but being ignored is not censorship, neither is being told you're not wanted as part of that specific community.</div> </div> </div> </div>While in the explicit logical term of 'censorship', yes a private board canceling out what someone says (if it violate rules, such as say most sites swear word filters), it still seems like censorship, especially if they only block out one side of an argument... BUT that's how i see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:59:54-07:00","id":982871,"title":"","content":"Godwin's Law in 9 pages......new record? Probably not.<br /> <br /> Don't mind me. Carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:00:12-07:00","id":982873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982854#post982854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, the true capitalism isn't like the big business corporations from cyberpunk fiction. Businessmen doesn't mean oligarchy. The free market is the opposite of oligopolies. I can accept businessmen can be in the fiction villains like Norman Osborn or Lex Luthor, but I hate when the anticapitalist radical groups never are the antagonist. Everybody knows about McCarthy's witch-hunt, but not about project Venona, or Stalin's chistka (purge), the equivalent like Catholic Inquisition executing almost Vatican leadership. I want more communists like antagonists like in the videogame &quot;Homefront: the revolution&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have a graduate degree in Business (Information System for full disclosure), so I have a more balanced understanding of business place in our society. While I do not believe businesses are evil, I do not think the free market will correct all of society's problems. It is not business' job to focus on the betterment of society. Business are economic engines that exist to grow and create profit. A business will not stop polluting unless a third party, be it government or the business' own customers, demand it to stop polluting. Yes, certain businesses exist that do support certain political/moral views (Onyx Path is one of these businesses as you are well aware). Yet if it came down to upholding that moral view or the business' survival, the business will choose survival over morality. No one wants to be responsible for laying off employees just to prove a moral point.<br /> <br /> Now, when I use the term &quot;business&quot; I mean the decision makers (CEO, CIO, CFO). In large corporations, finding the decision maker is difficult. One of the issues I have with Corporations is the dilution of responsibility. If corporation breaks the law, who do you send to jail? The Employee who was ordered to break the law? The Manager who ordered the employee to break the law? The CEO, who created the strategy that forced the manager to force the employee to break the law or the manager would lose his job?<br /> <br /> Mr Robot has anticapitalist protagonists, yet I wouldn't call them heroes. They probably do more damage than the corporation they are fighting.<br /> <br /> /I don't know why I am getting involved in this shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:03:43-07:00","id":982874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982873#post982873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> /I don't know why I am getting involved in this shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate it. Especially your question about Fox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:06:13-07:00","id":982875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982854#post982854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, the true capitalism isn't like the big business corporations from cyberpunk fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is referring to cyberpunk fiction, pharmaceutical companies jack up prices for life saving medications in the here and now, and money in politics is a hot issue on both sides of the Party Line in America, privatized schools, prisons, and more are all extreme examples, but we also have to deal with the impact a capitalist system has had on smaller businesses thanks to corporations like Walmart. The effect corporate lobbying groups have had on the environment and people's health. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982854#post982854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Businessmen doesn't mean oligarchy. The free market is the opposite of oligopolies. I can accept businessmen can be in the fiction villains like Norman Osborn or Lex Luthor, but I hate when the anticapitalist radical groups never are the antagonist. Everybody knows about McCarthy's witch-hunt, but not about project Venona, or Stalin's chistka (purge), the equivalent like Catholic Inquisition executing almost Vatican leadership. I want more communists like antagonists like in the videogame &quot;Homefront: the revolution&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I put it to you that in all of the societies where capitalism has been the adopted system of doing things, oligarchy has been the inevitable result. And sure, you could say the same of China and Russia, but those are both incredibly conservative societies that came out of violet coups. What bothers me is when conservatives assume all forms of communism must be taken to that extreme, or conflating Democratic Socialism with Communist Russia. Basically, it operates against strawmen notions of the idea without bothering to read the books, philosophies and arguments of Communism itself. The truth is that there is no perfect system right now, we still need to figure out what is important to us as a society.<br /> <br /> And for the record, the reason why you see all of those businessmen villains, is because in most of the Western World we live in a capitalist society, and the smallfolk are violated and forgotten by the plutocratic oligarchies on a regular basis. In short, those are the villains you see because they are <i>relatable to your average viewer.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982854#post982854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I hate &quot;V of Vendetta&quot;. Anarchy is a nerd child suffering school bullying, a potential Steve Jobs or Bill Gates with broken self-estreem, with broken wings, without social skills because he would rather to be alone. Anarchy is a group of narcos calling at the door of a Mexican family and telling: &quot;I like your wife, your daughter has to go to the shower because she will the next&quot; (and this happened). I don't like estatism, when the state has too control, but total anarchy isn't the right answer. Anarchy only can work when everybody are saints.</div> </div> </div> </div>V for Vendetta isn't about Anarchy, it's about how conservative view points and a willingness to fear and mistreat refugees can blossom into a political party that will seize complete power, much as it did in Turkey. I imagine you don't like V for Vendetta because the methods that government uses to take full control are a lot of the same views you see in Conservative Republicans today. The entire point of the movie and comic wasn't that anarchy is good, it's that things like the Nazis in Germany don't just spring up because that's how evil rolls, they come from conservative values playing into fear that a group of people can make use of to seize more power. They require that good people do nothing while it happens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982854#post982854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It is hard to imagine a more stupid or more dangerous way of making decisions than by putting those decisions in the hands of people who pay no price for being wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thomas Sowell Read</div> </div> </div> </div>Except failure is its own consequence, isn't it? It's curious that this point is brought out this way, as if without the drive to maximize profit, communism will fall flat, producing endless cheap phones, toys, crops that are lacking or otherwise scarce, etc. And yet, it's capitalism that has led to these things. It's capitalism that drives you to create the best product you can as 'cheaply' as you can. It's capitalism where corporations and businesses employ no degree of profit sharing, so that the new peasant caste is forced to labor in their offices and workshops without seeing increased profit for harder or more efficient work, there is no explicit philosophy in Capitalism that is meant to keep wealth from accumulating in the hands of a few, the only thing it really has is a competitor with a better product will win out - except that's not true either, is it? A competitor with a better product would win out if people were objective, and if a wealthy few were unable to trounce them with marketing and deals. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Communism was designed with these concerns in mind, it is designed to help prevent money and influence accumulating in the hands of a privileged few, and when communism fails it's because these principles were 'ignored'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:13:20-07:00","id":982877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982874#post982874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Especially your question about Fox.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my Fox News question got lost wandering around in the smoke of this flame war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:14:53-07:00","id":982878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982839#post982839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...I got a question that hopefully doesn't start a flame war. What do you guys think about Fox News?<br /> <br /> I've watched a fair bit of Fox News living in Texas (It's all the Doctor's offices show on TV). One thing I noticed is that when they have debates with a liberal and a conservative, they don't actually debate. They play parts.<br /> <br /> The Liberal usually have a complex explanation of the liberal side of the argument (which actually a decent representative of the liberal PoV). The Conservative doesn't even bother to argue their point with the liberal, but instead just spews easily repeatable sound bites. I actually started using this technique for my Socially manipulative NPCs and sometimes in real life (give people easily digestible and repeatable phrases)<br /> <br /> Is this what you guys see too? Or is this point of view filtered though my liberal bias?</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend not to watch Fox News because they have a very, very bad habit of not checking their sources and focusing more on infotainment than journalism. Of course, I can make similar arguments in regards to CNN, MSNBC, and essentially every US news source.<br /> <br /> I actually tend to get my news from Reuters and PBS. They're the least biased sources I can find. So sad that one of them isn't even based in my home country.<br /> <br /> And having lived in Texas for 8 years I know <i>exactly</i> what you mean. The doctors here in Louisiana surprisingly play HGTV, or HLN or whatever the network with the house flippers and home makeovers is. Much more useful to me as it gives me landscaping/renovation ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982877#post982877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think my Fox News question got lost wandering around in the smoke of this flame war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! I had only just gotten here and was in process of responding!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:18:47-07:00","id":982883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982878#post982878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend not to watch Fox News because they have a very, very bad habit of not checking their sources and focusing more on infotainment than journalism. Of course, I can make similar arguments in regards to CNN, MSNBC, and essentially every US news source.<br /> <br /> I actually tend to get my news from Reuters and PBS. They're the least biased sources I can find. So sad that one of them isn't even based in my home country.<br /> <br /> And having lived in Texas for 8 years I know <i>exactly</i> what you mean. The doctors here in Louisiana surprisingly play HGTV, or HLN or whatever the network with the house flippers and home makeovers is. Much more useful to me as it gives me landscaping/renovation ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really don't watch CNN or MSNBC either. I don't think there is enough news for three 24 hour news stations. So they have to create controversy for ratings. I get my news from BBC myself. Or Fark (not the least bias around, but at least it is entertaining.)<br /> <br /> I miss Florida where the Doctor's office would play Discovery Health.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:19:35-07:00","id":982885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982830#post982830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This does not strike me as a typical conservative understanding of what trigger warnings constitute. Not knocking you by saying that, mind! Just that it's surprising.<br /> <br /> It's one of those issues where I feel like people often talk past one another to the strawman way over there, y'know? What you're describing is what I'm actually seeing when I see trigger warnings used, but people seem to insist in every case that it's the part where people are shutting something down because they find them offensive.<br /> <br /> Universities are probably the perfect example. The practice of trigger warning usage is for PTSD things and really just to give people a heads up that content will be explored in a given class, with the potential (not always) of alternative material being offered for the aforementioned PTSD grouping.<br /> <br /> But when you read about it in the media, it's always people spending 99% of the conversation on those people using it to shut down conversations, or some theoretical notion of disallowing the teaching of topics due to potentially triggering content (Which does not seem to actually be an idea discussed by any faculty at any university ever?)<br /> <br /> It's really weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not at universities, but online OH MY GOODNESS YES. Go read Tumblr sometime. Actually, don't do that. Do literally anything else. Go shopping. Go kill someone. Go put on a one-man-production of <i>The King in Yellow</i>. Anything would be less sanity-shattering than going to read Tumblr with the expectation that there are rational human beings in abundance there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:19:49-07:00","id":982886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982877#post982877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think my Fox News question got lost wandering around in the smoke of this flame war.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I personally didn't answer the question because even a lot of people with conservative viewpoints understand just how loaded with buzzwords Fox News is, and also because the question wasn't really aimed at me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:20:36-07:00","id":982888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982886#post982886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I personally didn't answer the question because even a lot of people with conservative viewpoints understand just how loaded with buzzwords Fox News is, and also because the question wasn't really aimed at me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No worries. Someone did answer my question. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:23:08-07:00","id":982890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982857#post982857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I didn't use Hitler as an example because he was Christian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hitler was neopagan, he didn't like Christianity (but he liked more islam). Did you know German Catholic regions voted againts him? What do you know about the nuns Edith Stein and Maria Restitute Kafka, or Maxilian Kolbe, Sophie School and the White Rose, or the Catholic priests in the Dachau concetration camp? Have you readen anything about Pope Pius XI's encyclical &quot;Mit brenneder Sorge&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> 10th October, 1941:<br /> &quot;Christianity is a rebellion against natural law, a protest against nature. Taken to its logical extreme, Christianity would mean the systematic cultivation of the human failure&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st May 1937 speech.<br /> &quot;As long as they concern themselves with their religious problems, the State will not concern itself with them. If they try by whatever means, by letters, encyclicals and the like, to claim rights which are those of the State alone, we shall force them to return to the realm of spiritual and pastoral activities where they belong. Nor is it appropriate for them to criticize the morality of the state, when they have more than enough reason to worry about their own morals&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I regard Christianity as the most fatal, seductive lie that has ever existed.&quot;(unconfirmed?)<br /> <br /> <br /> 13th December, 1941, midnight<br /> <br /> &quot;Christianity is an invention of sick brains: one could imagine nothing more senseless, nor any more indecent way of turning the idea of the Godhead into a mockery.... &lt;here insults people who believe transubstantiation&gt;....<br /> &quot;When all is said, we have no reason to wish that the Italians and Spaniards should free themselves from the drug of Christianity. Let's be the only people who are immunised against the disease.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I am angry becuase I don't like the idea of geek fiction to be used to cause more disinformation againts Christian faith. I suffer a lot of people who wants to give me lessons but they don't understand for my own point of view they have only predjudices created by enemy propaganda. I don't like anti-system anti-heroes from modern fiction. We don't need to destroy the system but to change. Be careful because to kill a tyrant is easier to rule a country. <br /> <br /> * I say it again: Spain was the American empire, and now USA is the new American empire, and they also suffer her own black legend created by enemy propaganda. We need self-criticism to admit mistakes we have to avoid or correct, but not too much because then your rivals will try to break belief in yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 10-06-2016, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:26:58-07:00","id":982891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982890#post982890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hitler was neopagan, he didn't like Christianity (but he liked more islam). Did you know German Catholic regions voted againts him? What do you know about the nuns Edith Stein and Maria Restitute Kafka, or Maxilian Kolbe, Sophie School and the White Rose, or the Catholic priests in the Dachau concetration camp? Have you readen anything about Pope Pius XI's encyclical &quot;Mit brenneder Sorge&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> 10th October, 1941:<br /> &quot;Christianity is a rebellion against natural law, a protest against nature. Taken to its logical extreme, Christianity would mean the systematic cultivation of the human failure&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st May 1937 speech.<br /> &quot;As long as they concern themselves with their religious problems, the State will not concern itself with them. If they try by whatever means, by letters, encyclicals and the like, to claim rights which are those of the State alone, we shall force them to return to the realm of spiritual and pastoral activities where they belong. Nor is it appropriate for them to criticize the morality of the state, when they have more than enough reason to worry about their own morals&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am angry becuase I don't like the idea of geek fiction to be used to cause more disinformation againts Christian faith. I suffer a lot of people who wants to give me lessons but they don't understand for they they have predjudices created by enemy propaganda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hitler was absolutely <i>not</i> a neopagan and loathed Himmer and the Ahnenerbe's obsession with the occult. While he did rally against the Catholic Church, I believe that was strictly him trying to kick a source of foreign influence out of his nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:31:51-07:00","id":982894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982891#post982891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hitler was absolutely <i>not</i> a neopagan and loathed Himmer and the Ahnenerbe's obsession with the occult. While he did rally against the Catholic Church, I believe that was strictly him trying to kick a source of foreign influence out of his nation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for answering that faster and more succinctly than me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:35:37-07:00","id":982897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982890#post982890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hitler was neopagan, he didn't like Christianity (but he liked more islam). Did you know German Catholic regions voted againts him? What do you know about the nuns Edith Stein and Maria Restitute Kafka, or Maxilian Kolbe, Sophie School and the White Rose, or the Catholic priests in the Dachau concetration camp? Have you readen anything about Pope Pius XI's encyclical &quot;Mit brenneder Sorge&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> 10th October, 1941:<br /> &quot;Christianity is a rebellion against natural law, a protest against nature. Taken to its logical extreme, Christianity would mean the systematic cultivation of the human failure&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st May 1937 speech.<br /> &quot;As long as they concern themselves with their religious problems, the State will not concern itself with them. If they try by whatever means, by letters, encyclicals and the like, to claim rights which are those of the State alone, we shall force them to return to the realm of spiritual and pastoral activities where they belong. Nor is it appropriate for them to criticize the morality of the state, when they have more than enough reason to worry about their own morals&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am angry becuase I don't like the idea of geek fiction to be used to cause more disinformation againts Christian faith. I suffer a lot of people who wants to give me lessons but they don't understand for they they have predjudices created by enemy propaganda.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What you are doing is called 'quote mining' and it's very helpful for making your argument look superior, except it also takes them out of context, separating them from their greater meaning. Hitler's relationship with religion was conflicted, but self identifies several times as a Christian. Claiming he is not a Christian because he didn't practice it correctly would be owning the No True Scotsman fallacy. As already mentioned, he was <i>not</i> neo-pagan, and was uncomfortable with some of his peers and their occult obsessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:36:33-07:00","id":982899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982891#post982891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While he did rally against the Catholic Church, I believe that was strictly him trying to kick a source of foreign influence out of his nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. It existed on a continuum of religious tension and civil society conflicts in Germany that had antecedents in the Kulturkampf of the nineteenth century and the Thirty Years War of the seventeenth century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:41:24-07:00","id":982902,"title":"","content":"Oh to Hell with this. Hitler was raised Catholic. He just wasn't a very <i>good</i> Catholic. He replaced all of the Christ iconography in German and Austrian schools with pictures of his smiling face and <i>de jure</i> declared war against the Vatican by surrounding it with a hostile force.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm sorry, but at a certain point you actually <i>can </i>declare a &quot;No True Scotsman&quot; fallacy and <i>not be wrong.</i> Assuming that argument makes the arguer wrong is a <i>fallacy</i> fallacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:55:36-07:00","id":982908,"title":"","content":"What makes it wrong? If he identified as Christian, he identified as Christian. It says absolutely nothing about Protestantism that he did. He also was definitely not a neopagan.<br /> <br /> These are just two things that are true, they carry no moral judgement about either idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:11:19-07:00","id":982921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982902#post982902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh to Hell with this. Hitler was raised Catholic. He just wasn't a very <i>good</i> Catholic. He replaced all of the Christ iconography in German and Austrian schools with pictures of his smiling face and <i>de jure</i> declared war against the Vatican by surrounding it with a hostile force.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm sorry, but at a certain point you actually <i>can </i>declare a &quot;No True Scotsman&quot; fallacy and <i>not be wrong.</i> Assuming that argument makes the arguer wrong is a <i>fallacy</i> fallacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>If opposing the Catholic Church is enough to make you not Christian, then anyone outside of the Catholic Church can no longer be considered a Christian. Hitler identified as a Christian, was raised Christian, and calling him a Neo-Pagan or Atheist is fallacious when he expressed hatred of both concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:31:36-07:00","id":982933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982921#post982921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If opposing the Catholic Church is enough to make you not Christian, then anyone outside of the Catholic Church can no longer be considered a Christian. Hitler identified as a Christian, was raised Christian, and calling him a Neo-Pagan or Atheist is fallacious when he expressed hatred of both concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but it also doesn't invalidate the position that Hitler's Christianity had little to do with his Nazi ideology and that Hitler being Christian does not in itself constitute an indictment of Christianity.<br /> <br /> Edited for clarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:42:25-07:00","id":982938,"title":"","content":"Hitler was zealously in favour of anything that was traditional to Bavaria and to a lesser degree Germany in general. Since being a moderate Protestant was German culture at the time, that's what he was and attempted to promote. Not for the religion itself, but as part of the traditional German character, as far as I know. However I think he had a greater emphasis on the forms (i.e. going to mass) than on actual belief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:05:46-07:00","id":982952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982933#post982933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is true, but it also doesn't invalidate the position that Hitler's Christianity had little to do with his Nazi ideology and that Hitler being Christian does not in itself constitute an indictment of Christianity.<br /> <br /> Edited for clarity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's true, except that the original context for my bringing it up was because I specifically didn't use Hitler as an example for a point because he is not Atheist, and mentioned off hand that he was Christian. It hasn't been a jab at Christianity so much as supporting my assertion that he was a Christian, and not an atheist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-06-2016, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:46:01-07:00","id":982968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982952#post982952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's true, except that the original context for my bringing it up was because I specifically didn't use Hitler as an example for a point because he is not Atheist, and mentioned off hand that he was Christian. It hasn't been a jab at Christianity so much as supporting my assertion that he was a Christian, and not an atheist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the counter assertion, that he was not a &quot;true Christian&quot; is also true. He wasn't an atheist, because he thought there was a God. He wasn't a pagan, because he thought there was a God. But he also wasn't a Christian, because nothing he did indicated that he *believed* there was a God. He did not believe in salvation or repentance for sins As far as we know based on both word and deed. As was mentioned, he propagated Christianity almost or entirely out of the idea that being Christian was part of being German.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:57:09-07:00","id":982971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982968#post982968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that the counter assertion, that he was not a &quot;true Christian&quot; is also true. He wasn't an atheist, because he thought there was a God. He wasn't a pagan, because he thought there was a God. <b>But he also wasn't a Christian, because nothing he did indicated that he *believed* there was a God. He did not believe in salvation or repentance for sins As far as we know based on both word and deed. </b>As was mentioned, he propagated Christianity almost or entirely out of the idea that being Christian was part of being German.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're gonna split that hair, then there are <i>a lot </i>of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_true_Scotsman\" target=\"_blank\">not &quot;true Christians&quot; </a>running about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:59:14-07:00","id":982974,"title":"","content":"I remember reading(a long time ago, so bear with me) he wasn't a fan of Christianity at all. He was, at best, apathetic towards it, and didn't really follow any of its teachings. He was a fan of Islam, however, in that he respected the way the religion was practiced in many parts of the world. <br /> <br /> Oh, and I don't really have a point to this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:02:34-07:00","id":982975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982971#post982971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're gonna split that hair, then there are <i>a lot </i>of <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_true_Scotsman&amp;quot;]not</a> &amp;quot;true Christians&amp;quot; [/URL]running about.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as I started earlier, having a fallacy in my argument <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argument_from_fallacy\" target=\"_blank\">doesn't automatically make it wrong.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:02:36-07:00","id":982976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982968#post982968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that the counter assertion, that he was not a &quot;true Christian&quot; is also true. He wasn't an atheist, because he thought there was a God. He wasn't a pagan, because he thought there was a God. But he also wasn't a Christian, because nothing he did indicated that he *believed* there was a God. He did not believe in salvation or repentance for sins As far as we know based on both word and deed. As was mentioned, he propagated Christianity almost or entirely out of the idea that being Christian was part of being German.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;We tolerate no one in our ranks who attacks the ideas of Christianity ... in fact our movement is Christian.&quot;<br /> <br /> He also pushed for a church in Germany that was exclusively Germany's. If being Christian was a part of being German he sure spent a lot of time trying to undermine the pre-existing churches in his country, which he disliked due to outside influence in his country. <br /> <br /> Seriously, claiming that he wasn't a Christian because he didn't preach salvation and </span></span></span>repentance <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">is basically the <i>definition</i> of that fallacy that got you riled up so much. If the person claims they are Christian, identifies their movement as a Christian movement, and pushes for churches in their country, it's pretty safe to say they're Christian, whether you agree with their personal actions or not.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:03:17-07:00","id":982977,"title":"","content":"Now who's quote-mining? Then ISIS is Islamic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:05:47-07:00","id":982979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982975#post982975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And as I started earlier, having a fallacy in my argument <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argument_from_fallacy\" target=\"_blank\">doesn't automatically make it wrong.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're right, being bad at arguing doesn't necessarily invalidate your point, however you seem to have completely missed the point of 'fallacies' in general. They are not an 'I win' button. What it does mean is that the argument you are presenting is flawed. If you're going to assert that he is in fact not a Christian the onus is on you to find a better stronger argument that points to that, one with less fault in its reasoning or assumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:07:08-07:00","id":982981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982977#post982977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now who's quote-mining? Then ISIS is Islamic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Members of ISIS are Muslim/Islamic. Not all practitioners of Islam are ISIS. Hitler was a Christian, not all Christians are Hitler.<br /> <br /> Is this a difficult concept to understand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:31:10-07:00","id":982993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982979#post982979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You're right, being bad at arguing doesn't necessarily invalidate your point, however you seem to have completely missed the point of 'fallacies' in general. They are not an 'I win' button. What it does mean is that the argument you are presenting is flawed. If you're going to assert that he is in fact not a Christian the onus is on you to find a better stronger argument that points to that, one with less fault in its reasoning or assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think I used &quot;argument from fallacy&quot; to point out that your argument is based on a fallacy of I'm not aware that they're not auto win buttons? Here, let me break your argument down for you:<br /> Hitler says he is a Christian.<br /> Therefore, Hitler is a Christian.<br /> <br /> Guess I'm an atheist now then. Sure, I believe in God, Jesus Christ and the Holy Spirit. But as long as I say I'm an atheist and that everything I do is based in atheism, and that I want to spread atheism throughout the world it doesn't matter what I BELIEVE. Why would that determine my BELIEF SYSTEM?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","user":"Frishman","date":". 10-06-2016, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:45:25-07:00","id":982999,"title":"","content":"OK, how about this:<br /> <br /> Why are you trying to say Hitler wasn't Christian?<br /> <br /> Do you have a set of facts to present to demonstrate his record of identifying as Christian was a lie and not his true beliefs, and are trying to factually correct the record?<br /> <br /> Or are you trying to promote him not being Christian to some other end?<br /> <br /> If it's the first, you need those facts. Hitler's dead and gone and we can't ask him what he believes in his heart. We have a historical record, which indicates he identified as Christian; even if not in a particularly devout way. What evidence are you presented to promote an alternative interpretation that should be considered more correct?<br /> <br /> If it's the second.. none of this really matter, because the issue would be why you want to paint Hitler as not-Christian than whether or not the facts support one interpretation over another.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:53:28-07:00","id":983003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982993#post982993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess I'm an atheist now then. Sure, I believe in God, Jesus Christ and the Holy Spirit. But as long as I say I'm an atheist and that everything I do is based in atheism, and that I want to spread atheism throughout the world it doesn't matter what I BELIEVE. Why would that determine my BELIEF SYSTEM?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because words mean something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:53:57-07:00","id":983004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982993#post982993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do you think I used &quot;argument from fallacy&quot; to point out that your argument is based on a fallacy of I'm not aware that they're not auto win buttons? Here, let me break your argument down for you:<br /> Hitler says he is a Christian.<br /> Therefore, Hitler is a Christian.<br /> <br /> Guess I'm an atheist now then. Sure, I believe in God, Jesus Christ and the Holy Spirit. But as long as I say I'm an atheist and that everything I do is based in atheism, and that I want to spread atheism throughout the world it doesn't matter what I BELIEVE. Why would that determine my BELIEF SYSTEM?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hitler believed in Jesus and God. He's got more credibility as a Christian than you do as an atheist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:58:38-07:00","id":983007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982993#post982993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think I used &quot;argument from fallacy&quot; to point out that your argument is based on a fallacy of I'm not aware that they're not auto win buttons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Argument from fallacy does not mean that fallacious arguments aren't worth pointing out, if it did it would implement an immediate paradox. My argument is not fallacious because I never said 'that's a logical fallacy, so you're wrong'. My argument was that your argument was fallacious, therefor it is a fallacious argument. <b>Then</b> I went ahead and provided evidence and my own argument to support why he was in fact Christian.<br /> <br /> As for quote mining, I offer the context with which both sets of quotes were given - one group said he wasn't Christian because he said mean things about Catholics after bridling under foreign influence. The other quote does not have that context. He said it in spite of criticisms toward his position being non-Christian.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982993#post982993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here, let me break your argument down for you:<br /> Hitler says he is a Christian.<br /> Therefore, Hitler is a Christian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually if you want to break down my argument, it would be:<br /> <br /> Hitler was raised Christian, Hitler identified as Christian, Hitler claimed his movement was a Christian movement. His most anti-christian moments were against groups he considered to be corrupted by the Jews, and then he tried to put forth his own Christian institutions.<br /> <br /> But I guess my argument is much easier to defeat once you strawman it, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982993#post982993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess I'm an atheist now then. Sure, I believe in God, Jesus Christ and the Holy Spirit. But as long as I say I'm an atheist and that everything I do is based in atheism, and that I want to spread atheism throughout the world it doesn't matter what I BELIEVE. Why would that determine my BELIEF SYSTEM?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you say you're an Atheist and then you claim you believe in God, Jesus Christ, et al, then you identified as an Atheist immediately before removing yourself from the group. Again, you're attacking a Strawman of my argument, because I understand what you're saying - if you say one thing and do another thing, it doesn't make what you said true. The problem with this is that Hitler <i>never</i> denounced Jesus, or anything along those lines. In other words, political tensions with churches aside, you've offered no reason to believe he wasn't Christian on a personal level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-06-2016, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:04:26-07:00","id":983014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982993#post982993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here, let me break your argument down for you:<br /> Hitler says he is a Christian.<br /> Therefore, Hitler is a Christian.</div> </div> </div> </div>And next time you break down an argument, make sure it's with a funky beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:10:22-07:00","id":983018,"title":"","content":"I don't understand why we are having an argument about Hilter's religion. Atheist, pagan, Christian, it doesn't change what he did. His actions would be against the tenants of any one of those religion / philosophies. <br /> <br /> It is almost like trying to argue Hiller was this religion, not that one, is trying to judge the entire religion based on his actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:32:19-07:00","id":983025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist#post979988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, any conservative gamers around? The Ron Paul / Gary Johnson crowd is also very welcome!</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to fall into that grey area between Libertarian and Socialist, since no one party line fits what I believe. That said, I very much support Ron and Gary's efforts and would vote for them in a heartbeat over Trillary Hump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:50:06-07:00","id":983038,"title":"","content":"Hitler is openly Christian, it's a matter of historical record. You can even make an argument based on antisemitic Christian teachings and church policy for the preceding centuries as having influenced his beliefs if you'd like. It's a dumb argument, but there's probably more evidence for it than him being a secret athiest or germanonordic pagan.<br /> <br /> This is like the Godwin'd version of the Lost Cause myth. This derail is pointless, so I'd like to get back to a more useful tangent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981996#post981996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaming culture, as part of the wider modern geek culture, is one that's facing a lot of push (and blow back for it) from the left as its rise to more mainstream status as caused a large number of minority individuals to feel it is the right time to start pushing back at a lot of the regressive elements in the geek community. Conservative members are put in a difficult spot by this because the left and the regressive forces are both frequently too heavy handed with making the narrative a binary choice of &quot;with us&quot; or &quot;against us.&quot; While I don't personally think there's a lot of middle ground on the topics at hand, I don't think the most vocal left in the gamer world is doing itself a favor by alienating the conservatives that would at worst simple stay out of it by calling such individuals inherently siding for the regressive attitudes by not actively pushing against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>How should vocal activists on the left approach more moderate conservatives with regards to the deplorable beliefs of their fellows? This tribalism reflex you're describing where conservative members feel driven to side with regressive elements because of the &quot;with us or against us&quot; attitude of activists has always puzzled me, to the point where I've always assumed it was a post-hoc rationalization.<br /> <br /> There's a larger issue of epistemic closure in conservative thought that I'd find it fascinating to get some thoughts on too. Already in the middle of the thread we had a few posts about how the media was 'biased against conservatives', urging to seek out alternative sources. This belief has permeated US conservative thought for decades, to the point where the notion of fact-based journalism is seen as inherently against conservative policy. Reality, to paraphrase a comedian, now has a liberal bias. Information that conflicts with conservative thought is immediately dismissed <i>on the basis it conflicts with conservative thought</i>, not on merit or scientific study, which makes discussion on topics ranging from immigration to climate change to economics impossible.<br /> <br /> Probably my favorite example is from four years ago. The Romney campaign was certain of victory in an election everyone else in the world knew they were certain to lose; their internal polling had been wildly skewed to the point where their candidate failed to write a concession speech. While everyone had data on demographic changes in the US, conservative pollsters believed the electorate would be far whiter than any other pollster &quot;just because&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","user":"Shinjo","date":". 10-06-2016, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:56:05-07:00","id":983045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983018#post983018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why we are having an argument about Hilter's religion. Atheist, pagan, Christian, it doesn't change what he did. His actions would be against the tenants of any one of those religion / philosophies.<br /> <br /> It is almost like trying to argue Hiller was this religion, not that one, is trying to judge the entire religion based on his actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>THANK YOU. THAT'S WHAT I'VE BEEN TRYING TO SAY. FORGIVE ME FOR BEING A DUMB COONASS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T19:19:23-07:00","id":983079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983045#post983045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> THANK YOU. THAT'S WHAT I'VE BEEN TRYING TO SAY. FORGIVE ME FOR BEING A DUMB COONASS.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983018#post983018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why we are having an argument about Hilter's religion. Atheist, pagan, Christian, it doesn't change what he did. His actions would be against the tenants of any one of those religion / philosophies.<br /> <br /> It is almost like trying to argue Hiller was this religion, not that one, is trying to judge the entire religion based on his actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just gonna go ahead and state for the second time now that literally all I did was say: &quot;I did not use Hitler as an example because he was Christian.&quot; In the context of not using him as an example for existent atheists who committed crimes against humanity. Everything about this derail that followed was from some person apparently assuming that I was saying all Christians are Hitler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T19:22:44-07:00","id":983080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983038#post983038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How should vocal activists on the left approach more moderate conservatives with regards to the deplorable beliefs of their fellows?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that's more for self-identifying conservatives to answer.<br /> <br /> However I think any reasonable answer would need to start with being willing to engage with conservative philosophic assumptions. The vocal left frequently pushes too hard against conservatives that might agree with their goals by forcing a specific philosophic framework (aka things like privilege and representational politics). I think perhaps looking at some of the US Supreme Court rulings where Justice Kennedy (the &quot;swing&quot; member before Scalia's death, but considered a moderate conservative) sided with the liberal Justices and look at how he approached things and how he phrased his reasons (ex: Kennedy is very big on the concept of personal dignity as a more conservative/libertarian rationale for his rulings over the liberal reasoning you'll get from Ginsberg). <br /> <br /> As I mentioned earlier, my reasoning for being pro-abortion is a conservative philosophic structure (and a faith based one at that) even if it doesn't follow the same logic most conservatives do. A lot of left/liberal leaning individuals would probably have some issues with my logic behind it (esp. since it really isn't based at all in any feminist principles on female body autonomy). So being able to frame seemingly liberal positions from a conservative philosophic framework is something that can be done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This belief has permeated US conservative thought for decades, to the point where the notion of fact-based journalism is seen as inherently against conservative policy. </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think the problem is that the US conservative <b>movement</b> and conservative media have long since abandoned actual conservative principles. A huge number of right wing politicians cloak themselves in the label of conservative, but then push far right radical agendas. The conservative media has openly pushed this same issue by encouraging the concept of &quot;purity&quot; to conservative movements like the Tea Party where you have to always be pushing the most far right platforms to be considered a &quot;true&quot; conservative while centrist and moderate conservatives were decried for their lack of ideological purity.<br /> <br /> I think the majority of right leaning Americans are not actually on board with trying to conflate conservatism with reality denying policies, but the polarization in our politics makes it hard for them to feel like they have a place; which I'm aware is a running theme in my feelings on US conservatism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T19:41:40-07:00","id":983089,"title":"","content":"I have many many strong disagreements with certain elements within the very broad coalition which is called the political right. Some of which I find as problematic as left wingers. Unfortunately, when ever I try to discuss my issues with the political right with liberals, I find the desire to be critical of my own side thrown back in my face. I'm criticized for daring to associate with these conservatives, they are decried as villains, the motives of all conservatives are attacked, and the leftists I'm talking with refuse to show any of the willingness to criticize any aspect of the left like I will do for people on the right. Obviously, this isn't every leftist, but it happens with such great frequency that my first response in any conversation with somebody on the left is to circle the wagons.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, those conservatives that I disagree with are very frequently willing to discuss our differences of opinion in a cordial manner. For example, I'm an atheist and I live in the Bible Belt. I know lot's of conservatives who literally believe that the earth is 6,000 years old and are sure that I'll go to hell unless and change my godless ways. I frequently get into religious debates with these people and find it vastly more pleasant, no comparison what so ever, than discussing politics with people on the left. So, when there are two different sides for me to consider and one is willing to meet me half way and the other thinks that I am either with them or against them, then I obviously would choose to associate with the former group.<br /> <br /> Of course, these are my own experiences and others' may vary. But I have witnessed this pretty consistently as somebody who many conservatives have plenty of things to disagree with me about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:02:22-07:00","id":983101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983045#post983045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THANK YOU. THAT'S WHAT I'VE BEEN TRYING TO SAY. FORGIVE ME FOR BEING A DUMB COONASS.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Hey, how about we don't use racially charged slurs? Like, if you're Cajun and comfortable referencing yourself that way, that's your prerogative, but since the nature of this medium makes it impossible for people to tell your ethnicity, maybe don't do it here. If you're not Cajun, don't even use it in self-reference.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:14:54-07:00","id":983111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983089#post983089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have many many strong disagreements with certain elements within the very broad coalition which is called the political right. Some of which I find as problematic as left wingers. Unfortunately, when ever I try to discuss my issues with the political right with liberals, I find the desire to be critical of my own side thrown back in my face. I'm criticized for daring to associate with these conservatives, they are decried as villains, the motives of all conservatives are attacked, and the leftists I'm talking with refuse to show any of the willingness to criticize any aspect of the left like I will do for people on the right. Obviously, this isn't every leftist, but it happens with such great frequency that my first response in any conversation with somebody on the left is to circle the wagons.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, those conservatives that I disagree with are very frequently willing to discuss our differences of opinion in a cordial manner. For example, I'm an atheist and I live in the Bible Belt. I know lot's of conservatives who literally believe that the earth is 6,000 years old and are sure that I'll go to hell unless and change my godless ways. I frequently get into religious debates with these people and find it vastly more pleasant, no comparison what so ever, than discussing politics with people on the left. So, when there are two different sides for me to consider and one is willing to meet me half way and the other thinks that I am either with them or against them, then I obviously would choose to associate with the former group.<br /> <br /> Of course, these are my own experiences and others' may vary. But I have witnessed this pretty consistently as somebody who many conservatives have plenty of things to disagree with me about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I for one think that everyone believes that they are the hero of their story, and I don't think conservatives are villains.<br /> <br /> When someone tries to start the conversation by taking away my rights, though, it starts to feel like maybe they're the hero of their own stories, but they're the villains of mine. Even then, I try to engage in the hopes of turning that around.<br /> <br /> What would you say is a conservative position that you hold to be a correct and true belief, for instance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:43:43-07:00","id":983121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983111#post983111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I for one think that everyone believes that they are the hero of their story, and I don't think conservatives are villains.<br /> <br /> When someone tries to start the conversation by taking away my rights, though, it starts to feel like maybe they're the hero of their own stories, but they're the villains of mine. Even then, I try to engage in the hopes of turning that around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel exactly this way as well and it happens very frequently. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983111#post983111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you say is a conservative position that you hold to be a correct and true belief, for instance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like going down that road is just opening the door for exactly what I feared to happen. Not from you necessarily, but from somebody else here who will attack me once I start discussing polices. I don't know if I want to bring up an issue just so people can try to convince me otherwise. <br /> <br /> Well, in the interest of communication, I guess I'll discuss one issue. I of a proponent of homeschoolings, both in that I support the right of parents to do it and my wife and I are home schoolers ourselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:43:56-07:00","id":983122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983089#post983089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have many many strong disagreements with certain elements within the very broad coalition which is called the political right. Some of which I find as problematic as left wingers. Unfortunately, when ever I try to discuss my issues with the political right with liberals, I find the desire to be critical of my own side thrown back in my face. I'm criticized for daring to associate with these conservatives, they are decried as villains, the motives of all conservatives are attacked, and the leftists I'm talking with refuse to show any of the willingness to criticize any aspect of the left like I will do for people on the right. Obviously, this isn't every leftist, but it happens with such great frequency that my first response in any conversation with somebody on the left is to circle the wagons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of this is probably the left's unwillingness to put extremists in charge of political parties and movements. You can point at PETA or ecoterrorists or antivaccine proponents (which honestly crosses political spectrums, but is generally associated with leftist leanings) and criticize them to get the sort of derisive opinion and compromise you're looking for. None of those are contributing to the major planks of serious political parties, however, which might be where you're running into a feeling that a leftist won't compromise to the same degree they're asking of you. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983089#post983089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, those conservatives that I disagree with are very frequently willing to discuss our differences of opinion in a cordial manner. For example, I'm an atheist and I live in the Bible Belt. I know lot's of conservatives who literally believe that the earth is 6,000 years old and are sure that I'll go to hell unless and change my godless ways. I frequently get into religious debates with these people and find it vastly more pleasant, no comparison what so ever, than discussing politics with people on the left. So, when there are two different sides for me to consider and one is willing to meet me half way and the other thinks that I am either with them or against them, then I obviously would choose to associate with the former group.<br /> <br /> Of course, these are my own experiences and others' may vary. But I have witnessed this pretty consistently as somebody who many conservatives have plenty of things to disagree with me about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leftist arguments, especially online, tend towards knifefights and the ever-joked-about circular firing squads. It's an eternal war of ideas in competition, life-or-death struggle sort of stuff. From my experience leftists don't put value in compromise for compromise's sake, as opposed to caring about the best possible solution. I can think of two examples to point out the difference in philosophies. <br /> <br /> In the first, LGBT rights. For an activist, nothing less than equal rights is good. In a situation where the left compromises with the right on this topic we'd get something like &quot;Don't Ask, Don't Tell&quot; which was grossly unjust and stupidly inefficient for the US military. Compromise only leads to a worse outcome when both positions lack equivalent worth; in fact, trying to treat both positions as equal, or false equivalence, is at the heart of why leftists decry the media as unbearably biased... towards the right.<br /> <br /> In my second example, abortion. The rhetoric of the religious right often equates abortion with murder, which follows from believing life begins at conception. When religious conservatives allow compromise on this, you might find it laudable, yet leftists immediately question the motive behind it. If their opponents believe abortion is murder, why are they alright with <i>some</i> sanctioned unborn murder but not others? These compromises lack coherency with stated beliefs, so &quot;true&quot; beliefs have to be divined from what is left unsaid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:47:39-07:00","id":983123,"title":"","content":"I also think there's some confirmation bias. I can speak to many similar situations in my life as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> , but just switching the political affiliations around. Being affiliated with the left, most left leaning people are more willing to accept my non-left positions in stride, where right leaning people tend to treat my differences with them with more hostility.<br /> <br /> I feel every &quot;side&quot; is prone via Tribalism to excuse an &quot;acceptable&quot; amount of divergence as long as you identify as part of the group, where the same positions from an outsider might not be met with the same level of understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:56:35-07:00","id":983126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983122#post983122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leftist arguments, especially online, tend towards knifefights and the ever-joked-about circular firing squads. It's an eternal war of ideas in competition, life-or-death struggle sort of stuff. From my experience leftists don't put value in compromise for compromise's sake, as opposed to caring about the best possible solution. I can think of two examples to point out the difference in philosophies.<br /> <br /> In the first, LGBT rights. For an activist, nothing less than equal rights is good. In a situation where the left compromises with the right on this topic we'd get something like &quot;Don't Ask, Don't Tell&quot; which was grossly unjust and stupidly inefficient for the US military. Compromise only leads to a worse outcome when both positions lack equivalent worth; in fact, trying to treat both positions as equal, or false equivalence, is at the heart of why leftists decry the media as unbearably biased... towards the right.<br /> <br /> In my second example, abortion. The rhetoric of the religious right often equates abortion with murder, which follows from believing life begins at conception. When religious conservatives allow compromise on this, you might find it laudable, yet leftists immediately question the motive behind it. If their opponents believe abortion is murder, why are they alright with <i>some</i> sanctioned unborn murder but not others? These compromises lack coherency with stated beliefs, so &quot;true&quot; beliefs have to be divined from what is left unsaid.</div> </div> </div> </div>This compromises you're talking about are policy compromises. They aren't compromises that happen in discussions between private people, but in compromises between competing political factions. No two people are going to debate the issue of gay rights and say that don't ask don't tell is the ideal solution. When two people talk about an issue, they don't compromise by finding a middle position but rather by being polite, by civilly discussing the issues, understanding the point of view of the opponent, and so on. Just saying &quot;I'm 100% right on this issue and anybody who disagrees is a villain.&quot; is an attitude that runs contrary to this. <br /> <br /> In fact, you're statements already seem to be couching your argument is such a way that your position is so right and that of your opponent so wrong, that possibly respecting a differing opinion is absurd. For example, you say &quot;Compromise only leads to a worse outcome when both positions lack equivalent worth; in fact, trying to treat both positions as equal, or false equivalence, is at the heart of why leftists decry the media as unbearably biased... towards the right.&quot; which in so many words is a statement that you are unwilling to respectfully consider an opposing view, that you demand that opposing view be assumed inferior from the get go. I can't really judge somebody from just a few posts on a forum, but that is the message I'm getting and it seems to coincide with an attitude I see all the time in real life and online.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:01:11-07:00","id":983127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983122#post983122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of this is probably the left's unwillingness to put extremists in charge of political parties and movements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... don't conflate the left with the Democrats completely. Dr. Jill Stein is the nominee of the Green Party this year and is perfectly willing to court the fringe left.<br /> <br /> The Democrats have been good at keeping themselves left-centrist at their establishment core, and dominating left wing politics hard enough that the farther left minor parties can't get the traction to be significant third party threats, or threats to internal upset similar to the Tea Party (for all that Bernie got close, he's not an extremist, and his odds were a lot longer than some people like to portray). But that's not that totality of the American left.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:04:07-07:00","id":983128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983123#post983123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think there's some confirmation bias. I can speak to many similar situations in my life as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> , but just switching the political affiliations around. Being affiliated with the left, most left leaning people are more willing to accept my non-left positions in stride, where right leaning people tend to treat my differences with them with more hostility.<br /> <br /> I feel every &quot;side&quot; is prone via Tribalism to excuse an &quot;acceptable&quot; amount of divergence as long as you identify as part of the group, where the same positions from an outsider might not be met with the same level of understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. There has to be confirmation bias, likely on both sides. I don't know how to judge it necessarily. There may be a matter of affiliation. I might say to a conservative that I disagree with &quot;I'm a conservative but I disagree with you on this issue.&quot; and I get a polite debate and to a liberal &quot;I'm a conservative and I disagree with you on this issue.&quot; and get a less polite debate. Where as if I instead said to the conservative &quot;I'm a liberal and I disagree with you on this issue.&quot; and to the liberal &quot;I'm a liberal but I disagree with you on this issue.&quot; and get the opposite amounts of politeness even if my position are unchanged. I don't think this is true, but of course I wouldn't, I am biased.<br /> <br /> We're all biased and it is hard to overcome. That is why I think it is a good idea to go into any discussion being open to the possibility that I may be the one who is wrong and to try not act in a way that I wouldn't want the other person to do. <br /> <br /> In person that is easier, there is a lot more politeness in the real world, where as online things tend to be a lot more adversarial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:25:22-07:00","id":983135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983121#post983121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in the interest of communication, I guess I'll discuss one issue. I of a proponent of homeschoolings, both in that I support the right of parents to do it and my wife and I are home schoolers ourselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you support parents being able to choose any curriculum they desire, up to and including material denying evolution and climate science, teaching that the Founding Fathers were Christian Dominionists, and in general not teaching standards in most fields?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:29:18-07:00","id":983138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983135#post983135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you support parents being able to choose any curriculum they desire, up to and including material denying evolution and climate science, teaching that the Founding Fathers were Christian Dominionists, and in general not teaching standards in most fields?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I do, they should be able to teach their children their beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:58:23-07:00","id":983151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983127#post983127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh... don't conflate the left with the Democrats completely. Dr. Jill Stein is the nominee of the Green Party this year and is perfectly willing to court the fringe left.<br /> <br /> The Democrats have been good at keeping themselves left-centrist at their establishment core, and dominating left wing politics hard enough that the farther left minor parties can't get the traction to be significant third party threats, or threats to internal upset similar to the Tea Party (for all that Bernie got close, he's not an extremist, and his odds were a lot longer than some people like to portray). But that's not that totality of the American left.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dr Jill Stein gets something like 3% of the vote, last I recall? Holding her up as an example against Donald Trump to say &quot;ah, but the left does this too!&quot; isn't fair in the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T22:55:01-07:00","id":983165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982878#post982878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend not to watch Fox News because they have a very, very bad habit of not checking their sources and focusing more on infotainment than journalism. Of course, I can make similar arguments in regards to CNN, MSNBC, and essentially every US news source.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, MSNBC/HLN/ABC/CBS and CNN are all left leaning news stations. Fox was the only right leaning one, but with Murdoch's sons in charge, its starting to go left leaning.. And wit MSNBC they don't even TRY to hide their willful liberal bias..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982883#post982883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't watch CNN or MSNBC either. I don't think there is enough news for three 24 hour news stations. So they have to create controversy for ratings. I get my news from BBC myself. Or Fark (not the least bias around, but at least it is entertaining.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I get mine from several stations, such as CBS and BBC too.. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983018#post983018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why we are having an argument about Hilter's religion. Atheist, pagan, Christian, it doesn't change what he did. His actions would be against the tenants of any one of those religion / philosophies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especailly when we are supposed to be chatting about conservatives in gaming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983089#post983089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have many many strong disagreements with certain elements within the very broad coalition which is called the political right. Some of which I find as problematic as left wingers. Unfortunately, when ever I try to discuss my issues with the political right with liberals, I find the desire to be critical of my own side thrown back in my face. I'm criticized for daring to associate with these conservatives, they are decried as villains, the motives of all conservatives are attacked, and the leftists I'm talking with refuse to show any of the willingness to criticize any aspect of the left like I will do for people on the right. Obviously, this isn't every leftist, but it happens with such great frequency that my first response in any conversation with somebody on the left is to circle the wagons.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, those conservatives that I disagree with are very frequently willing to discuss our differences of opinion in a cordial manner. For example, I'm an atheist and I live in the Bible Belt. I know lot's of conservatives who literally believe that the earth is 6,000 years old and are sure that I'll go to hell unless and change my godless ways. I frequently get into religious debates with these people and find it vastly more pleasant, no comparison what so ever, than discussing politics with people on the left. So, when there are two different sides for me to consider and one is willing to meet me half way and the other thinks that I am either with them or against them, then I obviously would choose to associate with the former group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen the same sort of response. Even trying to talk to some left wingers i have met about what BAD things conservatives do, just gets them smacking me for 'being a bigotted right winger. <br /> Where as my fellow right leaning comrades i chat to, even when i am badmouthing right wing politicians or policies will listen to me, make counter arguments, and generally TRY to come to an agreement.. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983123#post983123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think there's some confirmation bias. I can speak to many similar situations in my life as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> , but just switching the political affiliations around. Being affiliated with the left, most left leaning people are more willing to accept my non-left positions in stride, where right leaning people tend to treat my differences with them with more hostility.<br /> <br /> I feel every &quot;side&quot; is prone via Tribalism to excuse an &quot;acceptable&quot; amount of divergence as long as you identify as part of the group, where the same positions from an outsider might not be met with the same level of understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey.. We blue shirts are better than you red shirts.. At least when kirk takes US on away missions we don't always die off horribly in the first minute <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T22:55:09-07:00","id":983166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983126#post983126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, you're statements already seem to be couching your argument is such a way that your position is so right and that of your opponent so wrong, that possibly respecting a differing opinion is absurd. For example, you say &quot;Compromise only leads to a worse outcome when both positions lack equivalent worth; in fact, trying to treat both positions as equal, or false equivalence, is at the heart of why leftists decry the media as unbearably biased... towards the right.&quot; which in so many words is a statement that you are unwilling to respectfully consider an opposing view, that you demand that opposing view be assumed inferior from the get go. I can't really judge somebody from just a few posts on a forum, but that is the message I'm getting and it seems to coincide with an attitude I see all the time in real life and online.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not entirely wrong, but you are not quite correct either! I can respectfully consider all kinds of opposing views so long as they're backed up by solid arguments, empirical evidence, and consistent reasoning. I don't demand that an opposing view be inferior, but if it has been proven inferior I expect it to be treated as such and not held up equal to other, better ideas. To go to science for a less charged example, it'd be like trying to convince me we should compromise between oxygen and phlogiston, since the truth just has to be in the middle. Oxygen is a better theory that explains why metals gain mass when they rust and wood loses mass when burned, I'd rather we just go with theory that fits reality better. If conservative science man come to me with a different take on phlogiston or some new idea entirely, I'm going to expect it to pass at least as many hurdles as oxygen does before I'll give it equal validity, that's all. If conservatism has a new idea and it IS better, I'll adopt it and discard my old one!<br /> <br /> But sometimes, and I really don't mean to offend here, it seems like many conservatives don't weigh their politics this way. It's perplexing to people wandering around in the center-left like me, building make-shift ideology out of the scraps of the various belief-systems around us. And if you go further left they've basically given up on convincing conservatives of anything and really do have attitudes exactly like you describe. I'm not here to debate policies here in this tread, it's the conservative gamer thread after all, but given opportunity to reach out to a few reasonable sounding conservatives I'm very curious how you all view stuff like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T23:01:01-07:00","id":983170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983138#post983138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes I do, they should be able to teach their children their beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>So &quot;being able to teach their beliefs&quot; should include &quot;making them totally unfit for functioning in the real world&quot;? You don't think the state has a responsibility to protect those kids from their parents?<br /> <br /> What about health care? Should parents be able to refuse to get their kids treated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T23:18:25-07:00","id":983176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983128#post983128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this is true, but of course I wouldn't, I am biased.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that simple, but in my experience it's part of the equation. I live in a very conservative part of the world. While I've never tested the scenarios you proposed, I have definitely received different reactions depending on whether or not the person I'm talking to knows about my general political stances before hand, or if they don't and assume I'm like the vast majority of everyone else here (~80% Republican, and split the rest between Dem, Ind., etc.,).<br /> <br /> It's rarely overtly rude or nasty, but as you note there's a big difference online vs. face-to-face. There have still been times in face-to-face situations where things have gotten decidedly uncomfortable though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983138#post983138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes I do, they should be able to teach their children their beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you do you feel home-schooling parents should have to balance raising their children with the skills they'll need to succeed past what homeschooling can offer, with this? What happens when teaching one's beliefs and teaching vital life skills come into conflict?<br /> <br /> As a note, I have nothing against either home-schooling (in theory, I've met a few individuals that should not have home-schooled their kids because they really did not have the skills or commitment to do so) or teaching children beliefs. I had a religious education and do not regret it in the slightest, and I had a lot of friends that were home-schooled (my private religious school was very small, so I ended up doing a bunch of after school classes with the local home-schooling group for things my school and those parents couldn't effectively do). But I have also seen a lot of home-schooled students struggle intensely in college/university, or get sucked into unaccredited higher education that meant they had higher &quot;degrees&quot; that were meaningless to most employers. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983151#post983151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dr Jill Stein gets something like 3% of the vote, last I recall? Holding her up as an example against Donald Trump to say &quot;ah, but the left does this too!&quot; isn't fair in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>This year. The Green party has on years and off years, but with the Libertarian party they represent the closest things we have to viable third party threats to the two-party system. The Green party has not been successful (even before Stein) in keeping the far left from having too much control of their platform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T23:22:12-07:00","id":983179,"title":"","content":"Saying Hitler was Christians is like saying Spanish communists who burned covents, raped nuns, shooted priests and tortured who declined apostasy were Christians. Maybe in the beginning of his political career Hitler to get more votes presented himself as a Christian, but really he hated Christianity. He wasn't really atheist, but his opinion was Christian faith was other Jew invent.<br /> <br /> If Hitler really was Catholic, what happened to the nuns Edith Stein and Maria Restitute Kafka? Don't you know the story of the Franciscan friar Maxilian Kolbe? Even there is a movie about him!! Don't you know about Catholic priests in Dachau concentration camp and do you want to give lessons of History?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T00:31:15-07:00","id":983201,"title":"","content":"Dude...<br /> <br /> Besides the fact that we've all moved past the Hitler thing, every point you raised was already addressed. Drop it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T03:42:27-07:00","id":983237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983138#post983138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes I do, they should be able to teach their children their beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>At what point do the children's beliefs become important?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T05:01:24-07:00","id":983255,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">&quot;Parents have a prior right to choose the kind of education that shall be given to their children&quot;.<br /> <br /> Article 26.3 of Universal Declaration of Human Rights.<br /> <br /> <br /> This has made me to remember something I had readen in the news, and an article about the book &quot;the plague journal&quot; by Michael D' Obrien. (Let's say this is the anti- Code di Vinci). </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T05:49:07-07:00","id":983267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983237#post983237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At what point do the children's beliefs become important?</div> </div> </div> </div>When they are capable of articulating them. I'm going to raise my daughter Catholic, but I'm not going to force her into being Catholic, or Christian at all if that's not what she believes. I can always hope that is the path she will choose, but it *has* to be her choice. <br /> <br /> Also, if I ever get into another anger-fueled rant, if someone could just tell me to go lay down and take my medicine that'd be great...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T06:20:10-07:00","id":983276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983267#post983267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if I ever get into another anger-fueled rant, if someone could just tell me to go lay down and take my medicine that'd be great...</div> </div> </div> </div>Safe Word noted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T06:42:31-07:00","id":983285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983237#post983237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At what point do the children's beliefs become important?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody's born with beliefs, beliefs come from being educated and having experiences. Those beliefs should overwhelmingly come from the nfluence of parents. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983176#post983176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you do you feel home-schooling parents should have to balance raising their children with the skills they'll need to succeed past what homeschooling can offer, with this? What happens when teaching one's beliefs and teaching vital life skills come into conflict?<br /> <br /> As a note, I have nothing against either home-schooling (in theory, I've met a few individuals that should not have home-schooled their kids because they really did not have the skills or commitment to do so) or teaching children beliefs. I had a religious education and do not regret it in the slightest, and I had a lot of friends that were home-schooled (my private religious school was very small, so I ended up doing a bunch of after school classes with the local home-schooling group for things my school and those parents couldn't effectively do). But I have also seen a lot of home-schooled students struggle intensely in college/university, or get sucked into unaccredited higher education that meant they had higher &amp;quot;degrees&amp;quot; that were meaningless to most employers.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983170#post983170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So &amp;quot;being able to teach their beliefs&amp;quot; should include &amp;quot;making them totally unfit for functioning in the real world&amp;quot;? You don't think the state has a responsibility to protect those kids from their parents?<br /> <br /> What about health care? Should parents be able to refuse to get their kids treated?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, these two questions are similar so I will answer them together. Do I believe, in theory, that there is any degree of bad teaching where the government should step in and force kids out of home schooling and into public schools? Yes, probably so, but it isn't a matter of parenting teaching their children things I disagree with, but rather gross educational neglect - like children who are functionally illiterate or unable to do basic math. That sort of thing is often brought up by opponents of home schooling, but in truth it is exceedingly rare and numerous studies have been done that show that home schooling students do very well.<br /> <br /> As for the possibility that some aspect of home schooling might lead a child to less success than some ore option - that may be true. Then again, who gets to define a successful life? Is it just about money? I think that there are more important things than just money and I don't think that the government should be deciding those things for everybody else. It's not as though there aren't literally millions of public school educated kids who end up in educational dead ends, have terribly dysfunctional lives, or end up woefully ignorant of basic information. I don't trust the government to decide what the absolute truth is to the degree that it should force it on every child in the nation, I see that as highly dangerous. So if somebody wants to teach their children that the earth is 6000 years old, I may not like it and I intend to teach my kids evolution, but I wouldn't think of forcing evolution in their children just as I wouldn't want those parents forcing young earth creationism on my children.<br /> <br /> It's easy to say that the government's version of the truth is the one that should be mandated when you agree with the government. Imagined you were a parent that lived in a nation where something you found morally abhorrent was mandatory for all public school classes, you might be a little more sympathetic then about parents who want to opt out.<br /> <br /> As for health care, that a different topic and education is complicated enough without clouding the issue wih something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T06:43:10-07:00","id":983286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983276#post983276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Safe Word noted.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may mean it facetiously, but I honestly appreciate it. I don't like going down the rabbit hole, which is why I take maximum strength anti-depressants!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:30:40-07:00","id":983304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983286#post983286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You may mean it facetiously, but I honestly appreciate it. I don't like going down the rabbit hole, which is why I take maximum strength anti-depressants!</div> </div> </div> </div>A little from Column A, a little from Column B.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:37:12-07:00","id":983309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983285#post983285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nobody's born with beliefs, beliefs come from being educated and having experiences. Those beliefs should overwhelmingly come from the nfluence of parents.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't actually answer my question. At some point, a person is going to have their own relationship (or lack thereof) with the Divine (or lack thereof). When do you feel that that relationship is valid enough that the parents no longer should get to dictate what religious practices their child engages in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:47:49-07:00","id":983314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983309#post983309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't actually answer my question. At some point, a person is going to have their own relationship (or lack thereof) with the Divine (or lack thereof). When do you feel that that relationship is valid enough that the parents no longer should get to dictate what religious practices their child engages in?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a difficult question and somewhat of a tangent from home schooling. Any minor who lives in their parents' house is going to necessarily be subject to their rules. Though rules may well include going to church, reading certain ideologically driven books, or listening to their parents' express their beliefs. No one can escape being subject to this without having the ability and willingness to leave home. Now, parents may choose to allow their children to go their own way ideologically long before that, but they aren't obligated to.<br /> <br /> Of course, parents don't have mind control beams and if a teenager disagrees, a parent can't truly force hem not to. Though by the teenage years, many beliefs have already been formed and it was likely the parents who did that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T08:30:49-07:00","id":983338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983314#post983314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a difficult question and somewhat of a tangent from home schooling. Any minor who lives in their parents' house is going to necessarily be subject to their rules. Though rules may well include going to church, reading certain ideologically driven books, or listening to their parents' express their beliefs. No one can escape being subject to this without having the ability and willingness to leave home. Now, parents may choose to allow their children to go their own way ideologically long before that, but they aren't obligated to.<br /> <br /> Of course, parents don't have mind control beams and if a teenager disagrees, a parent can't truly force hem not to. Though by the teenage years, many beliefs have already been formed and it was likely the parents who did that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only mildly related to homeschooling and more something that confuses me about religion in general. Liberals tend to ease off when you become a teenager, unless your Grandmother (or whoever) feels a particular blasphemous rite is necessary for saving your soul. Conservatives tend to take a more &quot;My way or the highway&quot; approach to religion like you describe. I'm apalled by &quot;both sides&quot;. It baffles me that anyone thinks they have a better idea of what God (or whoever) says to you in the privacy of your own brain than you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":707,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","user":"etherial","date":". 10-07-2016, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T10:40:38-07:00","id":983405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983338#post983338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's only mildly related to homeschooling and more something that confuses me about religion in general. Liberals tend to ease off when you become a teenager, unless your Grandmother (or whoever) feels a particular blasphemous rite is necessary for saving your soul. Conservatives tend to take a more &amp;quot;My way or the highway&amp;quot; approach to religion like you describe. I'm apalled by &amp;quot;both sides&amp;quot;. It baffles me that anyone thinks they have a better idea of what God (or whoever) says to you in the privacy of your own brain than you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that by the time your child is a teenager, it may be too late to take a hard line stance on what they should believe. If you have to tell your teenager &quot;my way or the highway&quot; you missed your chance to instill your values into them. At that point, all you can can is try to be a good example to them. This applies to both religious and secular beliefs. I think that a lot of parents don't worry that much about their children's ideology until that child is in their teens, then suddenly expect the kid to believe in all the same stuff and it is seldom the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:31:42-07:00","id":983454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983338#post983338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's only mildly related to homeschooling and more something that confuses me about religion in general. Liberals tend to ease off when you become a teenager, unless your Grandmother (or whoever) feels a particular blasphemous rite is necessary for saving your soul. Conservatives tend to take a more &quot;My way or the highway&quot; approach to religion like you describe. I'm apalled by &quot;both sides&quot;. It baffles me that anyone thinks they have a better idea of what God (or whoever) says to you in the privacy of your own brain than you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also don't know of liberals who will beat their children for different beliefs, or cast them out of the house entirely, like I know many conservatives have and will.<br /> <br /> Finally, on homeschooling - my boyfriend was homeschooled. His parents deliberately sought out high-quality secular educational materials. I know it can be done <i>well.</i><br /> <br /> However, I categorically do not think parents have a right to take their kids out of school to force feed them things that are clearly wrong. You can talk about mandating morally reprehensible things all you like - I'm talking about good science versus bad. Something that can be objectively proven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-07-2016, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:41:57-07:00","id":983461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983314#post983314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a difficult question and somewhat of a tangent from home schooling. Any minor who lives in their parents' house is going to necessarily be subject to their rules. Though rules may well include going to church, reading certain ideologically driven books, or listening to their parents' express their beliefs. No one can escape being subject to this without having the ability and willingness to leave home. Now, parents may choose to allow their children to go their own way ideologically long before that, but they aren't obligated to.<br /> <br /> Of course, parents don't have mind control beams and if a teenager disagrees, a parent can't truly force hem not to. Though by the teenage years, many beliefs have already been formed and it was likely the parents who did that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The issue with homeschooling isn't that you're sidestepping government control. It's that by denying them interaction with other students and various teachers, all with their own views and experiences of life, you deny them the chance of cobbling together their own world views after taking all these perspectives into account. This has the negative effect of adults who have no regular dealings with people of other ethnicities, religions, beliefs, what have you. Even without homeschooling a parent still has the right to take them to whatever church they frequent, impress upon them certain beliefs, etc. By saying that you shouldn't have to send them to school where they will be exposed to contrary beliefs is to basically state outright that your beliefs can't hold up to the arguments school is going to present, so you'd rather them not even be exposed to those ideas, even with the home field advantage of being the one your kid comes home to every night, and likely trusts more than anyone else. <br /> <br /> Now that I've played Devil's Advocate, I don't actually have a problem with home schooling. If I were able to have kids, I would be tempted to home school them (provided I were a stay at home mom) if I could not send them to some expensive private school. The issue of a lack of diversity is something I've thought a lot about, and I would have to employ things like 'an hour of playing Devil's Advocate every day' or something to that effect, field trips to festivals, different churches, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:45:30-07:00","id":983462,"title":"","content":"Since we are identifying, I consider myself a libertarian-leaning conservative. For most of my life, I considered myself Republican, my family has a history of involvment with the Republican party as activists, volunteers, etc. I stopped identifying as Republican around 2010. I'm planning on voting for Gary Johnson, as he seems to be the sole reasonable candidate. I'm not 100% happy with his positions, but I don't need to be. Kasich was my first choice.<br /> <br /> I personally feel the primary issue with both major political parties is their tendency to ban things they personally dislike. The assumption is made that government should act as a sort of moral force that prohibits actions simply because they are objectionable from one viewpoint or another, rather than the action causing actual harm to others. We've got one party that wants to keep loving adult couples from being married, and another that wants to force people to bake cakes. I find both equally reprehensible, and ultimately senseless. Prohibition doesn't work, whether it's gin, joints, or sex.<br /> <br /> For all that, though, I'd be tarred and feathered at a Libertarian party gathering; I'm a &quot;statist.&quot; I believe in things like basic social safety nets, effective and well-funded public schools, and a robust, if restrained, foreign policy. I think government sucks at doing just about everything, but some things only government can accomplish. Sure, governments have trouble getting roads built, but I can't imagine turning that responsibility over to private citizens. Half the time neighborhood associations can't agree on the proper height for grass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=982839#post982839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...I got a question that hopefully doesn't start a flame war. What do you guys think about Fox News?<br /> <br /> I've watched a fair bit of Fox News living in Texas (It's all the Doctor's offices show on TV). One thing I noticed is that when they have debates with a liberal and a conservative, they don't actually debate. They play parts.<br /> <br /> The Liberal usually have a complex explanation of the liberal side of the argument (which actually a decent representative of the liberal PoV). The Conservative doesn't even bother to argue their point with the liberal, but instead just spews easily repeatable sound bites. I actually started using this technique for my Socially manipulative NPCs and sometimes in real life (give people easily digestible and repeatable phrases)<br /> <br /> Is this what you guys see too? Or is this point of view filtered though my liberal bias?</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a native Texan, I haven't noticed. I live in Austin, which is the blue dot in the great red sea of my fine state. When I do watch Fox News (rarely these days), most of the time the liberals strike me as being somewhat on-the-outs of their side, making money with Fox. So, they pander a bit here and there, playing the &quot;loyal opposition.&quot; Colmes was a great example of that, as is Joe Trippi. Both of them have valid reasons for being liberal black sheep, so they cashed in with Fox. By contrast, the conservative commentators tend to run the political gamut within their group; some are more reasonable and better speakers than others.<br /> <br /> I've come to view Fox not as the conservative network, but the working class network. It's got big, blonde hair, flashy graphics, and a focus on raw emotional appeals like Mom and Apple Pie, Danger to Children, etc. Roger Ailes, for all his disgusting failings, somewhat predicted the realignment of the white working class with the conservative movement, and he positioned Fox perfectly for it. That's why they win in the ratings game. Fox sells spectacle and fear.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I've noticed the same thing on MSNBC with the conservative guests, who often spend more time semi-apologizing and distancing themselves from some perceived scandal than actually providing a viewpoint. If you dig into their backgrounds, they are also often black sheep. MSNBC sells elitism and outrage.<br /> <br /> This is why I get my news from the BBC, The Economist, and Reuters. The overall bias is much lower, and I can more easily filter it out for the useful information.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:52:01-07:00","id":983471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983405#post983405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that by the time your child is a teenager, it may be too late to take a hard line stance on what they should believe. If you have to tell your teenager &quot;my way or the highway&quot; you missed your chance to instill your values into them. At that point, all you can can is try to be a good example to them. This applies to both religious and secular beliefs. I think that a lot of parents don't worry that much about their children's ideology until that child is in their teens, then suddenly expect the kid to believe in all the same stuff and it is seldom the case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why is it critical for the child's ideology to match the ideology of their parents? If it's not okay for the government to indoctrinate them, why is it okay for a family to indoctrinate them? If the concern is that teenagers are not going to respond to reason and careful arguments as to the validity of your own views, because it's 'too late' and they will only believe what they already believe, how can you be sure you haven't done the same thing, and are now passing down erroneous beliefs to them without the possibility of exposure to truth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:09:07-07:00","id":983484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983405#post983405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that by the time your child is a teenager, it may be too late to take a hard line stance on what they should believe. If you have to tell your teenager &quot;my way or the highway&quot; you missed your chance to instill your values into them. At that point, all you can can is try to be a good example to them. This applies to both religious and secular beliefs. I think that a lot of parents don't worry that much about their children's ideology until that child is in their teens, then suddenly expect the kid to believe in all the same stuff and it is seldom the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Teenagers are also, you know, <i>teenagers</i>. A certain amount of rebellion, exploration, and rejection of previously held truths is kind of what teenagers do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:20:47-07:00","id":983493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983471#post983471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why is it critical for the child's ideology to match the ideology of their parents? If it's not okay for the government to indoctrinate them, why is it okay for a family to indoctrinate them? If the concern is that teenagers are not going to respond to reason and careful arguments as to the validity of your own views, because it's 'too late' and they will only believe what they already believe, how can you be sure you haven't done the same thing, and are now passing down erroneous beliefs to them without the possibility of exposure to truth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is qualified to determine what beliefs are objectively erroneous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:33:46-07:00","id":983502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983493#post983493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is qualified to determine what beliefs are objectively erroneous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without putting words in Solana's post, there's a lot of passed-down beliefs that are objectively erroneous. 'Those people aren't human,' 'Sitting down to piss will turn you gay,' 'Left-handed people are evil,' 'you can't get pregnant the first time.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:44:15-07:00","id":983506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983493#post983493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is qualified to determine what beliefs are objectively erroneous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the child's parents, apparently. That is why it is ideal to expose them to as much as possible, and explain your position to them with reasoned arguments and information.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:49:45-07:00","id":983510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983502#post983502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without putting words in Solana's post, there's a lot of passed-down beliefs that are objectively erroneous. 'Those people aren't human,' 'Sitting down to piss will turn you gay,' 'Left-handed people are evil,' 'you can't get pregnant the first time.'</div> </div> </div> </div>And, you know, stuff like 'Evolution Isn't Real'<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:10:49-07:00","id":983524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983285#post983285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the possibility that some aspect of home schooling might lead a child to less success than some ore option - that may be true. Then again, who gets to define a successful life?</div> </div> </div> </div>This question is essential to the root of why homeschooling is as successful in the US as it is: US educational policy lacks a clear principled concept of why we educate children, and thus public education is constantly a mess as different philosophies of education are haphazardly smashed together in the mix of local, state, and federal directives.<br /> <br /> Since we, as a country, have no idea what we want schools to accomplish, private enterprises from home-schooling to expensive private schools perform well because they can set their own educational agendas.<br /> <br /> I get this can seem a funny thing (a lot of people respond to &quot;what's the point of school?&quot; with, &quot;teach kids stuff!&quot; without ever really digging into what we're trying to teach them), but defining success is something we don't really do as a country; which fails students of all types of education.<br /> <br /> Without a social guiding principle to measure to, my best answer to this though is &quot;success&quot; in primary and secondary education is optimizing the potential of the child to pursue their own careers and lives after they are educated. I know that's vague, but it's unavoidable. I do think this goes beyond basic skills like arithmetic and reading though. Civics is a good example. As members of a democracy, all adults should understand how their democracy works so they can advocate for their political beliefs. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't trust the government to decide what the absolute truth is to the degree that it should force it on every child in the nation, I see that as highly dangerous. So if somebody wants to teach their children that the earth is 6000 years old, I may not like it and I intend to teach my kids evolution, but I wouldn't think of forcing evolution in their children just as I wouldn't want those parents forcing young earth creationism on my children. </div> </div> </div>Phrasing this as a matter of &quot;truth&quot; is extremely problematic to me. Again, I went to a religious school. I was taught my faith's dogma on the creation of Earth and life in one class, and proper scientific method in another. How to reconcile these things were not &quot;facts&quot; but discussions and invitations to study and experiment with personal philosophies.<br /> <br /> The government doesn't mandate schools teach &quot;absolute truth&quot; but rather teach our best understanding of science in science classes. Teaching children that the Earth is 6000 years old as a matter of scientifically valid &quot;fact,&quot; its as bad as teaching a child that &quot;2+2 = 13&quot; as a matter of mathematically valid &quot;fact.&quot; It's making that child scientifically illiterate. Teaching your child the Earth is 6000 years old as a theological position is a different matter, and teaching your child how to approach conflicts between science and faith is an additional matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983462#post983462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've got one party that wants to keep loving adult couples from being married, and another that wants to force people to bake cakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sort of false equivalence is extremely counter productive. Nobody wants to created forced baker camps. The bakers are going to be making those cakes anyway, that's already what they voluntarily do for their profession. The only thing being forced on them is that sexual identity doesn't constitute a valid reason to deny service (and in some states <b>assumed</b> sexual identity since the laws are phrased that denial of service is allowed based on belief not fact).<br /> <br /> This is also something most people have long since considered settled case law. The same exact thing was tried in response to desegregation of private businesses. White business people would claim it was their right to deny service on any reasoning they saw fit in order to refuse service to black patrons. That argument didn't fly. &quot;Public accommodations&quot; even fully privately owned ones have been held to strict standards of anti-discrimination regulations for nearly 50 years.<br /> <br /> When you go into a business that qualifies as a public accommodation, you are going into a business that requires you to set aside your personal beliefs if they contradict the publicly demanded anti-discrimination regulations those businesses operate under.<br /> <br /> What the left wants in this case (and frankly plenty of right-leaning people as well) is that we recognize sexual and gender identities in the same class as ethnic identities; that the law shouldn't mandate you can't discriminate against black people in your bakery, and then not mandate the same for LGBTQ individuals.<br /> <br /> Basically, we already &quot;force&quot; people to bake cakes, the fight is over expanding who you &quot;have&quot; to bake cakes for.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:25:25-07:00","id":983530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983524#post983524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This question is essential to the root of why homeschooling is as successful in the US as it is: US educational policy lacks a clear principled concept of why we educate children, and thus public education is constantly a mess as different philosophies of education are haphazardly smashed together in the mix of local, state, and federal directives.<br /> <br /> Since we, as a country, have no idea what we want schools to accomplish, private enterprises from home-schooling to expensive private schools perform well because they can set their own educational agendas.<br /> <br /> I get this can seem a funny thing (a lot of people respond to &quot;what's the point of school?&quot; with, &quot;teach kids stuff!&quot; without ever really digging into what we're trying to teach them), but defining success is something we don't really do as a country; which fails students of all types of education.<br /> <br /> Without a social guiding principle to measure to, my best answer to this though is &quot;success&quot; in primary and secondary education is optimizing the potential of the child to pursue their own careers and lives after they are educated. I know that's vague, but it's unavoidable. I do think this goes beyond basic skills like arithmetic and reading though. Civics is a good example. As members of a democracy, all adults should understand how their democracy works so they can advocate for their political beliefs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Phrasing this as a matter of &quot;truth&quot; is extremely problematic to me. Again, I went to a religious school. I was taught my faith's dogma on the creation of Earth and life in one class, and proper scientific method in another. How to reconcile these things were not &quot;facts&quot; but discussions and invitations to study and experiment with personal philosophies.<br /> <br /> The government doesn't mandate schools teach &quot;absolute truth&quot; but rather teach our best understanding of science in science classes. Teaching children that the Earth is 6000 years old as a matter of scientifically valid &quot;fact,&quot; its as bad as teaching a child that &quot;2+2 = 13&quot; as a matter of mathematically valid &quot;fact.&quot; It's making that child scientifically illiterate. Teaching your child the Earth is 6000 years old as a theological position is a different matter, and teaching your child how to approach conflicts between science and faith is an additional matter.<br /> <br /> This sort of false equivalence is extremely counter productive. Nobody wants to created forced baker camps. The bakers are going to be making those cakes anyway, that's already what they voluntarily do for their profession. The only thing being forced on them is that sexual identity doesn't constitute a valid reason to deny service (and in some states <b>assumed</b> sexual identity since the laws are phrased that denial of service is allowed based on belief not fact).<br /> <br /> This is also something most people have long since considered settled case law. The same exact thing was tried in response to desegregation of private businesses. White business people would claim it was their right to deny service on any reasoning they saw fit in order to refuse service to black patrons. That argument didn't fly. &quot;Public accommodations&quot; even fully privately owned ones have been held to strict standards of anti-discrimination regulations for nearly 50 years.<br /> <br /> When you go into a business that qualifies as a public accommodation, you are going into a business that requires you to set aside your personal beliefs if they contradict the publicly demanded anti-discrimination regulations those businesses operate under.<br /> <br /> What the left wants in this case (and frankly plenty of right-leaning people as well) is that we recognize sexual and gender identities in the same class as ethnic identities; that the law shouldn't mandate you can't discriminate against black people in your bakery, and then not mandate the same for LGBTQ individuals.<br /> <br /> Basically, we already &quot;force&quot; people to bake cakes, the fight is over expanding who you &quot;have&quot; to bake cakes for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another popular talking point is that said political party is going to force you to marry homosexuals, except such a thing has never happened. The government is not going to force you to marry anyone - it just happens that there are plenty of faiths and churches that will, and the government must recognize such a status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:58:25-07:00","id":983577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983524#post983524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we, as a country, have no idea what we want schools to accomplish</div> </div> </div> </div>The country, unfortunately, has decreed its primary educational purpose in the vast majority of states; and that purpose is tests. Tests, tests, tests, tests, and when we feel like we've given enough state-mandated(and kickback-collected) tests? Give them some more. And when we're done appointing a savior of education--from Marzano to Hattie, we will all likely be dead. <br /> <br /> Education is a business. A very successful one. For many of the kids, not so much. For the administrators, test makers, and politicians? Very much so. <br /> <br /> You're absolutely right about it, really. But unfortunately, I don't see the issue being solved anytime soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:06:01-07:00","id":983607,"title":"","content":"Testing is important. The problem is the concept of using testing to punish schools. Low test scores should be used to identify schools were we spend <b>more</b> resources to find out why they're failing and what we can do about it, instead of ensuring that underfunded schools stay underfunded by cutting their resources so they can't adequately teach.<br /> <br /> That's the thing about testing. The point is to give the test-giver and the test-taker feedback on how well things are going. If a kid fails a test, you don't give them a suspension, you look for ways for them to get more/better/etc. education so they don't fail again.<br /> <br /> Test making... isn't actually that profitable. The test makers rake it in on test prep courses for well off students that can afford having the extra tutoring with materials written by the test makers. It's like video games. Consoles don't make money, the games do, but you need people to buy your console to get them to play the games. Test makers need the tests in schools so they can make their money writing study programs for passing the tests.<br /> <br /> Administrators are definitely a bigger issue. Money is part of it, but not the totality of it. Distribution of them is a big deal. A rural district with one high school gets the roughly same amount of administrative staff as an urban district with four high schools. This of course is idiotic from an economic stand point, but it also drastically impacts how useful administrators can be. School Boards are an entirely different beast though, because most board members are not paid, have no idea about education, and have insane control over how schools operate.<br /> <br /> Politicians... education is a football. I don't think it really makes any of them anything. They all promise to fix it, none of them do, and at this point it's just a standard campaign promise made because you have to make it, with exceedingly few politicians actually working on it as a serious problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:16:44-07:00","id":983656,"title":"","content":"Edit: Nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 10-08-2016, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T01:01:17-07:00","id":983818,"title":"","content":"Why not school voungers? State pays private schools, or charter shcools.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The most urgent necessity is, not that the State should teach, but that it should allow education. All monopolies are detestable, but the worst of all is the monopoly of education&quot;.<br /> <br /> Frederic Bastiat<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The aim of public education is not to spread enlightenment at all it is simply to reduce as many individuals as possible to the same safe level, to breed a standard citizenry, to put down dissent and originality&quot;<br /> <br /> Henry Louis Mencken, <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The object of education is to form beings fit to govern themselves and not be ruled by others&quot;<br /> <br /> Herbert Spencer<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T02:00:30-07:00","id":983828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983818#post983818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not school voungers? State pays private schools, or charter shcools.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the US? Because it's adding a giant mess on top of a steaming pile of shit. There's nothing theoretically wrong with a well regulated voucher program (plenty of other countries work it out just fine), but the current state of US public education just isn't built to handle it.<br /> <br /> This also goes back to what I was saying about the US education system having no idea what it wants to educate children for. Without a solid philosophic concept of what the goal of successful education is, it is impossible to put regulatory limits on voucher use that are consistent and effective. If a non-public school wants voucher money there's usually regulation regarding curriculum and enrollment to ensure there's an even playing field (so you don't get things like cream skimming).<br /> <br /> There's no band-aid program to fix the problems in the US education system. It needs a complete overhaul from the ground up, and there's pretty no zero political will to make that happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The most urgent necessity is, not that the State should teach, but that it should allow education. All monopolies are detestable, but the worst of all is the monopoly of education&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Irrelevant in the US. There is no monopoly on education by public schools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The aim of public education is not to spread enlightenment at all it is simply to reduce as many individuals as possible to the same safe level, to breed a standard citizenry, to put down dissent and originality&quot; </div> </div> </div>Clever, but ill-informed. There have certainly been times where this was the case, but the US system doesn't have anything resembling an &quot;aim&quot; with public education to even claim it does this effectively. There's lots of examples of public education in the world that disprove this as being inherently true of all public education systems. So when this happens it's either out of systemic purpose or systemic blundering.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T13:21:41-07:00","id":984029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983818#post983818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not school voungers? State pays private schools, or charter shcools.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The most urgent necessity is, not that the State should teach, but that it should allow education. All monopolies are detestable, but the worst of all is the monopoly of education&quot;.<br /> <br /> Frederic Bastiat<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The aim of public education is not to spread enlightenment at all it is simply to reduce as many individuals as possible to the same safe level, to breed a standard citizenry, to put down dissent and originality&quot;<br /> <br /> Henry Louis Mencken,<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The object of education is to form beings fit to govern themselves and not be ruled by others&quot;<br /> <br /> Herbert Spencer</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a whole lot of argument from authority right there. Would you like to explain why all of those quotes are factual? 'cause from my perspective maintaining a minimum standard of education in a citizenry is a pretty bitchin' thing.<br /> <br /> As for charter schools, there are a few examples where they do very well, and many examples where private business pockets the money, or they lack a consistent campus, or any number of other factors that are a problem. I was pulled out of public schools in middle school and put into a Christian Charter School, when I went back to the public school system for high school, none of my credits in charter school counted, and I had to take those grades over again. Charter schools as they exist right now are not a good substitute, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T19:02:41-07:00","id":984171,"title":"","content":"Charter schools tend to work best as a supplement to traditional public schools. They're capable of focusing more completely on forms of education that serve a more niche group (such as online education for students that would have any of a number of issues with attending a traditional physical school) and/or be the cutting edge of new styles of education since it is much easier for charter schools to incorporate new research into education compared to traditional schools.<br /> <br /> Charter schools tend to be less effective when they're used to create &quot;public&quot; religious school options (since there's already a lot of competition there with traditional private religious education, they have to compete by cutting corners leading to the above example of a lapse in accreditation and credit transfer), or when they're attempts to privatize pubic schools which leads to a lot of corruption in the system as profits trump effective education.<br /> <br /> This is, again, a concept that can work just fine. There are European public school systems that balance these things well, so it can be done, Implementing it in the existing US system has proven a very mixed bag. In an ideal world, we could revamp the system and use these things well since it's clear these are tools that could make things better. Of course... well... the world is far from ideal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:48:01-07:00","id":984531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983506#post983506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except for the child's parents, apparently. That is why it is ideal to expose them to as much as possible, and explain your position to them with reasoned arguments and information.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's long been a tradition in America to grant parents far-reaching rights regarding their children. That's respect for the family unit, not an endorsement of what all parents believe or do. And personally, I'm more glad for that right every time I see someone blithely speak (as you seem to) about reaching into that unit and meddling with children with the power of government to ensure they are raised &quot;right.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, unsurprisingly, it seems the thread for conservative gamers has been hijacked by people that are anything but. Color me unsurprised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T13:15:16-07:00","id":984573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=984531#post984531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's long been a tradition in America to grant parents far-reaching rights regarding their children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... it's been a tradition of doing so for mainstream families.<br /> <br /> America has an extremely long tradition of overriding parental rights when it comes to minority communities. I'm relatively confident in the assumption that you personally don't think the historical examples of such were good things, but let's not kid ourselves that this has been a &quot;pure&quot; ideological position of the US. <br /> <br /> Even with the legal abuses of minority family units mostly removed, there's still plenty of social stigmas (for example people pushing to force English education on all citizens instead of it being a matter of family choice) that end up disrespecting minority families' rights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, unsurprisingly, it seems the thread for conservative gamers has been hijacked by people that are anything but. Color me unsurprised. </div> </div> </div>It's... almost like safe spaces are something that crosses political affiliations in the desire to have them...<br /> <br /> Of course, as a thread this one didn't really have a set purpose, so of course it's morphed and mutated as things get discussed. As well, it's worth revisiting the point that &quot;conservative&quot; and &quot;liberal&quot; are highly reductive as labels. I might be more liberal than conservative, but I have views that are conservative in philosophy, and I think there are a number of issues that get coopted by politicians/pundits/etc. on each side that shouldn't really be so. The education stuff is a good example. Home schooling, voucher programs, and charter schools are not &quot;conservative&quot; policy positions, lots of non-conservative individuals think they're great ideas. It's how they're implemented/regulated that get into political differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T15:29:19-07:00","id":984622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=984573#post984573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well... it's been a tradition of doing so for mainstream families.<br /> <br /> America has an extremely long tradition of overriding parental rights when it comes to minority communities. I'm relatively confident in the assumption that you personally don't think the historical examples of such were good things, but let's not kid ourselves that this has been a &quot;pure&quot; ideological position of the US.<br /> <br /> Even with the legal abuses of minority family units mostly removed, there's still plenty of social stigmas (for example people pushing to force English education on all citizens instead of it being a matter of family choice) that end up disrespecting minority families' rights.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's... almost like safe spaces are something that crosses political affiliations in the desire to have them...<br /> <br /> Of course, as a thread this one didn't really have a set purpose, so of course it's morphed and mutated as things get discussed. As well, it's worth revisiting the point that &quot;conservative&quot; and &quot;liberal&quot; are highly reductive as labels. I might be more liberal than conservative, but I have views that are conservative in philosophy, and I think there are a number of issues that get coopted by politicians/pundits/etc. on each side that shouldn't really be so. The education stuff is a good example. Home schooling, voucher programs, and charter schools are not &quot;conservative&quot; policy positions, lots of non-conservative individuals think they're great ideas. It's how they're implemented/regulated that get into political differences.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a very, VERY malleable term. In the past few days, I've talked to my parents who are outspoken economic conservatives and consider themselves to be social liberals, libertarian friends, my people in the BLM/LGBQT activist movements, and out-and-out social anarchists, and everyone has a different barometer for where that conservative/liberal line is drawn.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't have a horse in this race. In America, I'm considered a radical leftist, but I don't give a shit about the political affiliations of creative collaborators, as long as it doesn't negatively effect their output.<br /> <br /> I think the terms &quot;liberal&quot; and &quot;conservative&quot; can be good placeholders, but they can also be incredibly toxic and divisive. All of us want the best for our friends, family, and world (at least, most of us do), and creating these black and white lines of right vs. left creates a very inflexible and obtrusive environment that hinders both sides of the argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-09-2016, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T15:50:26-07:00","id":984628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=984531#post984531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's long been a tradition in America to grant parents far-reaching rights regarding their children. That's respect for the family unit, not an endorsement of what all parents believe or do. And personally, I'm more glad for that right every time I see someone blithely speak (as you seem to) about reaching into that unit and meddling with children with the power of government to ensure they are raised &quot;right.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, unsurprisingly, it seems the thread for conservative gamers has been hijacked by people that are anything but. Color me unsurprised.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was tradition in America to beat your children as a form of discipline, it's also widely accepted as harmful and ineffective by people who study the long term ramifications of it. It was tradition in America to keep slaves and fuel your industry and agriculture with them. Have I pointed out why saying: &quot;But it's tradition,&quot; isn't necessarily a good argument to make? You haven't actually provided a reason why mandatory public education is disrespectful to families. You're acting like I'm advocating for Plato's Republic, where every child is ripped away from their parents and raised separate from them. I have a great deal of respect for the family unit, I think that shows if you pay attention to my post about what I would do with children of my own. But again, I don't see shielding your children from scientific literacy and intellectual concepts as a parental 'right'. The UN might assert that it is, but the argument isn't whether or not the UN says so, it's about whether it should be or not.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T16:05:26-07:00","id":984639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=984628#post984628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was tradition in America to beat your children as a form of discipline, it's also widely accepted as harmful and ineffective by people who study the long term ramifications of it. It was tradition in America to keep slaves and fuel your industry and agriculture with them. Have I pointed out why saying: &quot;But it's tradition,&quot; isn't necessarily a good argument to make? You haven't actually provided a reason why mandatory public education is disrespectful to families. You're acting like I'm advocating for Plato's Republic, where every child is ripped away from their parents and raised separate from them. I have a great deal of respect for the family unit, I think that shows if you pay attention to my post about what I would do with children of my own. But again, I don't see shielding your children from scientific literacy and intellectual concepts as a parental 'right'. The UN might assert that it is, but the argument isn't whether or not the UN says so, it's about whether it should be or not.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think we spend a lot of time bending over backwards to support the idea that everyone's opinion is equal. That's not the case. Just because Trump and Clinton share a stage doesn't mean we should treat anything they say as equivalently valid.<br /> <br /> If you don't think LBQT people deserve the same rights as you, I'm sorry, but you're wrong. Same for an unwillingness to recognize that people of color suffer from greater persecution, more scrutiny, and harsher sentencing terms. Ditto if you don't respect a woman's right to choose. At best, you belong to the camp of &quot;There's always adoption!&quot; without recognizing the trauma that comes from giving birth. At worst, you don't respect women. I like divergent opinions. I like arguing those opinions. But when your opinions adversely affect the lives of people I love, I won't hesitate to draw a line in the sand. No. You're not a bad person. But you're a wrong person, and your fault is preventing people I love and respect from living full and healthy lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T20:00:52-07:00","id":984724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=984531#post984531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, unsurprisingly, it seems the thread for conservative gamers has been hijacked by people that are anything but. Color me unsurprised.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's why I'm not touching the education topic* with a ten foot pole. It will just lead me to ranting and raving and I consider myself a guest in this thread. You don't shit in your host's house, even if they got a lot of their own shit lying around. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> *And any topic about Religion, Women rights, Gay rights, and a few other topics I probably missed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:06:23-07:00","id":985171,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty much the opposite of conservative, in pretty much all ways relevant. But, through time and circumstance I've acquired a -very- mixed group. Like, an MRA, a Feminist, a gay black christian, a single-issue(guns) conservative who tries not to come off as sounding racist, and an activist transman. None of them hang out much outside of game, and there are issues that I could not possibly introduce to my games without at least one side of the table rolling their eyes, if by some miracle we're all together. Sometimes I get around this by running different games on different nights of the week, sometimes I do it by banning certain topics ahead of game night. ALWAYS, I remind everyone ahead of time to stay respectful of each other, even if you can't stand their facebook feeds recently. Some people would wonder, why on earth would I do that to myself?<br /> <br /> Simple! They're all good gamers, and I know how to write a good story for each of them, in whatever setting we play. They treat each other decently, and we've had to democratically boot people before, so everyone is pretty socially aware during game.That's all it really takes to get along, is an active desire to do so, and a bit of self-moderation.<br /> <br /> Something I've noticed about myself that I find interesting is that when I'm running World of Darkness games, I secretly and spontaneously become some kind of hippie-Christian. It goes away after the session, but I keep it on my mind all throughout before I turn back into a godless nihilist. Nobody ever thinks to look in a spiritually righteous direction, or more likely they are actively running in the opposite direction, but the promise of God's Salvation is (almost)always an option, open to all, not just the one christian sect that &quot;got it right&quot;. Eternal bliss awaits christians, jews, muslims, buddhists, wiccans and etcetra. I reward characters with faith, and Heaven is as real as Hell(I refuse to answer this question definitely with them in regards to some kind of Heaven, but to you guys the answer is yes, there exists an Eternal Paradise, and there exists a Creator). Satan(not Lucifer, some noble romantic fallen angel, but The Devil who takes souls, the Father of Lies, Immortal Tempter, Etc.) most certainly walks the earth, in flesh as well as in spirit, wearing many faces and pretending at many roles, seeking always to lead astray the faithful and wicked alike. God, on the other hand, influences the world through the good works of good people, which makes Him much harder to see. Of course, since the WoD is generally a game about bad people, in all the years since I've had this secret headcanon, I've never had anyone die &quot;in grace&quot;, even with my standards relaxed and the pearly gates literally WIDE OPEN.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":".  Clarification 10-10-2016, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},