 engraved in people's minds.<br /> <br /> Voltaire (centuries before Jefrey Baratheon, the crossbowman king to have born).<br /> <br /> <br /> I am Spanish, and I can my opinion from my own point of view from here. Here in Spain you can't kill an intruder in your home, or some children can try blackmail teachers with with false accusationts mistreament. I was tought in a Catholic chapel school, and my father was teacher there, and after the director.<br /> <br /> I went to the university, but I couldn't end the studies. Spanish university isn't harder but trickier, a minefield for studients (questions in the tests about matter weren't tought in class &quot;in that year&quot;, or they weren't in the notebooks but teacher mentioned it sometime in the class. The Spanish socialist has ruined our education, and that is the most retrograde action. The politics don't want us to have a good education, but brainwash us to get more votes in the future.<br /> <br /> If I say you must avoid monopoly of education by state, you have to take care.<br /> <br /> * Isn't it ironical? Lot of people can allow supernatural creatures in the fiction, but God is too to much his existence be accepted by fiction characters. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's an incredibly simplified and largely insulting viewpoint. It's paramount to assuming that all leaders who are also religious have an imperative to persecute people who don't prescribe to their beliefs. When we look at atheist leaders who persecute religious groups, they all have something particular in common (and it's not their lack of religion). It's the fact that they're demagogues, typically with severe paranoid leanings.<br /> <br /> As far as religion goes, I think Onyx Path has done a good job of representing religion at its best and at its worst. Groups like the Lancaea Sanctum, Malleus Maleficarium, and Long Night aren't presented as frothing radicals or as saints. Religious characters aren't excluded from the game at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-11-2016, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:11:06-07:00","id":985522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985485#post985485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Voltaire also wasn't exactly a cheerleader for Catholicism, nor was he using the term &quot;atheist&quot; the way we would use it today. He is riffing on Pufendorf's usage, in which Atheism is not a belief system but an act. An &quot;Atheist&quot; wasn't someone who proclaimed to not believe in God, but rather a Christian who was guilty of &quot;Atheism,&quot; or behaving amorally.</div> </div> </div> </div>He also had other, stranger takes on what was religious in origin. A unified origin of humans, for example; we know that scientific evidence validates this viewpoint, if not from some working method, but here's a couple of quotes from him on the subject. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scientific_racism#Voltaire\" target=\"_blank\">Beware for the horrific, stark ignorance displayed therein.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-11-2016, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:22:29-07:00","id":985535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985504#post985504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as religion goes, I think Onyx Path has done a good job of representing religion at its best and at its worst. Groups like the Lancaea Sanctum, Malleus Maleficarium, and Long Night aren't presented as frothing radicals or as saints. Religious characters aren't excluded from the game at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might make an argument that the Lancea et Sanctum are assholish monsters, but that's because they <i>literally are monsters</i> and not because they're Christians.<br /> <br /> Hell, even the Seer Ministry that literally has the job of oppressing mankind through religion is presented pretty reasonably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:23:58-07:00","id":985537,"title":"","content":"Please, don talk me about to be paramount to assuming that all leaders who are also religious have an imperative to persecute people who don't prescribe to their beliefs, because for my point of view It's paramount to assuming that all no-Christians leaders have an imperative (by cryptocracy or secret lobby, like mason lodges or sith orders) to try eradicate Church in the modern Western society. <br /> <br /> I hat that stupy stereotype in the fantasy fiction about equivalent to inquisitors and crusaders who want to terminate all it is different and they can't understand, or may be a &quot;menace for religious monopoly&quot;. I don't want any more &quot;we are the friends of humanity from X-Men comics, we want to kill all mutants because we are good Christians&quot;. I don't want fiction to be used to tell people who goes to church each Sunday they are a potencial menace againts freedom (but we can't speak about jihadism because it is islamophobia)... why not to talk about 100.000.000 victims by comunism? Or, we can't tell anything bad about comunism, we are too busy with senator McCarthy, we want know nothing about Stalin's chekas and the &quot;great purge&quot;.<br /> <br /> Have you readen anything about the persecution againts Catholics in the Spanish 30's years? And now I am watching the signals here we are following the same steps, making the same mistakes. In this new century we could be a new Cristero war in Mexico, and a civil war in Spain, maybe in all Europa. Have you imagined how would be a Hugo Chavez (or senator Palpatine) like president of USA? Russia could try invade Oriental Europe, thinking NATO would dare to face her, or China invading Vietnam, Corea, Japan and Philipines. I don't talk about a videogame or a novel, but in this century in the real life.<br /> <br /> Please, no more lessons about Torquemada or crusades. Why not to talk now about Ucranian Holodomor, or French Terror by Robespierre and Jacobines?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:40:29-07:00","id":985551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985537#post985537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> why not to talk about 100.000.000 victims by comunism? Or, we can't tell anything bad about comunism, we are too busy with senator McCarthy, we want know nothing about Stalin's chekas and the &quot;great purge&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do though. We've never not, at least in the US. You speak of McCarthy and Stalin like they're somehow mutually exclusive. Yeah, when I was in school we learned that McCarthyism was a bad thing, but the millions murdered in Stalin's purges was also pretty much the foremost thing we learned about the Soviet Union.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you readen anything about the persecution againts Catholics in the Spanish 30's years? </div> </div> </div>I have actually, and that was terrible. What about the forty years after that under Franco, though?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Please, no more lessons about Torquemada or crusades. Why not to talk now about Ucranian Holodomor, or French Terror by Robespierre and Jacobines? </div> </div> </div>The only person in this entire thread to bring up Torquemada and the Crusades has been you. Multiple times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:46:26-07:00","id":985557,"title":"","content":"Someone nudge Luis Carlos.....he's stuck on repeat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","