-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hat that stupy stereotype in the fantasy fiction about equivalent to inquisitors and crusaders who want to terminate all it is different and they can't understand, or may be a &quot;menace for religious monopoly&quot;. I don't want any more &quot;we are the friends of humanity from X-Men comics, we want to kill all mutants because we are good Christians&quot;. I don't want fiction to be used to tell people who goes to church each Sunday they are a potencial menace againts freedom (but we can't speak about jihadism because it is islamophobia)... why not to talk about 100.000.000 victims by comunism? Or, we can't tell anything bad about comunism, we are too busy with senator McCarthy, we want know nothing about Stalin's chekas and the &quot;great purge&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>We know tons about it, it was horrible - but it was also a problem of statism and absolutism, not necessarily atheism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985537#post985537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you readen anything about the persecution againts Catholics in the Spanish 30's years? And now I am watching the signals here we are following the same steps, making the same mistakes. In this new century we could be a new Cristero war in Mexico, and a civil war in Spain, maybe in all Europa. Have you imagined how would be a Hugo Chavez (or senator Palpatine) like president of USA? Russia could try invade Oriental Europe, thinking NATO would dare to face her, or China invading Vietnam, Corea, Japan and Philipines. I don't talk about a videogame or a novel, but in this century in the real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mean Donald Trump. Also, Putin's a Christian (probably) and China's a weird thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985537#post985537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, no more lessons about Torquemada or crusades. Why not to talk now about Ucranian Holodomor, or French Terror by Robespierre and Jacobines?</div> </div> </div> </div>See, there's this thing that you do, and it's saying that we aren't allowed to talk about one bad thing unless we also reference another. You do it again and again, and you don't seem to understand how that's a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:01:47-07:00","id":985576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985535#post985535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might make an argument that the Lancea et Sanctum are assholish monsters, but that's because they <i>literally are monsters</i> and not because they're Christians.<br /> <br /> Hell, even the Seer Ministry that literally has the job of oppressing mankind through religion is presented pretty reasonably.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the Sanctum are most certainly monsters, but I think OPP has done a pretty good job of showing us the best and the worst. They present the Sanctum as being composed of a wide variety of monsters with a wide variety of relationships to their faith. There's a reason why the LS continues to be relevant even among the younger and less monstrous vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985537#post985537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, don talk me about to be paramount to assuming that all leaders who are also religious have an imperative to persecute people who don't prescribe to their beliefs, because for my point of view It's paramount to assuming that all no-Christians leaders have an imperative (by cryptocracy or secret lobby, like mason lodges or sith orders) to try eradicate Church in the modern Western society.<br /> <br /> I hat that stupy stereotype in the fantasy fiction about equivalent to inquisitors and crusaders who want to terminate all it is different and they can't understand, or may be a &quot;menace for religious monopoly&quot;. I don't want any more &quot;we are the friends of humanity from X-Men comics, we want to kill all mutants because we are good Christians&quot;. I don't want fiction to be used to tell people who goes to church each Sunday they are a potencial menace againts freedom (but we can't speak about jihadism because it is islamophobia)... why not to talk about 100.000.000 victims by comunism? Or, we can't tell anything bad about comunism, we are too busy with senator McCarthy, we want know nothing about Stalin's chekas and the &quot;great purge&quot;.<br /> <br /> Have you readen anything about the persecution againts Catholics in the Spanish 30's years? And now I am watching the signals here we are following the same steps, making the same mistakes. In this new century we could be a new Cristero war in Mexico, and a civil war in Spain, maybe in all Europa. Have you imagined how would be a Hugo Chavez (or senator Palpatine) like president of USA? Russia could try invade Oriental Europe, thinking NATO would dare to face her, or China invading Vietnam, Corea, Japan and Philipines. I don't talk about a videogame or a novel, but in this century in the real life.<br /> <br /> Please, no more lessons about Torquemada or crusades. Why not to talk now about Ucranian Holodomor, or French Terror by Robespierre and Jacobines?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you're going to assume that all atheist leaders are out to burn you, there's not much I can do to help you. The fact of the matter is, most atheists don't hate you. At least most of the ones I know don't. Most of us just want to live together. And most of us think everyone should have the right to believe what they want to be and live happy and healthy lives regardless of their faith. That's not to say there haven't been horrible atheist leaders who have committed atrocities. Look at Stalin. Hell, even a lot of the current Nordic states often present a pretty toxic, militant approach to people of faith, but that doesn't make all atheist leaders villains. Demagogues use faith, and lack of faith as a cudgel to convince their people that acts of horrible violence are acceptable. They do that by dehumanizing the other side, by convincing them that every Muslim/Christian/atheist/etc. is a monster who wants to eradicate them from the face of the Earth. Sound familiar?<br /> <br /> And I don't think anyone is immune to the horrors of the French Revolution or Stalin's regime. I don't think most people consider violence to be the sole domain of religious zealots. But I think it's easy, through confirmation bias, to assume that the world is against you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-11-2016, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:12:57-07:00","id":985588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985576#post985576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, the Sanctum are most certainly monsters, but I think OPP has done a pretty good job of showing us the best and the worst. They present the Sanctum as being composed of a wide variety of monsters with a wide variety of relationships to their faith. There's a reason why the LS continues to be relevant even among the younger and less monstrous vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imma go ahead and disagree with you there. The LS Covenant Book horrified me as a player and the LS went from one of my favorite Covenants to one I couldn't stand the thought of playing. It portrayed them as being exclusively the worst sort of Religious Fanatics the world has to offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:15:51-07:00","id":985591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985588#post985588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imma go ahead and disagree with you there. The LS Covenant Book horrified me as a player and the LS went from one of my favorite Covenants to one I couldn't stand the thought of playing. It portrayed them as being exclusively the worst sort of Religious Fanatics the world has to offer.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's bad for vampires?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:18:10-07:00","id":985593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985588#post985588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imma go ahead and disagree with you there. The LS Covenant Book horrified me as a player and the LS went from one of my favorite Covenants to one I couldn't stand the thought of playing. It portrayed them as being exclusively the worst sort of Religious Fanatics the world has to offer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Really? It's been a while since I read the book, so I may be incorrectly filtering my memory of it, but I recall them being a nuanced, if monstrous group in a sea of nuanced but monstrous groups.<br /> <br /> The more monstrous among them justify their evil as a part of God's plan, as being the monsters the world needs, preying on both humans and younger vampires who are looking for salvation. But conversely, the Ordo Dracul is presented that's ostensibly about finding out the truth through science while their leaders pursue inhuman, alien agendas. The Circle of the Crone presents themselves as offering liberation through chaos even though their precepts drive their members to be monsters. I think they're all monstrous groups, but they're equivalently monstrous.<br /> <br /> The key point for me is that it doesn't cast faith in and of itself as terrible. It distinguishes the Sanctum as distinct from the Catholic Church. It's not faith that twists these creatures. It's age and complacency, and the sort of religion they promote is a twisted and inaccurate reflection of church doctrine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-11-2016, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:05:28-07:00","id":985618,"title":"","content":"I think that Luis does have a point about anti-Christian or anti-Catholic elements within the geeky subculture. Other elements within society too, like entertainment and academia. Then again, within the wider culture, it's different, at least in the USA. We couldn't, for example, have an openly atheist president. Even though both of our two main candidates probably are just atheists paying lip service to Christianity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:06:50-07:00","id":985619,"title":"","content":"Please, I don't want more subtext messages about &quot;the world would be better without religions&quot;. I don't want more characters like the villain from the last Tarzan's movie (with a Christian rosary to strangle) or factions like the &quot;church&quot; from the &quot;golden compass&quot; (why do you think there was a boycot againt the movie?). Can you believe it? I have readen &quot;God&quot; was forbidden in the script of the Disney movie &quot;Frozen&quot;, or some parts from the books &quot;the famous five&quot; by Enid Blyton has been censured/changed because it was about... the main characters went to church in Sunday! A children book &quot;my grandfather is a pirate&quot; by Jan L\u00f6\u00f6f in 1966 now is policitally incorrect because there are Muslims characters. <br /> <br /> This afternoon itself in a facebook group, somebody published a picture, a cartoon, about a man withing a church shooting a priest whose altar boy was down on his kness to do... you can't imagine the quanty of messages hostile againt Catholic religion I can find. Once when Benedictin XVI was chosen Pope, the satirical magazine &quot;el Jueves&quot; (the Thursday, like the French Charlie Hebbo or the American MAD) showed it wearing a nazi uniform, and talking about a beer like better than wine. <br /> <br /> When I want to enjoy fiction, the last wish is to find more messages about religious fanaticism. Why not talking about revolucionary fanaticism? <br /> <br /> * This is a subliminal message. The next time you see a episode of the telecomedy &quot;the Big Bang Theory&quot;, a picture of a character or only a mention, then your brain will rememeber the name ofr George Lemaitre, priest and the scientific father of the famous teory of the big bang (but the name he used was &quot;cosmic egg&quot;).<br /> <br /> * &quot;The more I learn the people, better I like my dog&quot; Mark Twain. &quot;the more I read about Westeros and characters from Games of Thrones, better I love Christianism. (Me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:23:51-07:00","id":985626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985619#post985619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, I don't want more subtext messages about &amp;quot;the world would be better without religions&amp;quot;. I don't want more characters like the villain from the last Tarzan's movie (with a Christian rosary to strangle) or factions like the &amp;quot;church&amp;quot; from the &amp;quot;golden compass&amp;quot; (why do you think there was a boycot againt the movie?). Can you believe it? I have readen &amp;quot;God&amp;quot; was forbidden in the script of the Disney movie &amp;quot;Frozen&amp;quot;, or some parts from the books &amp;quot;the famous five&amp;quot; by Enid Blyton has been censured/changed because it was about... the main characters went to church in Sunday! A children book &amp;quot;my grandfather is a pirate&amp;quot; by Jan L\u00f6\u00f6f in 1966 now is policitally incorrect because there are Muslims characters. <br /> <br /> When I want to enjoy fiction, the last wish is to find more messages about religious fanaticism. Why not talking about revolucionary fanaticism? </div> </div> </div> </div>I feel your pain, I really do. You make good points and there are similar things that I find irritating as well. Even some of the same things. <br /> <br /> Though I also think you should be careful about painting atheists with the same broad brush.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:29:47-07:00","id":985633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985474#post985474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I mean, I am an atheist and I haven't pois... Well, I'm probably an outlier <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! That reminds me...completely unrelated, but you should probably Antidote yourself, Sarge. The sooner the better, I would say. <br /> <br /> Again, completely unrelated. &gt;_&gt;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:31:13-07:00","id":985634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985633#post985633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh! That reminds me...completely unrelated, but you should probably Antidote yourself, Sarge. The sooner the better, I would say. <br /> <br /> Again, completely unrelated. &gt;_&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>I take one every day, just in case. Can't be too careful with atheists about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:36:53-07:00","id":985638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985619#post985619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* This is a subliminal message. The next time you see a episode of the telecomedy &quot;the Big Bang Theory&quot;, a picture of a character or only a mention, then your brain will rememeber the name ofr George Lemaitre, priest and the scientific father of the famous teory of the big bang (but the name he used was &quot;cosmic egg&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Lemaitre was a genius, but the Big Bang model was developed by four individuals of which Lemaitre was one, although depending on your viewpoint he had the most important contribution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:38:39-07:00","id":985639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Freedom to write, freedom to read, freedom to own material that you believe is worth defending means you're going to have to stand up for stuff you don't believe is worth defending, even stuff you find actively distasteful, because laws are big blunt instruments that do not differentiate between what you like and what you don't, because prosecutors are humans and bear grudges and fight for re-election, because one person's obscenity is another person's art. Because if you don't stand up for the stuff you don't like, when they come for the stuff you do like, you've already lost.&quot;<br /> -Neil Gaiman </div> </div> </div>Every single piece of artwork/literature is going to offend someone. I agree too many writers find the Christian Church easy picking for antagonists. I don't mind a well-thought out critique on the Church, but there are too many two dimensional villains. I personally couldn't make it too far into Preacher because, while I am Agnostic, I was raised Christian and the portrayal in that comic was too far from what I grew up with. Heck, if you look at my past posts on the forum, I have raged against sexist female portrayals. However, I disagree with the idea that censorship is the way to go. Yes, I vote with my dollars and reward creative material that I want more of. Yet just because I won't buy a comic with big breasted blond woman in chain mail bikini's doesn't mean that someone else won't find such a comic interesting. <br /> <br /> But I'm am anti- censorship in general. As long as you aren't releasing personal identifiable information and you can find a publisher, I'm not going to argue with your right to publish what you want. I may hate and despise your work, but I am not going to say &quot;No! The government ban this material!&quot; I'd probably be a bad moderator on any forum because I would let flame wars engulf the place. <br /> <br /> (I should note that I am American, so my cultural values influence my views on this matter. Also, violence against Christian Churches in America is usually racially motivated. You don't hear too many stories about White Churches being burnt down. )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:43:18-07:00","id":985642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985619#post985619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, I don't want more subtext messages about &quot;the world would be better without religions&quot;. I don't want more characters like the villain from the last Tarzan's movie (with a Christian rosary to strangle) or factions like the &quot;church&quot; from the &quot;golden compass&quot; (why do you think there was a boycot againt the movie?). Can you believe it? I have readen &quot;God&quot; was forbidden in the script of the Disney movie &quot;Frozen&quot;, or some parts from the books &quot;the famous five&quot; by Enid Blyton has been censured/changed because it was about... the main characters went to church in Sunday! A children book &quot;my grandfather is a pirate&quot; by Jan L\u00f6\u00f6f in 1966 now is policitally incorrect because there are Muslims characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a boycott against The Golden Compass because God is the main villain and it's a children's book. There are plenty of families out there that are atheist or agnostic or even those who are attempting to rebuild the beliefs and customs their ancestors had before Christians got involved. Why is it okay to condemn them having a book that represents story elements important to them, but complain when a movie has any religious subtext removed from it? While we're on the subject, care to offer some context for your claims regarding Disney, or 'The Famous Five'? I'm not prone to taking someone's word for it, especially with claims like that. God comes up in Disney movies plenty. My Grandfather is a Pirate is not 'politically incorrect' for including muslim characters, it is being redrawn because its depictions of Arabian peoples is stereotypically offensive, in much the same way that some instances of 'Song of the South' in America are stereotypical and offensive toward black people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985619#post985619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This afternoon itself in a facebook group, somebody published a picture, a cartoon, about a man withing a church shooting a priest whose altar boy was down on his kness to do... you can't imagine the quanty of messages hostile againt Catholic religion I can find. Once when Benedictin XVI was chosen Pope, the satirical magazine &quot;el Jueves&quot; (the Thursday, like the French Charlie Hebbo or the American MAD) showed it wearing a nazi uniform, and talking about a beer like better than wine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The criticism the Catholic Church receives regarding child molestation is entirely justified, given the facts uncovered and the steps they took to protect those individuals. I'm not advocating for priests being shot, or that every priest is a pedophile, but if you don't want to be conflated with the phenomena maybe don't hide and protect those individuals in your organization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985619#post985619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I want to enjoy fiction, the last wish is to find more messages about religious fanaticism. Why not talking about revolucionary fanaticism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Revolutionary fanaticism isn't something people deal with on a regular basis today. That makes it less identifiable to a wide audience. Most everyone has some experience with religious fanatics and the harm that they do. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985619#post985619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* This is a subliminal message. The next time you see a episode of the telecomedy &quot;the Big Bang Theory&quot;, a picture of a character or only a mention, then your brain will rememeber the name ofr George Lemaitre, priest and the scientific father of the famous teory of the big bang (but the name he used was &quot;cosmic egg&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>This statement is implying that atheists think religious people can't think, which is a pretty gross generalization. Most Atheists 'are' aware that a Priest came up with that theory. In my experience, it's more often protestant Christians who aren't aware that the theory was proposed by a priest. There was no God in Lemaitre's cosmology, no supernatural being to light the fuse that set off the Big Bang. It was just logical theorizing based on careful observations, i.e. good science. Lemaitre is proof that even devoutly religious people can do good science if they don't allow their religious beliefs to trump their intellectual integrity. <br /> <br /> And there's the rub, a religious person must put aside their beliefs in order to carry out 'good science', whereas an atheist does not have a religion to interfere with their intellectual integrity. There are plenty of other issues that might tarnish an Atheists abilities, Absolutism and Statism were already mentioned above, but a religious person can <i>also</i> fall prey to these phenomena. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985619#post985619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* &quot;The more I learn the people, better I like my dog&quot; Mark Twain. &quot;the more I read about Westeros and characters from Games of Thrones, better I love Christianism. (Me).</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize that most of the people in Westeros aren't actually Atheists, right? Tywin and his children are at best Agnostic, with Tyrion being a hard ball atheist and also one of the most redeeming personalities in the series. The rest of the story is people irrationally doing things based on their superstitions and beliefs, of which the High Sparrow and his flock are perhaps the most notable. George R.R. Martin has very little positive to say about theists over atheists, even when there is evidence that their gods might be real or have some power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:58:21-07:00","id":985654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985618#post985618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Luis does have a point about anti-Christian or anti-Catholic elements within the geeky subculture. Other elements within society too, like entertainment and academia. Then again, within the wider culture, it's different, at least in the USA. We couldn't, for example, have an openly atheist president. Even though both of our two main candidates probably are just atheists paying lip service to Christianity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of ties into why there's so much anti-Christian/-Catholic content in geek stuff: In the US of A we only relatively recently managed to get intense censorship law out of our films (Hays Code: 1922-1945) wherein you couldn't negatively portray Christian faith leaders. These days thanks to the rise of the Religious Right a lot of non-Christians also face extra social difficulties, and it can feel like people are constantly assaulting gaming and nerd culture that are associated with that movement.<br /> <br /> In other words, a lot of nerdy stuff comes out of the USA, and we're still in the throes of Christian...I don't want to use the phrase domination, but certainly influence. They're not at the height of their power politically or socially, but a lot of us see the Bible being carried hand in hand with regressive social policies, restrictive gender roles, or just assholes judging and yelling at us.<br /> <br /> So naturally a lot of us can draw from and relate to oppression married to religious justification. As a progressive liberal with entirely too many questions about his own sexuality who grew up in the American South I'm not a fan of any sort of emotionally-driven organization. But that's the issue, not the faith or the religion behind those organizations: systems can be taken advantage of.<br /> <br /> Combine a massive, organized, hierarchical system with social and political power with enough ties to real-world issues that audiences can relate to, then in fantasy or supernatural settings associations with grand history and magical realms and a <i>fantastic </i>architect and costume designer and you have a very attractive antagonist faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:03:49-07:00","id":985660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985591#post985591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's bad for vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to swallow as anything but an enemy sect if you're a Christian, I think. I'm not, but again, the whole reason I'm in this thread in the first place is because I like to be kind to the conservative or christian gamers who come to my table.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of wordcount dedicated to their misdeeds and monstrosity and heresy. Less wordcount devoted to the expectation of good works and faith in God as your way to Salvation. It's there though, if you read. Even with vampires being Damned, there is a way out: Survive long enough to be there for Revelations to unfold. In the end you, a wretched sinner unworthy before Him, will be judged alongside all the other wretched sinners and, if found worthy, shall be Forgiven and enter into the kingdom of Heaven, as reward for bearing a dark burden that is almost unbearable. And that is stuff that she found appealing. So, she held her nose, leapt into the Sanctum, and has loved the experience precisely because of my active attempts to not vilify Christianity, even though the LeS as an institution is very easily vilified.<br /> <br /> Basically, as a Christian she saw LeS as a thing that needed to be reformed, and styled herself an undead Martin Luther. Hella cool, and in the end she might even be the very first person ever, in any of my games, to be worthy of Heaven in the end. But until then, it's a long, hard road. Until the Time of Tribulation comes, she knows that should she perish, Hell awaits her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":". 10-11-2016, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:14:56-07:00","id":985667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985619#post985619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, I don't want more subtext messages about &quot;the world would be better without religions&quot;. I don't want more characters like the villain from the last Tarzan's movie (with a Christian rosary to strangle) or factions like the &quot;church&quot; from the &quot;golden compass&quot; (why do you think there was a boycot againt the movie?). Can you believe it? I have readen &quot;God&quot; was forbidden in the script of the Disney movie &quot;Frozen&quot;, or some parts from the books &quot;the famous five&quot; by Enid Blyton has been censured/changed because it was about... the main characters went to church in Sunday! A children book &quot;my grandfather is a pirate&quot; by Jan L\u00f6\u00f6f in 1966 now is policitally incorrect because there are Muslims characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every instance I've heard of &quot;The Famous Five&quot; being banned had to do with its racist context (in terms of Roma, Jews, and people of color). The argument behind banning &quot;The Golden Compass&quot; was actually because of the implication that it was <i>anti-</i>Christian. And I'd say that Disney's approach to films aren't anti-religious so much as they're religion-neutral. Not promoting a specific god isn't the same as promoting the absence of gods. I'm not especially familiar with &quot;My Grandfather Was a Pirate&quot;, but my understanding is that it was removed less for portraying Muslims and more for portraying a racist version of Middle Easterners. As for Tarzan, while the perception seems sensationalist, casting church members in villainous roles makes some degree of sense. After all, racial and religious superiority, under pretext of missionary work, was one of the fundamental means by which King Leopold managed to conquer and enslave Congo. It's a dark and intrinsic aspect of that history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985619#post985619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This afternoon itself in a facebook group, somebody published a picture, a cartoon, about a man withing a church shooting a priest whose altar boy was down on his kness to do... you can't imagine the quanty of messages hostile againt Catholic religion I can find. Once when Benedictin XVI was chosen Pope, the satirical magazine &quot;el Jueves&quot; (the Thursday, like the French Charlie Hebbo or the American MAD) showed it wearing a nazi uniform, and talking about a beer like better than wine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you suggesting we censor speech? I don't endorse murdering anyone, but the Catholic church does have a troubling issue of covering up the sins of their most abhorrent members, and it's something that needs to be discussed. I'm from the American South, and my life and social media is plastered with racist, misogynistic rhetoric. I don't agree with it a single inch, but that doesn't mean I don't think they should have the right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985619#post985619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I want to enjoy fiction, the last wish is to find more messages about religious fanaticism. Why not talking about revolucionary fanaticism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Americans (which is where the majority of pop culture is targeted) haven't directly experienced revolutionary fanaticism, but plenty have stories of religious fanatics. It might not be fair, but it is more relatable.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. I think popular media too easily characterizes Christians as either buffoons or crazies. It too often characterizes Muslims as fanatic radicals. But that goes both ways. I remember the anti-Dungeons and Dragons Satanism scare of the 90s. I remember the banning of Harry Potter and the Tipper Gore crusade against &quot;inappropriate&quot; music. I can still hear One Million Moms screaming about our sinful media.<br /> <br /> Censorship isn't appropriate. It wasn't appropriate when the government levied obscenity charges against Jello Biafra or William S. Burroughs. It wasn't appropriate when industry-wide labeling protocol tried to neuter the comic book or record industries. But a company deciding they want to change the content or something to accommodate their audience isn't the same thing.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see a more balanced promotion of faith in popular media. But let's be honest. Sensationalism sells, and there's plenty of sensationalism to go around. &quot;Muslim&quot; terrorists are all over our TVs, even though they don't represent the majority of that faith, because groups like Al Qaeda and ISIS have sensationalized radical Islam. &quot;Christian&quot; fanatics are all over our TVs, even though they don't represent the majority of that faith, because groups like the Westboro Baptist Church and One Million Moms are happy to make fools of themselves. I'm not aware of any atheist groups or factions that provide fodder that juicy on such a regular basis.<br /> <br /> I do think there's a reason why the knee jerk reaction to Christianity is so prevalent in American culture though. I can only speak for myself, but as someone who grew up in the South, Baptism reigned supreme (It still does); and most of the geeky stuff that pop culture geeks loved, from witches and wizards to vampires and werewolves, was seen as deviant at best and outright sinful at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-11-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:17:53-07:00","id":985672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985660#post985660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's hard to swallow as anything but an enemy sect if you're a Christian, I think. I'm not, but again, the whole reason I'm in this thread in the first place is because I like to be kind to the conservative or christian gamers who come to my table.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of wordcount dedicated to their misdeeds and monstrosity and heresy. Less wordcount devoted to the expectation of good works and faith in God as your way to Salvation. It's there though, if you read. Even with vampires being Damned, there is a way out: Survive long enough to be there for Revelations to unfold. In the end you, a wretched sinner unworthy before Him, will be judged alongside all the other wretched sinners and, if found worthy, shall be Forgiven and enter into the kingdom of Heaven, as reward for bearing a dark burden that is almost unbearable. And that is stuff that she found appealing. So, she held her nose, leapt into the Sanctum, and has loved the experience precisely because of my active attempts to not vilify Christianity, even though the LeS as an institution is very easily vilified.<br /> <br /> Basically, as a Christian she saw LeS as a thing that needed to be reformed, and styled herself an undead Martin Luther. Hella cool, and in the end she might even be the very first person ever, in any of my games, to be worthy of Heaven in the end. But until then, it's a long, hard road. Until the Time of Tribulation comes, she knows that should she perish, Hell awaits her.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right. They aren't pretty, but I think Requiem was equal opportunity with its villains. The Sanctum is a twisted reflection of the Church, the Circle is a twisted reflection of paganism, the Ordo Dracul is a twisted reflection of scientific rationalism, and the Carthians are a twisted reflection of revolutionary political movements.<br /> <br /> And I like that. I'm glad you're trying to represent faith in a positive light. As an agnostic (even playing with a group that's exclusively agnostic/atheist), I do the same. A Cuban-American Catholic priest associated with the Malleus Malificarum is one of the few decent people in my Hunter Miami game, and the Cuban persecution of religion is going to be a recurring background element in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-11-2016, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:48:18-07:00","id":985737,"title":"","content":"I'm not Christian myself, but my gaming group includes a Christian linguist who literally squee'd with joy when I showed her Paternoster.<br /> <br /> Then she went and translated the entire Paternoster creed into latin and made an awesome battle priest who recited the creed as she cast her spells.<br /> <br /> She really likes Paternoster (and so do I for that sake).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:10:02-07:00","id":985752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985737#post985737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not Christian myself, but my gaming group includes a Christian linguist who literally squee'd with joy when I showed her Paternoster.<br /> <br /> Then she went and translated the entire Paternoster creed into latin and made an awesome battle priest who recited the creed as she cast her spells.<br /> <br /> She really likes Paternoster (and so do I for that sake).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now I'm curious. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What's the Paternoster?<br /> <br /> Does that translate as something like Night Father?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:12:29-07:00","id":985753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985752#post985752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Now I'm curious. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What's the Paternoster?<br /> <br /> Does that translate as something like Night Father?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's a Seer of the Throne Ministry, specifically the one that reveres The Father, the Exarch of Prime.<br /> <br /> Edit: here's a good link for you - <a href=\"http://kingofthehill.wikidot.com/paternoster\" target=\"_blank\">http://kingofthehill.wikidot.com/paternoster</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:19:21-07:00","id":985758,"title":"","content":"&quot;Pater noster&quot; means, &quot;our father,&quot; and is most well known for being the Latin opening to the Lord's Prayer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:22:13-07:00","id":985761,"title":"","content":"You can be opposed to censorship and support artistic freedom and still get irritated (and complain) when it seems like all of the entertainment media you're exposed to is bigoted against people like yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:30:28-07:00","id":985769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985758#post985758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Pater noster&quot; means, &quot;our father,&quot; and is most well known for being the Latin opening to the Lord's Prayer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume they meant the Ministry, at least, because they say she translated it into Latin. If it were the Lord's Prayer she could simply have looked it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:50:58-07:00","id":985785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985761#post985761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can be opposed to censorship and support artistic freedom and still get irritated (and complain) when it seems like all of the entertainment media you're exposed to is bigoted against people like yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T21:35:48-07:00","id":985938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985761#post985761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can be opposed to censorship and support artistic freedom and still get irritated (and complain) when it seems like all of the entertainment media you're exposed to is bigoted against people like yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. Just ask anyone black, female, homosexual, asian, muslim, hindi, atheist, etc, etc, etc.........","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T01:29:28-07:00","id":985998,"title":"","content":"How to explain it better? English isn't my naive languange. Let's imagine you end a hard work day, but you discover your car has been destroyed by vandals. A cop has been seing all, but he only fines you because it was badly parked, and you talk about that, you are answered: &quot;Don't complain, your great-grandfather was a highwayman). That is like I feel when I read about Christians suffering persecution and injustices in all world, and after I find fiction with the same anti-Christians predjudices. Don't talk about crusders, but let's talk about a backery was reported because they are Christians and didn't want make a wedding cake for a gay couple. Are you quiet when the censorships is to stop homophobia or islamophobia?<br /> <br /> I make remember you again from here the news I read are different. What do you know about the &quot;pussy riot&quot; in Madrid, the topless church protest by Rita Maestre, council of the group &quot;Ahora Madrid&quot;? or radical feminists trying assault a Catholic cathedral in Argentina. Do you know nothing about the destruction by vandalic acts by radical pro-abortion activist in the cathedral of Santiago de Chile in July 25th 2013? and am I who has to feel guilty about the facts from the past? Can you suposse how I feel when after I read &quot;preacher&quot; teleserie will be renewed for a new season? <br /> <br /> I invite, or I challenge you, to read news from fides.org, to notice about the real situation of Christians in another places of the world. What do you know about the patriotic church, created and controlled by Chinese dictatorship, the only Christian faith allowed in China? or the kidnapping of Christians Copt girls in Egypt to be forced to corvent to islam and marry Muslim men. In the current age, the persecutions againts Christiany is causing more victims than in the Roman empire.<br /> <br /> Maybe in your country Christian faith is still respected, but here we live a lot of anti-Christian feeling in the media. Madonna's &quot;Like a virgin&quot; videoclip is Sesame Street next to some things I have seen, for example blaspheme photographies from a expositure in Spain(paid with public money, with our taxes!!!). I have seen with my own eyes some nasty pictures in the news about that. That wasn't freedom speech, but anti-Christian hate. <br /> <br /> * The pasternoster is the lord's prayer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T03:34:02-07:00","id":986026,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11152\" data-vbnamecard=\"11152\">Luis Carlos</a><br /> <br /> Maybe it's time to make a separate thread about this? Raising awareness about the persecution of people of faith (or a single faith) isn't really a conservation about being conservative, or about conservative ideas. Having a debate about whether or not Western cultural output has grown anti-Christian instead of acceptably Christian critical is also not really a discussion about conservatism.<br /> <br /> Whether you choose to agree with my suggestion or not, it might help further conversation if you demonstrate a bit more perspective about all this. Maybe it is the language barrier, or just a matter of passion, but it is growing increasingly more difficult to tell if you have any idea of how entitled and condescending it is for a member of the world's largest and most powerful religion to speak as if all the sins done in the name of that religion are things of the past, and all the negative feelings towards Christianity are undeserved hate-mongering without any greater context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T04:10:52-07:00","id":986036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985998#post985998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or radical feminists trying assault a Catholic cathedral in Argentina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me stop you right there buddy, thats wasnt &quot;christian prosecution&quot;. That was 5 to 10 radical feminist thinking that just because they have a noble goal &quot;legalized abortion&quot; they had justification to behave like assholes.<br /> <br /> Only the most leftist/militant feminist glorified said act. The society at large condemn the whole protest for the actions of 5 to 10 women who think if they burn a church the pope will say yes to abortion. Even their group (the one organizing the protest) condemn their actions. The police even shoot rubber bullets at them, you can claim legal indifference.<br /> <br /> So no, there isnt a christian prosecution in Argentina, nor even christian hate mongering. We have indifference toward christianity. Demographically speaking most people answer to be christians when asked about religion on census but that because most teenagers take the first communion to get gifts and money but 90% of them dont practice the religion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=985998#post985998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for example blaspheme photographies from a expositure in Spain(paid with public money, with our taxes!!!). I have seen with my own eyes some nasty pictures in the news about that. That wasn't freedom speech, but anti-Christian hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you elaborate on this? You mean photographies that your religion finds blasphemous? Or hate speech in the form of photographs? There is a big difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T04:28:02-07:00","id":986042,"title":"","content":"The first. I know Luis Carlos from before, he's always been like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T04:47:01-07:00","id":986049,"title":"","content":"Sorry. (I am too mulish, am I not?) I want to explain it the reason. Today it's October 12th, the Hispanity day, the national Spanish day, like July 4th for Northamerican. And in the last days I suffer, we are sufffering here, a revival of the black legend about American coquest by Spanishs (here the liberals are strongly hispanophobic, they despise our History). I don't refer about something wrote in an almost unkown blog, but some annoying gestures and comments by some Spanish liberal politicians. How would you feel if in the weeks before the Thanksgiving Day medias and &quot;intellectuals&quot;