bcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987316#post987316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be much easier if you guys could just confess you hate Christianity and Christians. No moderator is going to suspended or ban you for that. Just don't point out any peccadillo of religious &quot;minorities&quot;, ever, haha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Advanced and in-depth knowledge of sociology and history does not equate to hating any single religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T10:36:09-07:00","id":987327,"title":"","content":"You should learn about infanticide and child abandonment in the ancient Rome and Greece. This caused a serious demographic crysis. The jew community was about to be the main minority in the Roman Empire until the arrive of Christianity.<br /> <br /> I am not kidding when I say Westeros, the world of the books of &quot;games of thrones&quot;, the &quot;song of fire and ice &quot; saga are a good example of how could be the western civilitation without merciful Christian teachings. And Christianity allowed the scientific mindset, because now the Nature wasn't explained with fays and genies, but rules could be discovered by reason and investigation. There were inventions and discoveries in another civilitations, but only Christianity made possible the empirism, rationalism and humanism. And Christiany gave dignity to all citizens, men and women, workers and nobles. Before the Jesus' parable about the poor Lazarus and rich Epulon nobody questioned about somebody had got so much and other were so poor. Western civilitation was the first to end the slavery. <br /> <br /> Sorry, now I leave you because I have to pay Arya Stark, I had asked her to kill some Melissandre's followers who were asking me about some fugitive R'hllor temple (sacred?) prostitutes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 10-14-2016, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:01:17-07:00","id":987359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=986468#post986468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we're seeing a lot of this in the present time. The sad puppies think queer individuals, women, and people of color having representation in fantasy/sci-fi indicates persecution against white men. Folks scream about Black Lives Matter being a group promoting racist terrorist ideals. Christians think just because criticism of the church is now acceptable in media that they're being persecuted.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it's easy for Christians to feel persecuted when it seems more or less socially acceptable to attack the church seemingly <i>ad infinitum</i><i>, </i>yet any efforts made to critique, say, Islam, are generally met with condemnation and jeers of &quot;Islamophobia! Bigotry!&quot;<br /> <br /> People have died for criticising - or mocking, as the case may be - Islam. And while there's frequently an initial rallying cry of condemnation for the aggressors and sympathy for the attacked, there is always a tinny chorus of simpering voices - often <i>liberal</i> voices - that wheedle out &quot;well, you know, <i>you really shouldn't have said that</i><i>...&quot; </i>as if murder is somehow a measured and acceptable response to comedy.<br /> <br /> In an ideal world, it would be acceptable for anybody to criticise any religion - but in the world we live in, that's far from the case.<br /> <br /> While I don't particularly think that Christians are being persecuted and that Christianity as a whole is under attack, I can sympathise with adherents of the faith that feel they're being treated unfairly in certain regards - there <i>are </i>double standards in these sorts of matters, and a great deal of people consistently refuse to admit that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=986468#post986468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just because other voices are granted credence in a public space doesn't mean that your voice is being silenced. Treating women and people of color more fairly doesn't mean that white men aren't being treated fairly. It just means they have to compete on a more level playing ground. So many groups have spent decades, even centuries, with an uneven advantage, and they think that advantage being chipped away is equivalent to persecution.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, given that these people haven't actually been <i>alive</i> for centuries, it's somewhat difficult for me to see how these people would even be able to tell that their advantages are being &quot;chipped away&quot;, as you say. This isn't a collective of people that's watching nervously at a morass of social advantages slowly being taken away from them, it's a bunch of folks who are understandably a bit concerned about the fact that huge swathes of people are blaming them for all kinds of stuff that, frankly, they had nothing to do with and never countenanced in the first place.<br /> <br /> The people I've spoken to about this aren't mad that their &quot;white privilege&quot; doesn't exist anymore - they're pissed off because when they try to discuss their concerns about the changing face of society (whether those concerns happen to be legitimate or not), they're met with cries of &quot;stop whitesplaining to us!&quot; and insinuations that their opinions are somehow worth less than those of people who happen to belong to an ethnic or sexual minority, by virtue of those people belonging to a minority.<br /> <br /> The mere fact that racial slurs - and yes, &quot;whitesplain&quot; <i>is</i> a racial slur, intended to cast aside someone's opinions on the basis of race - like that have entered the mainstream with nary a word of protest from a lot of people is, frankly, a bit worrying.<br /> <br /> People have committed horrible violence in the name of Black Lives Matter. Whether you think the organisation's core goals are noble or not, justified or not, this is pretty much undeniably true. If you want to dismiss people who are afraid they might wind up being the victim of BLM-inspired violence as &quot;idiots&quot; and &quot;perhaps smart people just being bigoted/stupid&quot; then, well, fine.<br /> <br /> To me, though, that seems like a fairly dismissive and callous response for a more liberal sort - aren't you guys supposed to be the nice ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","name":"Seviphas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:09:23-07:00","id":987362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987327#post987327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should learn about infanticide and child abandonment in the ancient Rome and Greece. This caused a serious demographic crysis. The jew community was about to be the main minority in the Roman Empire until the arrive of Christianity.<br /> <br /> I am not kidding when I say Westeros, the world of the books of &amp;quot;games of thrones&amp;quot;, the &amp;quot;song of fire and ice &amp;quot; saga are a good example of how could be the western civilitation without merciful Christian teachings. And Christianity allowed the scientific mindset, because now the Nature wasn't explained with fays and genies, but rules could be discovered by reason and investigation. There were inventions and discoveries in another civilitations, but only Christianity made possible the empirism, rationalism and humanism. And Christiany gave dignity to all citizens, men and women, workers and nobles. Before the Jesus' parable about the poor Lazarus and rich Epulon nobody questioned about somebody had got so much and other were so poor. Western civilitation was the first to end the slavery. <br /> <br /> Sorry, now I leave you because I have to pay Arya Stark, I had asked her to kill some Melissandre's followers who were asking me about some fugitive R'hllor temple (sacred?) prostitutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just had to toss in a line about the Jews, didn't you? You can at least pretend to hide the antisemitism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:32:50-07:00","id":987378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987359#post987359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it's easy for Christians to feel persecuted when it seems more or less socially acceptable to attack the church seemingly <i>ad infinitum</i><i>, </i>yet any efforts made to critique, say, Islam, are generally met with condemnation and jeers of &quot;Islamophobia! Bigotry!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that there's a dangerous and discernible hostility towards the rights of Muslims in America and Europe. We have bans and proposals limiting people's ability to wear the clothing or eat according to the dietary restrictions of their faith. America has a Presidential candidate who's outright suggested banning Muslims and a sitting president who faced a loud controversy over the suggestion that he might be a &quot;secret&quot; Muslim. The closest I can find to &quot;persecution&quot; on the part of Christians (and even then, only the more radical elements of Christianity) are the suggestion that they should bake cakes for gay couples or hey maybe they shouldn't teach creationism in schools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987359#post987359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People have died for criticising - or mocking, as the case may be - Islam. And while there's frequently an initial rallying cry of condemnation for the aggressors and sympathy for the attacked, there is always a tinny chorus of simpering voices - often <i>liberal</i> voices - that wheedle out &quot;well, you know, <i>you really shouldn't have said that</i><i>...&quot; </i>as if murder is somehow a measured and acceptable response to comedy.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's a tinny chorus of simpering voices that say maybe women shouldn't vote or maybe rape isn't bad. Tinny simpering voices that are loudly broadcast on mainstream media. I agree that murder is a measured and acceptable response to comedy, and I suspect that the majority of the world agrees with me. I don't blame Christianity for the bombing of abortion clinics or assaults on LGBQT or marginalized racial or religious minorities. I don't blame Judaism for the acts of war perpetrated by Israel. I don't blame Islam for bombings and beheadings executed by radicals. I blame fanatics who exploit that ideology for their own hateful agendas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987359#post987359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In an ideal world, it would be acceptable for anybody to criticise any religion - but in the world we live in, that's far from the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are loud and aggressive voices criticizing Islam throughout the world, loud enough that they're a major voice in the sort of policy our governments adopt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987359#post987359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't particularly think that Christians are being persecuted and that Christianity as a whole is under attack, I can sympathise with adherents of the faith that feel they're being treated unfairly in certain regards - there <i>are </i>double standards in these sorts of matters, and a great deal of people consistently refuse to admit that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still haven't seen what these double standards are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987359#post987359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, given that these people haven't actually been <i>alive</i> for centuries, it's somewhat difficult for me to see how these people would even be able to tell that their advantages are being &quot;chipped away&quot;, as you say. This isn't a collective of people that's watching nervously at a morass of social advantages slowly being taken away from them, it's a bunch of folks who are understandably a bit concerned about the fact that huge swathes of people are blaming them for all kinds of stuff that, frankly, they had nothing to do with and never countenanced in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Christianity is still a disproportionate voice throughout the world. Calling out the transgressions of the past isn't the same as blaming people in the present for it. It's just recognition of the past in the hope that it won't be repeated in the future. When I hear people criticizing Christian (again fringe) values, it's usually about abuse (still neglected) in the Catholic Church, denial of health care for women on religious grounds, and outright homophobia and transphobia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987359#post987359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The people I've spoken to about this aren't mad that their &quot;white privilege&quot; doesn't exist anymore - they're pissed off because when they try to discuss their concerns about the changing face of society (whether those concerns happen to be legitimate or not), they're met with cries of &quot;stop whitesplaining to us!&quot; and insinuations that their opinions are somehow worth less than those of people who happen to belong to an ethnic or sexual minority, by virtue of those people belonging to a minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Whitesplaining&quot; isn't about countering someone's opinion because they happen to be white. It's about countering someone's opinion because they're speaking on an opinion they don't know about without taking the effort to learn about that culture's experience. For instance, comparing what it's like to being a Christian in America (sometimes people say something mean about the Catholic Church) vs. what it's like to be a Muslim in America (dealing with profiling, violence, and vandalism on a regular basis).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987359#post987359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mere fact that racial slurs - and yes, &quot;whitesplain&quot; <i>is</i> a racial slur, intended to cast aside someone's opinions on the basis of race - like that have entered the mainstream with nary a word of protest from a lot of people is, frankly, a bit worrying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh please. Maybe we could come up with a nicer term for it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987359#post987359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People have committed horrible violence in the name of Black Lives Matter. Whether you think the organisation's core goals are noble or not, justified or not, this is pretty much undeniably true. If you want to dismiss people who are afraid they might wind up being the victim of BLM-inspired violence as &quot;idiots&quot; and &quot;perhaps smart people just being bigoted/stupid&quot; then, well, fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Son of Sam killed numerous people because a dog told him to. I'm not going to go ranting about the threat of dogs to society. Representatives from Black Lives Matter have repeatedly ad vocally denounced acts of violence, both internally and externally. They've made significant efforts to communicate with people in power and tried to build bridges in the community. They've made their intents clear and apparent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987359#post987359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, though, that seems like a fairly dismissive and callous response for a more liberal sort - aren't you guys supposed to be the nice ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. It's not about being nice.<br /> <br /> But I can say, personally, I try my damnedest to treat everyone with respect. I have Christian friends. I have Christian family. I have friends who are pastors and who used to be pastors but left the church for personal reasons. I have no problem with Christianity whatsoever. When people cross the line and end up denying someone else their basic rights, that's when I get angry. So far the only arguments I've heard for persecution in this thread are &quot;People say mean things about us&quot; or &quot;We're unfairly represented in the media&quot; or &quot;They won't let us be dicks to other people we don't like&quot;. Particularly in the case of Luis Carlos who tinges his perspective with veiled bigotry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-14-2016, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:57:23-07:00","id":987390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=986601#post986601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know what is the tall poppy syndrome? The hate againts who highlight because rivalry or envy (Anytimes the number one isn't the most respected but all opposite). And the hasty generalitation? If there is a rotten apple in the basket it doesn't mean all apples to be rotten. Take care about that type of predjudices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imperialism isn't a just system ruined by a few rotten apples. It's an inherently exploitative system in which some people find justification, typically by infantilizing or dehumanizing the people they're subjecting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=986601#post986601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can be self-critical and admit there were some shameful things happened in the past, but we weren't worse than the rest. We were the first empire who start treat new subjects like true citizens. The enemy propaganda by rival powers have lied or exagerated a lot about our past, and today the black legend is used to distract to cover the actions by others. It's time to say stop to anti-Spanish and anti-Catholic legend. But moreover, I don't want listen anymore about &quot;bad Christians&quot; when the people are silent about the victims by revolutionary groups and communist dictatorships, and persecution and hostility againts Christians in another places of the world. Yes, there is also a persecution in the Western countries, a subtle psychololical harassment. Shouldn't asking freedom for Asia Bibi and the end of anti-blasfemy Pakistani law be more important than talking about Torquemada? If you criticize Spanish inquisition but you keep quiet about Mao's cultural revolution, Ucranian Holodomor, Staling's great purge, the tortures in the chekas, or in the Rumanian prison of Pitesti, then you are a hypocrite. Bit by bit people are starting to be sick about that anti-Christian speech (more annoying when at same time respect for Muslims againts islamophobia is asked). To believe all said againts Spanish History is so stupy and dangerous like to believe all horrible things said againts USA by Russia Today New or HispanTV.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are the only one who's been talking about Torquemada. And no one here is denying the evils of Stalin or Mao.<br /> <br /> So people say mean things in the popular and social media. Sweetheart, that's not persecution. It's life. I'm frequently assaulted with things I find offensive. I have a Presidential candidate who's openly and aggressively racist, misogynistic, and xenophobic. Neo-nazi diatribes are just a click away on my Facebook account. People directly on my Facebook account spit rhetoric I find exploitative, offensive, and directly harmful to progress. Before I was self-employed, I had to deal with people on a regular basis spitting venom about &quot;feminazis&quot;, &quot;trannies&quot;, and &quot;blacks&quot;, bitching about how their rights were being taken away. Even in my more liberal circles, there are people who accept rapists and abusers into their spaces despite their avowed standards. That's life. You can ignore it, or you can fight it. But don't talk to us about persecution. Regardless of your ideology, you're going to face people who don't agree with you, often in the most venomous and violent fashion. That's just the price we pay for living in an open society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-14-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:14:42-07:00","id":987398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987378#post987378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The difference is that there's a dangerous and discernible hostility towards the rights of Muslims in America and Europe. We have bans and proposals limiting people's ability to wear the clothing or eat according to the dietary restrictions of their faith. America has a Presidential candidate who's outright suggested banning Muslims and a sitting president who faced a loud controversy over the suggestion that he might be a &quot;secret&quot; Muslim. The closest I can find to &quot;persecution&quot; on the part of Christians (and even then, only the more radical elements of Christianity) are the suggestion that they should bake cakes for gay couples or hey maybe they shouldn't teach creationism in schools.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's entirely reasonable for society to restrict the ability of people to wear clothing that disguises their features, and honestly, I do find it repugnant that people should be <i>forced</i> to bake somebody a cake if they don't want to.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a shitty thing to do to refuse to make a cake for someone when you're a store that makes cakes, and maybe that's offensive - but frankly, people should have the right not to provide a service to anybody, for any reason, if they're working freely and for themselves. This sort of thing should be dealt with by the free market - by people choosing not to give their money to businesses run by people that offend them - not the Thought Police.<br /> <br /> The fact that some people are hostile to Islam should not exempt Islam itself from criticism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987378#post987378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And there's a tinny chorus of simpering voices that say maybe women shouldn't vote or maybe rape isn't bad. Tinny simpering voices that are loudly broadcast on mainstream media. I agree that murder is a measured and acceptable response to comedy, and I suspect that the majority of the world agrees with me.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to <i>assume </i>that you meant to say &quot;murder <i>isn't </i>a measured and acceptable response to comedy&quot;, here, because if you didn't then our moral compasses are so wildly divergent that any discussion at all is completely futile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987378#post987378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There are loud and agressive voices criticizing Islam throughout the world, loud enough that they're a major voice in the sort of policy our governments adopt.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are plenty of voices just as loud <i>defending </i>Islam, so I'm not sure that your stance really makes a great deal of sense. Obama and Merkel have both come out with fairly supportive statements regarding Islam and Muslims, and those two are pretty damned influential.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987378#post987378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Christianity is still a disproportionate voice throughout the world. Calling out the transgressions of the past isn't the same as blaming people in the present for it. It's just recognition of the past in the hope that it won't be repeated in the future. When I hear people criticizing Christian (again fringe) values, it's usually about abuse (still neglected) in the Catholic Church, denial of health care for women on religious grounds, and outright homophobia and transphobia.</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean, I fundamentally disagree that Christianity's influence is all that disproportionate. Not much more to say on that front, as I imagine our perspectives are irreconcilable.<br /> <br /> Most people in positions of power just give lip service to Christianity or God or whatever and then just run merrily along in their avaricious pursuit of wealth and power, so I suppose I have difficulty seeing Christianity as a real cultural or political force these days. Maybe you couldn't really run for President of the United States without at least <i>pretending </i>to be Christian, sure, but show me anyone who's sat in the White House in the last century who did anything more than give the bare minimum lip service to the teachings of Christ to fool the masses, and... well, I'll eat my hat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987378#post987378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Whitesplaining&quot; isn't about countering someone's opinion because they happen to be white. It's about countering someone's opinion because they're speaking on an opinion they don't know about without taking the effort to learn about that culture's experience.</div> </div> </div> </div> Then why is it <i>white</i>splaining? Are you suggesting that only white people are capable of cultural ignorance? And you don't think that line of thinking is even a <i>little </i>racist? Casual, everyday contempt is how it starts, man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987378#post987378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh please.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think your callous disregard for those who don't fit into your preconceived notions of oppressed groups speaks for itself here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987378#post987378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nope. It's not about being nice.</div> </div> </div> </div> So you don't feel that compassion is a fundamental liberal virtue?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987378#post987378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But I can say, personally, I try my damnedest to treat everyone with respect. I have Christian friends. I have Christian family. I have friends who are pastors and who used to be pastors but left the church for personal reasons. I have no problem with Christianity whatsoever. When people cross the line and end up denying someone else their basic rights, that's when I get angry. So far the only arguments I've heard for persecution in this thread are &quot;People say mean things about us&quot; or &quot;We're unfairly represented in the media&quot; or &quot;They won't let us be dicks to other people we don't like&quot;. Particularly in the case of Luis Carlos who tinges his perspective with veiled bigotry.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have nothing much to say in response to this; I don't personally feel that Christianity is under attack in society myself, and I'm not religious so I have no particular dog in this fight. <br /> <br /> All I'm really saying here is that I can sympathise with and understand why Christians might feel that they're being unfairly treated when any criticism of Islam is so frequently met with virulent hostility.<br /> <br /> I will say, though, that you've claimed to try very hard to treat everybody respectfully in the same post where you've tried to justify the use of language that implicitly insults an entire race. Is that respectful behaviour in your book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","name":"Seviphas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:21:44-07:00","id":987401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987398#post987398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's entirely reasonable for society to restrict the ability of people to wear clothing that disguises their features, and honestly, I do find it repugnant that people should be <i>forced</i> to bake somebody a cake if they don't want to.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a shitty thing to do to refuse to make a cake for someone when you're a store that makes cakes, and maybe that's offensive - but frankly, people should have the right not to provide a service to anybody, for any reason, if they're working freely and for themselves. This sort of thing should be dealt with by the free market - by people choosing not to give their money to businesses run by people that offend them - not the Thought Police.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you're getting at, but you honestly think this is right?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/CQKoqwoUkAApwtZ.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-14-2016, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:32:41-07:00","id":987409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987401#post987401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand what you're getting at, but you honestly think this is right?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/CQKoqwoUkAApwtZ.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly? No, I don't.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I'll admit that it's a tricky issue - where does one person's right to refuse to provide their labour infringe upon somebody else's right to walk down the street and not feel like a violently despised outcast in their own hometown? I'm not going to pretend that I have the answer to that question, and even if I were to sit down and think about it for a while I'm not sure I'd come to any kind of satisfactory conclusion.<br /> <br /> All I will say is that I think it's a shitty thing to do to refuse to make people a cake to help them celebrate their love, even though I think they had the right to do it. A favourite quote of mine comes to mind, here: &quot;To have a right to do a thing <i>is not at all the same as to be right in doing it</i>.<i>&quot; </i>Ultimately, you can't <i>make</i> someone support you - you can only do the best you can to persuade them, and hope they'll see the light on their own.<br /> <br /> I'll also say that a sign like that - &quot;No dogs, negros, mexicans&quot; - well, let's just say that anyone who tried to hang a sign like that was probably not so great a human being. And I don't think anyone has the right to make a black person or a Mexican living amongst them feel like an unwanted stranger in his own home on the grounds of the colour of their skin or the nation of their ancestry. So, yeah, I'd be in favour of tearing that sign down and throwing stuff at anyone who tried to put it back up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","name":"Seviphas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:40:49-07:00","id":987415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987398#post987398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's entirely reasonable for society to restrict the ability of people to wear clothing that disguises their features, and honestly, I do find it repugnant that people should be <i>forced</i> to bake somebody a cake if they don't want to.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a shitty thing to do to refuse to make a cake for someone when you're a store that makes cakes, and maybe that's offensive - but frankly, people should have the right not to provide a service to anybody, for any reason, if they're working freely and for themselves. This sort of thing should be dealt with by the free market - by people choosing not to give their money to businesses run by people that offend them - not the Thought Police.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally agree with you there, and I definitely think it's a debatable point. Should a restaurant be able to not serve people of color of LQBT people? Should a bakery be able to deny them a wedding cake because they disagree with interracial or gay marriage? I may find it deplorable, but I'm generally inclined to say yes. However, there's a question of whether or not this denies them the right to generally sit in a restaurant or have a wedding. If the intolerance of a city or town means those resources aren't available to them, then, well, fuck those business owners, frankly. I'm not entirely sure where we draw the line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987398#post987398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that some people are hostile to Islam should not exempt Islam itself from criticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. It shouldn't, and there's plenty of examples of criticism in the media. But it doesn't mean those criticizing Islam aren't subjected to criticism from others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987398#post987398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to <i>assume </i>that you meant to say &quot;murder <i>isn't </i>a measured and acceptable response to comedy&quot;, here, because if you didn't then our moral compasses are so wildly divergent that any discussion at all is completely futile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Sorry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Avowed pacifist here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987398#post987398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are plenty of voices just as loud <i>defending </i>Islam, so I'm not sure that your stance really makes a great deal of sense. Obama and Merkel have both come out with fairly supportive statements regarding Islam and Muslims, and those two are pretty damned influential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because one of those sides is actively and tangibly trying to deny people their rights. That doesn't mean that we shouldn't allow them voices. But it does mean we should fight their bigotry adamantly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987398#post987398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I fundamentally disagree that Christianity's influence is all that disproportionate. Not much more to say on that front, as I imagine our perspectives are irreconcilable.</div> </div> </div> </div>noted<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987398#post987398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people in positions of power just give lip service to Christianity or God or whatever and then just run merrily along in their avaricious pursuit of wealth and power, so I suppose I have difficulty seeing Christianity as a real cultural or political force these days. Maybe you couldn't really run for President of the United States without at least <i>pretending </i>to be Christian, sure, but show me anyone who's sat in the White House in the last century who did anything more than give the bare minimum lip service to the teachings of Christ to fool the masses, and... well, I'll eat my hat.</div> </div> </div> </div>When being Jewish or Muslim significantly hinders your odds of that position, I'd say Christianity is represented fairly disproportionately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987398#post987398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why is it <i>white</i>splaining? Are you suggesting that only white people are capable of cultural ignorance? And you don't think that line of thinking is even a <i>little </i>racist? Casual, everyday contempt is how it starts, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a problematic term (and I'll get to that below), but the terms &quot;whitesplaining&quot; and &quot;mansplaining&quot; are typically used because it speaks to the specific and nuanced methods of rhetoric by which white people and men shut down minorities and women.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987398#post987398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your callous disregard for those who don't fit into your preconceived notions of oppressed groups speaks for itself here.</div> </div> </div> </div>My fellow white people rank very, <i>very</i> low on my list of priorities. It's not anywhere in the triage queue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987398#post987398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you don't feel that compassion is a fundamental liberal virtue?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like compassion is a fundamental human virtue. I try hard to be compassionate, and I think I generally succeed. But being compassionate doesn't mean treating everyone's grievance with equivalent weight. White people need to get in line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987398#post987398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have nothing much to say in response to this; I don't personally feel that Christianity is under attack in society myself, and I'm not religious so I have no particular dog in this fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987398#post987398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say, though, that you've claimed to try very hard to treat everybody respectfully in the same post where you've tried to justify the use of language that implicitly insults an entire race. Is that respectful behaviour in your book?</div> </div> </div> </div>And here it is. &quot;Mansplaining&quot; and &quot;Whitesplaining&quot; are terms I have some problem with, but again, they don't rank very highly on the list.<br /> <br /> These aren't terms that are meant to insult an entire race or an entire gender. Rather, they speak to racial and gender terms specifically because of existing conditions that make them specific to those racial and gender dynamics. As someone with a black girlfriend and friends who span the racial divide, it's something I've seen firsthand. That's not to demean <i>all</i> white people or <i>all </i>mean, but it is to say that these actions are specific to existing conditions. &quot;Whitesplaining&quot; isn't about the virtue or genetic worth of a white person. It's about privilege and experience, and usually it's unintentional. Ditto &quot;mansplaining&quot;. It's a peculiar social tic that comes implicitly from being raised as a privileged majority in a society that's conditioned and dehumanized the o the other. It's something I've done and something I try to avoid, and it doesn't make you a bad person.<br /> <br /> That said, I understand that it can be worrying. There was a common sentiment where I grew up that &quot;Not all black people are n*****s, but all n*****s are black&quot;, and I can see the parallel. But it's not troubling enough for me to see it as a clear and present concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:43:24-07:00","id":987417,"title":"","content":"Oh boy.....where do i start with this. And as i know english is not your first language im gonna do it also in spanish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987195#post987195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, I can detect lots of diferents fallacies, amon them the one of the straw man. Don't try to be sarcastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you point out the fallacies/straw man arguments i dont understand to whom you are reffering to here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987195#post987195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* A day later and still reading in facebooks posts about genocide in America by Spanish conquers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, just maybe columbus day is not the best day to find &quot;how great Spain was&quot; on the social network. Just saying.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Quizas....solo quizas el dia de colon no es el mejor dia del a\u00f1o para encontrar post en facebook sobre lo linda que fue la historia de espa\u00f1a. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987195#post987195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* About &quot;black lives matter&quot;, do allow me this speech:. Let's imagine in Germany a Spanish inmigrant is killed by cop, and then Spanish community starts a wage of riots.. what the rest of Europe would think about the Spanishs?</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know that it wasnt &quot;just one inmigrant/african american&quot; right? This wasnt a everything was dandy and then 1 cop killed a african american person and this just exploded from thin air. This was a systematic issue that has been happening since 70s. Even after social movement after social movement is still happening.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Vos sabes que esto de no fue &quot;solo un inmigrante/afroamericano&quot;, no? No es que todo estaba bien y de repente a un policia se le ocurrio matar a un afroamericano y todo exploto de la nada. Esto es un problem sistematico de hacer A\u00d1OS. Exceso de brutalidad policiaca es algo que viene pasando en estados unidos a las minorias desde hacer mucho mucho tiempo.</div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987195#post987195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martin Luther King's dream wasn't only freedom, dignity and respect for black community, it was also a dream of reconciliation and mutual trust, without bad feelings, men from every races going together to the same church each Sunday. Martin Luther King wished young people wanted to be like Dr Ben Carson or the economist Thomas Sowell, not like the characters from the videogame Grand Thief Auto. I suggest to look for the testimonies of two Christian blackskin women who survived dooms in Uganda; Marguerite Baratkise (the mother Teressa of Burindi) and Immacul\u00e9e Ilibagiza,. Now they teach to forgive, although they lost allmost all their families in the Rwandand genocide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you equating the people who died from police brutality as characters from GTA? Or that because they arent neurosurgeons they somehow failed to Martin luther king?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Estas igualando a las personas que murieron por brutalidad policiaca como personajes del GTA? O que como no eran neurocirujanos de alguna forma fallaron a Martin Luther King?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987195#post987195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* If you were Ramsay Bolton, and Sansa Stark is front of you with your very hungry dogs (your &quot;wives&quot;)... wouldn't you rather she had been tought to be a merciful Christian, or instead she was like a Nietzsche's \u00dcbermesch who disregard the Jew-Christian slave-master morality?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ummm who is Ramsey Bolton in this example of yours? People who oppose the curch? People who think spain pass is full of questionable acts? Because ramsey was rapist, war criminal and terrorist of state who had to die. This comparison is aweful as there is no &quot;jail&quot; in GoT and the political landscape as informed by the series makes it clear he had to die. You saying that the character should apply a morality that is non functional in the setting.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Umm quien es Ramsey Bolton en este ejemplo tuyo? La gente que se opone a la iglesia? La gente que piensa que espa\u00f1a tomo un par de descicioner turbias? Porque Ramsey era un violador, criminal de guerra y terrorista de estado que tenia que morirse. Tu comparasion es horrible y no aplicable. No existen carceles en GoT y las circunstancias politicas segun la seria aseguraban claramente que se tenia que morir. Vos decis que tendrian que aplicar un sistema de moralidad no funcional en el setting? </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987327#post987327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not kidding when I say Westeros, the world of the books of &quot;games of thrones&quot;, the &quot;song of fire and ice &quot; saga are a good example of how could be the western civilitation without merciful Christian teachings. And Christianity allowed the scientific mindset, because now the Nature wasn't explained with fays and genies, but rules could be discovered by reason and investigation. There were inventions and discoveries in another civilitations, but only Christianity made possible the empirism, rationalism and humanism. And Christiany gave dignity to all citizens, men and women, workers and nobles. Before the Jesus' parable about the poor Lazarus and rich Epulon nobody questioned about somebody had got so much and other were so poor. Western civilitation was the first to end the slavery.<br /> <br /> Sorry, now I leave you because I have to pay Arya Stark, I had asked her to kill some Melissandre's followers who were asking me about some fugitive R'hllor temple (sacred?) prostitutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its been a long time since i read the books but isnt the Light of the seven a similar version of the catholisim?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:12:44-07:00","id":987434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987415#post987415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I generally agree with you there, and I definitely think it's a debatable point. Should a restaurant be able to not serve people of color of LQBT people? Should a bakery be able to deny them a wedding cake because they disagree with interracial or gay marriage? I may find it deplorable, but I'm generally inclined to say yes. However, there's a question of whether or not this denies them the right to generally sit in a restaurant or have a wedding. If the intolerance of a city or town means those resources aren't available to them, then, well, fuck those business owners, frankly. I'm not entirely sure where we draw the line.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not an easy question to answer, yeah. I think we broadly agree on this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987415#post987415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're right. It shouldn't, and there's plenty of examples of criticism in the media. But it doesn't mean those criticizing Islam aren't subjected to criticism from others.</div> </div> </div> </div> Pretty much; those who criticise have no grounds to complain about any criticism they receive in return. If you hurl your thoughts out into the marketplace of ideas, and those thoughts are critical of somebody else, well... it's better for everyone if those ideas get picked apart to see what's valid and what's not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987415#post987415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah. Sorry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Avowed pacifist here.</div> </div> </div> </div> Naturally as a far right lunatic (my actual political views, incidentally, tend to coincide with either the far right or the far left, depending on what we're talking about, according to every political analysis quiz I've ever taken) I'm a staunch advocate of the use of force. But I can respect anyone who has at least taken the time to consider their position on violence enough to be able to say that they <i>have</i> a position.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987415#post987415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> When being Jewish or Muslim significantly hinders your odds of that position, I'd say Christianity is represented fairly disproportionately.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps. Admittedly, I tend to look at this from a perspective of &quot;who are these people, really?&quot; rather than &quot;who do these people profess to be?&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe it's the case that, say, Donald Trump and Hillary Clinton both profess to be Christians (honestly I really have no idea whether they do or not) but I tend to just assume they're inhuman monsters garbed in human flesh rather than creatures possessed of actual religious conviction. So, are they Christian? Well, probably depends who you ask. Is saying you are enough to make you one? I'd say not, but others might disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987415#post987415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My fellow white people rank very, <i>very</i> low on my list of priorities. It's not anywhere in the triage queue.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it's very easy to not worry about certain groups of people just because they're not in trouble <i>now - </i>there's a danger, I think, that in striving for equality by specifically tossing aid at the disadvantaged rather than simply striving to create an equal playing field for all we run the risk of simply reversing the positions of advantage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987415#post987415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel like compassion is a fundamental human virtue. I try hard to be compassionate, and I think I generally succeed. But being compassionate doesn't mean treating everyone's grievance with equivalent weight. White people need to get in line.</div> </div> </div> </div> I tend to feel that class privilege and the privilege of wealth far outweighs anything like white or male privilege, admittedly. If you're living in the gutter, it doesn't really matter if you're black or white - everything sucks, and everything will probably continue to suck for however long you've got left.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I'd argue that there are things women can get away with that men never could - women don't have some of the advantages that men do, but they <i>do</i> have certain edges that men <i>lack. </i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987415#post987415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And here it is. &quot;Mansplaining&quot; and &quot;Whitesplaining&quot; are terms I have some problem with, but again, they don't rank very highly on the list.<br /> <br /> These aren't terms that are meant to insult an entire race or an entire gender. Rather, they speak to racial and gender terms specifically because of existing conditions that make them specific to those racial and gender dynamics. As someone with a black girlfriend and friends who span the racial divide, it's something I've seen firsthand. That's not to demean <i>all</i> white people or <i>all </i>mean, but it is to say that these actions are specific to existing conditions. &quot;Whitesplaining&quot; isn't about the virtue or genetic worth of a white person. It's about privilege and experience, and usually it's unintentional. Ditto &quot;mansplaining&quot;. It's a peculiar social tic that comes implicitly from being raised as a privileged majority in a society that's conditioned and dehumanized the o the other. It's something I've done and something I try to avoid, and it doesn't make you a bad person.<br /> <br /> That said, I understand that it can be worrying. There was a common sentiment where I grew up that &quot;Not all black people are n*****s, but all n*****s are black&quot;, and I can see the parallel. But it's not troubling enough for me to see it as a clear and present concern.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that it's very easy to slip from using the term to critique certain things done by certain white people to critiquing <i>all white people - </i>language shapes thought as much as the other way around - that said, you already seem to appreciate that, so there's really no need for me to keep talking there.<br /> <br /> I will note, however, that I've seen both terms used explicitly as racist/sexist slurs; maybe you don't mean them that way, but I've seen them used in the same sort of way that other people might utter all kinds of horribly unpleasant things that don't really bear repeating here. This is, ultimately, my point of concern - not everyone who says &quot;whitesplain&quot; is a bad person or a racist, but some of the people who use it <i>are</i><i>, </i>and if it gets normalised as an acceptable expression then it grants legitimacy to the latter sort of person.<br /> <br /> Perhaps our perspectives are simply different because I've had experience as a minority and a majority both; it's easy for the coin to flip and the shoe to land on the other foot. Indeed, maybe where you are it's not a legitimate problem - geography is ultimately a factor here, and we're likely not even in the same country - but where I live, it'd be all too easy for white people to become targets if racial tensions were to flare up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987195#post987195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> * If you were Ramsay Bolton, and Sansa Stark is front of you with your very hungry dogs (your &quot;wives&quot;)... wouldn't you rather she had been tought to be a merciful Christian, or instead she was like a Nietzsche's \u00dcbermesch who disregard the Jew-Christian slave-master morality?</div> </div> </div> </div> Frankly, I think Sansa's grievances against Ramsay were such that her upbringing would have been largely irrelevant in any case - after everything she'd been through, that girl wanted <i>justice, </i>and she damn well got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11105,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","user":"Seviphas","date":".  Responded to another post that caught my eye. 10-14-2016, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","name":"Seviphas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T15:30:18-07:00","id":987464,"title":"","content":"Eh, far too much said already, just going to make a few points;<br /> <br /> The events of the War of the Five Kings in ASoIaF/GoT is based on actual historical events done by Christians. If you look to Westeros as what it's like without the &quot;mercy&quot; of Christianity, you have it backwards. Westeros's events are less horrible than what actually happened in reality (we had multiple Red Weddings!), so if you think the presence of Christianity matters to the morality of a society... you're arguing that Christianity makes things worse than a variety of a pantheistic/henoistic religions.<br /> <br /> When people say things like &quot;Christianity founded Western civilization,&quot; they're not entirely wrong, it just is usually followed by a massive white-washing of how exactly that happened. Christianity unified Europe by doing as much as possible to eliminate all non-Christians from their midst; using pretty much any and every means over the course of history. Then they appropriated a ton of things and invented ways to justify them as Christian in origin to deny the contributions of other cultures to Western civilization.<br /> <br /> The issue with the criticisms of Islam in the West, is that so much of it is done by people that either clearly do not have sufficient education in Islam to know what they're talking about, or don't care because they want to conflate all of Islam with fanatics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T17:17:02-07:00","id":987500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987434#post987434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to feel that class privilege and the privilege of wealth far outweighs anything like white or male privilege, admittedly. If you're living in the gutter, it doesn't really matter if you're black or white - everything sucks, and everything will probably continue to suck for however long you've got left.</div> </div> </div> </div>A white person with no high school diploma has better job prospects than a black person with a college degree. While wealth and class privilege do indeed permeate everything, so do race and sex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T20:46:49-07:00","id":987587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987409#post987409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Honestly? No, I don't.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I'll admit that it's a tricky issue - where does one person's right to refuse to provide their labour infringe upon somebody else's right to walk down the street and not feel like a violently despised outcast in their own hometown? I'm not going to pretend that I have the answer to that question, and even if I were to sit down and think about it for a while I'm not sure I'd come to any kind of satisfactory conclusion.<br /> <br /> All I will say is that I think it's a shitty thing to do to refuse to make people a cake to help them celebrate their love, even though I think they had the right to do it. A favourite quote of mine comes to mind, here: &quot;To have a right to do a thing <i>is not at all the same as to be right in doing it</i>.<i>&quot; </i>Ultimately, you can't <i>make</i> someone support you - you can only do the best you can to persuade them, and hope they'll see the light on their own.<br /> <br /> I'll also say that a sign like that - &quot;No dogs, negros, mexicans&quot; - well, let's just say that anyone who tried to hang a sign like that was probably not so great a human being. And I don't think anyone has the right to make a black person or a Mexican living amongst them feel like an unwanted stranger in his own home on the grounds of the colour of their skin or the nation of their ancestry. So, yeah, I'd be in favour of tearing that sign down and throwing stuff at anyone who tried to put it back up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Must be easy to say that when you almost certainly aren't one of those people whose choices are limited and you're afraid every minute of a society that allows that to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T21:22:58-07:00","id":987593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987587#post987587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Must be easy to say that when you almost certainly aren't one of those people whose choices are limited and you're afraid every minute of a society that allows that to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>While your point is valid, I can't believe that forcing people to violate their values to adhere to other people's values is the moral choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T21:38:14-07:00","id":987597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987593#post987593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While your point is valid, I can't believe that forcing people to violate their values to adhere to other people's values is the moral choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>When talking about bigotry, we don't take any one example in a vacuum. Refusing to bake a cake is, itself, not really illegal. The question is, why are you refusing <i>this</i> cake for <i>this</i> wedding? Are you refusing cakes for people having their second marriage? Are you refusing cakes to couples who can't prove that they're both virgins? Are you refusing cakes to couples who aren't christian? Because if suddenly you've decided that these specific values are vital to your otherwise non-religious baking business, then it's pretty clear that the bakery is hiding their bigotry behind the values.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T22:57:10-07:00","id":987631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987593#post987593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While your point is valid, I can't believe that forcing people to violate their values to adhere to other people's values is the moral choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do their beliefs have anything to do with it?<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't do business with people who don't follow my religious practices.&quot;<br /> <br /> Don't see many bakers who will refuse to bake a cake for a second marriage, do they? How about followers of other branches of their religion, or other religions entirely?<br /> <br /> No, sir - they're refusing to do business with someone who makes them <i>personally uncomfortable, </i>and then pretend that the law should cover their personal discomfort and <i>not</i> the actual practice of their religion.<br /> <br /> And even if it did, the fuck am I supposed to do if there's only one cake baker in my town? Call in a super expensive cake from another town entirely?<br /> <br /> You create a double standard where some people get to not do things because they feel like it and the rest of us are fucked.<br /> <br /> What exactly isn't moral about compelling businesses to avoid prejudice in serving customers? If it were up to people like you, we'd still have WHITE ONLY counters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T23:55:12-07:00","id":987649,"title":"","content":"Beyond the specifics there's also a simple fact:<br /> <br /> Forcing people to abide by morals that aren't not necessarily their own <b>is what laws do</b>.<br /> <br /> You don't get to believe in the value of, &quot;if you can take it, you can keep it,&quot; and then take people's stuff by force, because the law says that makes you a mugger.<br /> <br /> The whole point of having laws is to have a common set of rules that everyone has to abide by despite their personal beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T01:05:20-07:00","id":987666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=986267#post986267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the Atomic bomb, how do you think History will remember Harry S Truman, the American President that made the decision to use the Atomic bomb on Japan? I've read a <a href=\"http://www.ushistory.org/us/51g.asp\" target=\"_blank\">few articles on the topic</a>, but people seem divided on his decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between an invasion and occupation and the Bomb, the Bomb was kinder. Especially if you factor in the Soviets involving themselves.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T06:19:54-07:00","id":987718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987587#post987587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Must be easy to say that when you almost certainly aren't one of those people whose choices are limited and you're afraid every minute of a society that allows that to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it's very easy to pretend that people who don't agree with you have never suffered hardship; that they sit in ivory towers and hand down judgments and opinions without knowing what it's like to struggle or be in danger - that they disagree out of ignorance, that they simply <i>don't get it. </i><br /> <br /> It seems to me a very limited way of thinking, honestly, especially when you're talking to strangers on the internet who you really know nothing about beyond the fact that they have different political views than you and probably like roleplaying games or something. Why are you so quick to presume you understand the circumstances of people you've never met?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987500#post987500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A white person with no high school diploma has better job prospects than a black person with a college degree. While wealth and class privilege do indeed permeate everything, so do race and sex.</div> </div> </div> </div> If that's true, I'd be interested to see the evidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","name":"Seviphas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T07:23:54-07:00","id":987737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987593#post987593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While your point is valid, I can't believe that forcing people to violate their values to adhere to other people's values is the moral choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't mind my asking, do you identify as a libertarian?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:21:58-07:00","id":987759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987256#post987256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The decadence of Europe started in 1789 (I could also establish that it all began with Nominalism). Leave republicanism and secularism for the Americas (and I bet secularism isn't working there, either).</div> </div> </div> </div>How did Europe start to become decadent in 1789? (I assume this is a reference to the French revolution) Are you aware how brutal and violent life often was in the Middle Ages? I don't see any real increase in &quot;decadence&quot; beginning in the late 18th century. What exactly do you mean by &quot;decadence&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T09:16:57-07:00","id":987785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987434#post987434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps. Admittedly, I tend to look at this from a perspective of &quot;who are these people, really?&quot; rather than &quot;who do these people profess to be?&quot; Maybe it's the case that, say, Donald Trump and Hillary Clinton both profess to be Christians (honestly I really have no idea whether they do or not) but I tend to just assume they're inhuman monsters garbed in human flesh rather than creatures possessed of actual religious conviction. So, are they Christian? Well, probably depends who you ask. Is saying you are enough to make you one? I'd say not, but others might disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the question is whether or not they're Christian so much as the expectation that they need to play at it. If you're expected to prescribe to a specific religious affiliation to have a chance at political office, I'd say that suggests pretty strong Christian dominance in the US. Here in Atlanta, a city that's fairly progressive, we have churches on almost every block. A fairly radical bloc of Christianity has significant buy in American political policy and promote ideas that seem out of touch with modern life. This is only exacerbated by the fact that economic, cultural, and economic conservatives are tethered to the same party. So people like my parents, who are American Libertarians and prescribe to fairly progressive social values grudgingly support politicians who don't represent their social interests. The same for Americans who support aggressive (and I'd say wrong-headed, but that's neither here) stances on foreign trade and immigration for cultural reasons. 83% of Americans identify as Christian, and while that's a pretty wide tent with a lot of variance in passion and values, I think it's hard to argue that Christianity doesn't have significant sway in our culture, politics, and values. If anything, the voices opposing Christian ideals are so loud because they're so outnumbered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987434#post987434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's very easy to not worry about certain groups of people just because they're not in trouble <i>now - </i>there's a danger, I think, that in striving for equality by specifically tossing aid at the disadvantaged rather than simply striving to create an equal playing field for all we run the risk of simply reversing the positions of advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still think triage is an acceptable way to look at things, because the racial and gender disparities are so uneven. It's been decades since the civil rights movement, but all you have to do is look at wage gaps or harsher sentencing laws for people of color to recognize that a blanket approach to equality doesn't work. It's not about calling out people in white hoods anymore. That's not where racism exists. It's seeped its way into our fundamental systems, and we'll never fix these problems without addressing them directly. Treating your neighbors nicely and pretending you're color blind doesn't work anymore. That means open and honest communication with people about what it means to be a women, a person of color, an immigrant, or a Muslim in America and treating their grievances with the sympathy and honesty they deserve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987434#post987434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to feel that class privilege and the privilege of wealth far outweighs anything like white or male privilege, admittedly. If you're living in the gutter, it doesn't really matter if you're black or white - everything sucks, and everything will probably continue to suck for however long you've got left.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that these problems compound on each other. Being poor is terrible, and it's a self-perpetuating cycle that's hard to break out of. We should be directly addressing privilege and lack of privilege in all its forms. That might mean pointing out that someone is &quot;richsplaining&quot; when they gripe about how poor people should just get off their asses and work harder without recognizing how difficult it is to break out of a cycle of poverty. It means calling someone out when they ask why someone in the Rust Belt doesn't just move away.<br /> <br /> People of color are dealing with both institutionalized racism and the challenges that come from being poor. There's a poverty epidemic in the black community, and it's not due to anything inherent about their race. The specter of segregation and the present threat of gerrymandering mean that many people of color are trapped in disadvantaged neighborhoods with high crime rates, low accessibility to public facilities, and miserable schools. Add on the fact that they're under greater scrutiny by employers, officers, and random passerby and that they're less likely to get the benefit of the doubt in a criminal case and more likely to get significantly harsher sentences (20% more time according to the more conservative recent studies), and the odds are stacked even more strongly against them. The problem is that if we address the economic problems, create more jobs, raise wages, white people are disproportionately going to feel the advantages of those changes.<br /> <br /> And that doesn't end when they manage to claw their way to success. Let's talk personal experience. I've been dating a black woman. She's managed to earn herself a comfortable middle class lifestyle. She's brilliant, well dressed, eloquent, and more knowledgeable on me in most of the interests we have in common (film, literature, politics, etc.). Meanwhile, I'm a scruffy poor (I'd say charming. You just have to trust me on that one) white boy. That doesn't stop people from deferring to me by nature in conversation, speaking over her, and treating the things I say with significantly more weight. I have no doubt that if we went to the same job interview, and I appeared hung over, disjointed, and wearing rumpled clothes, I'd have a better chance of getting it than her. I have a black friend, a tiny, completely non-intimidating black woman with piercings and dyed hair (and I know that gives her some advantages. Adopting &quot;white&quot; fashion choices, even when they're punky or hipster definitely gives black women an advantage). I've been riding with her when she's been pulled over, and I've seen the attitude of the cop change as soon as he sees me in the back seat. At most low wage service industry jobs I've worked, I've seen (almost without fail) competent, driven black workers be treated to disproportionate scrutiny as soon as something goes missing.<br /> <br /> The worst part of it is, this isn't really even about evil racists and misogynists trying to keep black people from drinking out of their water fountains or trying to keep women from working alongside them. Sure, that still exists, and it's a sliding scale. It runs the gamut from the proud and out racism and misogyny of Donald Trump to Rick and Morty fans wringing their hands over the perception that bringing in women writers is going to neuter the show and turn it PC, to people like you and me who are completely well intentioned and sometimes let subconscious biases get the best of us. I sometimes have to have it pointed out when I'm &quot;mansplaining&quot; and &quot;whitesplaining&quot;, and I'm glad my friends do it.<br /> <br /> But the most insidious problem is just how institutionalized it is. Even if we get rid of the out-and-out bigots, the system is still gamed, and the psychic impact of what women and people of color deal with on a daily basis is staggering. There was a fascinating study to get at the heart of the gender gap in STEM fields. It found that girls perform significantly better on the same tests when they're told that it's a broad curriculum test vs. being told that it will test their aptitude at math and science. This extends to how we perceive women. A different study indicates that teachers grade girls more poorly on science and math tests when they know the names of the students vs. when these tests are delivered to the teachers anonymously. I have little doubt that similar tests involving black and white children would deliver similar results. Our cultural perceptions of race and gender have a significant and direct effect on both self-value and performance. Another study: officer and random civilians are shown a split second picture of faces and told to say whether they had a negative or positive response to that person. Both black and white participants were more likely to elicit a negative response from black faces than from white faces. I feel like everyone should ask their female and black friends about the precautions they take in their everyday lives or the harassment they deal with on a daily basis. I've known quite a few friends who are shocked when they actually put it in words, because it's simply become part of their daily routine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987434#post987434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, I'd argue that there are things women can get away with that men never could - women don't have some of the advantages that men do, but they <i>do</i> have certain edges that men <i>lack. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I think those &quot;advantages&quot; are really just a drop in the bucket when you look at the daily trials women face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987434#post987434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will note, however, that I've seen both terms used explicitly as racist/sexist slurs; maybe you don't mean them that way, but I've seen them used in the same sort of way that other people might utter all kinds of horribly unpleasant things that don't really bear repeating here. This is, ultimately, my point of concern - not everyone who says &quot;whitesplain&quot; is a bad person or a racist, but some of the people who use it <i>are</i><i>, </i>and if it gets normalised as an acceptable expression then it grants legitimacy to the latter sort of person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Venom towards white people and men are always going to bubble to the surface, but I really can't manage to blame people for that. There's only so much a person can deal with. When I hear these terms used out of exasperation or anger, it's usually from women or people of color with nuanced views of race and gender who have just reached their tipping point and need to vent. But my experience may be different from your.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987434#post987434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps our perspectives are simply different because I've had experience as a minority and a majority both; it's easy for the coin to flip and the shoe to land on the other foot. Indeed, maybe where you are it's not a legitimate problem - geography is ultimately a factor here, and we're likely not even in the same country - but where I live, it'd be all too easy for white people to become targets if racial tensions were to flare up.</div> </div> </div> </div>We probably are. There aren't a lot of places quite like the American South, and living in Atlanta, which is a strongly mixed race community and a bastion of LGBQT activity sitting in the heart of a very <i>very</i> conservative state adds a unique wrinkle to that. America certainly doesn't hold a monopoly on racism, but ours is certainly unique, and it's only magnified here in the South. If you don't mind me asking, where are you from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-15-2016, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:48:33-07:00","id":987866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987718#post987718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it's very easy to pretend that people who don't agree with you have never suffered hardship; that they sit in ivory towers and hand down judgments and opinions without knowing what it's like to struggle or be in danger - that they disagree out of ignorance, that they simply <i>don't get it. </i><br /> <br /> It seems to me a very limited way of thinking, honestly, especially when you're talking to strangers on the internet who you really know nothing about beyond the fact that they have different political views than you and probably like roleplaying games or something. Why are you so quick to presume you understand the circumstances of people you've never met?</div> </div> </div> </div>Said clearly by someone who's never been through that shit.<br /> <br /> You reveal by your statements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:27:10-07:00","id":987885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=981974#post981974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Catholic Inquisition wasn't worse than Protestant Wich-hunt, only we lost the propaganda war. The black anti-Catholic legend lied or exaggerated a lot of things. For example the iron maiden wasn't used in the middle age, the chastity belts are also other historical legend. The &quot;Droit du seigneur&quot; is another myth, or at least if it happened it wasn't allowed by laws. What do you know about the medieval &quot;peace and truce of God&quot;? The dark age wasn't so dark. Why not to talk about Irish slaves? Yes, Irish slaves in Northeamerica suffered more than black people, but we don't see movies about Irish slaves.<br /> <br /> And now USA is suffering her own black legend to be presented like the new evil empire, but the world isn't better with Russia or China like supreme power. North-american like the new American empire is following the same steps of Spanish nation. We aren't forgiven to be Christians.<br /> <br /> If you don't like Russia Today news, I don't like those shits like Garth Ernnis' Preacher comics. Self-criticism doesn't mean self-deprecating. We don't need lessons from people who knows nothing about Spanish anti-Catholic failed genocide in the 30's, the reasons of the Mexican Cristero war, or the Pakistani anti-blasphemy law what has condemme some Christians with false acusations.<br /> <br /> Do you remember when Kamala Khan, the new Miss Marvel with Pakistani origin, asked freedom for Asia Bibi? Me neither.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Still reading through the topic and this caught my attention. I'm pretty sure it got addressed later, but: I always find it amusing, when <i>any </i>group, or party, or religion or whatnot's best defense, regarding their horrible deeds, or corruption, or any objectionable thing is &quot;But! The other guys are just as horrible or even more than us!&quot; Uhm, that's not makes your group and it's deeds less horrible. The Nazis weren't less horrible just because the Communists killed even more people and vice versa. That's war-mentality and/or finding excuses by relativising. Look, the enemy burned down our villages and raped our women, so it's okay to do the same! No, it's not. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T16:36:02-07:00","id":987999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987785#post987785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't think the question is whether or not they're Christian so much as the expectation that they need to play at it. If you're expected to prescribe to a specific religious affiliation to have a chance at political office, I'd say that suggests pretty strong Christian dominance in the US. Here in Atlanta, a city that's fairly progressive, we have churches on almost every block. A fairly radical bloc of Christianity has significant buy in American political policy and promote ideas that seem out of touch with modern life. This is only exacerbated by the fact that economic, cultural, and economic conservatives are tethered to the same party. So people like my parents, who are American Libertarians and prescribe to fairly progressive social values grudgingly support politicians who don't represent their social interests. The same for Americans who support aggressive (and I'd say wrong-headed, but that's neither here) stances on foreign trade and immigration for cultural reasons. 83% of Americans identify as Christian, and while that's a pretty wide tent with a lot of variance in passion and values, I think it's hard to argue that Christianity doesn't have significant sway in our culture, politics, and values. If anything, the voices opposing Christian ideals are so loud because they're so outnumbered.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure. I'll freely admit that I probably don't have the greatest grasp on the influence of religion in American politics, since I'm all the way across the ocean from you guys. The only people I've really encountered in my ordinary life - aside from the occasional caller at my door who wants to talk to me about my lord and saviour Jesus Christ - who were vocally religious have been Muslim, not Christian. Different worlds, I suppose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987785#post987785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I still think triage is an acceptable way to look at things, because the racial and gender disparities are so uneven. It's been decades since the civil rights movement, but all you have to do is look at wage gaps or harsher sentencing laws for people of color to recognize that a blanket approach to equality doesn't work. It's not about calling out people in white hoods anymore. That's not where racism exists. It's seeped its way into our fundamental systems, and we'll never fix these problems without addressing them directly. Treating your neighbors nicely and pretending you're color blind doesn't work anymore. That means open and honest communication with people about what it means to be a women, a person of color, an immigrant, or a Muslim in America and treating their grievances with the sympathy and honesty they deserve.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can't offer too much of a comment on here, admittedly; I'm not American and I grew up in a place where being Muslim generally put you in a position of strength, not weakness. The Muslim communities where I come from generally looked out for each other - maybe they had to due to external pressures, maybe not, but the fact of the matter was that you didn't run around fucking with the Asian kids. This naturally lead to the point where the subsequent generations of Muslim immigrants realised that they had the advantage of certain communal bonds and attachments that a lot of other people didn't, and that lead to the more belligerent members of that community exploiting those networks to attack people outside of that community with impunity.<br /> <br /> It's why I tend to believe that majority groups will have a tendency to act like assholes regardless of what exactly they are. It's not something exclusive to white people, as so many people seem to claim these days. A former co-worker of mine (a black guy, in case it's relevant) couldn't even go out to eat dinner with his Muslim girlfriend, because people that neither of them even <i>knew</i> just didn't like to see an Asian girl dating a black guy. And he was one of the most friendly and optimistic people populating that nihilistic hell-hole of a retail night shift, too.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that while it's generally worthwhile to listen to the experiences of people from backgrounds different to your own, it's possible to go too far - &quot;trust but verify&quot; is better than &quot;listen and believe&quot;, in my book. Just because someone thinks they're oppressed doesn't mean they are, after all. Conversations are great to have, but I've seen some people suggest that people should just accept anything somebody from a minority says about their experience as gospel truth - which is a level of trust I don't even extend to many of my friends, let alone total strangers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987785#post987785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And that doesn't end when they manage to claw their way to success. Let's talk personal experience. I've been dating a black woman. She's managed to earn herself a comfortable middle class lifestyle. She's brilliant, well dressed, eloquent, and more knowledgeable on me in most of the interests we have in common (film, literature, politics, etc.). Meanwhile, I'm a scruffy poor (I'd say charming. You just have to trust me on that one) white boy.</div> </div> </div> </div> You seem pretty friendly. I'll take you at your word.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987785#post987785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That doesn't stop people from deferring to me by nature in conversation, speaking over her, and treating the things I say with significantly more weight. I have no doubt that if we went to the same job interview, and I appeared hung over, disjointed, and wearing rumpled clothes, I'd have a better chance of getting it than her. I have a black friend, a tiny, completely non-intimidating black woman with piercings and dyed hair (and I know that gives her some advantages. Adopting &quot;white&quot; fashion choices, even when they're punky or hipster definitely gives black women an advantage). I've been riding with her when she's been pulled over, and I've seen the attitude of the cop change as soon as he sees me in the back seat. At most low wage service industry jobs I've worked, I've seen (almost without fail) competent, driven black workers be treated to disproportionate scrutiny as soon as something goes missing.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can imagine that happening, yeah. I've heard the question &quot;is he black?&quot; one too many times when folks are talking about potential thieves (from when I worked in retail, for instance, or just when I was listening in on conversations about theft in the workplace).<br /> <br /> Here, though, I can't imagine a scruffy white kid would have a better shot at a job than a well-dressed black lady. I almost wonder if we're simply coming from two background so different that there's not even really any argument or dissent to be had - we've simply experienced very different things, and perhaps that's about all there is to be said. Maybe, anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987785#post987785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The worst part of it is, this isn't really even about evil racists and misogynists trying to keep black people from drinking out of their water fountains or trying to keep women from working alongside them. Sure, that still exists, and it's a sliding scale. It runs the gamut from the proud and out racism and misogyny of Donald Trump to Rick and Morty fans wringing their hands over the perception that bringing in women writers is going to neuter the show and turn it PC, to people like you and me who are completely well intentioned and sometimes let subconscious biases get the best of us. I sometimes have to have it pointed out when I'm &quot;mansplaining&quot; and &quot;whitesplaining&quot;, and I'm glad my friends do it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Admittedly, I'm not sure I'd want to be friends with people who actually used the term &quot;whitesplain&quot; in casual conversation - I'd rather have somebody explain their point of view without incendiary buzzwords. I don't think they really add anything to the conversation, overall - we'll all be better off if we can get more people to the discussion table in good faith without all this resentment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987785#post987785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A different study indicates that teachers grade girls more poorly on science and math tests when they know the names of the students vs. when these tests are delivered to the teachers anonymously.</div> </div> </div> </div> As a side note, I've always thought it was a bit ridiculous that we've even <i>got </i>names on papers. Surely it'd be better to create a system where the test marker doesn't know whose exam they're grading? I mean, if you absolutely must have a system where the markers know the entrants personally, it'd be better to mitigate the impacts of any biases they may have (whether they're sexist, racist, or simply because they don't like that particular student very much) by just not letting them know whose test they have in front of them.<br /> <br /> Seems self-evident to me, anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987785#post987785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have little doubt that similar tests involving black and white children would deliver similar results. Our cultural perceptions of race and gender have a significant and direct effect on both self-value and performance. Another study: officer and random civilians are shown a split second picture of faces and told to say whether they had a negative or positive response to that person. Both black and white participants were more likely to elicit a negative response from black faces than from white faces. I feel like everyone should ask their female and black friends about the precautions they take in their everyday lives or the harassment they deal with on a daily basis. I've known quite a few friends who are shocked when they actually put it in words, because it's simply become part of their daily routine.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah. Here seems to be the thing, really: it's not some grand display of racism or hatred, but rather a subtle undercurrent that permeates every interaction that you have with somebody else. You'll get treated just a <i>little</i> different because you're black, but it'll happen a hundred times a day, and that adds right the hell up, I'd imagine. Maybe nobody's hanging up signs that say you can't drink at the fountain anymore, but people look at you askance and slip things into conversation every now and again that make sure you <i>know</i> they see you as &quot;other&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987785#post987785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think those &quot;advantages&quot; are really just a drop in the bucket when you look at the daily trials women face.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm. Agree to disagree on this one, I think!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987785#post987785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Venom towards white people and men are always going to bubble to the surface, but I really can't manage to blame people for that. There's only so much a person can deal with. When I hear these terms used out of exasperation or anger, it's usually from women or people of color with nuanced views of race and gender who have just reached their tipping point and need to vent. But my experience may be different from your.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't really encounter people that use those terms! Where I live, if someone's angry with white people they'll probably spit out something far less pleasant in my general direction, or just outright attack me. It's happened before - back when I was in high school a bunch of people literally took to the streets looking for, specifically, white people to beat up. To this day I never learned why - nobody seemed to know.<br /> <br /> Apparently there's some sort of stereotype around here that white people are weak, or cowardly, or just generally not able or willing to defend themselves - so a bunch of teenagers decided to stalk the streets looking for white people to beat to the ground and leave bleeding. It didn't really get better in college - glance in the wrong direction and &quot;what're you looking at, white boy?&quot; would be a pretty damn common refrain. It's these kinds of experiences that cause me to react... well, poorly, when people insist that racism against white people just isn't a thing, or doesn't matter when it happens. I've seen people get beaten to within an inch of their lives just for being a few shades too pale; didn't happen to me personally, but I've witnessed the aftermath. That's what happens when resentment or casual contempt boils over, and it's why I speak out against it where I can.<br /> <br /> In my lifetime, I've witnessed pretty much equal amounts of racism directed against whites as I have against non-whites. One particularly striking example from my youth was when I was wandering around eavesdropping on a few conversations late at night in the park, and an older black fellow said something to the effect of: &quot;If I had a mixed race kid, I'd have to make him black. I'd beat the white out of him.&quot; And that was considered acceptable where I grew up. Nobody really said anything, or cared very much. That stuck with me for years later - especially since it seemed to fly in the face of the whole &quot;racism is something white people do to everybody else&quot; narrative inculcated in so many of us when we're young.<br /> <br /> It's easy to say these things don't happen - a lot of people will say so until they're blue in the face. That's what bothers me, really. I wonder if that's how minorities elsewhere feel when they're treated like shit by white people, or when less well-intentioned folks say that racism simply doesn't happen anymore. I may not <i>be</i> them, but I've walked a mile or so in shoes that looked a little bit like theirs, so I actually can sympathise a little here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987785#post987785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We probably are. There aren't a lot of places quite like the American South, and living in Atlanta, which is a strongly mixed race community and a bastion of LGBQT activity sitting in the heart of a very <i>very</i> conservative state adds a unique wrinkle to that. America certainly doesn't hold a monopoly on racism, but ours is certainly unique, and it's only magnified here in the South. If you don't mind me asking, where are you from?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm from a merry little place in Britain that's widely known for being a hotbed of racial and religious tension, along with just being a generally fairly miserable place to live. I try not to let it bother me very much; the sun still shines down on us just like it does everywhere else, after all, and while we did have cops with assault guns walking the streets at one point, well... you've just got to get on with it, at the end of the day.<br /> <br /> ... man, this talk about race relations and all that is pretty darned depressing. I think I'll hop out of the thread at this point; feel free to PM me if you'd like to keep chatting, but I think I'm about done here. It's been an interesting discussion, but I've had my fill of it for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","name":"Seviphas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T18:28:15-07:00","id":988037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you remember when Kamala Khan, the new Miss Marvel with Pakistani origin, asked freedom for Asia Bibi? Me neither.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you remember when Marvel released a book about a young member of a marginalized American minority who was just trying to live her life and was treated as an ordinary teenager, enamored with superheroes and free from polarizing rhetoric about race, religion, and politics? <i>because she's a teenage girl in a superhero comic who doesn't reflect on those things and isn't required to?</i><br /> <br /> I do. That was pretty great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-15-2016, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T18:30:35-07:00","id":988041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987999#post987999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... man, this talk about race relations and all that is pretty darned depressing. I think I'll hop out of the thread at this point; feel free to PM me if you'd like to keep chatting, but I think I'm about done here. It's been an interesting discussion, but I've had my fill of it for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am right there with you. I have to say, it's been refreshing to have a discussion about this with someone who has a different perspective but is willing to be civil. Too often it comes down to either griping with my similarly radical friends or out and out arguing with bigoted extremists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T18:48:26-07:00","id":988048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you remember when Kamala Khan, the new Miss Marvel with Pakistani origin, asked freedom for Asia Bibi? Me neither.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you remember when Laura Carrot from VeggieTales was raped by her father but forced to bring her incestuous child to term because her radically Baptist family believes that every life is precious?<br /> <br /> <i>Me neither, because that would be ridiculous and inappropriate given the target audience and the intent of the series.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-15-2016, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T18:51:23-07:00","id":988050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987597#post987597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When talking about bigotry, we don't take any one example in a vacuum. Refusing to bake a cake is, itself, not really illegal. The question is, why are you refusing <i>this</i> cake for <i>this</i> wedding? Are you refusing cakes for people having their second marriage? Are you refusing cakes to couples who can't prove that they're both virgins? Are you refusing cakes to couples who aren't christian? Because if suddenly you've decided that these specific values are vital to your otherwise non-religious baking business, then it's pretty clear that the bakery is hiding their bigotry behind the values.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might not, but I do. Each event needs to be examined for why it was wrong/right, and what we can learn from it, which can be applied in the more general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987631#post987631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do their beliefs have anything to do with it?<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't do business with people who don't follow my religious practices.&quot;<br /> <br /> Don't see many bakers who will refuse to bake a cake for a second marriage, do they? How about followers of other branches of their religion, or other religions entirely?<br /> <br /> No, sir - they're refusing to do business with someone who makes them <i>personally uncomfortable, </i>and then pretend that the law should cover their personal discomfort and <i>not</i> the actual practice of their religion.<br /> <br /> And even if it did, the fuck am I supposed to do if there's only one cake baker in my town? Call in a super expensive cake from another town entirely?<br /> <br /> You create a double standard where some people get to not do things because they feel like it and the rest of us are fucked.<br /> <br /> What exactly isn't moral about compelling businesses to avoid prejudice in serving customers? If it were up to people like you, we'd still have WHITE ONLY counters.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, let us consider this hypothetical scenario. There is a bakery in this town that is owned by a same-sex couple. There is also a group who are generally anti-same-sex-marriage and related ideas. They conduct this agenda through means <u>entirely within the law</u>: protest marches, leaflet distribution, the occasional radio or TV ad, etc. They are planning an event of some kind, and want cake. And for some reason (maybe they don't know the bakery is owned by a same-sex couple, maybe they just don't care about gay people in bakeries, maybe that's the only bakery in town) they want that bakery to bake the cake. Now, the couple really doesn't like the group and strongly disagree with their views. Should they be forced to support an organisation that they so strongly disagree with? That they feel, sincerely and truly, is against their existence and way of life? If they should, then where does that line stop? At what point does the shop owners rights to serve or not serve as they wish win out over the rights of an individual to have a fungible service provided by the people they want? What if there isn't a bakery (or whatever) around that they do like? Should the government subsidise transport costs for the cake or whatever to be transported?<br /> <br /> Particularly given that baking a wedding cake is a colossal pain for bakers, which is why they charge like wounded buffalos (apart from all the other reasons, of course. Weddings, man), what if the bakers refuse to because they're too busy? Should they be forced to then? Where do you draw the line? There isn't a clear, easy line, and given that 99% of the time there is alternatives, and how capitalism works, if a business wants to give up the income, then let the market punish them. It's a lot less problematic, and doesn't involve effectively people being forced to violate their beliefs in a totally unnecessary way.<br /> <br /> Beliefs are beliefs - you don't get to say &quot;these are OK to violate, these aren't&quot;. There's a degree of wiggle room where people are being physically harmed or harassed or similar, but outside of those scenarios (which are already covered by current laws)? No. It's called acceptance and tolerance, it doesn't just go one way. And failing that, you can ignore them and think they're a tool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987649#post987649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond the specifics there's also a simple fact:<br /> <br /> Forcing people to abide by morals that aren't not necessarily their own <b>is what laws do</b>.<br /> <br /> The whole point of having laws is to have a common set of rules that everyone has to abide by despite their personal beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is clearly not that case. Nobody is being physically hurt, or really even particularly inconvenienced. And yet these individuals were forced to violate deeply and sincerely held beliefs purely because other people disagreed with them. And that's what this was: a difference of opinion. So I see no meaningful difference between this, and a person being forced to watch a movie they don't like, or a movie theatre being forced to screen a movie they don't like/don't think is consistent with the image they want to portray, or someone being forced to give a public speech that goes against their values.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=987737#post987737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you don't mind my asking, do you identify as a libertarian?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't. I do agree with some of the ideas, but I don't &quot;identify&quot; as any particular political label, mostly because they're all far too broad to be meaningful. I try to work out the best thing on any given issue with reference to broad principles, for example liberty, safety and kindness. There are situations - rare, but nonzero - where some liberty must be given up for the greater good, but at no point should such sacrifice be done without extreme consideration and trying to find alternatives. Similarly safety and kindness.<br /> <br /> Are the ideas I come up with the One True Way of Making Society Perfect? Probably not. But they aren't obviously harmful, and I try to be consistent and nice, values which <i>seem</i> (and this could be my own biased perspective) too willingly discarded in favour of fervour and tribalism.<br /> <hr />And that's all I have to say about that. This whole conversation looks waaay too prone to exploding, and I don't have nearly the skill to navigate such properly without inadvertently offending someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T19:14:32-07:00","id":988055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988050#post988050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might not, but I do. Each event needs to be examined for why it was wrong/right, and what we can learn from it, which can be applied in the more general.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, let us consider this hypothetical scenario. There is a bakery in this town that is owned by a same-sex couple. There is also a group who are generally anti-same-sex-marriage and related ideas. They conduct this agenda through means <u>entirely within the law</u>: protest marches, leaflet distribution, the occasional radio or TV ad, etc. They are planning an event of some kind, and want cake. And for some reason (maybe they don't know the bakery is owned by a same-sex couple, maybe they just don't care about gay people in bakeries, maybe that's the only bakery in town) they want that bakery to bake the cake. Now, the couple really doesn't like the group and strongly disagree with their views. Should they be forced to support an organisation that they so strongly disagree with? That they feel, sincerely and truly, is against their existence and way of life? If they should, then where does that line stop? At what point does the shop owners rights to serve or not serve as they wish win out over the rights of an individual to have a fungible service provided by the people they want? What if there isn't a bakery (or whatever) around that they do like? Should the government subsidise transport costs for the cake or whatever to be transported?<br /> <br /> Particularly given that baking a wedding cake is a colossal pain for bakers, which is why they charge like wounded buffalos (apart from all the other reasons, of course. Weddings, man), what if the bakers refuse to because they're too busy? Should they be forced to then? Where do you draw the line? There isn't a clear, easy line, and given that 99% of the time there is alternatives, and how capitalism works, if a business wants to give up the income, then let the market punish them. It's a lot less problematic, and doesn't involve effectively people being forced to violate their beliefs in a totally unnecessary way.<br /> <br /> Beliefs are beliefs - you don't get to say &quot;these are OK to violate, these aren't&quot;. There's a degree of wiggle room where people are being physically harmed or harassed or similar, but outside of those scenarios (which are already covered by current laws)? No. It's called acceptance and tolerance, it doesn't just go one way. And failing that, you can ignore them and think they're a tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about me makes you think that I would support them not serving them cake?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T19:16:19-07:00","id":988057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988050#post988050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might not, but I do. Each event needs to be examined for why it was wrong/right, and what we can learn from it, which can be applied in the more general.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, let us consider this hypothetical scenario. There is a bakery in this town that is owned by a same-sex couple. There is also a group who are generally anti-same-sex-marriage and related ideas. They conduct this agenda through means <u>entirely within the law</u>: protest marches, leaflet distribution, the occasional radio or TV ad, etc. They are planning an event of some kind, and want cake. And for some reason (maybe they don't know the bakery is owned by a same-sex couple, maybe they just don't care about gay people in bakeries, maybe that's the only bakery in town) they want that bakery to bake the cake. Now, the couple really doesn't like the group and strongly disagree with their views. Should they be forced to support an organisation that they so strongly disagree with? That they feel, sincerely and truly, is against their existence and way of life? If they should, then where does that line stop? At what point does the shop owners rights to serve or not serve as they wish win out over the rights of an individual to have a fungible service provided by the people they want? What if there isn't a bakery (or whatever) around that they do like? Should the government subsidise transport costs for the cake or whatever to be transported?<br /> <br /> Particularly given that baking a wedding cake is a colossal pain for bakers, which is why they charge like wounded buffalos (apart from all the other reasons, of course. Weddings, man), what if the bakers refuse to because they're too busy? Should they be forced to then? Where do you draw the line? There isn't a clear, easy line, and given that 99% of the time there is alternatives, and how capitalism works, if a business wants to give up the income, then let the market punish them. It's a lot less problematic, and doesn't involve effectively people being forced to violate their beliefs in a totally unnecessary way.<br /> <br /> Beliefs are beliefs - you don't get to say &quot;these are OK to violate, these aren't&quot;. There's a degree of wiggle room where people are being physically harmed or harassed or similar, but outside of those scenarios (which are already covered by current laws)? No. It's called acceptance and tolerance, it doesn't just go one way. And failing that, you can ignore them and think they're a tool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is clearly not that case. Nobody is being physically hurt, or really even particularly inconvenienced. And yet these individuals were forced to violate deeply and sincerely held beliefs purely because other people disagreed with them. And that's what this was: a difference of opinion. So I see no meaningful difference between this, and a person being forced to watch a movie they don't like, or a movie theatre being forced to screen a movie they don't like/don't think is consistent with the image they want to portray, or someone being forced to give a public speech that goes against their values.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't. I do agree with some of the ideas, but I don't &quot;identify&quot; as any particular political label, mostly because they're all far too broad to be meaningful. I try to work out the best thing on any given issue with reference to broad principles, for example liberty, safety and kindness. There are situations - rare, but nonzero - where some liberty must be given up for the greater good, but at no point should such sacrifice be done without extreme consideration and trying to find alternatives. Similarly safety and kindness.<br /> <br /> Are the ideas I come up with the One True Way of Making Society Perfect? Probably not. But they aren't obviously harmful, and I try to be consistent and nice, values which <i>seem</i> (and this could be my own biased perspective) too willingly discarded in favour of fervour and tribalism. <hr />And that's all I have to say about that. This whole conversation looks waaay too prone to exploding, and I don't have nearly the skill to navigate such properly without inadvertently offending someone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As someone who's pretty far to the left on the American political spectrum, and someone who identifies as nominally queer, I'm inclined to agree with you. It's better to disseminate the information widely and enact aggressive boycotts of bigoted individuals/organizations rather than to enact legislation. Provisions need to be made in certain circumstances, of course. Case in point, Southern segregation, where the rights of business owners to not serve people of color meant that people of color simply didn't have access to products and services. There are some pretty horrifying stories about black people having to surreptitiously go to veterinarian offices after hours (and in doing so, threatening their own freedom and the livelihoods of the doctors) just to get treatment. More contemporaneously, we can look at women being denied gender-specific health care because it &quot;conflicts with the religious leanings&quot; of their employers or their health providers. And frankly, fuck them. Fuck those bigoted pieces of shit so hard.<br /> <br /> That said, I can perfectly understand why LGBQT people are defensive about being denied service. It wasn't too long ago that &quot;sexual deviancy&quot; could earn you prison time, chemical castration, or severe shock therapy. Even today, being gay in the wrong place at the wrong time can result in being beat within an inch of your life or outright lynched. And that's just in America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-15-2016, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T19:18:59-07:00","id":988059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988055#post988055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about me makes you think that I would support them not serving them cake?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a general &quot;you&quot;, not specific/accusatory &quot;you&quot;. Sorry I didn't make that clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T20:10:00-07:00","id":988083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988050#post988050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let us consider this hypothetical scenario. There is a bakery in this town that is owned by a same-sex couple. There is also a group who are generally anti-same-sex-marriage and related ideas. They conduct this agenda through means <u>entirely within the law</u>: protest marches, leaflet distribution, the occasional radio or TV ad, etc. They are planning an event of some kind, and want cake.</div> </div> </div> </div>This scenario is flawed. Despite certain people insisting otherwise, organizations aren't people, and the laws regarding discrimination are different for it. Nothing in the US anti-discrimination laws dictate that you have to violate your beliefs to provide public accommodations to an organization that works towards political ends you don't support outside of specific circumstances (the exceptions are generally around things like political campaigns to prevent a party/candidate from being silenced by lack of access to venues to speak to the public so if your local TV station gives access to the party the station owner favors, they have to give access to the opposing party/ies as well or just stay out of it).<br /> <br /> A bakery doesn't have to associate with a politically active organization that supports a cause the bakery owner disagrees with. Anti-discrimination laws in public accommodations apply to individuals, which means if there's a risk of discrimination it would only matter if members of the organization wanted a cake and the owner wanted to deny them due to their being members of said organization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Particularly given that baking a wedding cake is a colossal pain for bakers, which is why they charge like wounded buffalos (apart from all the other reasons, of course. Weddings, man), what if the bakers refuse to because they're too busy? </div> </div> </div>They're free too. There's no &quot;affirmative action&quot; provision here. If they're honestly busy and the same-sex couple doesn't order the cake far enough ahead of time? Tough on them. There's only an issue if they lie about how busy they are, such as refusing the same-sex couple on the grounds of being too busy, but then accept the order from a heterosexual couple that was in line next.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where do you draw the line? </div> </div> </div>The line is already drawn in the law. As I've already pointed out, the fight is not where the line should be but in expanding the legal protections to acknowledge minorities that were not covered at the time the law was written. There's plenty of room to debate if the current line the law draws is the right one, but it's not the issue at hand in the real cases regarding anti-LGBTQ discrimination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There isn't a clear, easy line, and given that 99% of the time there is alternatives, and how capitalism works, if a business wants to give up the income, then let the market punish them. </div> </div> </div>It is a very false assumption that &quot;99% of the time there is alternatives,&quot; and frankly it doesn't matter if it was true or not. The law isn't just for the majority of the population living in urban areas with large numbers of businesses to choose from. The law is also for small towns in the middle of nowhere without that competition when it comes to niche items. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beliefs are beliefs - you don't get to say &quot;these are OK to violate, these aren't&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Actually, as a society, we do this all the time. Again, that's one of the purposes of having laws; to define when society says the norms of society override personal beliefs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a degree of wiggle room where people are being physically harmed or harassed or similar, but outside of those scenarios (which are already covered by current laws)? </div> </div> </div>This is not the <b>Constitutional</b> limitation. We have Amendments that cover this. The metric is overriding government interest in violating personal rights (including exercising beliefs), not strictly harm. If the government presents a solid case in the courts that an anti-discrimination law serves and overriding government interest, they get to violate your personal beliefs.<br /> <br /> And no, these are not solidly covered under the current law; that's why there's a fight over the bakery thing. It's a continuation of a larger fight because the way overriding interests are judged do not currently recognize sexual and gender identities as groups for consideration like race, religion, or biological sex.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is clearly not that case. </div> </div> </div>I don't see how the specifics of this case (or any other) disprove my assertion that laws enforce social norms in a fashion that inherently violates individual beliefs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nobody is being physically hurt, or really even particularly inconvenienced. </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of LGBTQ people in areas that don't have the large markets you're assuming are a constant that would beg to differ.<br /> <br /> If this really wasn't an issue for people... why are they getting into expensive legal battles just to get equal treatment in public spaces?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yet these individuals were forced to violate deeply and sincerely held beliefs purely because other people disagreed with them. </div> </div> </div>No. They chose to go into a line of work that does not accept their beliefs as justifications for their actions in the public sphere.<br /> <br /> When you operate a business that's a public accommodation, you deal with laws that dictate things you are and are not allowed to do. Just like any other business. There's regulations and laws you have to abide by whether your beliefs conflict with them or not. If you can't handle those restrictions, it is on you as a business owner to find something else to do.<br /> <br /> This really, really, really, is not about &quot;a difference of opinions.&quot; It's about people that either want to use belief to trump the law, or didn't understand the laws that govern the business they went into.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T01:58:18-07:00","id":988187,"title":"","content":"I don't complain about &quot;the others were worse&quot; but I am sick because I am reproached everytime, or in the most unexpected moment, about facts happened centuries ago I was born, but they say nothing about horrible things done by the others. That is a double standar to judge. Nobody can trust anybody who protest about any things, but keeps quiet like a tomb about others. Who is to teach lessons about intolerance and fanaticism with he has forgoten to respect human dignity, trying humilliate whose point of view is different? <br /> <br /> Move your butts and ask the end of anti-blasfemy Pakistani law and freedom for Asia Bibi and other Christians codemmed to death!! Demand building of Christian churchs to be allowed in Saud Arabian!! Protest againts tortures againts members of Falung Gong in China!! Why not to talk about Hillary Clinton's plans about a &quot;Christian spring&quot;? That is a hidden regalism (regalism is when the clergy is controlled by secular powers).<br /> <br /> Why can you talk about bad Christians but can't we tell about the rape epidemic in Rotterdam by &quot;Asians&quot;? (because that would be fomenting hate, wouldn't it be). We can't ask respect for other people and at the same time hostily and comptet againt Christianity is showed time after time. <br /> <br /> Oper Doors says 2015 has been the worst year for Christiany in the modern age, 7.100 Christians killed (20 victims each day!). Maybe now we should start to say it isn't the most convenient time to talk about Christian fanatics, but about anti-Christian fanaticism, about the menace of misotheism for the coexistence. Don't forget that killed Italian nun, sor Maria Laura Mainetti, or the attacks againts Norwegian Christian churchs for the 90's years (by black metal fans), or the bombs in the cathedral of la Almudena in Madrid or the Basilica of our Lady of the Pillar of Zaragoza, by the anarchist terrorist group Mateo Morral. These facts have happened in Europe, but in a near future it could also be in North American land. If we educate children againts racism, machism ( = male chauvinims), xenophobia and homophobia we also have to teach to say stop againts irrational anti-clericalism. The worst genocide en Spain wasn't by Inquisition, but the comunist forces in the 30's years. In only a month more people were killed by the rojos (red ones, communists) than Inquisition in all History. Do you still think anticomunism is ridicuolus? <br /> <br /> * Freedom means also responsability. You can't be always blaming capitalist system and all Caucasian rich people for all the troubles and injustices in the society. You also need sincere self-criticism sometime, (but without losing necesary self-esteem). A great power is a great responsabilty, higher power is higher responsability, but not always the powerful one is the guilty and the weak one is so innocent victim.<br /> <br /> * My advice about controversial threads is a good debate is like a chess game, where both players are trying to understand the opponent's mind to prepare the best answer. Try understand the rest of people, the same way a police study about criminal psychology or a psychiatrist the patient's mind. Understanding doesn't mean agreing. To convince isn't to force others giving you the reason. <br /> <br /> * I say again, Catholic Church built the Western civilitation. My English level isn't enough to explain it better, but orphanages, hospital and first universities were build by the Church. Christiany made possible the end of slavery, infanticide and child abandonment of unwished newborns. Scientific ideas were possible because the Christians didn't explain Nature with genies and fays, but a a set of rules or laws established in the Creation, and they could be discovered by investigation and reasoning. The good things by Christian religion have been more than the mistakes, incoherences and nonseses by our ancesters.<br /> <br /> And History shows us how who tried to live without Christian morality, were worse than Inquisition, for example the French Terror by Robespierre and the Jacobines, or Mao's cultural revolution. Mc Carthy's witch-hunt wasn't worse thant Stalin's purges. We should respect more our Christian roots, others need more reports and critiques than us. We should start to distrust who try warning us about Christian fanaticism because their medicine may be worse than the illness. Some Christians in the past did horrible things despite Gospel teachings, not by fault of Bible. Even the comunism is a bastard son of the Christian civilitation, where here the worker started to have got a dignity until then unknown. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 10-16-2016, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T05:57:40-07:00","id":988216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988083#post988083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This scenario is flawed. Despite certain people insisting otherwise, organizations aren't people, and the laws regarding discrimination are different for it. Nothing in the US anti-discrimination laws dictate that you have to violate your beliefs to provide public accommodations to an organization that works towards political ends you don't support outside of specific circumstances (the exceptions are generally around things like political campaigns to prevent a party/candidate from being silenced by lack of access to venues to speak to the public so if your local TV station gives access to the party the station owner favors, they have to give access to the opposing party/ies as well or just stay out of it).<br /> <br /> A bakery doesn't have to associate with a politically active organization that supports a cause the bakery owner disagrees with. Anti-discrimination laws in public accommodations apply to individuals, which means if there's a risk of discrimination it would only matter if members of the organization wanted a cake and the owner wanted to deny them due to their being members of said organization.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They're free too. There's no &quot;affirmative action&quot; provision here. If they're honestly busy and the same-sex couple doesn't order the cake far enough ahead of time? Tough on them. There's only an issue if they lie about how busy they are, such as refusing the same-sex couple on the grounds of being too busy, but then accept the order from a heterosexual couple that was in line next.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The line is already drawn in the law. As I've already pointed out, the fight is not where the line should be but in expanding the legal protections to acknowledge minorities that were not covered at the time the law was written. There's plenty of room to debate if the current line the law draws is the right one, but it's not the issue at hand in the real cases regarding anti-LGBTQ discrimination.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It is a very false assumption that &quot;99% of the time there is alternatives,&quot; and frankly it doesn't matter if it was true or not. The law isn't just for the majority of the population living in urban areas with large numbers of businesses to choose from. The law is also for small towns in the middle of nowhere without that competition when it comes to niche items.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, as a society, we do this all the time. Again, that's one of the purposes of having laws; to define when society says the norms of society override personal beliefs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is not the <b>Constitutional</b> limitation. We have Amendments that cover this. The metric is overriding government interest in violating personal rights (including exercising beliefs), not strictly harm. If the government presents a solid case in the courts that an anti-discrimination law serves and overriding government interest, they get to violate your personal beliefs.<br /> <br /> And no, these are not solidly covered under the current law; that's why there's a fight over the bakery thing. It's a continuation of a larger fight because the way overriding interests are judged do not currently recognize sexual and gender identities as groups for consideration like race, religion, or biological sex.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't see how the specifics of this case (or any other) disprove my assertion that laws enforce social norms in a fashion that inherently violates individual beliefs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There are a lot of LGBTQ people in areas that don't have the large markets you're assuming are a constant that would beg to differ.<br /> <br /> If this really wasn't an issue for people... why are they getting into expensive legal battles just to get equal treatment in public spaces?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No. They chose to go into a line of work that does not accept their beliefs as justifications for their actions in the public sphere.<br /> <br /> When you operate a business that's a public accommodation, you deal with laws that dictate things you are and are not allowed to do. Just like any other business. There's regulations and laws you have to abide by whether your beliefs conflict with them or not. If you can't handle those restrictions, it is on you as a business owner to find something else to do.<br /> <br /> This really, really, really, is not about &quot;a difference of opinions.&quot; It's about people that either want to use belief to trump the law, or didn't understand the laws that govern the business they went into.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make a pretty compelling argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T11:34:17-07:00","id":988316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988187#post988187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Move your butts and ask the end of anti-blasfemy Pakistani law and freedom for Asia Bibi and other Christians codemmed to death!! Demand building of Christian churchs to be allowed in Saud Arabian!! Protest againts tortures againts members of Falung Gong in China!!</div> </div> </div> </div>We do those things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988187#post988187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can you talk about bad Christians but can't we tell about the rape epidemic in Rotterdam by &quot;Asians&quot;? (because that would be fomenting hate, wouldn't it be). We can't ask respect for other people and at the same time hostily and comptet againt Christianity is showed time after time.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do those things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988187#post988187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I say again, Catholic Church built the Western civilitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rome built the West; the Church just continued what Rome did best - maintaining a bureaucracy and educational system in the face of governmental disintegration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988187#post988187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scientific ideas were possible because the Christians didn't explain Nature with genies and fays, but a a set of rules or laws established in the Creation, and they could be discovered by investigation and reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Greeks were doing that long before the Christians came around. It's no coincidence that literally all of the Church's scientific teachings were taught <i>from</i> translated Greek and Roman texts, or else texts by Arabic scholars. It isn't until very late that Christians produced much of scientific worth. There was no Dark Age, but it wasn't fantastic either. The Church set up universities, certainly, which quickly took on lives of their own, constantly straining against the oppressive restrictions on curriculum and freedom of expression imposed by the Church. It wasn't until we stopped letting Christianity rule in them that we started to see real progress.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988187#post988187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And History shows us how who tried to live without Christian morality</div> </div> </div> </div>I live without Christian morality everyday.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988187#post988187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">were worse than Inquisition, for example the French Terror by Robespierre and the Jacobines</div> </div> </div> </div>A problem almost entirely brought on by a sense of revenge, not a lack of Christian feeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988187#post988187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or Mao's cultural revolution. Mc Carthy's witch-hunt wasn't worse thant Stalin's purges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because McCarthy didn't have the complete dictatorial power that Stalin did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988187#post988187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should respect more our Christian roots</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Respect is earned, not given.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988187#post988187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Christians in the past did horrible things despite Gospel teachings, not by fault of Bible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, the Bible is driven by violence. It advocates for genocide and slavery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T11:47:16-07:00","id":988322,"title":"","content":"You live with a part of Christian morality althoug you don't notice. For example if you are againts sexual relations with youngers is because Christiany tought you to reject pedophilie/pederasty. Did you know these were allowed in the ancient Greece and Rome (and any current groups want it to be allowed again)? <br /> <br /> Yes, Cathollic Church have got more merits than nobody to earn most respect than nobody, and to be forgiven for the mistakes made centuries ago. (Hello!! we are Angel and Spike, two evil vampires from &quot;Buffy the vampire slayer&quot; serie who now we are in the side of the good guys and nobody reproach us our past crimes!) (Hi! I am Trunks, Sayan Vegeta's son, who destroyed whole worlds, but I haven't got to be showed as a potential menace and nobody asks me to apologize about the horrible things my ancestors did). I am sick about this Raven Queen* Syndrome, to be blamed for actions by a previous generation. (Raven Queen is a character from dolls &quot;Ever After High&quot;).<br /> <br /> Yes, Bible has got many episodes of violence, because humanity wasn't ready for the teachings of love to neighbor and mercy. But in the Bible there are examples of forgiveness, like the story of the prophet Jonas (the who was within a whale) or Gomer, the cheating wife of the prophet Oseas. (Oseas and Gomer, a true proof of love, a story to be told in the cinema). Sodoma had been forgiven with only ten just men living there.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, I take no pleasure in the death of the wicked, but rather that they turn from their ways and live.</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Turn!</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Turn from your evil ways! </span></span></span>&quot; Ezekiel 33 11.<br /> <br /> Sorry, you can't use the past to try manipulate by means of guilty feelings. This doesn't work like this. Self-criticism doesn't mean self-hate. Now it is time to say to defend freedom, tolerance and human rights, we must report the anti-Christian hate. Some horrible things in the past happened, but we learnt the lesson to not repeat the same mistakes. Now the priority is to defende Christians who suffer harassments and persecutions in another places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 10-16-2016, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:01:16-07:00","id":988379,"title":"","content":"Couple of things.<br /> <br /> First, we're all dealing with our own baggage. I as a Hungarian am dealing with the baggage of Hungary's role in both world wars, the nazism, the communism etc. I'm sternly against collective blaming, and I'm not responsible for misdeeds in the past, just as you aren't responsible for your countrie's or religions's past, but this is my country's baggage. I could cite contemporary events too, but don't want to delve too much into actual politics. Things happened or happening on the other side of the world is my problem too, to some extent, but I can only help those people as much as I could to dealing with their own baggage. What I want to say with this is citing horrible things from other countries won't invalidate the horrible things from our countries and our past. I won't take blame and regret for the communist or nazi resim's misdeeds, but I'm fully acknowledging both. Sorry, but the depredation of Catholics around the world won't nullify the Inquisition, or other horrible actions of the church. The thing is, regardless of religion, philosophy, or country, people as a crowd in general are horrible and stupid. Everyone did horrible things and it's equally right or wrong to bring up, or not bring up those in a discussion. I just think that responding to people who brings up your religion's or country's misdeeds with &quot;but the other party did the same, or worse and look what's happening in Pakistan!&quot; is not an answer. Yes, so what? The horrible things still happened from your side. That every community has a stain on their past and/or present doesn't mean those stains are cancelling out each other.<br /> <br /> As a sideonte, I particularly dislike it when anybody's opinion got smothered with dragging up the past. It's just the Nazi card from the list of fallacies. It invalidates your opinion, you can't really counterargue with it, because those things happened and usually it derails the topic absolutely. Inevitably somebody will get angry, then everybody starts hurling over accusations, past grievances and what-happened-to-my-uncle/insert anything and who-killed-the-most-people. It's just silly tribalism and not productive at all.<br /> <br /> Second point is about what we could or couldn't thank for Catholicism. I think it' just not that simple. There wasn't really such thing as non-religious science, or philosophy for a long time in Europe. Does that mean that every progress is due to the church or the religion itself? Don't think so. Those had a part in it to various extents depending on the actual thing, naturally, but it's just more complex than saying we should thank Catholicism for everything. I could understand the mentality. Everyone likes to think they had the most part in humanity's successes. Hell, we even see the same in any topic around here about the Technocracy! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's just how people works. We like to diminish our misdeeds and exaggerating successes, while doing the exact opposite to others.<br /> <br /> Third, sorry, but as I see it, Catholics around the world still acting in ways I'm sternly opposed, so, speaking about those things is just as right as speaking about things in the Middle-East, or China. Moreover, there's much more Catholic people around there (yet) than Muslim, so the things from them i don't agree with are having more influence on my life than things happening to Catholics in the Middle-East or Asia. It's somewhat selfish, but it's just how things work. That Poland getting closer and closer to outright ban abortion or that there in Hungary a lesbian couple got thrown out from a pub at one of the biggest universities in the capital and just the whole atmosphere here is, sorry, but more of my problem than what's happening in Pakistan to Catholics. However, we shouldn't neglect those things, partly because of we have <i>some </i>part of that region's problem, as everyone in the Western world has and because if we just shrug at them, then their problems will soon became our problems too.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I just want to say, that the recent pope is a very sympathetic figure to me, he mostly say good things and I find it somewhat amusing in a sardonic way that he got much heat from Catholics around the world.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":".  minor corrections 10-16-2016, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:12:09-07:00","id":988385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988322#post988322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You live with a part of Christian morality althoug you don't notice. For example if you are againts sexual relations with youngers is because Christiany tought you to reject pedophilie/pederasty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. See, here's the thing. I'm Jewish. Christian morality's good stuff is vastly stuff you just took from us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, Cathollic Church have got more merits than nobody to earn most respect than nobody, and to be forgiven for the mistakes made centuries ago. </div> </div> </div>The problem is that you want people to treat things as individual events that exist in a vacuum and ignore the continuity of history, and how past actions influenced the present; or at least when it comes to stuff you don't like.<br /> <br /> You're more than happy to want credit now for all the good stuff Christians have done throughout history, but you also want to reject all the bad reputation stuff that happened as counting.<br /> <br /> You don't get it both ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, Bible has got many episodes of violence, because humanity wasn't ready for the teachings of love to neighbor and mercy. </div> </div> </div>... yeah, we totally covered that in Leviticus (chapter 19 is where the phrase &quot;love thy neighbor&quot; shows up first). Sorry, but no, Christians didn't invent these, Jesus' whole beef with the Jewish leaders of his day was based around them being to legalistic about the wording of such things and less into the spirit of it; not that he was bringing something new that Judaism didn't already introduce as a cultural value.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some horrible things in the past happened, but we learnt the lesson to not repeat the same mistakes. Now the priority is to defende Christians who suffer harassments and persecutions in another places. </div> </div> </div>I don't think you have learned the lessons of the past, and will not repeat them. You talk just like countless Christians before you soon before a lot of non-Christians died; esp. with the idea that Christian persecutions are the ones that deserve priority. Why do a few thousand Christians deserve priority over millions of non-Christians facing similar hardships? Because making it all about Christian suffering without any care about anyone else in the world is the first step to blaming non-Christians and attacking them for your own problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:48:42-07:00","id":988472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988322#post988322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You live with a part of Christian morality althoug you don't notice. For example if you are againts sexual relations with youngers is because Christiany tought you to reject pedophilie/pederasty. Did you know these were allowed in the ancient Greece and Rome (and any current groups want it to be allowed again)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm against sexual relations with children because I believe in the rational, humanist viewpoint that children are incapable of consent, and my understanding of pedophilia as a psychological condition comes from the work of modern psychiatry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988322#post988322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Cathollic Church have got more merits than nobody to earn most respect than nobody, and to be forgiven for the mistakes made centuries ago. (Hello!! we are Angel and Spike, two evil vampires from &quot;Buffy the vampire slayer&quot; serie who now we are in the side of the good guys and nobody reproach us our past crimes!) (Hi! I am Trunks, Sayan Vegeta's son, who destroyed whole worlds, but I haven't got to be showed as a potential menace and nobody asks me to apologize about the horrible things my ancestors did). I am sick about this Raven Queen* Syndrome, to be blamed for actions by a previous generation. (Raven Queen is a character from dolls &quot;Ever After High&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>No one's saying that the church doesn't do positive things or have a positive impact in people's lives, but ignoring their transgressions, many of which still continue into the present day, is an act of moral negligence. When most people speak with derision about Catholicism or Protestantism, they aren't talking about the Crusades or the Inquisition. They're talking about the out-of-touch policy that persists and continues to harm people in the present day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988322#post988322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Bible has got many episodes of violence, because humanity wasn't ready for the teachings of love to neighbor and mercy. But in the Bible there are examples of forgiveness, like the story of the prophet Jonas (the who was within a whale) or Gomer, the cheating wife of the prophet Oseas. (Oseas and Gomer, a true proof of love, a story to be told in the cinema). Sodoma had been forgiven with only ten just men living there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you suggesting we should ignore the more worrying chapters of the Bible rather than recognize the Bible as a flawed moral thesis that got some things right and some things wrong?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988322#post988322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, you can't use the past to try manipulate by means of guilty feelings. This doesn't work like this. Self-criticism doesn't mean self-hate. Now it is time to say to defend freedom, tolerance and human rights, we must report the anti-Christian hate. Some horrible things in the past happened, but we learnt the lesson to not repeat the same mistakes. Now the priority is to defende Christians who suffer harassments and persecutions in another places.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do that. We also defend against the violations of Christian radicals who would deny us our rights at home. See acts of violence and policy against women's reproductive rights, anti-gay rhetoric and conversion therapy, and child abuse in the Catholic Church. We live in a nuanced world, and most of us can reflect that fighting injustice against Christian sects and countering regimes and crimes committed by people who belong to no religion or other religions aren't mutually exclusive or an indictment of those specific religions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:52:16-07:00","id":988476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_conta