 as your beliefs make you a second class citizen here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I wouldn't have worded it exactly that way(because I respect a few of the mods here, Darksider specifically), I do feel this thread has been thrown off it's intended course. I could be wrong, I guess. But I don't think so.<br /> <br /> Opinions are given, then dismissed if they don't fit the person's ideologies or narrative(from both sides), and largely why I--and a few others--have stayed out of this thread for the most part. There are some really good people on these forums, and I try to just associate with them. Fewer issues, in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:07:33-07:00","id":988819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988627#post988627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why are you trying to start shit, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lmao. You just posted this:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><u><b>&quot;Howdy and welcome! Run far, far away from this awful thread.&quot;</b></u></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> A few posts earlier as a response to someone new entering this thread. You have NO room to talk when it comes to &quot;starting shit.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T08:21:37-07:00","id":988868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=988819#post988819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lmao. You just posted this:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><u><b>&amp;quot;Howdy and welcome! Run far, far away from this awful thread.&amp;quot;</b></u></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> A few posts earlier as a response to someone new entering this thread. You have NO room to talk when it comes to &amp;quot;starting shit.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You just said you've avoided this thread because of the quality of the posting within, but somehow I shouldn't suggest someone do the same?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T14:56:25-07:00","id":989031,"title":"","content":"Honestly, i'm not that surprised that conservatives are feeling that way. I'm not saying that it's intentional from the majority of non-conservative, non-religious people. It's certainly not my intention to make anyone feeling as a second-class citizen. That would be grossly hypocrite. However, RPGs, as a conception at least arguably are somewhat left-leaning from the beginning. It's an escapist hobby, where you could be anyone and anything you want. Even D&amp;D, which earlier editions got a lot of heat for not being inclusive was that way and look at the trends from 2000 onward. Look at 5e or Pathfinder, the two biggest games on the market.<br /> <br /> Yes, the majority of the games had and has tropes that were &quot;conservative&quot; and positive (mostly), for example, the paladin class as a whole. However, the base assumption of D&amp;D was built on characters who are somewhat antisocial, non-comformist, don't give a shit about laws, or being actively vigilantes and basically outsiders in the society. In other words, adventurers. That was the very beginning of every RPG.<br /> <br /> (C)WoD in particular was always quite leftist, just look at the very core of the setting! Gothic-punk. Yes, it has mainly conservative splats too in every game and not just as adversaries, but as player splats. Regardless the games base assumptions are very leftist and always were. Look at the first (or any) edition of Vampire. Look at Mage, Werewolf, Changeling. It's not that surprising that most of the fans there are left-leaning too. I'm not saying that conservatives shouldn't play these games, or that there is no room for them in the games and in the community, because that's not true and it shouldn't be true, ever. But the core of these games has a leftist worldview, so it naturally attracts mostly leftist people.<br /> <br /> What I want to say with this, I don't want to make anybody feeling excluded. I have friends and acquaintances in every hobby who are right-leaning, or proudly conservative and I'm playing with them, and mostly we are good with each other, even when we're arguing about things sometimes. It's just more important that the other is a mostly nice person, not a jerk and we have shared interests. It's somewhat the nature of online social media, because the lack of personality, that these things got more heated than they would be IRL.<br /> <br /> However, that conservative gamers are feeling uncomfortable sometimes here is just not surprising to me. If I'd happen to go to a church sermon, for whatever reason, or to a gathering, or an event, or a site, where the majority of the people are conservative and right-leaning and/or religious, I'd feel uncomfortable, especially if they're trying to &quot;convert&quot; me and constantly explaining how i'm wrong. I think the best either side of the argument could do on a site like this, where the main theme and goal isn't politics, or worldviews, but a beloved hobby, is to just staying away from topics which are clearly for the other side, like this. Otherwise it will inevitably devolve to shouting and it's toxic to the community.<br /> <br /> I myself made the mistake above, so from now on, I'll try not to do it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":".  small corrections 10-17-2016, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T07:33:32-07:00","id":989347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=989031#post989031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, i'm not that surprised that conservatives are feeling that way. I'm not saying that it's intentional from the majority of non-conservative, non-religious people. It's certainly not my intention to make anyone feeling as a second-class citizen. That would be grossly hypocrite. However, RPGs, as a conception at least arguably are somewhat left-leaning from the beginning. It's an escapist hobby, where you could be anyone and anything you want. Even D&amp;D, which earlier editions got a lot of heat for not being inclusive was that way and look at the trends from 2000 onward. Look at 5e or Pathfinder, the two biggest games on the market.<br /> <br /> Yes, the majority of the games had and has tropes that were &amp;quot;conservative&amp;quot; and positive (mostly), for example, the paladin class as a whole. However, the base assumption of D&amp;D was built on characters who are somewhat antisocial, non-comformist, don't give a shit about laws, or being actively vigilantes and basically outsiders in the society. In other words, adventurers. That was the very beginning of every RPG.<br /> <br /> (C)WoD in particular was always quite leftist, just look at the very core of the setting! Gothic-punk. Yes, it has mainly conservative splats too in every game and not just as adversaries, but as player splats. Regardless the games base assumptions are very leftist and always were. Look at the first (or any) edition of Vampire. Look at Mage, Werewolf, Changeling. It's not that surprising that most of the fans there are left-leaning too. I'm not saying that conservatives shouldn't play these games, or that there is no room for them in the games and in the community, because that's not true and it shouldn't be true, ever. But the core of these games has a leftist worldview, so it naturally attracts mostly leftist people.<br /> <br /> What I want to say with this, I don't want to make anybody feeling excluded. I have friends and acquaintances in every hobby who are right-leaning, or proudly conservative and I'm playing with them, and mostly we are good with each other, even when we're arguing about things sometimes. It's just more important that the other is a mostly nice person, not a jerk and we have shared interests. It's somewhat the nature of online social media, because the lack of personality, that these things got more heated than they would be IRL.<br /> <br /> However, that conservative gamers are feeling uncomfortable sometimes here is just not surprising to me. If I'd happen to go to a church sermon, for whatever reason, or to a gathering, or an event, or a site, where the majority of the people are conservative and right-leaning and/or religious, I'd feel uncomfortable, especially if they're trying to &amp;quot;convert&amp;quot; me and constantly explaining how i'm wrong. I think the best either side of the argument could do on a site like this, where the main theme and goal isn't politics, or worldviews, but a beloved hobby, is to just staying away from topics which are clearly for the other side, like this. Otherwise it will inevitably devolve to shouting and it's toxic to the community.<br /> <br /> I myself made the mistake above, so from now on, I'll try not to do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually think CoD is a better choice for those attracted to a perpectives then OWOD, its more shades of grey, so I think rightwingers are better off in CoD, not that CoD is rightwing, its a just a cool setting which is less black and white.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:44:11-07:00","id":989544,"title":"","content":"Somewhat agree, but I won't say WoD is b&amp;w. It's more that the original writers and the games in general pretty much took a stance in the argument. Gothic-<i>punk. </i>The punk angle is a very important part of WoD and one of the reasons why i love it. There are viable player splats, that could be considered conservative. The Ventrue, the Tremere, Technocracy, Order of Hermes, Celestial Chorus, seelie Sidhe, seelie Trolls, Silver fangs, Shadow Lords, etc. Even then, those splats are frequently portrayed in a less-flattering way. Yes, the Ventrue run the Camarilla, but basically everyone hates them. The Technocracy evolved into a playable faction, but they are also the main antagonists of the game and again, not exactly portrayed in a flattering way most of the time. The OoH, pretty much like the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> The WoD games' base assumptions are not exactly that the MAN and the status quo are good things. It's not b&amp;w for me, the above splats received interesting books that portrayed them in positive light, or discussed their viewpoints and really the &quot;leftist&quot; splats were got their fair share of heat too. But its unarguable, IMO that the games and writers clearly took a stance and I'm happy they did, because it reverberates with my feelings and worldview and I think rpgs don't have to be absolutely neutral and &quot;politicaly&quot; sanitized every time.<br /> <br /> CoD, I think is indeed went to the opposite direction. It distanced itself from &quot;real-world garbage&quot;. It didn't want to make political or philosophical statements (ok, the later is not true, but not the kind Wod did) and portrayed the splats along different angles. The punk angle, as a base assumption of the setting is pretty much absent. Requiem doesn't really have a<br /> &quot;punk covenant&quot;, the Carthians are communists. The environmentalist angle didn't get a central stage in WWtF, if it got any. And so on.<br /> <br /> So, to sum up, I don't think WoD is b&amp;w and CofD is more grays, because WoD is just different shades of grays and blacks too. But the core setting and the games in WoD have a very prominent leftist and punk angle, while CofD is largely neutral on this and focusing more on the character's immediate life instead of these large questions about the world and society. Neither is better than the other and I think there's room and need for both.<br /> <br /> To reiterate my earlier post, I don't think conservative gamers should feel excluded in WoD communities. I have friends, who are pretty much pro-Tremere, pro Celestial Chorus or OoH, while I'm more a Brujah/Torreador person and we're good. One of them particularly hates the Hollow Ones, while they are my favorite mage group. It's just doesn't surprise me that the majority of WoD fans are leftists and if a conservative gamer voices her opinion in the various threads, she likely meets a tide of opposing opinions. I just think we should do it politely, because i equally don't like intolerance from either side. Frankly, I'm a leftist person, but I feel sometimes very fed up with the contemporary liberal trends, because I feel more and more that it's just another kind of radicalism. I guess the problem is not with the ideas themselves, but with human nature. <br /> <br /> In the end, I absolutely think if conservatives here have the courtesy of not telling us (aka leftist fans) constantly how we're wrong in our worldviews in various threads, then we should have the courtesy of not doing it for them in their &quot;safe space&quot; thread, so I apologize for doing that, however I'm upholding my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:54:35-07:00","id":989617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=989544#post989544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Requiem doesn't really have a &quot;punk covenant&quot;, the Carthians are communists. The environmentalist angle didn't get a central stage in WWtF, if it got any. And so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only really understand the concept of &quot;punk&quot; based on this sort of thing and TV Tropes, but the Circle of the Crone looks rather punk to me, especially in the second edition. A lot of it is about rejecting, overthrowing and burning the established order to the ground and one of their unifying philosophies is letting each other do they want, whatever that may be. They do seem closer to Sabbat Loyalists (without the Vaulderie in most cases) or Predator Kings than Anarchs though. It's more of a regressive, &quot;law of the jungle&quot; anarchy that they tend to stand for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T19:32:03-07:00","id":989670,"title":"","content":"The Carthians aren't just communists. They experiment with every kind of ideology, and refocus them on Kindred needs, and it is usually not nice. The stereotypes are fascist Carthians and communist Carthians, but there's more room for a variety of different methods within differing Assemblies of Carthians.<br /> <br /> It's weird, it seems to me that more conservative folks tend to prefer Old World of Darkness even if the Chronicles of Darkness seem less condemnatory of institutions we might associate with conservatism. EDIT: I originally referenced Awakening, but I think it's more fair to say that the Seers of the Throne and the Exarchs aren't strawmen but are better described as particular concepts and ideas turned towards oppressing the world. I think Paternoster is one that really helps sell that if you read it with an understanding that they aren't representative of all religious individuals but rather the idea of religion-as-oppression, which is not the same thing. Y'know, the people that a secularist and a Catholic would both condemn for misusing the Word of God to commit evil, yadda yadda.<br /> <br /> I don't really think there's a link, but maybe it's a generational thing? Though I've also noticed that lots of the conservative gamers I've spoken to that like Old World of Darkness tend to be interested in rehabilitating groups like the Technocracy. I wonder how many older folks who played oWoD were previously on the left but became more conservative over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 10-18-2016, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T19:59:10-07:00","id":989680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=989670#post989670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really think there's a link, but maybe it's a generational thing? Though I've also noticed that lots of the conservative gamers I've spoken to that like Old World of Darkness tend to be interested in rehabilitating groups like the Technocracy. I wonder how many older folks who played oWoD were previously on the left but became more conservative over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a plausible idea. After all there are powerful conservative-ish groups in WoD, who are arguably producing real results. They are just not generally painted in a very positive light, so the tendency of taking them and focusing on their redeeming qualities might be a good bet. I also think you're right about the generational thing. Generally, as people get older, they tend to value more things like safety, community, strong leadership, financial stability.<br /> <br /> As you get more and more things you don't want to lose, the spitting in the status quo's face starts seeming as a less and less good idea, after all. If I just look at my own country's revolutions in the past 200 years, it always started with young, angry intellectuals and frequently at the universities. People with &quot;radical&quot; ideas, strong discontent with the current state of things, energy and not too much to loose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 10-18-2016, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:40:48-07:00","id":989696,"title":"","content":"I would take strong issue with the idea that role playing games are inherently liberal or leftist. There is nothing about role playing as a hobby that has any politics leanings. The World of Darkness is leftist in many regards, though not completely nor to the degree that conservatives can't enjoy it. In fact, I have lots of very conservative friends who love playing WW games in the WoD and have for many years. Along the same lines, there are probably just as many right wing messages in the fantasy genre as there are left wing messages in the WoD but there is nothing contradictory about about leftists playing fantasy games.<br /> <br /> Many times when the bad guys in the WoD are conservative or the good guys are liberal, it is in ways which are completely nonpartisan in regard to modern political divides. For example, the original V:tM setting made an assumption that the players would probably side with the Anarchs against the oppressive elders. Well, in that regard, the players would be liberal from the perspective of vampire politics, but it's not as though many modern conservatives favor immortal feudalism, so the game is effectively non-partisan. Though I suppose that I have noticed that right wing gamers I know are more sympathetic to the Tremere and Ventrue, as examples. They like Gangrel too - rugged outdoorsmen, hunters, rural, and/or libertarian types. <br /> <br /> Werewolf was much more overtly leftist, especially on environmentalism (if one considers that leftist) and often gets very heavy handed inserting other left wing messages into the game. This has always bee something that troubled me about W:tA. It actually wouldn't take many slight tweaks in interpretation to make things in that game more friendly to conservatives, save for environmentalism which is pretty central to the setting.<br /> <br /> Mage: the Ascension... This is the most right wing game ever made. It is accidentally right wing, the left wing game designers didn't know they were making the most conservative game ever, but they did. How so?<br /> <br /> Well, the conservative gamers don't see the Technocracy as conservative and in fact, it isn't consvative at all. It is progressive, that is what it is at its very essence. In fact, it is like a right win conspiracy theory made manifest. A world spanning globalist group of progressives who want to force modern values on everyone, want to eliminate freedom of speech and expression, want to eliminate religion, want to establish a &quot;New World Order&quot; - they invented Info Wars the RPG. When I was young, I didn't know how left leaning the M:tA creators were and I was amazed at how right wing the game seemed to be. Even when I looked at the setting from the perspective of Technocractic good guys, it was a matter of thinking that progressives have done a lot of good in the past few hundred years.<br /> <br /> Subsequent WW games were relatively non-partisan save for a few minor biases on the part of authors that found their way in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T21:33:54-07:00","id":989714,"title":"","content":"I would say Roleplaying is generally somewhat of a liberal hobby. I mean, a huge part of the hobby involves literally putting yourself into the shoes of people who are parts of different creeds, races, nationalities, religions, etc, and thinking about the best ways to improve their lives. Further in many RPGs (like D&amp;D) the beliefs and values of &quot;Good&quot; groups and organizations tend to be more similar to liberal ideology than conservative ideology. It's also not uncommon in the least for games to offer people ways to safely explore sexuality or gender, and quite a few games have been making that a big thing.<br /> <br /> In general I don't think that the values of Conservative America (which I will note that Conservative America has decided that Donald Trump's racist, sexist, xenophobic remarks best match their own, personal values and beliefs) are really reflected that much in modern-day RPG culture. One can certainly draw comparisons to the Orcish hordes attacking Minis Tirith, and certainly there are a few gamelines that are created to cater towards conservatives, and there will inevitably be elements in RPGs that conservative gamers appreciate. But I think that on the whole most RPGs are intended to be more progressive than conservative especially on the social side of the scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:58:30-07:00","id":989905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=989696#post989696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf was much more overtly leftist, especially on environmentalism (if one considers that leftist) and often gets very heavy handed inserting other left wing messages into the game. This has always bee something that troubled me about W:tA. It actually wouldn't take many slight tweaks in interpretation to make things in that game more friendly to conservatives, save for environmentalism which is pretty central to the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the surface, I suppose, but you're also playing monsters that have a culture older than human civilization by a fairly large margin (or incomprehensibly older, in the case of the Ananasi, Mokole, and Rokea) and there were apparently some efforts by humans to make cities earlier than Catalhuyuk and other archeological sites that the Garou and Fera just entirely wiped out in the days of the Impergium, forcing a Traditional Economy or else for thousands of years until some figures said that the constant brutalization was a bad move and they stopped (still before human civilization and even people with pale skin were a thing). Very few of them trust humanity to do anything good with technological development, and so while they support a great many efforts to undo terrible shit, they also by and large don't want humans even living in cities, and also have problems with human numbers, such that some of them question the wisdom of not directly reducing human numbers. And, of course, the Ratkin are so completely gone that they want all human civilization to collapse and eat itself. Trying to rate the game on a left to right spectrum would be misleading, because it's too critical of everything humans do to really side with human politics in any but the loosest, most transient fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T09:26:09-07:00","id":989916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=989714#post989714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say Roleplaying is generally somewhat of a liberal hobby. I mean, a huge part of the hobby involves literally putting yourself into the shoes of people who are parts of different creeds, races, nationalities, religions, etc, and thinking about the best ways to improve their lives. Further in many RPGs (like D&amp;D) the beliefs and values of &amp;quot;Good&amp;quot; groups and organizations tend to be more similar to liberal ideology than conservative ideology. It's also not uncommon in the least for games to offer people ways to safely explore sexuality or gender, and quite a few games have been making that a big thing.<br /> <br /> In general I don't think that the values of Conservative America (which I will note that Conservative America has decided that Donald Trump's racist, sexist, xenophobic remarks best match their own, personal values and beliefs) are really reflected that much in modern-day RPG culture. One can certainly draw comparisons to the Orcish hordes attacking Minis Tirith, and certainly there are a few gamelines that are created to cater towards conservatives, and there will inevitably be elements in RPGs that conservative gamers appreciate. But I think that on the whole most RPGs are intended to be more progressive than conservative especially on the social side of the scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you only believe this because of your liberal biases. There is nothing more liberal about putting oneself int the mindset of different sorts of people, at least not liberal in any sort of of modern political sense. Is exploring gender and sexuality in an RPG liberal? Maybe, but that is just one possible idea you can explore with an RPG, that doesn't make the hobby inherently liberal.<br /> <br /> The whole post would be the equivalent of me saying that in RPG's you usually play the hero and since conservatives are good and liberals are bad, obviously RPG's are an nherently conservative hobby.<br /> <br /> In fact, as this thread shows, I think that many liberals are in need of a greater ability to get into the mindset of people unlike themselves, because they don't seem to understand conservatives much at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T09:48:18-07:00","id":989923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=989916#post989916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, as this thread shows, I think that many liberals are in need of a greater ability to get into the mindset of people unlike themselves, because they don't seem to understand conservatives much at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many people need this in general, regardless of political belief. The internet allows people to stay on sites that validate their beliefs, thus people rarely encounter people who disagree with their opinions.<br /> <br /> I also do not believe that the characters you play can predict which side of the political spectrum you fall on. I play a lot of &quot;conservative&quot; characters (Texas Ranger from Deadlands, Bronze Faction Sidereal from Exalted, any character from Dogs in the Vineyard, Dies Ultima Glasswalker* from WtA) and I vote Liberal. I don't play these characters as villains either. <br /> <br /> *Okay, this character was pretty liberal as she moved away her family to join a less militant pack. She still had strong ties to her family though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 10-19-2016, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:12:04-07:00","id":989940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=989923#post989923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Many people need this in general, regardless of political belief. The internet allows people to stay on sites that validate their beliefs, thus people rarely encounter people who disagree with their opinions.<br /> <br /> I also do not believe that the characters you play can predict which side of the political spectrum you fall on. I play a lot of &amp;quot;conservative&amp;quot; characters (Texas Ranger from Deadlands, Bronze Faction Sidereal from Exalted, any character from Dogs in the Vineyard, Dies Ultima Glasswalker* from WtA) and I vote Liberal. I don't play these characters as villains either. <br /> <br /> *Okay, this character was pretty liberal as she moved away her family to join a less militant pack. She still had strong ties to her family though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, trying to understand people who are different from themselves and to get into their mindset is something that would improve everyone and that everyone could stand to do more of. In fact, the world would be a better place if we all tried to understand each other a bit better and perhaps came to realize that we aren't so different. They is why RPG's are going to save the world <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, I agree about playing characters different from ourselves. I have long enjoyed playing religious characters and I am an atheist. I do wonder if playing a character very different from oneself and playing that character as a hero helps to increase our tolerance? I would like to think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:50:49-07:00","id":989962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=989916#post989916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that you only believe this because of your liberal biases. There is nothing more liberal about putting oneself int the mindset of different sorts of people, at least not liberal in any sort of of modern political sense. Is exploring gender and sexuality in an RPG liberal? Maybe, but that is just one possible idea you can explore with an RPG, that doesn't make the hobby inherently liberal.<br /> <br /> The whole post would be the equivalent of me saying that in RPG's you usually play the hero and since conservatives are good and liberals are bad, obviously RPG's are an nherently conservative hobby.<br /> <br /> In fact, as this thread shows, I think that many liberals are in need of a greater ability to get into the mindset of people unlike themselves, because they don't seem to understand conservatives much at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were (and actually still are - if you can believe it) religious groups that insist roleplaying games are a tool of Satan. In general the anti-RPG movement that appeared during the late 70's and early 80's, coupled with the &quot;RPGs are Satanic&quot; scare that occurred around that time pushed many RPG players and makers towards a more liberal mindset (conservative Americans were, again, literally saying the hobby was a tool of Satan).<br /> <br /> Growing up at the time myself, I remember attending church services and and having the pastor discuss how satanic D&amp;D was and how playing it would imperil your immortal soul by opening you up to demonic influences. I managed to keep my books hidden from my parents, but one of my friend's mothers found his stash of D&amp;D books and literally burned them all in their backyard. I finally took a few choice books (such as the Complete Paladin's handbook) and showed them to the pastor at the church and convinced him that it was a game where you play heroes who kill evil monsters and he backed off his anti-RPG stance.<br /> <br /> Still, throughout the 80's, 90's and even into the 00's, many RPG designers and writers tended towards being liberal due to the simple fact that their hobby had served as something of a punching bag by conservative religious America for so long. Religious conservatives (which made up a powerful block among conservative Americans) had made it clear that RPGs were something that was <i>evil.</i> Further, roleplaying games were traditionally aimed at a younger audience (teenagers and college kids), and younger people in the 90's and 00's were typically more liberal than conservative. So most RPG games tended to have a more liberal bias than a conservative one.<br /> <br /> In a very specific strain, it was not entirely unlike what the gay community of the 70's, 80's and 90's experienced. Conservative America made it very clear there was no room at their table for members of the LGBT community. As a result, many LGBT people became liberal by default - what other choice did they have? Why would they vote for people who literally called for their deaths? In a similar way, religious conservatives pushed the idea that RPGs were immoral, and so by default many RPG writers, designers and players tended towards being liberal because, well, why would you want to hang out with people who think your hobby is a tool of of the devil?<br /> <br /> So what ended up happening is that many RPG books were written by liberal leaning authors, were written to include liberal elements and were designed to attract liberal readers.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's starting to change today.<br /> <br /> By the middle of the 2000's, and certainly by today, RPGs are more mainstream and the idea that they are Satan's tools or can cause people to commit suicide is seen as fairly quaint by most Americans. Furthermore, the average age of RPG players has increased and as people get older they often also begin to become more conservative. Plus, many writers today (RPG authors or otherwise) often feel under siege by the liberal left which is frequently willing to attack them for writing material that isn't deemed as &quot;politically correct.&quot; So you're starting to see many newer RPGs and RPG authors have a more neutral stance or even lean slightly conservative in some respects.<br /> <br /> Still, I would say that the hobby as a whole continues to trend more liberal than conservative. If you doubt that, just look again at the title of this thread. Conservative roleplayers are getting more common, but they're still something of a rarity in the hobby when compared to liberal roleplayers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T11:10:12-07:00","id":989970,"title":"","content":"I neer said that the hobby wasn't more liberal, I believe that it is more liberal than conservative. That doesn't mean that RPG's are inherently a more liberal hobby than a conservative hobby. Just because more X do Y doesn't mean that Y is an inherently X hobby - you could say that about any activity and demographic. <br /> <br /> Even in the height of the D&amp;D is Satanism scare, most conservatives didn't believe that or care and even fewer do now. When you say what conservatives supposedly believe, you are talking about a minority of conservatives in every case, sometimes even a small minority. <br /> <br /> I don't have any statistics to back this up, but from my own observations, online forums are considerably more left leaning than the public is, and so when you have an already left leaning hobby (in practice, not in theory) then the forum is going to be dominated by members of the left. This is exacerbated by a general atmosphere of hostility expressed towards conservatives and conservatism - which you can easily see in this thread, and which causes people to stop using forums. It gets on your nerves after a while when you're trying to enjoy your hobby and constantly hear insults about how terrible you are. I have talked to a number of people who have lost interest in certain forums (this one or others) because of these attitudes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T11:46:16-07:00","id":989990,"title":"","content":"Again, I think roleplaying, in and of itself, encourages liberalism to some degree.<br /> <br /> It's similar to the way acting encourages liberalism (and not just because &quot;Hollywood forces people to be liberal.&quot;) Rather as actors travel around the world, work closely with people of different races, creeds and beliefs over long periods of time, do their best to accurately portray the lives of people who had very different beliefs and lifestyles from their own, it naturally tends to make people more socially liberal and accepting of different people. When you spend a year working on a movie about, I don't know, gay rights, and you work closely with a number of gay people, it's only natural to come away with a more accepting attitude towards gays.<br /> <br /> It's similar to how going off to college tends to make people more liberal - you spend your time living and learning and interacting with people who come from vastly different lifestyles than your own. It's only natural to become more accepting of people who don't believe the same things you do. Even at more conservative focused colleges, students are still often a bit more liberal after they've graduated than they were when they first started attending.<br /> <br /> Roleplaying as a medium is perhaps not as extreme as either of those, but there are still elements involved that encourage players to play as characters who are completely different from who and what they are in real life and who have completely different beliefs from their own. And when you're playing a half-orc and you face discrimination because of your physical appearance, even if it's just a game you're playing for fun, it can give you a new appreciation for other humans in real life who faced discrimination because of their appearance, or beliefs.<br /> <br /> So I would say that roleplaying naturally lends itself towards being a little more liberal than conservative, and then (as a result of some of the things I mentioned in my last post) many authors and players are specifically liberal which pushes the hobby as a whole firmly into the &quot;liberal&quot; category. This in turn makes the hobby less appealing to conservatives, so you have more and more &quot;liberal confirmation bias&quot; popping up throughout the hobby.<br /> <br /> Again, that's been changing lately, but I think even if RPGs as a whole were written by and for conservative gamers, the hobby itself still has a natural inclination towards getting people into a somewhat more socially liberal mindset.<br /> <br /> ---------------------<br /> <br /> And yeah, liberals can be loudmouthed jerk-off assholes too. To be fair though, when conservative America chooses to nominate someone like Donald Trump to represent themselves and to speak for them and their beliefs, when conservatives stand beside him, they are standing beside the hurtful things he has said.<br /> <br /> If conservatives don't like that, then they need to quite choosing for people like Donald Trump to speak for them. Seriously, it's because conservative Americans continually embrace racist, sexist, xenophobic people like Donald Trump that I can't stomach the thought of standing with conservatives or voting for conservatives, even though I actually lean conservative on many issues (gun control, Affirmative Action, Death Penalty, etc).<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, it's only natural that if you invite a loudmouthed, racist, xenophobic bigot into your house and let him sit at the head of the table and cheer at the things he says, for people to believe that you're also a racist, xenophobic bigot.<br /> <br /> This is the problem that so many conservatives face in America right now, and sadly there's no easy solution until the more moderate members stand up, speak out, and take their movement back from the radical extremists who hijacked it (now where have I heard <i>that</i> one before?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-19-2016, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:02:23-07:00","id":990004,"title":"","content":"Once again, your idea is based on straw manning conservatives as less open minded or tolerant, which is not the case. Go back and reread my example about playing the hero - that is how you sound to a conservative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:29:25-07:00","id":990025,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean, conservatives <i>did</i> decide that the person they feel best reflects the beliefs and values of American conservatism is someone who believes the majority of Mexican immigrants are rapists and murderers. Someone who is willing to call his own daughter, &quot;a piece of ass.&quot; Someone who has called for a ban on Muslim traveler's to the US... hell, I'm not even going to go on with him.<br /> <br /> So no. I don't think that &quot;open minded&quot; or &quot;tolerant&quot; are words I would use to describe Donald Trump or the people who chose for him to represent conservatives, the people who cheer for him at rallies or the people who will vote for him in November which is, again, a majority of Republicans and conservatives in America.<br /> <br /> Even prior to Donald Trump though, I don't know that open minded or tolerant are words I would have used to describe a Republican party. Remember that Mike Huckabee (a pretty major figure in conservative and Republican circles) has called for gays to be rounded up and put into camps so their &quot;disease&quot; can be studied. We still have the Republican party's platform openly opposing gay rights, women's rights, transgender rights, etc.<br /> <br /> If anything, over the last decade or so Republicans and conservatives have become even <i>less</i> tolerant and open minded than they were before (I mean, how else do you explain Donald Trump's rise to power in which he says things that ex-Republican presidents and presidential nominees find shocking and horrifying)?<br /> <br /> And keep in mind this all coming from someone who desperately wishes he could, in good conscience, vote for Republican candidates because I agree with a number of conservative principles and ideals. But so long as the Republican party and conservative Americans embrace repugnant radicals, there is simply no way I can bring myself to vote in solidarity with them.<br /> <br /> In short, the sorts of words I would tend to associate with roleplaying (open mindedness, tolerance, acceptance, etc) are not words I would use to describe modern-day conservative America. When conservative America begins to embrace those ideas, then I would probably be willing to consider myself a conservative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-19-2016, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:59:34-07:00","id":990087,"title":"","content":"To be fair a lot of conservatives have said they don't like or approve of Donald Trump in this thread. And on national television.<br /> <br /> But also to be fair as far as I can tell very few have shared their beliefs and reasons behind their beliefs, outside of the spiritualists and Mangle77.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T14:43:14-07:00","id":990105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=990087#post990087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair a lot of conservatives have said they don't like or approve of Donald Trump in this thread. And on national television.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true.<br /> <br /> Still, there's no denying that conservative America has chosen Trump to be its face. He is who the majority of conservatives support and cheer for. Sadly though this is not a huge surprise - unfortunately the Republican party (and conservative America) has a fairly checkered past of appealing to and welcoming racists, sexists and bigots into their midst in exchange for more votes and money. Donald Trump is nothing more than the end result of the policies that the Republican party has been pursuing for decades.<br /> <br /> So it <i>is</i> nice that some conservatives are willing to decry Donald Trump and those who stand by their principles and against him have my respect (as I pointed out earlier in the thread, Kasich's actions during this election have won my highest respect in that regard) - it's just a darn shame those same conservatives didn't, years ago, start decrying the Republican party's policies and statements that paved the way for the rise of someone like Mr. Trump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:11:19-07:00","id":990415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=990004#post990004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, your idea is based on straw manning conservatives as less open minded or tolerant, which is not the case. Go back and reread my example about playing the hero - that is how you sound to a conservative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conservatives are less open minded and tolerant. Or more precisely, conservative beliefs correlate with close-mindedness and intolerance. There's multiple studies in neuroscience that back that claim and a wealth of polling data in places like the US and Europe that show this again and again.<br /> <br /> There's the analysis of the General Social Survey from the present back to 1972 (<a href=\"http://fivethirtyeight.com/features/are-white-republicans-more-racist-than-white-democrats/\" target=\"_blank\">seen here on 538</a>) where white Republicans are more likely to answer positively on questions such as &quot;Are blacks more lazy than hard-working?&quot; or &quot;Do blacks 'lack the motivation to pull themselves out of poverty?&quot; or even &quot;Do you oppose a close relative marrying a black person?&quot;. The American National Election Study finds the same kind of split (<a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/clinton-wasnt-wrong-about-the-deplorables-among-trumps-supporters/2016/09/12/93720264-7932-11e6-beac-57a4a412e93a_story.html?utm_term=.36ae884476d5\" target=\"_blank\">WAPO article here</a>) where &quot;those with negative racial stereotypes consistantly favored Republican candidates - any of them - over any Democratic candidate in hypothetical matchups&quot;. Or the <a href=\"https://texaspolitics.utexas.edu/set/banning-muslims-entering-us-june-2016#party-id/\" target=\"_blank\">Reuters poll</a> from this summer that shows Republicans support bans on Muslims entering the US by enormous margins over Democrats and Independents; there's <a href=\"http://www.publicpolicypolling.com/main/2015/08/trump-supporters-think-obama-is-a-muslim-born-in-another-country.html\" target=\"_blank\">Public Policy Polling</a> that show &quot;66% of Trump's supporters believe that Obama is a Muslim to just 12% that grant he's a Christian. 61% think Obama was not born in the United States to only 21% who accept that he was. And 63% want to amend the Constitution to eliminate birthright citizenship, to only 20% who want to keep things the way they are.&quot;<br /> <br /> This stuff makes up modern conservatism, not just here but across the world. There's the Lord Ashcroft polls post-Brexit in the UK which gives a stark picture of the beliefs of your average Leave voter as someone who hate immigration and multiculturalism. Or the rise of <a href=\"http://www.economist.com/blogs/graphicdetail/2016/05/daily-chart-18\" target=\"_blank\">extreme right-wing</a> parties across Europe, almost all focusing on openly racist policies such as the Golden Dawn in Greece of Jobbik in Hungary; with the threat of voters leaving the traditional center-right parties causing pandering to racists this stuff becomes normalized in political discourse.<br /> <br /> My belief is that this all comes back to scientific discoveries with regards to differences in how our brains process information. There's <a href=\"http://blogs.discovermagazine.com/intersection/2011/09/07/your-brain-on-politics-the-cognitive-neuroscience-of-liberals-and-conservatives/\" target=\"_blank\">evidence</a> that liberal-thinking correlates to &quot;increased gray matter volume in the anterior cingulate cortex&quot;, whereas conservatism correlates to &quot;increased volume of the right amygdala&quot;. The article does a far better job explaining it than I can, but the short of it is that conservatives process information through emotional reactions, with special sensitivity to fear and disgust, while liberals are better able to manage uncertainty and control emotions when making decisions. I'm going to quote one piece in full, bolding the most relevant part:<br /> <br /> &quot;Past studies, as well as the ones mentioned here, have shown that liberals are more likely to respond to \u201cinformational complexity, ambiguity, and novelty\u201d. Considering the role of the ACC in conflict monitoring, error detection, and pattern recognition/ evaluation, this would make perfect sense. Liberals, according to this model, would be likely to engage in more flexible thinking, working through alternate possibilities before committing to a choice. Even after committing, if alternate contradicting data comes along, they would be more likely to consider it. Sound familiar? <b>This is how science works, and why there might be so many correlations between scientific beliefs (</b>and lesser belief in religion<b>) and tendency to be liberal.</b> Is this a hard and fast rule? Of course not. But you can see the group differences overall.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is where I was trying to bring discussion earlier with you, because it's the heart of how difficult it becomes to have meaningful discussion. I'd really like to understand how conservatives see their own decision-making process introspectively, because so often it seems like this quote sums it up:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=983493#post983493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nobody is qualified to determine what beliefs are objectively erroneous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T00:06:37-07:00","id":990832,"title":"","content":"Formerly conservative gamer here. Checking in and wanting to say a few things. <br /> <br /> First some backstory for those who don't know me. I used to be a huge poster for a while, even ran the Shadownessence Mage the Awakening forum and secured the first fan interview with Bill Bridges back then. <br /> <br /> Also was a huge American Libertarian at the time. My opinions have changed since then, even though I still have some views that are very much in the American Right Wing. <br /> <br /> How did the rest change? Mainly it happened because I started to listen. I have always been a poor, bisexual, white, cisgender male who has had his share of discrimination against myself due to my sexuality and hobbies (such as RPGs and the like)<br /> <br /> But after listening to my minority/female friends I started to realize something... it didn't matter who many times my goth/geek self was picked on or discriminated against, because at the end of the day I could hide those facts about myself if I so wished.<br /> <br /> And despite what my taste in clothing, music, Hobbies were I still had it easier than many of my compatriots because the system was designed for me.<br /> <br /> And the most insidious part of the whole thing was that society had been making me think that without even trying.<br /> <br /> Gay men are effeminate. Lesbians are manish. Women like RomComs. Men don't cry. Trans people are just people who like to wear the opposite genders clothing. Boys like action figures, girls like dolls. <br /> <br /> All an insidious set of lies we are told so that we know our role. It's all based on tradition. On what traditionally things have been. And it digs into your brain without you even realizing it. It shapes your entire world view without you noticing. <br /> <br /> My own wake up call came with my father telling me that calling someone &quot;faggot&quot; was fine because, growing up he knew a gay hairdresser who called himself that. No self awareness that the man was probably trying to avoid others calling him that in a hurtful manner. <br /> <br /> The semi-recent GamerGate controversy only strengthened my new convictions. As I watched other people inform me that my significant other of 9 years MUST be cheating on me because she was a nude model. And then when I reflected that claim and agreed with another user who I had disageed with on almost every other political thing I was called a &quot;cuck&quot; who loved his liberal &quot;hug box&quot;<br /> <br /> So to my conservative friends I say this... I know you aren't the hateful racist, sexist , homophobic, transphobic, ect that pop culture tries to say you are. But look at the people who say similiar things as you and decide if you want them representing you. Because it's the Internet and the loudest voice come first. <br /> <br /> And to my liberal friends I ask this, don't be to harsh on our conservative brethren. They do mean well. They just don't get that what they want can be considered oppressive to others. <br /> <br /> Because the one thing I've learned in my near 40 years on this planet is this... We can always learn more","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2704,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","user":"DeimosMasque","date":". 10-21-2016, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T07:46:52-07:00","id":990953,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't think that too many RPGs would really have much of a left or right wing bias.<br /> <br /> Probably more left wing if anything, almost purely as I think left wing is where you would tend (tend) to find more of the intense people who like sitting indoors with friends rolling dice, experiencing intense emotions about imaginary things, rather than the more outgoing, lighthearted and enthusiastic personalities who are well adjusted and at home in their communities, outdoorsy and sportsy, open to meeting new people, keen on experience and common sense more than theory, who you would tend find on the right wing.<br /> <br /> Myself, pretty centrist-independent is about the only way to view my politics. I'm very skeptical about both the markets and enlightened self interest on the one hand and about left wing movements and class identity on the other, and I'm an agnostic (one who believes that at least all religions are myths, and at most there is no deity) who is very secularist in politics.<br /> <br /> I would say if anything I'm on the right wing side, because I tend to view my responsibility as much more of a defender of the groups I belong to against myths towards them than to be self critical towards my own groups and celebrate other groups. I tend to be more critical of people who believe denigrating myths about their my group than people who believe overly glorifying myths about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T21:58:29-07:00","id":993316,"title":"","content":"Man, I am getting more liberal as I age, but I'm surprised to see so many liberals giving Conservatives a hard time on here. I think it's obvious the hobby isn't inherently political. I think I've actually played with more Conservatives than Liberals in the hobby, especially growing up.<br /> <br /> I do think knowing more people with different views is helpful. My wife is a Moderate Republican, I never viewed our sexuality as guarantee on politics or felt it should be an indicator. Obviously we wanted to get married, but Foreign policy and Economics can matter a lot too. We game regularly with 2 very conservative Christians, but also a very liberal Christian, and a very liberal atheist. Mostly we get along and all complaints go down to playing style. Unless the argument can be said that Rail-roading is politically leaned, we don't have an issue.<br /> <br /> Sure sometimes Politics comes up, but it's mostly ignored since only two of us really enjoy talking about it at length. I've never felt the hobby was anti-conservative, and neither did I get that impression from anyone else. I mean they have become much more pro-gay and with more art that is not fanservice with a diverse cast, but to call that liberal seems unfair toward conservatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T04:48:34-07:00","id":993428,"title":"","content":"I use the fantasy to try explain softer my point of view. In my fiction works the mages and mutants (humans with superpowers) are an allegory of the businessmen class. A great power is a great responsability, and you can suposse higher power means higher responsability, but anytimes it isn't most powerful one's fault, nor the weak one is the innocent victime. And don't trust who say they want to protect the defenseless (mugless/ftatscans) masses againtes the ones with a superior power. The businessmen are like wizards who affirm their power is got by talent and training, but they are envied and feared by the people (sometimes the fear is justificied), and the crusader templars/witch hunters/D&amp;D clerics are like the pro-estatists who fights againts abuse by arcane spellcasters, but the people have to obey their rules. Other example is the marvel first civil war... can you trust people with special powers without control by goverment, or maybe can't you trust goverment who controll too much?<br /> <br /> * I am very used to some negative stereotypes, they aren't offensive for me, only boring, but the double standar is annoying for me. You can't try humilliate anybody with hard criticism, but after be quiet about the actions by others. Sorry, but here the media in my country tell a different view of the reality. The thins I have readen in some Spanish-languange facebook group is totally different you can read here. <br /> <br /> * In this last week I have seen some things, a girl who was banned in a facebook group because she published really obscene pictures to hurt (worse than that Charlie Hebbo's cover with the holy trinity), or I have readen a woman who was attacked in United Kingdom by a English man because she was... talking Spanish languange!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T08:34:56-07:00","id":993513,"title":"","content":"Conservative, Catholic, Curz supporter on the Trump train, looking for other like minded conservative thinking people. And if you haven't experienced the liberal bias from friends you role play with let me tell you its a lose lose situation. Be polite and tolerate their hubris and your stuck dealing with it, open your mouth and explain, not argue, just explain and suddenly your a right wing bigot.<br /> <br /> Thing is, its epidemic in the culture too, ever read Pentex the Werewolf the Apocalypse source book? Don't let me spoil it for you, but they really road the Big Business is evil train. (Never mind Big Business is liberal)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12570-anathema_dreamer","name":"Anathema_Dreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T09:15:31-07:00","id":993529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anathema_Dreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=993513#post993513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Be polite and tolerate their hubris</b> and your stuck dealing with it, open your mouth and explain, not argue, just explain and suddenly your a right wing bigot.<br /> <br /> Thing is, its epidemic in the culture too, ever read Pentex the Werewolf the Apocalypse source book? Don't let me spoil it for you, but they really road the Big Business is evil train. (Never mind Big Business is liberal)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You really need to go back and