st\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use the fantasy to try explain softer my point of view. In my fiction works the mages and mutants (humans with superpowers) are an allegory of the businessmen class. A great power is a great responsability, and you can suposse higher power means higher responsability, but anytimes it isn't most powerful one's fault, nor the weak one is the innocent victime. And don't trust who say they want to protect the defenseless (mugless/ftatscans) masses againtes the ones with a superior power. The businessmen are like wizards who affirm their power is got by talent and training, but they are envied and feared by the people (sometimes the fear is justificied), and the crusader templars/witch hunters/D&amp;D clerics are like the pro-estatists who fights againts abuse by arcane spellcasters, but the people have to obey their rules. Other example is the marvel first civil war... can you trust people with special powers without control by goverment, or maybe can't you trust goverment who controll too much?<br /> <br /> * I am very used to some negative stereotypes, they aren't offensive for me, only boring, but the double standar is annoying for me. You can't try humilliate anybody with hard criticism, but after be quiet about the actions by others. Sorry, but here the media in my country tell a different view of the reality. The thins I have readen in some Spanish-languange facebook group is totally different you can read here.<br /> <br /> * In this last week I have seen some things, a girl who was banned in a facebook group because she published really obscene pictures to hurt (worse than that Charlie Hebbo's cover with the holy trinity), or I have readen a woman who was attacked in United Kingdom by a English man because she was... talking Spanish languange!!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You ignored the topic ban you were issued and told the next suspension would be permanent. You can appeal the ban using the contact link posted in the forum rules.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:24:46-07:00","id":993665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=989696#post989696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage: the Ascension... This is the most right wing game ever made. It is accidentally right wing, the left wing game designers didn't know they were making the most conservative game ever, but they did. How so?<br /> <br /> Well, the conservative gamers don't see the Technocracy as conservative and in fact, it isn't consvative at all. It is progressive, that is what it is at its very essence. In fact, it is like a right win conspiracy theory made manifest. A world spanning globalist group of progressives who want to force modern values on everyone, want to eliminate freedom of speech and expression, want to eliminate religion, want to establish a &quot;New World Order&quot; - they invented Info Wars the RPG. When I was young, I didn't know how left leaning the M:tA creators were and I was amazed at how right wing the game seemed to be. Even when I looked at the setting from the perspective of Technocractic good guys, it was a matter of thinking that progressives have done a lot of good in the past few hundred years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted for truth. I wouldn't go so far as to say that it's the most right wing game ever \u2014 the Traditions are generally all over the map in terms of political persuasions, but tend toward moderate/liberal views \u2014 but yeah, Sergeant Brother is dead-on about the Technocracy. Ironically, I know a number of liberals who are convinced that the Technocracy represents <i>conservatives</i>, rather than everything conservatives despise. I can only explain it as them buying into stereotypes of conservatism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:48:55-07:00","id":993676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=993665#post993665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quoted for truth. I wouldn't go so far as to say that it's the most right wing game ever \u2014 the Traditions are generally all over the map in terms of political persuasions, but tend toward moderate/liberal views \u2014 but yeah, Sergeant Brother is dead-on about the Technocracy. Ironically, I know a number of liberals who are convinced that the Technocracy represents <i>conservatives</i>, rather than everything conservatives despise. I can only explain it as them buying into stereotypes of conservatism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. There's definitely some truth to that, and I think the Technocracy can definitely be filtered through the lens of conservatives' worst fears about neo-liberalism, &quot;nanny states&quot;, and globalization; but I think the problem with looking at any game through a lens of conservative/liberal warfare is that our understanding of those words are so oversimplified.<br /> <br /> It can definitely be perceived through the lens of a globalist One World philosophy that reflects the worst fears of libertarian leaning conservatives. It could be seen by Christian conservatives as a shocking indictment of scientific rationalism. Reagan era conservatives might see it as a stark reflection of the sort of bureaucratically heavy conceptions of China and the USSR. Communal anarchists might feel the same way. But liberals concerned about social rights and personhood could see it as a reflection of what happens when private enterprises are allowed to consolidate power at the expense of the people (the Technocracy could definitely be seen through the lens of Randian utopias). Others might even conceivably see it as a reflection of social conservatives wanting to subvert personal freedoms for the sake of a Christian-values state (with scientific rationalism as a contrary metaphor).<br /> <br /> It <i>can </i>be about those things, but I don't think it inherently is, and I think that's the strength of the game. It's so prone to flexible interpretation. If the core game is inherently about anything, it's the risk of totalitarianism (which I think most conservatives and liberals are afraid of) and the banality of evil that comes from believing that your ends justify the means. Wanting to shape the world in your image because you believe you're right and everyone will benefit is not a value exclusive to conservatives or liberals, and it's not a core value of either ideology. The fact that the world the Traditions ruled over was a clusterfuck too suggests to me that it's not about conservatism vs. liberalism. It's about the threat of unwavering power and self-assured self-justification regardless of ideology. The Technocracy's attempt to steamroll over marginalized groups (including pagans, an indigenous alliance, sexual &quot;deviants&quot;, and counterculture hackers) for the sake of a pure ideology could similarly be seen as an indictment of the xenophobia expressed by right wing nationalists.<br /> <br /> But I think the perspective that Sgt. Brother posits isn't about the values of conservatism vs. the values of liberalism. It's about the values most people share filtered through the most paranoid, straw man ideology of the most radical conservatives around. Demonizing your opponent is the easiest way to convince yourself of the absolute truth of your core values. Most progressives don't want to eradicate religion or make abortions mandatory, and they believe strongly in the right to free speech (along with the right to criticize the free speech of others). Viewing it through an &quot;Info Warsr&quot; prism doesn't mean asking any serious questions about your own ideology. It just reinforces the ideology you already have, and that strikes me as counterproductive to the strength of roleplaying games like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-26-2016, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:48:50-07:00","id":993713,"title":"","content":"I think there's an inherent problem in taking a line that's 15 - 20 years old and filtering it through the perception of the modern, deeply divided political spectrum. It's particularly easy to do when you're working with an exaggerated version of a particular group of people. But just as a thought experiment, I think I can adapt the Technocratic Union to fit the most exaggerated and demonized view of modern conservatism.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union isn't a neoliberal global order. It's privatized business. These aren't people who have been elected or appointed by elected officials. They're the sort of exceptional individuals that, according to Rand, have the right to cross boundaries because of their exceptionalism. What they practice isn't science either. It just resembles science, and they're happy to game the numbers in their favor, knowing that the parasite masses are too dumb to know better. Of course they aren't poisoning the environment. These statistics confirm it. Our schools run better than those supported with tax payer money. Trust us. We have a documentary to prove it. Iteration X promotes the establishment of a purely mechanized work force, and even though you'll be laid off because a robot can do your job cheaper, it will be fine. Trust us. The Wall Street Boys in the Syndicate aren't parasites. They're daring proponents of the free market. Ditto the Progenitors. Public health care creates slum hospitals. We can replace your heart, your brain, anything, just as long as you can afford to pay for it. The New World Order promotes fair and balanced news. The Void Engineers promote imperialism abroad <i>for the good of everyone</i>. Why haven't we exposed the rest of the world to our wonderful technologies? Because they just aren't ready for it yet. Sure, we're populists, but we're the only ones visionary enough to understand our toys.<br /> <br /> The Traditions are the disenfranchised, bulldozed by the three headed beast of social, cultural, and economic conservatism. The Akashic Brotherhood? The Chinese who are <i>not our friends</i>. Cultists of Ecstasy? Queers and cucks. The Euthanatos? Fuck you. If you're going to die, it's going to be because the medicine was too expensive. Suicide is a sin. The Celestial Chorus? Hippies and pacifists. The Dream Speakers? You mean those fucks marching on our pipelines? Run them over with your heavy machinery or lock them up for acts of eco-terrorism. The Order of Hermes? Satanists. Ditto the Verbena. The VA? Digital terrorists.<br /> <br /> After all, they don't despise the Traditions, but they don't think that &quot;minorities&quot; should be given preferential treatment over &quot;regular people&quot;. Sometimes marginalized people need to be sacrificed for the good of everyone.<br /> <br /> Is that what I believe conservatives are like? Hell no. But it's about as nuanced a view as liberals being God-hating, baby-killing, free speech censoring conspiracy globalists. That said, I do think the Technocracy more accurately reflects a massive global, vertically integrated, free market conglomerate mixed with a conservative think tank than it does a shadow government. But YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-26-2016, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T15:52:01-07:00","id":994252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=993713#post993713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's an inherent problem in taking a line that's 15 - 20 years old and filtering it through the perception of the modern, deeply divided political spectrum. It's particularly easy to do when you're working with an exaggerated version of a particular group of people. But just as a thought experiment, I think I can adapt the Technocratic Union to fit the most exaggerated and demonized view of modern conservatism.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union isn't a neoliberal global order. It's privatized business. These aren't people who have been elected or appointed by elected officials. They're the sort of exceptional individuals that, according to Rand, have the right to cross boundaries because of their exceptionalism. What they practice isn't science either. It just resembles science, and they're happy to game the numbers in their favor, knowing that the parasite masses are too dumb to know better. Of course they aren't poisoning the environment. These statistics confirm it. Our schools run better than those supported with tax payer money. Trust us. We have a documentary to prove it. Iteration X promotes the establishment of a purely mechanized work force, and even though you'll be laid off because a robot can do your job cheaper, it will be fine. Trust us. The Wall Street Boys in the Syndicate aren't parasites. They're daring proponents of the free market. Ditto the Progenitors. Public health care creates slum hospitals. We can replace your heart, your brain, anything, just as long as you can afford to pay for it. The New World Order promotes fair and balanced news. The Void Engineers promote imperialism abroad <i>for the good of everyone</i>. Why haven't we exposed the rest of the world to our wonderful technologies? Because they just aren't ready for it yet. Sure, we're populists, but we're the only ones visionary enough to understand our toys.<br /> <br /> The Traditions are the disenfranchised, bulldozed by the three headed beast of social, cultural, and economic conservatism. The Akashic Brotherhood? The Chinese who are <i>not our friends</i>. Cultists of Ecstasy? Queers and cucks. The Euthanatos? Fuck you. If you're going to die, it's going to be because the medicine was too expensive. Suicide is a sin. The Celestial Chorus? Hippies and pacifists. The Dream Speakers? You mean those fucks marching on our pipelines? Run them over with your heavy machinery or lock them up for acts of eco-terrorism. The Order of Hermes? Satanists. Ditto the Verbena. The VA? Digital terrorists.<br /> <br /> After all, they don't despise the Traditions, but they don't think that &amp;quot;minorities&amp;quot; should be given preferential treatment over &amp;quot;regular people&amp;quot;. Sometimes marginalized people need to be sacrificed for the good of everyone.<br /> <br /> Is that what I believe conservatives are like? Hell no. But it's about as nuanced a view as liberals being God-hating, baby-killing, free speech censoring conspiracy globalists. That said, I do think the Technocracy more accurately reflects a massive global, vertically integrated, free market conglomerate mixed with a conservative think tank than it does a shadow government. But YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are kernals of truth to some of it. Some liberals, not all, about 2300 roughly which is tiny amount, signed a petitition rescently to shut down and censor a showing of the red pill documentary in Australia rescently, which worked, which forced the people who wanted to watch it to try and find a new venue, which was more expensive.<br /> <br /> Just one example, the stereotypes each side has for the other, doesn't come from no where, they're not universal truths, no, but their not fabrications out of thin air either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T17:08:26-07:00","id":994291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=993529#post993529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You really need to go back and read the Terms of Use you agreed to when you joined. This thread is not about insulting people or making group attacks, regardless of political affiliation. You are getting off with a warning this time, don't do it again.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Group attacks against conservatives have been pretty much ubiquitous in this thread, created specifically for conservative gamers, and I yet haven't seen one warning issued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T17:29:23-07:00","id":994294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=994252#post994252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are kernals of truth to some of it. Some liberals, not all, about 2300 roughly which is tiny amount, signed a petitition rescently to shut down and censor a showing of the red pill documentary in Australia rescently, which worked, which forced the people who wanted to watch it to try and find a new venue, which was more expensive.<br /> <br /> Just one example, the stereotypes each side has for the other, doesn't come from no where, they're not universal truths, no, but their not fabrications out of thin air either.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sort of false equivalency doesn't help the conversation.<br /> <br /> According to <b>conservative</b> principles what happened in Australia is exactly how things are supposed to happen. Instead of the government coming in to decide who can watch what, a private business reacted to individuals on both sides exercising their right to free speech, and then made what they felt was the best financial decision for their business.<br /> <br /> If anything, this is an excellent example of, &quot;we don't need the nanny state to try and force social issues; the market will handle it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>This is not censorship</u> or a violation of the freedom of speech. Just because the makers of the film have the right to make their film doesn't mean any privately owned cinema has screen it. The freedom of speech does not mean you get to force other people to provide you a platform to speak from.<br /> <br /> Liberals using freedom of speech and techniques like threatening boycotts to pressure the market is not a fabrication (of course all political activists do this). Turning it into more than that is. And it only fuels liberal stereotypes of conservatives; like that they can't admit when the public has rejected their ideals so they have to construct the idea that liberals aren't playing fair rather than acknowledge that in the free exchange of ideas liberals might be winning fair and square.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T17:45:37-07:00","id":994301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=994291#post994291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Group attacks against conservatives have been pretty much ubiquitous in this thread, created specifically for conservative gamers, and I yet haven't seen one warning issued.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Then you didn't read my warning closely enough. Use the flag function if you believe a post has violated the rules. Red text posts are also not to be quoted and/or discussed, continue to do so and your posting privileges will be suspended. This is not a subject open for debate.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T17:50:35-07:00","id":994304,"title":"","content":"The free market is great until the outcomes it generates don't conform to your expectations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T18:04:45-07:00","id":994306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=994252#post994252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are kernals of truth to some of it. Some liberals, not all, about 2300 roughly which is tiny amount, signed a petitition rescently to shut down and censor a showing of the red pill documentary in Australia rescently, which worked, which forced the people who wanted to watch it to try and find a new venue, which was more expensive.<br /> <br /> Just one example, the stereotypes each side has for the other, doesn't come from no where, they're not universal truths, no, but their not fabrications out of thin air either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not. That's entirely my point. &quot;Liberalism&quot; and &quot;conservatism&quot; are such fickle and ambiguous terms that they don't really account for much, and the very ambiguous understanding of American conservatism and liberalism doesn't in any way reflect understanding of those terms abroad. The Info Wars perspective of jack booted UN troopers burning copies of The Fountainhead and sending Christians to the ovens is a grossly exaggerated take on neoliberalism. But, despite (very, <i>very) </i>technically falling under the umbrella of &quot;liberalism&quot; in America, neoliberalist ideals are largely anathema to most people who would prescribe as anarchists, socialists, or communists. Just look at what's happening with the GOP right now. It's falling apart because it's maintained a &quot;big tent&quot; coalition that unites together social, cultural, and fiscal conservatives. But these groups have become so dramatically radicalized that many of them see the other factions as repugnant. A libertarian has a lot more in common with a centrist Democrat than with a radical Christian social conservative.<br /> <br /> And as Heavy Arms and Caitiff Primogen pointed out, protests and economic/cultural influence on a ground level isn't the same as censorship. It's one of the core values of democracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T11:12:43-07:00","id":995266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=990025#post990025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I mean, conservatives <i>did</i> decide that the person they feel best reflects the beliefs and values of American conservatism is someone who believes the majority of Mexican immigrants are rapists and murderers. Someone who is willing to call his own daughter, &amp;quot;a piece of ass.&amp;quot; Someone who has called for a ban on Muslim traveler's to the US... hell, I'm not even going to go on with him.<br /> <br /> So no. I don't think that &amp;quot;open minded&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;tolerant&amp;quot; are words I would use to describe Donald Trump or the people who chose for him to represent conservatives, the people who cheer for him at rallies or the people who will vote for him in November which is, again, a majority of Republicans and conservatives in America.<br /> <br /> Even prior to Donald Trump though, I don't know that open minded or tolerant are words I would have used to describe a Republican party. Remember that Mike Huckabee (a pretty major figure in conservative and Republican circles) has called for gays to be rounded up and put into camps so their &amp;quot;disease&amp;quot; can be studied. We still have the Republican party's platform openly opposing gay rights, women's rights, transgender rights, etc.<br /> <br /> If anything, over the last decade or so Republicans and conservatives have become even <i>less</i> tolerant and open minded than they were before (I mean, how else do you explain Donald Trump's rise to power in which he says things that ex-Republican presidents and presidential nominees find shocking and horrifying)?<br /> <br /> And keep in mind this all coming from someone who desperately wishes he could, in good conscience, vote for Republican candidates because I agree with a number of conservative principles and ideals. But so long as the Republican party and conservative Americans embrace repugnant radicals, there is simply no way I can bring myself to vote in solidarity with them.<br /> <br /> In short, the sorts of words I would tend to associate with roleplaying (open mindedness, tolerance, acceptance, etc) are not words I would use to describe modern-day conservative America. When conservative America begins to embrace those ideas, then I would probably be willing to consider myself a conservative.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think Donalds Trump weirdly sexual relationship to his daughter is a reflection on conservatives. They're both adults and its none of my business.<br /> <br /> I will also say far from all conservatives support Trump, many Republican politicians have been flee from him like he's a zombie hoard.<br /> <br /> And not everyone who supports Trump is conservative, many are doing it as a fuck you to the establishment, not because they are agree with his opinions, but because as Mike Moore points out, the establishment fucking hates him, he's a rebellian against political correctness, against wall street, against the media, against corporations that pushed bad trade agreements that hollowed out North America's manufacturing sector, against career politicians, ect...<br /> <br /> I know people who hate neoliberalism, who try and convince me to support Trump, even though I can vote in American elections.<br /> <br /> And from this Canadians perpective, your all rightwing, Stephen Harper former Prime Minister of Canada and conservative party leader, is practically a communist compared to Hillary Clinton if you look at her record.<br /> <br /> Role Playing games are a flexible medium, I can run a game appealing to any sort of sensiblities within it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T12:07:44-07:00","id":995291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=995266#post995266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Donalds Trump weirdly sexual relationship to his daughter is a reflection on conservatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a reflection of his views on women, and the majority of conservative Americans supporting him is a reflection of their refusal to come to grasp with American conservative moment history regarding women's issues as largely being a negative one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will also say far from all conservatives support Trump, many Republican politicians have been flee from him like he's a zombie hoard. </div> </div> </div>This is so missing the point. Nobody said &quot;all,&quot; and the politicians really aren't the issue. The issue are the millions and millions of self-identifying American conservatives that are supporting him. The majority of the conservative people in the US picked Trump to be their representative, not some fringe group of them, and a few hundred politicians recoiling in disgust doesn't make up for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And not everyone who supports Trump is conservative, many are doing it as a fuck you to the establishment, not because they are agree with his opinions,.. </div> </div> </div>These two things are not mutually exclusive. The majority of the people voting for Trump as the &quot;fuck you&quot; are conservatives as well. It's important to remember that the majority of liberals have a positive view of the Democratic party. It's one of the reasons nobody thought Sanders really had a chance. It's hard to run a &quot;fuck you establishment&quot; race if most of the voters are generally satisfied with the establishment. The Democrats (with plenty of help from the Republicans) have managed to sell the American left heavily on the lack of success of progressive ideals on conservative obstruction over liberal failures.<br /> <br /> The people that Moore is talking about are vastly dominated by conservative identifying voters. The whole, &quot;Sanders lost so I'm voting Trump,&quot; is as much a non-factor as women vowing to vote against Obama because he beat Clinton in the primaries.<br /> <br /> So again, the whole &quot;not all&quot; is not really helpful in the face of, &quot;a sizeable majority.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And from this Canadians perpective, your all rightwing, Stephen Harper former Prime Minister of Canada and conservative party leader, is practically a communist compared to Hillary Clinton if you look at her record. </div> </div> </div>You have to recognize the... oddity... of spending most of a post going NotAllConservatives, and then ending in a YesAllAmericans line.<br /> <br /> Though I really wonder what record you're talking about when Clinton spent years int he 90s pushing for universal healthcare... that whole socialist thing that the US can't get behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:32:53-07:00","id":995352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=995291#post995291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is so missing the point. Nobody said &quot;all,&quot; and the politicians really aren't the issue. The issue are the millions and millions of self-identifying American conservatives that are supporting him.</div> </div> </div> </div>This much is true, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=995291#post995291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The majority of the conservative people in the US picked Trump to be their representative, not some fringe group of them, and a few hundred politicians recoiling in disgust doesn't make up for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This much is false. Trump won the majority of the <i>delegates</i>; but this was because various technicalities of the delegate selection process allowed him to claim a disproportionate number of delegates. I don't think he got more than 40% of the popular vote; and I would contend that with Open Primaries (which brought Democrats and others into the voting pool), loss of morale leading to reduced voter turnout once it was apparent that he'd clinched the nomination, and the rise of the alt-right (which has nothing to do with conservatism), I wouldn't even call that 40% figure an accurate measure of conservative views on Trump. Heck, even in the General Election, there's a sizeable portion of his \u201csupport\u201d, not just among politicians but also among the rank and file citizens, who aren't so much for Donald as they're against Hillary: \u201cas bad as Trump is, Hillary's worse\u201d. <br /> <br /> Donald Trump does not represent conservatives. Heck, he only technically represents the Republican Party: in the off chance that he becomes President, you won't need a Democrat-held Congress to keep him in check; the <i>Republicans</i> in Congress will be doing that. Look to the likes of Paul Ryan as the de facto leadership of the Republican Party, whether or not Trump gets elected; and look to him, not Trump, if you want a better sense of what conservatives are like. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T15:16:44-07:00","id":995375,"title":"","content":"I read somewhere that the primary reason most voters are behind either candidate this election is &quot;they're not the other one.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T15:53:56-07:00","id":995392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=995352#post995352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think he got more than 40% of the popular vote;</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, he got ~45% of the popular vote in an effective four way race. Though the caucus system in many states makes it really hard to pin down what we should consider the total numbers (in the few states that record both popular vote and caucus results, both Trump and Clinton usually ended up under performing in the delegate counts compared to the popular vote, so it's fair to say that Trump probably would have an even bigger primary popular vote lead if we ditched caucuses or at least had all states record a popular vote as well).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...I wouldn't even call that 40% figure an accurate measure of conservative views on Trump. Heck, even in the General Election, there's a sizeable portion of his \u201csupport\u201d, not just among politicians but also among the rank and file citizens, who aren't so much for Donald as they're against Hillary: \u201cas bad as Trump is, Hillary's worse\u201d. </div> </div> </div>Why they're doing it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> A recent CNN/ORC poll had 90% +/- 6 Republican voters supporting trump, and 78% +/- 5 Conservative voters supporting him. And that actually represents a low for him that seems to be the conservative recoil against all the sex scandals. A PPP pole from a month ago had him with 82% among Republicans, and 87% with very conservative voters.<br /> <br /> In any case that... he's got the majority support - and not by small margins - of the conservatives of the country. So maybe saying he was selected by a majority isn't the best way to phrase it, but cutting through the layers of nominee selection shows that the nomination process usually represents the public better than people think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Look to the likes of Paul Ryan as the de facto leadership of the Republican Party, whether or not Trump gets elected; and look to him, not Trump, if you want a better sense of what conservatives are like. </div> </div> </div>Paul Ryan still plans on voting for Trump despite &quot;not endorsing or defending&quot; him. I'm not really sure anti-Trump conservatives really want to follow the line of logic there... because it doesn't really end well. At the nicest, if Ryan represents the &quot;true&quot; American conservative, it means that the American conservative movement cares more about getting a Republican in office then maintaining the principles and moral integrity of their ideology beyond party affiliation.<br /> <br /> As well, Ryan is happy to waste millions of government dollars on pointless political gestures over actually working to get anything positive done. Hell, the one time Ryan and Mcconnell organized a bipartisan effort and managed the only veto override Obama is likely to ever have... they both immediately went back and realized they should have never done so because the bill is broken but they shoved it through (Ryan specifically fast tracked in the House), ignored Obama pointing out the issues with the bill, and Mcconnell went so far as to blame Obama for not making the objections to the bill strongly enough.<br /> <br /> So... no. You really don't want me to look to Paul Ryan as a representative American conservative. I know far too much about him to fall for the, &quot;he's not as loud or stupid as Trump!&quot; line of reasoning here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T17:30:20-07:00","id":995450,"title":"","content":"When you're trying to assert that Trump somehow represents conservative values, then why Republicans are supporting him <i>absolutely</i> matters. Remember that there's a <i>strong</i> \u201canybody but Clinton\u201d feeling among conservatives, which pushes Trump's numbers up simply because he's literally anybody but Clinton: they're not voting <i>for him</i>, but rather <i>against her</i>. To them, as bad as Trump is, Clinton is worse.<br /> <br /> Also, it wasn't just the Caucuses that skewed results; it was also the Open Primaries where Democrats got a chance to help select the Republican nominee, winner-take-all states where Trump got all of the delegates with little as a third of the vote, and the fact that \u201cRepublicans\u201d isn't a synonym for \u201cconservatives\u201d: Trump didn't do particularly well in Texas, for example.<br /> <br /> It's not as simple as \u201cTrump got the plurality of the popular vote, so most conservatives must like him\u201d. Or even \u201cTrump is supported by a majority of conservatives, so a majority of conservatives must agree with him\u201d.<br /> <br /> And while I personally can't bring myself to support Trump, I can understand and sympathize with the reasoning of those who are. It's not about sacrificing one's principles to get a Republican in office; it's about keeping a Democrat out of office because of the damage she'll do if she gets in. (In my case, I think it's a lost cause; Clinton's almost certainly going to win, and as a Californian, my vote's not going to matter anyway. So I'm just going to leave the top of the ballot blank. But if I lived in, say, Ohio, I'd definitely be doing a lot of soul-searching about which is the greater of two evils.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-29-2016, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T21:07:24-07:00","id":995493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=995450#post995450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you're trying to assert that Trump somehow represents conservative values, then why Republicans are supporting him <i>absolutely</i> matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>If &quot;never Clinton&quot; was such a big factor, and conservatives and Republicans mostly reject Trump, why aren't they all supporting the Libertarian ticket since Johnson and Weld are both ex-Republicans?<br /> <br /> Third party candidates might be snubbed a bit by mainstream thought, but that's how a lot of long running political parties in the US got started. That's how the Republican party got started: A bunch of ex-Whigs got tired of how the Whigs were going and decided to start up a third party that was more in line with the majority of the former Whig base.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I do not buy the lack of integrity that this implies. If someone that consistently has ~80+% of support from conservatives, either he represents what most conservatives believe, or most conservatives are throwing their principles into the trash for party loyalty. Never Trumpers tried repeatedly to get conservatives to move away from Trump without going to Clinton... and they've failed at almost every turn. The American conservative movement was offered dozens of non-Trump and non-Clinton options... and they rejected them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it wasn't just the Caucuses that skewed results; it was also the Open Primaries where Democrats got a chance to help select the Republican nominee, winner-take-all states where Trump got all of the delegates with little as a third of the vote, and the fact that \u201cRepublicans\u201d isn't a synonym for \u201cconservatives\u201d: Trump didn't do particularly well in Texas, for example. </div> </div> </div>Open primaries should skew against Trump (statistically they favor more centrist candidates so they should do better for Kaisch or Rubio, not Trump), but he still won the vast majority of them in the Republican primaries. Winner take all doesn't change the popular vote tallies. And yes, I know they're not the same. That's why I cited polls that had numbers for Republicans and conservatives separated out to account for that overlap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not as simple as \u201cTrump got the plurality of the popular vote, so most conservatives must like him\u201d. Or even \u201cTrump is supported by a majority of conservatives, so a majority of conservatives must agree with him\u201d. </div> </div> </div>Actually, it is as simple as the majority of conservatives support him, and thus the majority of conservatives are saying that they agree with him. That's what supporting and voting for him means. Of course nobody is in 100% agreement with their chosen candidate, but there's no evidence to show that the &quot;never Clinton&quot; camp is actually the primary factor in Trumps massive support by American conservatives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not about sacrificing one's principles to get a Republican in office; </div> </div> </div>Just because that might not be the justification people are using, doesn't mean that isn't exactly what they're doing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T00:11:57-07:00","id":995535,"title":"","content":"Edit:NM clicked link randomly and thought it was a different OT thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-30-2016, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:56:19-07:00","id":995871,"title":"","content":"&quot;At the nicest, if Ryan represents the &quot;true&quot; American conservative, it means that the American conservative movement cares more about getting a Republican in office then maintaining the principles and moral integrity of their ideology beyond party affiliation.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which makes them no different then democracts voting for Hillary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T18:03:41-07:00","id":995888,"title":"","content":"Not really:<br /> <br /> 1) Nobody is claiming Hillary should be held as a standard by which to judge American liberals.<br /> <br /> 2) The impression that comes from your repeatedly false claims about her make it clear you really aren't in a position to judge her record or political motivations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:40:50-07:00","id":996171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=995888#post995888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really:<br /> <br /> 1) Nobody is claiming Hillary should be held as a standard by which to judge American liberals.<br /> <br /> 2) The impression that comes from your repeatedly false claims about her make it clear you really aren't in a position to judge her record or political motivations.</div> </div> </div> </div> What false claims have I made about her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:45:06-07:00","id":996176,"title":"","content":"Really dearly hoping that the Republicans can realize the rot they've allowed to grow and push themselves to be the party of small government, rather than this wild mess of racists, Christian fundamentalists, and outright nationalists. Let the Trump alt-right nutjobs go somewhere far away or else watch your party slowly die off.<br /> <br /> They're going to bleed voters as long as they continue to oppose LGBT rights and continuously alienate nonwhite, non-Christian voters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:59:24-07:00","id":996187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=996176#post996176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really dearly hoping that the Republicans can realize the rot they've allowed to grow and push themselves to be the party of small government, rather than this wild mess of racists, Christian fundamentalists, and outright nationalists. Let the Trump alt-right nutjobs go somewhere far away or else watch your party slowly die off.<br /> <br /> They're going to bleed voters as long as they continue to oppose LGBT rights and continuously alienate nonwhite, non-Christian voters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They're really in a tough place. The social and economic branches of the Republican Party have increasingly less in common every day, and as the former becomes more radicalized, it further isolates the moderates. Siding with the current strand of cultural/social conservatism means more or less blacking out any chances of ever getting the non-white vote and potentially turning their centrist base to the Democratic Party (who I could see gleefully moving even closer center to pull them into the fold). But distancing themselves from that social/cultural base also means giving up a serious amount of ground in down-ticket seats throughout the South and Midwest.<br /> <br /> I wonder if, a decade or two down the line, we might see an America shaped by a centrist party borne from the Republican and Democratic base along with splinter parties on the left and right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:10:18-07:00","id":996225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=996187#post996187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They're really in a tough place. The social and economic branches of the Republican Party have increasingly less in common every day, and as the former becomes more radicalized, it further isolates the moderates. Siding with the current strand of cultural/social conservatism means more or less blacking out any chances of ever getting the non-white vote and potentially turning their centrist base to the Democratic Party (who I could see gleefully moving even closer center to pull them into the fold). But distancing themselves from that social/cultural base also means giving up a serious amount of ground in down-ticket seats throughout the South and Midwest.<br /> <br /> I wonder if, a decade or two down the line, we might see an America shaped by a centrist party borne from the Republican and Democratic base along with splinter parties on the left and right.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just absurd to see the Republican ticket be a blatantly racist nutjob who doesn't know the first thing about economics (or oublic relations, for that matter) and fundamentalist most known for passing heinously discriminatory legislation, when the average Republican vote (hopefully) has zero in common with either of them. Here's hoping the right can reclaim itself and abandon all this baggage.<br /> <br /> And ideally they'll compromise on LGBT rights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:35:38-07:00","id":996235,"title":"","content":"How the party of &quot;Christian values&quot; managed to nominate the least Christian man in America is something that gives me no end of bafflement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:00:54-07:00","id":996250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=996225#post996225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's just absurd to see the Republican ticket be a blatantly racist nutjob who doesn't know the first thing about economics (or oublic relations, for that matter) and fundamentalist most known for passing heinously discriminatory legislation, when the average Republican vote (hopefully) has zero in common with either of them. Here's hoping the right can reclaim itself and abandon all this baggage.<br /> <br /> And ideally they'll compromise on LGBT rights.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. I think the majority of Republicans are reasonable people who are moderate if a bit farther to the right than the Democrat base on social and fiscal issues. The problem is that, despite this, the radicals are loud enough and constitute a large enough of a minority that they're a necessary voting bloc if the party wants to keep winning elections in the short term. And that same loud minority will more or less bar them from being competitive in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:20:51-07:00","id":996263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=996235#post996235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the party of &quot;Christian values&quot; managed to nominate the least Christian man in America is something that gives me no end of bafflement.</div> </div> </div> </div> As a member of said party, I have to agree with this sentiment. I'd amend it to \u201cleast Christian candidate\u201d since there are plenty of men in America who are as little or less Christian than even Trump; but yeah, of the seventeen candidates that the Republicans started out with, Trump is the one who least matched the party's social conservative values. <br /> <br /> The problem we have right now doesn't stem from an increasingly radicalized social conservative wing of the party; it stems from an increasingly <i>marginalized</i> social conservative wing. If the social conservatives had had more of a say in the Primaries, Trump would never have been nominated. As it is, those of you who think that social conservatives are badwrong should take Trump's nomination as a good sign: when he won the nomination, they lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:36:57-07:00","id":996269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=996250#post996250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I think the majority of Republicans are reasonable people who are moderate if a bit farther to the right than the Democrat base on social and fiscal issues. The problem is that, despite this, the radicals are loud enough and constitute a large enough of a minority that they're a necessary voting bloc if the party wants to keep winning elections in the short term. And that same loud minority will more or less bar them from being competitive in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Careful with that characterization; many of those who you're calling radicals aren't. They just happen to believe things that clash with your beliefs. And even there, I'm not sure they clash as much as you might think they do. Not everyone who's, say, opposed to gay marriage is a homophobe; and social conservatives in general consider women's rights and abortion to be separate issues, having no problem with the former but a <i>massive</i> problem with the latter.<br /> <br /> Social conservatives may be painted as backwards bigoted radicals in the media; but that doesn't mean that they are. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:40:42-07:00","id":996271,"title":"","content":"Trump is Kylo Ren to Richard Nixon's Darth Vader. He is the petulant, vengeful echo of 1968 finally reverberating back on us after half a century in transit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:45:14-07:00","id":996274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=996269#post996269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Careful with that characterization; many of those who you're calling radicals aren't. They just happen to believe things that clash with your beliefs. And even there, I'm not sure they clash as much as you might think they do. Not everyone who's, say, opposed to gay marriage is a homophobe; and social conservatives in general consider women's rights and abortion to be separate issues, having no problem with the former but a <i>massive</i> problem with the latter.<br /> <br /> Social conservatives may be painted as backwards bigoted radicals in the media; but that doesn't mean that they are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry if I expressed that inelegantly. I'm not saying all social conservatives are radicals, but a large and very loud streak of radicalism has definitely gained prominence in the party.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that a moderate party that's fiscally fairly hawkish, agrees in civil unions rather than gay marriage, and restrictions on abortion rights that don't outright ban them would play well to the base (stances that don't sit well with me but which I found far more palatable than a lot of the touted extremism), but it will still drive off too much of the radical elements of their party to keep the ground they need as a viable party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T15:08:06-07:00","id":996287,"title":"","content":"Right now, the distinction between &quot;agrees with civil unions but not gay marriage&quot; and &quot;doesn't agree with either&quot; is as moot as the distinction between &quot;regulating abortion practices&quot; vs. &quot;banning abortions&quot;, due to their respective Supreme Court decisions. What's important to conservatives of all stripes is to get those decisions overturned so that individual states once again have the freedom to choose where to draw the line, instead of everyone being forced to draw the line all the way to the left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T15:38:52-07:00","id":996300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=996287#post996287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now, the distinction between &quot;agrees with civil unions but not gay marriage&quot; and &quot;doesn't agree with either&quot; is as moot as the distinction between &quot;regulating abortion practices&quot; vs. &quot;banning abortions&quot;, due to their respective Supreme Court decisions. What's important to conservatives of all stripes is to get those decisions overturned so that individual states once again have the freedom to choose where to draw the line, instead of everyone being forced to draw the line all the way to the left.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a blanket statement as well.<br /> <br /> Yes, that fear of federal intervention is a big part of a lot of conservative rhetoric, but there are plenty in the party who care less about federal vs. state law than they do about enacting their policy on a national level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T15:42:21-07:00","id":996302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=996269#post996269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not everyone who's, say, opposed to gay marriage is a homophobe</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. Opposition to same-sex marriage <i>is</i> homophobic. Not everyone who holds homophobic views is actively hateful towards gay people. This seems more of an issue of &quot;homophobe&quot; being a label that applies to the person as a whole instead of to their behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link"