k-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:07:23-07:00","id":997843,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I've seen a few examples of people willfully misinterpreting other posters' intent and meaning, and assigning motive that hasn't been clearly stated. Let's stop doing that right now. It doesn't do anything to further a constructive discussion.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:27:26-07:00","id":997858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=997842#post997842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I really do appreciate you taking the time out of your day for it, thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to echo this personally. I haven't been able to address your response to my own request yet and do plan to when I have access to an actual keyboard. But I do appreciate that you responded back. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:00:35-07:00","id":997899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=997785#post997785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">@ElvesofZion</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wow, that is lot of different topics... but I'll try to touch on each. I am putting my responses in spoiler tags because they got kinda long.</span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=997785#post997785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What are your thoughts on government regulation, particularly in light of the past (Big Tobacco, Big Lead, etc) as well as events in the present, like Animal Agriculture, the food industry with sugar, the recent issues with pharmaceutical companies, economic crises created by banks, and outright predatory organizations like payday loans</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some government regulation is reasonable in general. Although the method that such regulation is administered and enforced should be the subject of extreme scrutiny. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These examples all seem to have to do with consumer protection regulations, so I will stick to those for now. Generally speaking the act of purchasing is a contract between the purchaser and the seller, and I would say that it is the responsibility of the State (general term here, a discussion about regional vs. federal government is its own topic I think, although it does touch on all of these points as well) to ensure that contracts are upheld by both parties. The \u2018Big\u2019 part of those points mainly refers to the idea of them having a powerful lobbying arm, an are a that I would argue needs an extreme amount of reform. I don\u2019t believe that substances should be banned for sale because it is my business if I want to buy lead paint, not the governments. But it is their job to ensure that I am not sold something that claims to be lead free but actually does contain lead.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I am very torn on the pharma/medical front, I tend to disagree with conservatives and may libertarians on it. I generally think that the right to live should likely be protected. But the actual implementation of it leaves a lot of issues for me. As I said above, it is my right to use lead-based paints if i want to, but is it then the government and thus the peoples responsibility to take care of me if i get sick from it? I also understand the argument (in theory) that private industry helps drive innovation and progress in the medical field.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Banking is also a very large topic, my general feeling is that the government should step away from banks, way more then the currently are. But that the focus on a contract driven society would help create a culture where people are more wary of bad options like payday loans and sub-prime morgage scams.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=997785#post997785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">How do you feel about Social Security?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Social Security program is a nice idea but shows a fundamental problem with many socialist programs. They are very often mandatory by necessity. A safe (at least in theory, it has been tampered with) retirement account that any citizen can use is a very nice idea. The problem is that it is supposedly not a tax and yet it is mandatory, and a tax must be included in order to pay for the administration of the fund. An anecdote to help illuminate:. I have a good 401k with company matching, it would be much more financially profitable for me to take all of the money that goes to Social Security and put it there. But I cannot do so, because in order for Social Security to work it must be mandatory so there is enough money in the system from current workers to pay for the current retirees and admin the system.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=997785#post997785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What are your thoughts on the increasingly automated workforce, and experts who claim a minimum standard of living will need to be implemented at some point?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Technological progress is an inevitability, it has always happened. The invention of the printing press removed the need for scribes, cars replaced horses, etc. People will find work or leisure will become work: the rise of e-sports for example. I am not scared of progress.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I am not familiar with any particular papers on the need for an automatic living wage kind of thing specifically as a result of increased automation in the workforce. If you happen to have references I will gladly read them and then comment on them.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=997785#post997785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do you believe that private companies should be free to regulate themselves? Is there a point where you feel the government needs to step in and protect the consumer?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think my first point answered this for the most part, the idea of \u2018regulation\u2019 is thrown around as a buzz word by both \u2018sides\u2019 but I think the real question is in the deeper concepts of what a business is and what the government is for.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=997785#post997785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If it turns out that you don't believe in regulation, how do you reconcile the promise that capitalism will produce a superior product, when evidence exists to the contrary? (Fast food is of inferior nutritional value, devices are built to break down quickly because you'll need to go out and buy another one, safety and craftsmanship are sidelined when you can make a bigger profit with cheap labor, which leads to exporting jobs (bad for the local economy)).Advertisements do not create informed consumers, they often shore up an inferior product.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To start with, what we have in the US is barely capitalism at all. The true center of </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">capitalism </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">really has nothing to do with promoting a better product, at least not directly. The central tenet of </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">capitalism </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">that I think tends to be ignored is that \u2018a person deserves just compensation for their labors\u2019, anything else is an addition to that core idea and some of those additions are mutually incompatible. Laissez faire </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">capitalism </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">does introduce the idea that a completely free market will \u2018eventually\u2019 (key word there) result in the \u2018best\u2019 (another important one) products through the selection by the people. The \u2018eventual\u2019 is important because that part of laissez faire </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">capitalism </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">assumes that \u2018value\u2019 will be determined by the people with their purchasing power, and that over time the items of the most value will get bought and others will not. Value is a perception however, and it is totally dependent on the people to make that judgement. Fast Food is subjectively \u2018better\u2019 because it is convenient, the nutritional value is a different aspect. One that you (and an increasing number of people) perceive to be more important than the convenience, but that was not the case for a very long time in the US. It is changing overtime though and that is what is expected from laissez faire </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">capitalism </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, the best value, as perceived by the customer base, will eventually win out by being bought while the perceived lesser product will not.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As long as people are ok with the \u2018inferior\u2019 product because it is cheaper then it will continue to sell. That is the price of freedom in the market. People are free to make bad purchasing decisions.<br /> <br /> All that said, I am not totally sold on </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">laissez faire </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">capitalism myself, as evidence by me saying that there are some regulations that I agree with. The core of </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">capitalism, I do agree with. Every person that does work deserves fair compensation for that work, if that compensation isn't to be had then society has decided that the value of their work is nothing. It is not the governments place to force me to pay for things I don't value.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everything here is pretty summed up, since it is already really long and there is a lot to discuss on each topic. I am also not a politician or an economist so they are more stances based on ideals than true plans of action.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T16:30:42-07:00","id":997951,"title":"","content":"If any conservative wishes to answer, what does it mean to be conservative to you, what are the core tenets of conservatism. I ask this because in Ireland &quot;Conservatism = Traditionalism&quot;, but American conservatism seems to be somewhat different, so I'd like to understand it better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":". 11-03-2016, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T17:41:29-07:00","id":997979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=997508#post997508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you post an opinion/political stance and view having it challenged in the form of debate the same as being run out of town, then who's really asking for an echo chamber?<br /> <br /> Note that the LGBT thread has been absolutely full of folks who aren't queer themselves asking questions and having them answered. There's room for a healthy debate here, just the same as there is in a hypothetical thread about liberal politics, but relentless personal attacks (or in our dear friend Luis' case, implying the fucking Inquisition wasn't really all that bad) are hardly the same thing, just the same as disrespecting the core idea of safe spaces and calling homosexuals sinners isn't exactly a healthy side of the conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry it took so long to get back to you but the World Series and work were happening, but since you politely responded I figured I should do the same.Thing is this thread was created just to see if other conservatives enjoyed the same hobby. Pretty simple idea and look what it has turned into, I think you agree this whole thing is a mess. More to the point we didn't come here to have to defend our political idea but to talk about a game we all enjoy. Questions are can be a good thing but accusations are not, and some from the left are trying pretty hard to brow beat others into leaving. Which well they did, should that in itself make you think people are going about this in the wrong way. See they don't want a discussion, they want to prove themselves right have other acknowledge it.<br /> <br /> Like many of the conservatives in this tread many of us are the Gary Johnson/ Rand Paul types who don't put up with any who attacks somebody just because they are different. We don't agree with what Luis said any more than some of the stuff that has been thrown our way in this thread and others. You are right it's not ok to personally attack a member of the LGBT community, but I have seen examples of the left doing the same thing on these boards and people cheer them on, at least the mods saw it and cleaned it up, but it does happen..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T18:20:45-07:00","id":997998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=997951#post997951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any conservative wishes to answer, what does it mean to be conservative to you, what are the core tenets of conservatism. I ask this because in Ireland &amp;quot;Conservatism = Traditionalism&amp;quot;, but American conservatism seems to be somewhat different, so I'd like to understand it better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, since you asked, I took a look at the Wikipedia article on conservativism. It mentions that most European conservative writers do not consider conservativism in the US to be true conservativism but rather classical liberalism. Which, upon a glance at each of those pages I would agree that I at least am a classical liberal not a conservative, since I don't give two shakes about tradition and in fact think that holding to traditions can be and is in many cases harmful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:53:38-07:00","id":998065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=997899#post997899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Post</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot here, and I don't disagree with all of it by any means. I would like to share my own position though, for the sake of a back and forth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The \u2018Big\u2019 part of those points mainly refers to the idea of them having a powerful lobbying arm, an are a that I would argue needs an extreme amount of reform.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <br /> <br /> Do you have a position on how you'd like it to be reformed?</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don\u2019t believe that substances should be banned for sale because it is my business if I want to buy lead paint, not the governments. But it is their job to ensure that I am not sold something that claims to be lead free but actually does contain lead.</span> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that there were unsafe levels of lead in our entire environment. The lead lobbying groups and scientists claimed this was entirely natural, only for scientists who weren't on the payroll to explain that it wasn't. The argument that it doesn't really hurt anyone if you buy products with lead in it and everyone else doesn't - the rest of the population will still feel the effects of unnaturally high levels of lead in the environment. This is especially true because lead is so cheap and easy to work with, people will still use it, even if it is harmful. <br /> <br /> Another example would be cigarette companies, their product is highly addictive, often engineered to be more addictive for the sake of getting customers and keeping them. At some point, I feel, we need to step in and regulate the business to keep industry from taking advantage of consumers, because on paper it's nice to think that everyone is an informed objective consumer, we're not, we're animals who suffer cravings and lapses in judgment. A more or less identical situation is happening with sugar now, especially as children are targeted and marketed to before they're of an age to really understand what's going on, doctors get to deal with 10 year olds who have type 2 diabetes, and it's pretty terrible. <br /> <br /> Then we have things like global warming, which basically isn't going to be corrected if we let the free market have its way, it's had plenty of time to prove otherwise. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I am very torn on the pharma/medical front, I tend to disagree with conservatives and may libertarians on it. I generally think that the right to live should likely be protected. But the actual implementation of it leaves a lot of issues for me. As I said above, it is my right to use lead-based paints if i want to, but is it then the government and thus the peoples responsibility to take care of me if i get sick from it? I also understand the argument (in theory) that private industry helps drive innovation and progress in the medical field.</span> </div> </div> </div>What about people who 'just get sick'? What about people who were born sick? What about people who were born sick because their parents used products with lead in them?<br /> <br /> It's also worth pointing out that places with a single payer healthcare system still have better healthcare than we do, and not just in cost but in terms of quality. Private Industry has not lead to America beating other countries in terms of quality of care or life. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Banking is also a very large topic, my general feeling is that the government should step away from banks, way more then the currently are. But that the focus on a contract driven society would help create a culture where people are more wary of bad options like payday loans and sub-prime mortgage scams.</span> </div> </div> </div>I don't think a contract driven society would do much to change things. People don't do payday loans because they're ignorant to the danger, they do it out of desperation. It's sort of like signing a contract with Ursula or whatever, people would still do it - but the thing is, should we allow people to prey on the most desperate like that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Social Security </div> </div> </div>I don't really have any arguments for this. It's just a matter of personal preference for me - I think it's okay for me to pay taxes so that the widow down the street can get a social security check, and so on. It's a matter of solidarity for me, and paying into Social Security is a way for me to help others and myself. For a really good example of why I feel this way, you can watch the documentary 'Requiem for the American Dream', it's on Netflix, unless they took it down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Technological progress is an inevitability, it has always happened. The invention of the printing press removed the need for scribes, cars replaced horses, etc. People will find work or leisure will become work: the rise of e-sports for example. I am not scared of progress.</span> </div> </div> </div>There are many articles talking about it, and it's an issue of debate among experts, here's one example: <a href=\"http://harvardpolitics.com/world/automation/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harvardpolitics.com/world/automation/</a> - I'm sure you can find dozens and dozens more with a Google search.<br /> <br /> Right, so the issue is that in the Industrial Revolution and in similar leap periods, the technology only eased the burden on labor. Things are quite a bit different this time. We don't just have self-driving cars, we're looking at doctor's being replaced by diagnostic machines, therapists being replaced by artificial intelligence (already being tested in some areas, and they're, unfortunately for me, a huge hit. People much prefer confiding their darkest issues with a machine rather than an actual human person). Food service jobs go away, and so to do customer service jobs. It's a leap where the thing that set humans apart from beasts of burden or machines - our brains - are being the equipment outmoded. <br /> <br /> And I don't mind the idea of everyone using the leisure time to become artists, or athletes, or esports stars, but if you had any experience as one of these things you'd know that expecting everyone 'to make it' with careers like that is nuts. Sports athletes and esports stars alike have to take drugs to remain competitive, and run themselves into the ground. For every one successful writer, there are hundreds of us who can't quit their day job because they will never make ends meet.<br /> <br /> That's the purpose of a minimal standard of living. Corporations are going to profit immensely from automation, the dwindling middle class will not. A minimum standard of living gives people the money they need to survive without becoming homeless, and if you get a job as a writer or a League of Legends steamer, that's fine, it will raise your income above the bare minimum - you make it big like Neil Gaiman? Then maybe you don't need the minimum standard of living anymore. At least, that's the idea. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The true center of </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">capitalism </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">really has nothing to do with promoting a better product, at least not directly. The central tenet of </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">capitalism </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">that I think tends to be ignored is that \u2018a person deserves just compensation for their labors\u2019.</span> </div> </div> </div>The actual central tenet of Capitalism is that means of production be privately owned, and that these private interests be in charge of its use for the means of profit. That's kind of the defining principle of capitalism. However, it's an argument that requires explanation, and the explanation for why capitalism is a good system is that the government, or social interests, cannot best determine how the means of production should be used. Private interests, driven by profit, are most likely to succeed and produce a superior result because they are motivated by survival, in a perfect capitalist system without monopolies, the superior product will out, and inferior products will sink. In other words - Progress will follow Capital. That is the argument that capitalism makes. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure I've ever seen any economist or historian claim that Capitalism means just compensation for their labor. In fact the only time I've ever heard that is from FDR while proposing his New Deal, which were effectively a number of steps taken to redistribute wealth and insure that the people had more bargaining rights. In other words, a series of measures largely considered to be Socialist. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T21:03:21-07:00","id":998067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=997979#post997979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry it took so long to get back to you but the World Series and work were happening, but since you politely responded I figured I should do the same.Thing is this thread was created just to see if other conservatives enjoyed the same hobby. Pretty simple idea and look what it has turned into, I think you agree this whole thing is a mess. More to the point we didn't come here to have to defend our political idea but to talk about a game we all enjoy. Questions are can be a good thing but accusations are not, and some from the left are trying pretty hard to brow beat others into leaving. Which well they did, should that in itself make you think people are going about this in the wrong way. See they don't want a discussion, they want to prove themselves right have other acknowledge it.<br /> <br /> Like many of the conservatives in this tread many of us are the Gary Johnson/ Rand Paul types who don't put up with any who attacks somebody just because they are different. We don't agree with what Luis said any more than some of the stuff that has been thrown our way in this thread and others. You are right it's not ok to personally attack a member of the LGBT community, but I have seen examples of the left doing the same thing on these boards and people cheer them on, at least the mods saw it and cleaned it up, but it does happen..</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but original intent may not be the best move here.<br /> Go back to the first page - it was about conservative ideology within just a handful of posts and challenges to them came hot and fast, especially when someone started defending the Inquisition.<br /> <br /> I would add for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11726_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11726\" data-vbnamecard=\"11726\">Solana</a>'s post (and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1329_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1329\" data-vbnamecard=\"1329\">ElvesofZion</a>'s benefit):<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>One thing technology has always done is concentrate capital (defined as the means of production) into the hands of the wealthy. Essentially, every labor-saving technology allows a factory to be more productive, which means that fewer laborers are needed or the same number can produce the same amount. This means that the laborers have less collective power, very slightly, for each technological advancement For instance, this can have the negative effect in the future whereby a government can deploy its robot soldiers to oppress a populace without that pesky problem of the army turning on the government. This is not <i>necessarily</i> a bad thing - previously it served to get people out of shitty jobs and into good ones, but see point 3 below.</li> <li>No social action has ever prevented a technology from coming to market. Ever. So the question is not 'how do we stop it?', because that's impossible, but 'how do we adapt to it once it's here?' This is meant as an answer to Elves'</li> <li>As Solana indicates, what <i>will</i> happen is that technology will eliminate <i>substantial</i> numbers of jobs <i>without</i> creating enough jobs to fill the gaps that they left behind. There will be <i>structural unemployment</i> that people <i>have no ability to do anything about</i> on a substantial level.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>People often comment &quot;Well! We'll have jobs taking care of the robots, right?&quot; Sure. A few. Ones that themselves will increasingly vanish as robots take that over, too. And then when riots come from people not being able to feed themselves, we'd better hope the government doesn't already have a sufficient mass of effective robot soldiers that they can just push a button and say &quot;So long.&quot; - Something, by the by, that a libertarian government could not really guard against (indeed, if anything, there'd be greater pushes to it to cheapen the cost of maintaining a military.)</li> </ol></li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 11-04-2016, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T21:25:30-07:00","id":998076,"title":"","content":"If you go back and read you will see the 3rd post is where the ideology first started and it wasn't Conservative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T21:29:53-07:00","id":998077,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T22:10:58-07:00","id":998091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998076#post998076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you go back and read you will see the 3rd post is where the ideology first started and it wasn't Conservative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about my post? I specifically <i>asked if the conversation would be desired</i> and <i>suggested it be held elsewhere if so</i> precisely because I didn't want to drag the topic down with my not-so-conservative opinions. For the record, we did have a brief conversation via private message. None of what was said there was brought back up here because it was off-topic for this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T22:23:40-07:00","id":998096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998091#post998091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you talking about my post? I specifically <i>asked if the conversation would be desired</i> and <i>suggested it be held elsewhere if so</i> precisely because I didn't want to drag the topic down with my not-so-conservative opinions. For the record, we did have a brief conversation via private message. None of what was said there was brought back up here because it was off-topic for this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNope it was before yours. I saw your post and it was very polite, it deserves a thank you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T23:24:03-07:00","id":998109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998076#post998076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you go back and read you will see the 3rd post is where the ideology first started and it wasn't Conservative.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry, this isn't conservative?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm somewhere in the middle; I believe the Bible is God's word, but my thought's on how people have interpreted it can vary.<br /> <br /> I'm Pro Life.(With exceptions for rape, incest, and worst-case scenarios.) Don't want the kid? Plenty of people looking to adopt.<br /> <br /> I'm Pro Gun Control. Assault rifles are for the battlefield, not the suburbs.<br /> <br /> I'm Pro Death Penalty. You kill, you deserve to be killed; not as a &quot;deterrent&quot;, but to make damn sure you don't kill again.<br /> <br /> I'm... respectfully ambivalent about Marriage Equality.(I know what the Bible says, but the First Amendment says we shouldn't make laws based on religion, so while I wouldn't vote for it, I also wouldn't vote against.)<br /> <br /> I respect scientific evidence, but I question &quot;Atheist Dogma&quot;. (If the Universe exploded from a single point of infinite mass, where did that single point come from? How could something as complex as a DNA molecule occur by mere chance?)<br /> <br /> As a Multi-ethnic American, I try to see both sides of any race issue.<br /> <br /> On fiscal matters... I lean pretty far left. 1% of the populace controlling more than 50% of a nation's resources seems like a recipe for disaster. That's how Third World countries work.(Well, FAIL to work, technically.)<br /> <br /> I think America has SOME responsibility to act as the World's police, but only because no one else seems to want to step up. I sometimes think if we had just let the Soviets HAVE Afghanistan back during the Cold War, it would be THEM dealing with Islamic Extremists, and not us. Seems like every time we step in to help, the people we help turn around and attack us later, usually with the guns WE gave them. </div> </div> </div>I'm prepared to hear your arguments for why this is not conservative. It's the third post, it's the only one before Charlaquin's that details ideological postures. It's an almost definitively conservative post - the only part that deviates is where they say that they don't like the control of the world's resources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 11-04-2016, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T00:45:01-07:00","id":998132,"title":"","content":"Being Pro Gun Control is also not a politically conservative stance. Just pointing that out. Overall the opinions expressed in that post are on the conservative side of things with a few very notable exceptions.<br /> BTW, the part about there being an &quot;Atheist Dogma&quot; is an inaccurate use of the word dogma. There isn't an atheist authority that has set down a set of rules about what constitutes atheism, and if a better scientific theory about the creation of the universe comes about atheists don't have a codified belief system that needs to be abandoned in order to accommodate the new scientific theory. Being an atheist requires only one thing, a lack of belief in the existence of gods. To them, God and Santa Claus have the same level of validity. Some are smug about this, others are willing to just keep their opinion to themselves and let others choose to believe what they wish without being jerks about it. As long as someone's religious views aren't being used to justify harm towards others then I'm quite happy to be part of the latter camp.<br /> <br /> The &quot;where did that matter come from&quot; question is only really valid if Time is an actual universal constant that isn't relativistic and only moves in one direction. See the &quot;time is a circle&quot; monologue from True Detective for one hypothesis, and we already have mathematical models that demonstrate how time could move backwards relative to the perceptions of the observer.<br /> If one can believe in a God that has no beginning or end then they should be able to apply the same thinking to the existence of our universe and the material that makes it up. Something not tethered to Time in the fashion humans are would not have the same type of causal relationship to reality as we do, nor the same type of understanding of cause and effect as us (in regards to a cognitive entity). To that being the cause could very well be generated by the existence of the effect. The effect exists so the cause would have to (have) happen(ed) but would exist in an indeterminate state until observed. This is the state of being that Dr. Manhattan existed in the comics (to give an example of what this hypothetical being could be like), Yog-Sothoth from the Lovecraft Mythos would be another possible example.<br /> <br /> \u200bSorry for the tangent, this is what happens when I stay up past my bedtime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T02:13:50-07:00","id":998148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998132#post998132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being Pro Gun Control is also not a politically conservative stance. Just pointing that out. Overall the opinions expressed in that post are on the conservative side of things with a few very notable exceptions.<br /> BTW, the part about there being an &quot;Atheist Dogma&quot; is an inaccurate use of the word dogma. There isn't an atheist authority that has set down a set of rules about what constitutes atheism, and if a better scientific theory about the creation of the universe comes about atheists don't have a codified belief system that needs to be abandoned in order to accommodate the new scientific theory. Being an atheist requires only one thing, a lack of belief in the existence of gods. To them, God and Santa Claus have the same level of validity. Some are smug about this, others are willing to just keep their opinion to themselves and let others choose to believe what they wish without being jerks about it. As long as someone's religious views aren't being used to justify harm towards others then I'm quite happy to be part of the latter camp.<br /> <br /> The &quot;where did that matter come from&quot; question is only really valid if Time is an actual universal constant that isn't relativistic and only moves in one direction. See the &quot;time is a circle&quot; monologue from True Detective for one hypothesis, and we already have mathematical models that demonstrate how time could move backwards relative to the perceptions of the observer.<br /> If one can believe in a God that has no beginning or end then they should be able to apply the same thinking to the existence of our universe and the material that makes it up. Something not tethered to Time in the fashion humans are would not have the same type of causal relationship to reality as we do, nor the same type of understanding of cause and effect as us (in regards to a cognitive entity). To that being the cause could very well be generated by the existence of the effect. The effect exists so the cause would have to (have) happen(ed) but would exist in an indeterminate state until observed. This is the state of being that Dr. Manhattan existed in the comics (to give an example of what this hypothetical being could be like), Yog-Sothoth from the Lovecraft Mythos would be another possible example.<br /> <br /> \u200bSorry for the tangent, this is what happens when I stay up past my bedtime.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also not sure how the Big Bang Theory related to Dogma when the answer to anything before that, or how things worked at the time, will net you an answer of: 'I don't know', or 'We don't know, yet.' It seems more dogmatic to say that you have a book that explains that for us, and you should believe it because the book says you should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T07:00:21-07:00","id":998207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=997899#post997899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Social Security program is a nice idea but shows a fundamental problem with many socialist programs. They are very often mandatory by necessity. A safe (at least in theory, it has been tampered with) retirement account that any citizen can use is a very nice idea. The problem is that it is supposedly not a tax and yet it is mandatory, and a tax must be included in order to pay for the administration of the fund. An anecdote to help illuminate:. I have a good 401k with company matching, it would be much more financially profitable for me to take all of the money that goes to Social Security and put it there. But I cannot do so, because in order for Social Security to work it must be mandatory so there is enough money in the system from current workers to pay for the current retirees and admin the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would entirely defeat the point of Social Security, though. In the event of another stock market crash right before your retirement, your 401k would be worthless but Social Security would live on. And while one could argue &quot;that's one's choice whether to gamble on that or not&quot;, experience tells us that that's a choice we as a society cannot afford people to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":707,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","user":"etherial","date":". 11-04-2016, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T07:46:06-07:00","id":998224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998207#post998207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And while one could argue &quot;that's one's choice whether to gamble on that or not&quot;, experience tells us that that's a choice <b>we as a society cannot afford people to make.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Added emphasis.<br /> <br /> And that's really the crux of the matter, you believe that for the good of society my right to choose what happens with my money should be forsaken, I don't.<br /> That is where ideology takes over for facts. We can discuss what has happened until we are blue in the face, but when it comes to what SHOULD happen we will likely never agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T08:14:46-07:00","id":998230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998109#post998109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm sorry, this isn't conservative?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm prepared to hear your arguments for why this is not conservative. It's the third post, it's the only one before Charlaquin's that details ideological postures. It's an almost definitively conservative post - the only part that deviates is where they say that they don't like the control of the world's resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bLets see it's not Conservative for the pro gun control, and on fiscal matters they clearly stated they are to the far left. Those are the two big ones, which pretty much would get you dirty looks if you call yourself a conservative, which the poster called themselves a moderate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9486,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","user":"JBRocky","date":". 11-04-2016, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T08:35:51-07:00","id":998236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998224#post998224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Added emphasis.<br /> <br /> And that's really the crux of the matter, you believe that for the good of society my right to choose what happens with my money should be forsaken, I don't.<br /> That is where ideology takes over for facts. We can discuss what has happened until we are blue in the face, but when it comes to what SHOULD happen we will likely never agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, no, that's where economics wins out over ideology. We've seen what happens when the economy collapses and everyone is broke and it's not pretty. So our society made a conscious decision to insure against it. Like all insurance policies, the cost is slightly higher than the benefit, but it smooths out the precipitious drop at the bottom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T08:58:05-07:00","id":998246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998236#post998236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, no, that's where economics wins out over ideology. We've seen what happens when the economy collapses and everyone is broke and it's not pretty. So our society made a conscious decision to insure against it. Like all insurance policies, the cost is slightly higher than the benefit, but it smooths out the precipitious drop at the bottom.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wasn't referring to 'winning' anything. You are right that in American history the side that said we needed social security won and we have it.<br /> <br /> But I was referring to the point in conversation when something becomes an opinion. An opinion on whether that cost is justified. Some think it is, others disagree. Economics can answer what is likely to happen under each situation, but it is still an opinion of which one is better than the other. Not saying that that opinion cannot be discussed or changed, my personal opinions change all the time. Just that the conversation is quite different at that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:00:12-07:00","id":998248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998230#post998230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bLets see it's not Conservative for the pro gun control, and on fiscal matters they clearly stated they are to the far left. Those are the two big ones, which pretty much would get you dirty looks if you call yourself a conservative, which the poster called themselves a moderate.</div> </div> </div> </div>As has already been noted, pro-gun control is not an inherently non-conservative stance. It's not the stance of the Republic party, which considers itself to be the conservative party, but actual control policies are not inherently binary in this regard. A functional universal background check system is, for example, something the majority of conservatives consider a good idea. It's something the NRA used to support, and the NRA's move to being more radical over such topics as the organization came under the sway of corporate lobbyists over regular gun owners famously caused Bush Sr. to publicly rip up his NRA membership card in disgust when they opposed his conservative minded gun control package.<br /> <br /> What is now called, &quot;common sense&quot; gun legislation used to be incredibly non-partisan and centrist policy, with the debates only on the outer edges of the issue. The shift to convince the American right that any gun control is bad and a partisan issue is something that happened in my life time.<br /> <br /> And this goes back to a weird thing about all this. The idea of &quot;purity&quot; or needing to be completely one way or the other on the political spectrum. If the majority of an individuals policy positions are conservative, are they conservative, or are the not because they agree with liberals on some things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:05:05-07:00","id":998251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=997723#post997723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's enough of a baseline. I am happy to talk any specific point that anyone wants to bring up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with several of these positions. I think that when you actually discuss narrow topics, the conversation can become a lot more nuanced than simple tribal identifiers of &quot;conservative&quot; and &quot;liberal&quot; or whatever labels are preferred to be used.<br /> <br /> A spot that I find myself coming into conflict a bit on is the concept of &quot;Small Government&quot;. In general, I do prefer for government to be as small and non-intrusive as possible. However, I do think the government provides a vital role in maintaining stability, order and regulation that benefits society. An example that I can provide here is the Food and Drug Administration. While there can be a strong argument that poor food products in a market won't survive by customers preferring products that are considered poor value or substandard, there are examples in history of people taking actions for motive of profit that is drastically hazardous to the health of the populace. A prime example here is during the 18th century, Bakers would add adulterants to the breads they baked in order to reduce the amount of flour they use. Examples of adulterants included chalk (not strictly poisonous, but in the amounts used, not good for your health), alum, lead oxide and even copper sulfate. The FDA provides an important role by making sure that products are actually safe for consumption and it's a role that was determined to be necessary strictly due to the many bad examples throughout history of bad actors (BN: This doesn't mean the FDA doesn't have problems that can use fixing, but strictly that there is a vital service being provided that only the government can perform due to having the authority and expectation of society).<br /> <br /> And so the concept of &quot;Small Government&quot; is, I think, rather flexible from how I view it. I expect certain services from my government, and while I prefer government kept as small as possible, if there is a recognition of a service that should be provided, I do expect government to expand to provide that service. It's for that reason that I support a public health care option, as I think there needs to be a standard of affordable health care for society and because I think private health care options should have an expectation of minimum services at a particular rate so that private health care can actually rise or fall based on an expected standard.<br /> <br /> So, I'm curious as to what you think of that more nuanced look at &quot;Small Government&quot;. Do you think that the role of government can be expanded while still holding to a philosophy of &quot;Small Government&quot;?<br /> <br /> Side Note: I don't think you need to worry about defending the 18th Amendment because the 21st Amendment repealed it. So the 18th Amendment is pretty much only on there as a historical record. It has no effect or impact on the current day. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:05:07-07:00","id":998252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998248#post998248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this goes back to a weird thing about all this. The idea of &quot;purity&quot; or needing to be completely one way or the other on the political spectrum. If the majority of an individuals policy positions are conservative, are they conservative, or are the not because they agree with liberals on some things?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have actually been struggling with whether I should continue to post in this thread for this exact reason. Maybe I am not the 'conservative' that the OP wanted. I don't usually think of myself as one, even given that some of my ideals line up with the 'right'.<br /> <br /> Edit: To address <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a> since there was an interstitial post.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, every topic has much more nuance when you actually bother to discuss it rather than just using blanket terms.<br /> <br /> Small Government is another one of these for sure. You can see from my other posts that I do agree that there is a role for government in society. And that is an area that I am constantly adjusting my stance. The two sub descriptors of Libertarianism that I think are of import here are Minarchism and Anarchocapitalism.<br /> <br /> For Reference:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minarchism\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minarchism\" target=\"_blank\"> Night-watchman state - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minarchism\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minarchism </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libertarianism#Anarcho-capitalism\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libertarianism#Anarcho-capitalism\" target=\"_blank\"> Libertarianism - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libertarianism#Anarcho-capitalism\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libertarianism#Anarcho-capitalism </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Anarchocapatlism has an appeal to me from an ideological stand point. It is resonant that no authority should be able to force me to do a thing (preventing me from harming is different than forcing me to help). But at the same time there is a lot of things that I am not sure could be accomplished without some oversight in the form of a government, and government needs funding and authority to function. The most pragmatic approach I think for now is to try to maintain as small a government as possible and to constantly re-evaluate the needs for and methods of, all governmental institutions. As well, in the United States at least this means reviewing what is delegated to the federal government versus regional. <br /> <br /> I also believe that the Constitutional Amendment system has been sadly neglected in recent years. If there is actually a national desire to see something change that is fundamental to the Constitution, such as granting the federal government new powers, then an Amendment is the correct way to do that.<br /> <br /> Side Note: I realize it was repealed, but I was avoiding the statement of supporting ALL of them specifically not just because of the 18th but also because I would need to double check a few to be sure that I want to say that I support them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 11-04-2016, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:12:56-07:00","id":998259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998252#post998252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have actually been struggling with whether I should continue to post in this thread for this exact reason. Maybe I am not the 'conservative' that the OP wanted. I don't usually think of myself as one, even given that some of my ideals line up with the 'right'.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, I don't really think that every liberal or &quot;left&quot; policy is the correct course of action either (Example: I do not support using the No-Fly list as a basis for a gun control measure of denying purchasing a firearm to a person, because I see the No-Fly list as an unconstitutional policy which also causes more harm than good due to how it's implemented). I think there is a solid middle ground between &quot;conservative&quot; ideals and &quot;liberal&quot; ideals that will be more effective in the long run. Working out places of common ground and areas of largest concern might allow a more nuanced approach to finding a path that works the best for the most people, with the consideration that we're all living here together.<br /> <br /> This really does require the people involved in the conversation to not think the worst of who they're talking to, though. And that's been... problematic of late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 11-04-2016, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:25:41-07:00","id":998262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998259#post998259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it helps, I don't really think that every liberal or &quot;left&quot; policy is the correct course of action either (Example: I do not support using the No-Fly list as a basis for a gun control measure of denying purchasing a firearm to a person, because I see the No-Fly list as an unconstitutional policy which also causes more harm than good due to how it's implemented). I think there is a solid middle ground between &quot;conservative&quot; ideals and &quot;liberal&quot; ideals that will be more effective in the long run. Working out places of common ground and areas of largest concern might allow a more nuanced approach to finding a path that works the best for the most people, with the consideration that we're all living here together.<br /> <br /> This really does require the people involved in the conversation to not think the worst of who they're talking to, though. And that's been... problematic of late.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yes, I agree. I was specifically referring to this threads call for 'Conservatives' though. My comments may not be enough in line for that. Given the previous 'hijacking' of the thread I wouldn't want to continue it rather than take it more on track. I do think that the origianl basis for the thread is fundementally flawed though and that is why it went off 'track' so badly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:34:03-07:00","id":998267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998262#post998262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh yes, I agree. I was specifically referring to this threads call for 'Conservatives' though. My comments may not be enough in line for that. Given the previous 'hijacking' of the thread I wouldn't want to continue it rather than take it more on track. I do think that the origianl basis for the thread is fundementally flawed though and that is why it went off 'track' so badly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of think that there's no real authority that can definitively say whether a particular person is &quot;Conservative&quot; and so I think the only reasonable determination for that is whether a person self-identifies as &quot;Conservative&quot; or not. So if you consider yourself &quot;Conservative&quot;, I'm not really going to argue with you on that.<br /> <br /> Over all, I'm not sure what exactly the purpose of this thread was. But I don't think the OP is really participating in it much now and so the purpose of the thread is more of what we make of it, and I kind of like considering policies through a &quot;conservative&quot; view because a lot of places I generally hand out tend to focus more on the &quot;liberal&quot; view. It's refreshing and a good challenge to my initial premises regarding policies.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:37:50-07:00","id":998272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998259#post998259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example: I do not support using the No-Fly list as a basis for a gun control measure of denying purchasing a firearm to a person, because I see the No-Fly list as an unconstitutional policy which also causes more harm than good due to how it's implemented.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would not surprise me if some of the Congresscritters in support of using the No-Fly list to control guns are doing so specifically to challenge the Constitutionality of the No-Fly List <i>itself</i>. I know I am.<br /> <br /> FWIW, I consider myself a Small Government Socialist. The places I break with the Libertarian POV is where the math just doesn't bear them out and that liberty and prosperity can be increased through the use of Government Action due to economies of scale. Social Security, Public Education, The FDA, and the Interstate Highway System are a few examples of these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:13:02-07:00","id":998324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998230#post998230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bLets see it's not Conservative for the pro gun control, and on fiscal matters they clearly stated they are to the far left. Those are the two big ones, which pretty much would get you dirty looks if you call yourself a conservative, which the poster called themselves a moderate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but calling them a moderate borders on dishonesty. There's more than one form of conservatism - they're pretty definitively a social conservative.<br /> <br /> As Heavy Arms points out, you're making a case of &quot;Well they're left on guns and fiscal policy. They're a moderate!&quot;<br /> <br /> Mixing peas and carrots just means they aren't ideologically pure. The balance of their beliefs is conservative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 11-04-2016, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:25:55-07:00","id":998332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998324#post998324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, but calling them a moderate borders on dishonesty. There's more than one form of conservatism - they're pretty definitively a social conservative.<br /> <br /> As Heavy Arms points out, you're making a case of &quot;Well they're left on guns and fiscal policy. They're a moderate!&quot;<br /> <br /> Mixing peas and carrots just means they aren't ideologically pure. The balance of their beliefs is conservative.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hrm, what do you think makes a &quot;moderate&quot;... moderate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:35:18-07:00","id":998341,"title":"","content":"Was going to quote Heavy Arms and then Paradim but figured it's just easy to start typing and chat. <br /> <br /> Lets start with what the 3rd poster mentioned gun control he specifically brought up what he called Assault Rifles. Conservatives when they hear this will normally use the term Semi-Auto Rifles and possibly even explain the difference and why they don't believe they should be banned.<br /> <br /> Now to Universal background checks. Yes Conservatives do agree we need background checks but will also say we already have them and need to concentrate on enforcing the laws we already have in place. Simply put, we already have that in place and can't even enforce those properly why should we make more.<br /> <br /> Now to what Paradim said about the No-fly list. I totally agree with you there and it bothers me when people think it's a good idea to use the list as a way to determine guilt. This is not violation of the 2nd Amendment but the Due Process clause of the 5th the on where you are innocent until proven guilt, scary when both the ACLU and the NRA agree for the same reason. Now this doesn't mean I think terrorists should have guns but if you want to call some a terrorist take them to court and prove it. We have done this to groups before in our history such as blacks shortly after the civil war which is why there is a 14th amendment and to Japanese Americans when we put them in camps during WW2 and both are wrong.<br /> <br /> But more on the subject of finding the middle ground on gun control. One of the problems the right has with this is how many times will we have to compromise? Will it just be once, or will it be every time something bad happens with a gun so we have to go far beyond what we originally agreed to or were even asked to do? While people scoff at the idea it is a legitimate concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:46:21-07:00","id":998347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998324#post998324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, but calling them a moderate borders on dishonesty. There's more than one form of conservatism - they're pretty definitively a social conservative.<br /> <br /> As Heavy Arms points out, you're making a case of &quot;Well they're left on guns and fiscal policy. They're a moderate!&quot;<br /> <br /> Mixing peas and carrots just means they aren't ideologically pure. The balance of their beliefs is conservative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't appreciate you calling me dishonest just because I don't agree with you. I read his views on things and he has some Conservative views and some liberal ones, plus he says he is in the middle which what is normally called a moderate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:47:34-07:00","id":998348,"title":"","content":"I'm against gun control. Not because I think the president's going to come in and take away everyone's guns, but because I think no matter how many barriers you put in the way, as long as people think taking pictures of their toddlers with guns to support one thing or another or just show off is a brilliant idea, you're going to have problems. A criminal record doesn't tell you whether a person is a responsible person or not, or that their children or other people who have access to their house are responsible or not. That all ties into my beliefs regarding the need for education reform.<br /> <br /> I'm pro death penalty as well. But I believe with our current, clear problems with police corruption and judicial error, you're going to send wrongfully convicted people to prison and potentially allow the state to execute innocent men or women, which is a travesty. So just like above, I hold some conservative beliefs but they're conditional on changes in other aspects of society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-04-2016, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:38:15-07:00","id":998472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998348#post998348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm against gun control. Not because I think the president's going to come in and take away everyone's guns, but because I think no matter how many barriers you put in the way, as long as people think taking pictures of their toddlers with guns to support one thing or another or just show off is a brilliant idea, you're going to have problems. A criminal record doesn't tell you whether a person is a responsible person or not, or that their children or other people who have access to their house are responsible or not. That all ties into my beliefs regarding the need for education reform.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a fairly reductive argument that uses one example of gun violence as evidence for why basing gun control on criminal records won't actually solve the problem. Obviously as long as there are guns in this country there will be gun related accidents, deaths, and so on. I personally use the same evidence for why I would prefer the kind of gun regulations that exist in more extreme countries, like Japan as just one example. I may be a bit more lenient on this, because I think if you want to buy and register a gun at say, a shooting range, or for hunting, that's fine. Have people rent out a deposit box-like locker or safe on the premise, you can go to the shooting range and fire your gun. You can take it out hunting - so long as you don't take it beyond the specified areas, and check it back in by an appointed time. Precedent like Australia has shown that regulation can be a very effective response to gun violence.<br /> <br /> However, I live in America, and the culture is such that I don't believe that kind of regulation will ever get approved. Still, it's been shown to work quite well in other parts of the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pro death penalty as well. But I believe with our current, clear problems with police corruption and judicial error, you're going to send wrongfully convicted people to prison and potentially allow the state to execute innocent men or women, which is a travesty. So just like above, I hold some conservative beliefs but they're conditional on changes in other aspects of society. </div> </div> </div>I was pro death penalty for a long time, until my sister coaxed me into researching it thoroughly. Firstly, putting someone through the legal process of a death sentence takes <b>years</b>. It costs <b>a lot</b> of money going through the court cases, the appeal process, etc, etc. All of these things are done to help insure that innocent people are <b>not</b> put to death, removing them for the sake of cost, in other words putting someone on the express lane, just increases the chance you're going to kill an innocent person. In the end it's cheaper and arguably more humane to just keep them in prison, and if future evidence exonerates them, then you get to feel good about not murdering an innocent person.<br /> <br /> Since then, I wouldn't even want the Death Penalty 'in a perfect world', because I don't believe in justice as a form of punishment to make others feel better. I'd much rather our prison systems focus on rehabilitation, which they certainly don't, especially in areas where it has been privatized. Violence and negative behaviors don't come about because people are evil or past redemption, they happen because there is a huge population in this country who don't have hope of achieving the American Dream, whose virtues are diminished by poverty and the oppression that faces people trapped within it. They do bad things because those behaviors are learned in order to survive the situations they found themselves in. I would much rather spend the hundreds of millions of dollars spent sending people to an electric chair, on social programs to lift them out of poverty, and to show them how they can be a part of society rather than excluded from it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Reading this back, it felt a bit pushy and fairly heated. I apologize for my tone and am not trying to demean you for holding the views that you do, just trying to explain my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 11-04-2016, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T16:00:08-07:00","id":998483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=998472#post998472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a fairly reductive argument that uses one example of gun violence as evidence for why basing gun control on criminal records won't actually solve the problem. Obviously as long as there are guns in this country there will be gun related accidents, deaths, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're mistaking my point. The reduction is in a different angle. I think everyone should be able to have guns, but I think we need to build a more responsible and mature populace. As we can look across the ocean and see elsewhere, if people want to kill, they're going to kill. A gun or lack of one is not going to make a difference in a world where a truck can be used to kill dozens and the directions to make bombs are readily available online.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was pro death penalty for a long time, until my sister coaxed me into researching it thoroughly. Firstly, putting someone through the legal process of a death sentence takes <b>years</b>. It costs <b>a lot</b> of money going through the court cases, the appeal process, etc, etc. All of these things are done to help insure that innocent people are <b>not</b> put to death, removing them for the sake of cost, in other words putting someone on the express lane, just increases the chance you're going to kill an innocent person. In the end it's cheaper and arguably more humane to just keep them in prison, and if future evidence exonerates them, then you get to feel good about not murdering an innocent person. </div> </div> </div>'We took away fifty years of his life, but at least we didn't kill him, isn't much to cheer about considering how our prison system treats people and how they are treated outside. I understand the point of expenses, which is why, again, I said it is conditional on a better judicial system. It is an idealistic belief, but many are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since then, I wouldn't even want the Death Penalty 'in a perfect world', because I don't believe in justice as a form of punishment to make others feel better. I'd much rather our prison systems focus on rehabilitation, which they certainly don't, especially in areas where it has been privatized. Violence and negative behaviors don't come about because people are evil or past redemption, they happen because there is a huge population in this country who don't have hope of achieving the American Dream, whose virtues are diminished by poverty and the oppression that faces people trapped within it. They do bad things because those behaviors are learned in order to survive the situations they found themselves in. I would much rather spend the hundreds of millions of dollars spent sending people to an electric chair, on social programs to lift them out of poverty, and to show them how they can be a part of society rather than excluded from it. </div> </div> </div>Certainly many commit crime because it's the only options available to them. But some people hurt and kill people because they want to. Ideally with a better judicial system and prison system that doesn't nearly guarantee a return after a stint in prison, we'll be able to differentiate the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T11:40:21-08:00","id":1504860,"title":"","content":"I realise I am necrothreading, but I am curious. <br /> What are the political beliefs of the average, say, vampire or Exalted player <br /> The 50th percentile so to speak <br /> Assume that we are ignoring economic issues for simplicity sake <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b. Does anyone have a guess? I am willing to assume our average is to the left of centre, but only because I assume that a fundamentalist Christian is unlikely to play these games <br /> Then again, with Christianity in decline would a secular hard right person have the same taboo? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T19:28:20-08:00","id":1504894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1504860#post1504860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realise I am necrothreading, but I am curious.<br /> What are the political beliefs of the average, say, vampire or Exalted player<br /> The 50th percentile so to speak<br /> Assume that we are ignoring economic issues for simplicity sake<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b. Does anyone have a guess? I am willing to assume our average is to the left of centre, but only because I assume that a fundamentalist Christian is unlikely to play these games<br /> Then again, with Christianity in decline would a secular hard right person have the same taboo?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the players I know were right of the center; there was a few that were Neo-NAZIs, one that claimed to be conservative, but, get into all sorts of fetish-stuff; most were, your typical-goths/trench-coats/heavy-metal. One friend, even would go online pretending to be a 13-year old girl, and when a older-guy wanted to meet up, he'd show-up and beat him up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T00:19:59-08:00","id":1504910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1504894#post1504894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of the players I know were right of the center; there was a few that were Neo-NAZIs, one that claimed to be conservative, but, get into all sorts of fetish-stuff; most were, your typical-goths/trench-coats/heavy-metal. One friend, even would go online pretending to be a 13-year old girl, and when a older-guy wanted to meet up, he'd show-up and beat him up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure if the later even counts as an ideology lol. <br /> Still, I kinda wish I could get objective demographics. <br /> Maybe force everyone to get a political ideology quiz? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T18:50:57-08:00","id":1504991,"title":"","content":"I'm just a reporter, reporting what I saw, with my own eyes. I don't know if they were, or are, or truly count as, &quot;Conservative&quot;, but, some were kinda jerks, and you know what they stay; if young and a Conservative, you have no heart; if you're old and a liberal, you don't have a brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T12:57:18-08:00","id":1505035,"title":"","content":"I've played with players with conservative beliefs. Theyre pretty much the same as any other player, one was a really solid gm.<br /> <br /> People are ultimately people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T07:33:42-07:00","id":1506308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b