"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\">forum rules</a>.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T22:52:48-08:00","id":1525499,"title":"","content":"Engaging in CS2 gameplay and exploring <a href=\"https://scope.gg/teammate\" target=\"_blank\">cs2 teamfinder</a>\u200b was a game-changing experience that transformed my competitive journey. CS2's adrenaline-pumping matches pushed me to refine my skills and seek new challenges. Venturing into CS2 TeamFinder, I discovered a community of like-minded players passionate about teamwork and strategic gameplay. Collaborating with skilled teammates not only elevated my performance but also fostered lasting connections within the CS2 community. The platform's intuitive interface streamlined the process of finding compatible teammates, ensuring exhilarating matches and shared victories. CS2 and TeamFinder combined, creating a success story of skill enhancement, camaraderie, and unparalleled gaming adventures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27939-dazert1","user":"Dazert1","date":". 11-19-2023, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27939-dazert1","name":"Dazert1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27939_1.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T22:58:26-08:00","id":1525500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1506350#post1506350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking for myself I try to keep my political beliefs out of my games for the simple reason I come here for playing fun games with my mates or coming here on the boards and seeing what the new topics are and comment if I find it interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to be wary of bringing my own beliefs in as some sort of meta rule. I might present them positively in game but I won't portray them as utopian or even succesful. <br /> Its probably worth noting I prefer carmarilla games over anarch as written by a mile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T09:51:11-08:00","id":1525519,"title":"","content":"Why stir up needless trouble when you don't have to and we are all here to play in worlds that we like and put our spin on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T14:30:15-08:00","id":1525662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1525519#post1525519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why stir up needless trouble when you don't have to and we are all here to play in worlds that we like and put our spin on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true; most of my WoD, are very conservative, in that, the governments are almost always totalitarian or fascist and very, very corrupt. Back in day, I used to like World War 2, NAZI-stuff etc. I wasn't a NAZI, I just read a lot of books about them and played a lot of World War 2 video-games. <br /> <br /> Also, I'm reading, <i>The Condition of the Working Class In England</i> by Fredrich Engels; the Manchester he describes makes a good background for a 1800's English Requiem-game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T04:41:20-08:00","id":1525682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1525662#post1525662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in day, I used to like World War 2, NAZI-stuff etc. I wasn't a NAZI,</div> </div> </div> </div>Did anybody say you were?{eyebrow raised in confusion}<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T17:59:07-08:00","id":1525760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1525682#post1525682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did anybody say you were?{eyebrow raised in confusion}<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Back in day, I got a lot of, &quot;Dude-bros&quot;, liked me because they thought I was like them, until they found out I wasn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T12:15:39-08:00","id":1526128,"title":"","content":"Not a conservative and never was (nor ever will be), but I am an ex-leftist, if that counts.<br /> <br /> I used to be a far-leftist into intersectionality, Marxism, critical theory, and the like but it eventually overwhelmed me. All it did was get me in a very toxic environment surrounded by toxic people. Eventually, after a few breakdowns, I renounced that shit. I renounced it, rejected it, and condemned it. And I'm never going back to it. It's just secular Puritanism, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Now I'm just a nihilist, a hedonist, and an immoralist. I don't really fit neatly onto the political compass except maybe in the most vague sense of libertarianism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 11-29-2023, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T10:17:12-08:00","id":1527304,"title":"","content":"I loved the Fable and Fallout series myself Mabert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T12:13:45-08:00","id":1527319,"title":"","content":"In regards to political exetrimism. I view it as a losers game as it doesn't matter if your right, left or something else. There will always be someone who will be more of a zealot and put a target on you for not being exetreme enough or if you disagree with them on many issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T13:03:54-08:00","id":1527321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1527319#post1527319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to political exetrimism. I view it as a losers game as it doesn't matter if your right, left or something else. There will always be someone who will be more of a zealot and put a target on you for not being exetreme enough or if you disagree with them on many issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>This guy gets it<br /> <br /> I'm of the opinion that if everything is political, then nothing is truly political.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T10:12:27-08:00","id":1527381,"title":"","content":"People are free to identify with whatever ideologies they want. That said, this was supposed a thread about conservative identifying gamers, not a thread for &quot;not lefty identifying ones.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T18:21:11-08:00","id":1527403,"title":"","content":"And the only really truly, &quot;Conservative&quot;, RPG game I found was, &quot;The Price of Freedom&quot;; it has a lot of scary, right-wing stuff in it, but, they authors got overly excited about rules for helicopters, so, I think it was just, source, material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T10:59:28-08:00","id":1527634,"title":"","content":"How does one truly keep politics out of anything? We all have our beliefs/biases and we try to keep it out our games as best we can, but it's always going to creep in no matter how much we wish it otherwise. The best that can be done that's it done in subtle and nuanaced manner that makes everyone think and come together for a civil debate. Sorry for the rambling post folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T18:57:30-08:00","id":1528193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1527634#post1527634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one truly keep politics out of anything? We all have our beliefs/biases and we try to keep it out our games as best we can, but it's always going to creep in no matter how much we wish it otherwise. The best that can be done that's it done in subtle and nuanaced manner that makes everyone think and come together for a civil debate. Sorry for the rambling post folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>When we first started to RPG V:tM, we were in a suburb and politics really wasn't an issue. Yeah, we had extreme friends, but they were manageable. However, right now, I'm in an inner-city, and I don't care about national-politics, who's Conservative or Liberal; I'm more concerned about drug-addicts breaking into my car and house, than a person's political-beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T00:38:46-08:00","id":1528204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1527634#post1527634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one truly keep politics out of anything? We all have our beliefs/biases and we try to keep it out our games as best we can, but it's always going to creep in no matter how much we wish it otherwise. The best that can be done that's it done in subtle and nuanaced manner that makes everyone think and come together for a civil debate. Sorry for the rambling post folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's never perfect but being mindful of your bias' helps and sincerly engaging with a setting on its own terms helps. The other day someone commented that the anarchs are the best sect to run due to left wing dissident fantasies but if I actually engage my irl beliefs sincerly then I'm probably rooting for the hunters with inquisition in the same way as someone might root for Democrats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T20:12:14-08:00","id":1528244,"title":"","content":"Far Leftists born after 1983 aren't worth a damn. They don't know theory nor do they care about the working class proletariat.<br /> <br /> All they know is Starbucks, charge they phone, Everything Is Political, criticize and de facto censor &quot;problematic&quot; media, listen to punk rock, be intersectional, eat vegan hot chip, and lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 01-09-2024, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-10T10:43:05-08:00","id":1528333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1528204#post1528204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's never perfect but being mindful of your bias' helps and sincerly engaging with a setting on its own terms helps. The other day someone commented that the anarchs are the best sect to run due to left wing dissident fantasies but if I actually engage my irl beliefs sincerly then I'm probably rooting for the hunters with inquisition in the same way as someone might root for Democrats.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned before my Malkavian is an Anarch by default but finds there goals unrealistic and figures that such members will become like mommy and daddy sire. But this is getting off topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T03:45:05-08:00","id":1528986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1528244#post1528244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Far Leftists born after 1983 aren't worth a damn. They don't know theory nor do they care about the working class proletariat.<br /> <br /> All they know is Starbucks, charge they phone, Everything Is Political, criticize and de facto censor &quot;problematic&quot; media, listen to punk rock, be intersectional, eat vegan hot chip, and lie.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>So this is a group attack in a thread that could very easily devolve into group attacks if most people weren't bringing their A-game. Take a warning. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T06:58:27-08:00","id":1529004,"title":"","content":"Apologies on that.<br /> <br /> It was meant mainly as a joke and I was mainly parodying that dumb &quot;Women Born After 1993&quot; copypasta that made the rounds online a few years back. I didn't mean to actually attack anyone with that post.<br /> <br /> I will be more careful and considerate with my posts from now on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 01-20-2024, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T09:04:49-07:00","id":1533703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1504860#post1504860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realise I am necrothreading, but I am curious.<br /> What are the political beliefs of the average, say, vampire or Exalted player<br /> The 50th percentile so to speak<br /> Assume that we are ignoring economic issues for simplicity sake<br /> \u200b. Does anyone have a guess? I am willing to assume our average is to the left of centre, but only because I assume that a fundamentalist Christian is unlikely to play these games<br /> Then again, with Christianity in decline would a secular hard right person have the same taboo?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that role players probably lean left, but I actually know a lot of devout Christian conservatives who have or currently role play. Mostly D&amp;D, but WoD in some cases. I remember when I grew up, fundamentalist Christians basically hated role playing games and the fantasy genre in general. Now they love fantasy, especially Lord of the Rings, D&amp;D, and the like. It\u2019s a big improvement.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m an atheist myself but I have a lot of friends who are fundamentalist Christians and a surprising number are into role playing and nearly every one likes the fantasy genre.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m a right wing atheist and I\u2019m not even sure what taboo I would have against role playing? There are certain political elements to WoD that I object to, depending on the book and game line, but they aren\u2019t deal breakers for me.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know of any statistics regarding this, just my personal experiences and my own opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 04-06-2024, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T09:33:27-07:00","id":1533704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This statement reads as deeply unserious and I highly doubt it's veracity. For that matter, if someone is trashing and &quot;abandoning&quot; the reality that is institutionalized racism and the intersectionality of class and racial struggles due to supposedly toxic people. I think those toxic people are better off without that person around.<br /> <br /> In fact naw, Just sounds like an excuse to be racist.<br /> <br /> Given the hamfisted ageist criticism levied at younger people , I think I was right in my assessment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, I don't want to bring this back up but since the topic has been bumped, I might as well get this out of the way...<br /> <br /> You do realize I'm both Black and queer (specifically both a transgender male and bisexual), right?<br /> <br /> And the whole post about &quot;far-leftists born after 1983&quot; was meant as a joke. It's a parody of a copypasta. I was born in 1992 for fuck's sake, so I'm not THAT old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 04-06-2024, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T12:33:01-07:00","id":1533713,"title":"","content":"I fall into the Liberatian and moderate/centre conservative camp myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T14:03:52-07:00","id":1533719,"title":"","content":"I don't really fit anywhere on the political compass, tbh.<br /> <br /> At best, I'd be a libertarian centrist but even that's not entirely accurate. Like I said before, I used to be a far-leftist (partly due to my background) but I fell out of it and became heavily disillusioned with it.<br /> <br /> Said it before and I will say it again: I'm a hedonist, a nihilist, and generally apathetic. If everything is political, then nothing is!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T18:01:55-07:00","id":1533727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1533719#post1533719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If everything is political, then nothing is!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's possible for a trait to be ubiquitous but come in numerous variations. It would be like saying everything having a colour means that nothing does.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T18:35:32-07:00","id":1533730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1533727#post1533727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's possible for a trait to be ubiquitous but come in numerous variations. It would be like saying everything having a colour means that nothing does.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but some people obsessively politicize damn near everything in regards to often trivial things like pop culture and entertainment and this is a major problem on both wings of the political spectrum. Some people on social media will point to fictional in-universe politics as a way to try and prove that &quot;Everything is Political!&quot; and try to justify trying to shoehorn preachy hamfisted political messages into the most trivial of entertainment. Their go-to lines are &quot;Everything is political!&quot; (if left-wing) or &quot;Politics is downstream of culture!&quot; (if right-wing)<br /> <br /> Sometimes entertainment and fiction should just be that. Sometimes it can be used to convey a message and if it's done properly and usually with some nuance, it can be actually brilliant (see Metal Gear Solid) and sometimes there is no hidden meaning, commentary, or allegory at all and the fictional story really is just a fictional story (see The Lord of the Rings)<br /> <br /> So I've taken that mantra of &quot;If everything is political, then nothing is!&quot; as a response to those types of people who try to shoehorn deep social, political, or religious meanings into everything related to pop culture or entertainment. Not everything needs to have some sort of deep intellectual or political meaning nor does everything need to criticize or comment on something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 04-06-2024, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T20:31:02-07:00","id":1533732,"title":"","content":"I identify myself as a conservative, but that means a lot of different things to different people. I don\u2019t fit into the Republican box, I\u2019m a registered independent and I agree with the mainstream GOP on some things and not on other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T21:34:11-07:00","id":1533734,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day is we want all the same things, but have different opinions on how to get there. The problem arises when idealogical purity is more important than good governance and nothing gets done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T23:47:05-07:00","id":1533738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1533734#post1533734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the day is we want all the same things, but have different opinions on how to get there. The problem arises when idealogical purity is more important than good governance and nothing gets done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently somebody doesn\u2019t want the same things - somebody gave us all a thumbs down \ud83d\ude33<br /> <br /> I largely agree, most people want the same things - basically to make the world better for everyone - but sometimes they have different ideas of how to achieve that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T09:20:57-07:00","id":1533752,"title":"","content":"Not much we can do about that Sergeant Brother. People are going to believe whatever they want no matter what information is brought before them that debunks it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T09:25:12-07:00","id":1533753,"title":"","content":"Oh I agree that real world politics should be kept to a minimum in entertainment as we go to movies, play games or listen to music as an escape for our troubles Matt. Nobody likes to be preached, pandered or condasecded by folks who live in a bubble of privilege and don't really know how the rest of us live.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T09:36:30-07:00","id":1533755,"title":"","content":"I agree too. Shared hobbies really have the potential to bring people together and show us our shared humanity. Being overly political is divisive and undermines that. It would be better for everyone to be able to put politics aside and enjoy interests (like RPGs) together and we\u2019d not only be happier, but it would also help the realm of politics too by making people less divided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T14:17:16-07:00","id":1533768,"title":"","content":"I'm not a conservative but on a general note, it's very hard to get away from politics. It's the process of decision-making within a group of beings (&quot;beings&quot; to account for fictional scenarios in RPGs like aliens, fantasy-races etc.). Sure, you can try to get away from it. That's where the term &quot;escapism&quot; is apt, I think. You have a little accident with your car, the car gets damaged, you go to a local garage where you know a guy because he's your drinking-buddy at a local bar, you ask the guy &quot;Can you fix this?&quot;, he says &quot;Sure thing, boss... but next round's on you!&quot;, you thank him and that's it. Completely unrealistic. But it sounds nice, it feels nice. And that\u2019s because it's escapism.<br /> <br /> The moment you make it more realistic, drip by drip as you picture what would happen in reality this whole thing becomes political. Who's responsible for what, who decides what happens and how it happens? The moment you delve into such matters, things become political. Now on the one hand you might run into trouble when you have people who are politically active and are very aware of these types of interrogations and have very particular answers but on the other hand you also might run into trouble when people encounter these questions and aren't aware of how present politics are and can't deal with the fact how easily various situations can lead to questions of a political nature.<br /> <br /> You can have a guy with an Austrian accent being called a US-born special-ops super-soldier or something called John Matrix and you just nod right along &quot;No questions, go ahead, thumbs up from me.&quot; but even then\u2026 the moment you start to talk about what he has done, who is coming after him, who he\u2019s fighting and why and how he\u2019s fighting\u2026 it all becomes political again. The Rambo movies are very political, for example, as well.<br /> <br /> Politics are hard to get away from unless you cling to stereotypes and very conventional thinking. And that comes with the assumption that you\u2019re addressing an audience where politics aren\u2019t perceived because those aforementioned stereotypes and conventional thinking are just perceived as \u201cnormal\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T15:44:56-07:00","id":1533771,"title":"","content":"I think the &quot;D&amp;D wheelchair&quot; debate even existing puts a pretty big question mark on how much people really want apolitical escapist fantasy vs. escapism from politics they don't like.<br /> <br /> If apolitical entertainment via escapist fantasy was really something people valued, the debate wouldn't be a debate, it would be a bunch of whiners getting dragged on social media. There's nothing political about wheelchairs. It is very escapist to have a setting where someone in a wheelchair is just a character quirk. And it's certainly a fantasy when a wheelchair doesn't stop you from dungeon crawling.<br /> <br /> Every argument I've seen against wheelchairs in D&amp;D is a violation of at least one of the three things: &quot;It's not realistic!&quot; who cares it's fantasy. &quot;It's not part of the genre!&quot; who cares, escapism means we're free to get creative with genre conventions. &quot;It's putting politics in our game!&quot; if having people with wheelchairs in your game is political, then not having them in your game is also political, and it's not apolitical.<br /> <br /> Sure, it's probably a lot of loud voices on the Internet that are far from a majority, but it was still a lot of loud voices about something so trivial to simply not care about if you don't want to use it.<br /> <br /> It gets even weirder to me when we're... on a forum like this one, where we're united by a company that puts out pretty political games. When people say they want to play WtA or Exalted or Aeon, and say they want to keep real world politics &quot;out&quot; it's just a giant red flag to me because... why are you even playing these games? There are way better games if you want to have some raw power fantasy and don't have so many real world politics baked into the design of the games.<br /> <br /> Or when people say things like, &quot;You couldn't make [insert movie name] these days.&quot; Maybe that's a good thing? Entertainment media is a product of its time and place. If Blazing Saddles (I have no idea why so many people point to that as an example, it almost never got made over multiple issues back then) worked just as well in 1974 and 2024... that seems like a pretty bad thing to me. Thirty years should be a completely different media landscape where different movies are more relevant and different stories resonate more with audiences. We didn't stop making boundary pushing comedies or movies confronting racism at some point. Lots of &quot;classics&quot; were mixed in reception at the time, so it's impossible to say in 30 years which movies made around now are going to be seen as the stuff nobody makes any more... because that's just how culture works.<br /> <br /> It's a lot more useful to acknowledge politics so you can be clear about what you want or don't want than &quot;no politics&quot; usually ends up meaning. &quot;I want to punch Nazis, but I don't want to deal with active bigotry in play,&quot; is useful if I'm running a game of Adventure! because it actually tells me what to exclude to keep things fun. Having someone complain when punching Nazis involved seeing actual victims of the Nazi regime in play was ruining their fun because they thought a game about punching Nazis wouldn't get that &quot;political&quot; (yes, this has actually happened to me), happens because what &quot;no politics&quot; really means just isn't effective to leave as an assumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T04:05:14-07:00","id":1533802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1533771#post1533771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If Blazing Saddles (I have no idea why so many people point to that as an example</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because it uses a lot of racial slurs.<br /> <br /> Although the weird thing is that the way people talk about it, they almost seem to think that the racial slurs are something it endorses.<br /> <br /> Either way, it's a dumb thing to say both on the point that films with racial slurs still get made (did none of these people see Django Unchained), and there's still plenty of media that fucking makes fun of racism the way Blazing Saddles did (among which are... seriously, did none of these people see Django Unchained? The whole fucking scene mocking the KKK).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T04:10:17-07:00","id":1533803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1533755#post1533755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree too. Shared hobbies really have the potential to bring people together and show us our shared humanity. Being overly political is divisive and undermines that. It would be better for everyone to be able to put politics aside and enjoy interests (like RPGs) together and we\u2019d not only be happier, but it would also help the realm of politics too by making people less divided.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen another RPG forum in which a person refers to having been banned from yet another RPG forum in terms of slurs against transgender people and openly expressing contempt for the very idea of being transgender.<br /> <br /> I very much want to be divided from that person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T08:39:38-07:00","id":1533818,"title":"","content":"I also remember in Blazing Saddles how they also mocked racists in general including the Klan and Nazi's as half wits. In regards to gaming with say VTM, MTA or VTR we try to keep real world politics light in our game and focus on what is most important for our characters motivation.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-08-2024, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T15:04:52-07:00","id":1533855,"title":"","content":"OK...<br /> <br /> But that leads to part of my problem. If I'm playing Mage the Ascension, characters are going to members of Traditions/Crafts/Conventions, and they joined those groups because they align with the character's motivations, and all of those groups have strong ties to real world political issues. The Celestial Chorus isn't just a bunch of generic D&amp;D Clerics that cast magic by calling on divine power. They're people drawn from real world faiths, with biases born from those faiths as they try to incorporate into the Chorus's own attempt at a universalist umbrella monotheism. Mages need to care about stuff because that's the core of the &quot;will&quot; to bend reality. The Chorus is part of the Traditions' whole coalition to reshape modern society, and they want to make faith a strong part of that... something that's very relevant to real world politics.<br /> <br /> I don't know what keep it &quot;light&quot; means to you, but I can't imagine playing Ascension and not have real world politics matter to the game, because it matters to every faction in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T16:18:50-07:00","id":1533859,"title":"","content":"You can have real world ideologies in a setting or in individual games without using that setting or game to push an agenda or make certain potential players feel unwelcome. <br /> <br /> You can have a devout Christian Celestial Chorus member, an Asatru Verbena, a Marxist Virtual Adeot, and an Objectivist Son of Ether all as characters in the same party while not pushing or condemning any of those world views and regardless of what the players themselves believe. Maybe the characters can even argue politics or religion and it can be in good fun, maybe with the players of said characters disagreeing with the positions advocated by the characters.<br /> <br /> A game can have real world belief systems in it without trying to bully or exclude people based on their beliefs. I think that\u2019s what most of us mean, not that real world beliefs can never be mentioned in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T19:04:44-07:00","id":1533867,"title":"","content":"That just feels like goal post shifting to me. Instead of a nebulous &quot;light&quot; politics or apolitical escapism, you're just moving to an equally nebulous &quot;no pushing agendas,&quot; stance.<br /> <br /> I also never said anything about &quot;never mentioning&quot; something. But your statement sounds like playing WtA, without ever pushing or condemning environmentalism. It goes right back to &quot;why are you playing WtA instead of some other game?&quot; If you're not on board with &quot;environmentalism good, and it should be 'pushed' on people,&quot; what on Earth to you do with a game about fighting to save the planet from death because of the corruption of nature by human despoliation and pollution?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T19:33:47-07:00","id":1533868,"title":"","content":"All human interaction is nebulous. Where do we draw the line for anything? When it makes people uncomfortable, when it upsets them, when it pushes people away, when it divides us.<br /> <br /> How play games out in the real world is with people who I know, usually friends, and I want to do what I can to make that experience fun for them. If some subject in a game makes one of them uncomfortable then I would stop it. If some behavior around the table makes someone feel alienated, then we should talk about it and change things. It\u2019s not hard or fast rules, it\u2019s just being aware that other people have feeling and accommodating them - even if I don\u2019t personally find something offensive or upsetting that they do.<br /> <br /> For publishing an RPG, which I haven\u2019t done and likely won\u2019t, it will be a little different because I have to think about both the sensibilities of far more people and also must be willing to offend at least some since anything will offend at least someone.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is a game with heavy environmentalist themes. Can you play it without those themes? Absolutely. Are you losing something for doing that? Probably so, but that is subjective. Honestly, not many people oppose environmentalism if the issue is handled right. Can someone run a W:tA that includes environmental issues but still makes people from across the political spectrum feel relatively comfortable? Absolutely! <br /> <br /> It feels like a lot of people have this attitude of \u201cPeople who believe in x, y, and z are evil trash and we should exclude them and make them feel bad in any way possible.\u201d I don\u2019t think that is a good attitude. We can have games that include contentious political issues without deliberately alienating people or even necessarily pushing some agenda.<br /> <br /> in the case of W:tA, the environment is a pretty central themes and removing that issue would be a big departure that i can\u2019t understand not wanting to do. For other WoD games it\u2019s much more fuzzy (ironically) than W:tA and the games don\u2019t have to take on political issues or can do so in a more nuanced or multifaceted way. <br /> <br /> Can someone run a Vampire, Mage, Changeling, or Wraith Chronicle with a group of highly ideologically diverse people and everybody feels included and has fun? Yes, absolutely! Even with W:tA it can be done, outside of the environmental issue, which most people support to varying degrees. <br /> <br /> So let\u2019s say that there is a W:tA game that somebody wants to run and there is a player who is against environmentalism. Not wanting to destroy the planet or anything, just doesn\u2019t believe in global warming, thinks environmental regulations hurt the economy, that sort of stuff. They want to play because they like werewolves and shaman related ideas. It\u2019s certainly possible to include environmental themes without making that person feel attacked, even if it\u2019s just a matter of how everybody acts in towards the person if not the subject matter in game. Maybe the werewolves can fight against a Pentex subsidiary that is causing pollution but also is sacrificing kids from the surrounding neighborhood and the ST can tell an environmental story while giving the anti-environmentalist player something compelling too.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s just one kind of extreme example, in most cases being ideologically inclusive is way more natural. Just be nice and think of other people\u2019s feelings. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T21:26:44-07:00","id":1533873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1533868#post1533868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels like a lot of people have this attitude of \u201cPeople who believe in x, y, and z are evil trash and we should exclude them and make them feel bad in any way possible.\u201d I don\u2019t think that is a good attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a lot of us it's a necessary attitude. I don't want to have it, I have to have it to protect myself. It's the basic Tolerance Paradox issue where you have to exclude people who want to abuse inclusivity to diminish others. There are evil ideologies. It's not our job to use our gaming fun time to try to fix people that hold them.<br /> <br /> I would hope that you agree that under the First Amendment, the US is an inherently secular nation where regardless of a huge Christian majority, Christianity cannot be established as the national religion.<br /> <br /> There are people in this country that want to make the US a Christian theocracy. As someone who's rights (if not life) is at risk if they gain enough political power, the gaming table is not a place to attempt to resolve that, nor can I have fun at a table with someone that would take my rights away from me because I'm a member of a different faith from them. I can game with a very diverse set of people, but you have to see there are limits here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For other WoD games it\u2019s much more fuzzy (ironically) than W:tA and the games don\u2019t have to take on political issues or can do so in a more nuanced or multifaceted way. </div> </div> </div>I think the fantasy filter might be at play a bit here since the other games don't shy away from political issues, they just tie them to fictional groups.<br /> <br /> Vampire and Mage are both inextricably about statism vs. various anti-statist ideologies. The Camarilla is the vampire &quot;state&quot; that seeks to impose its rules on the Anarchs, Sabbat, and Independents, and even the Anarchs and Sabbat have core themes about the struggles of trying to effectively govern an area without becoming statists and lose their ideological opposition to the Camarilla. The Technocracy and even the Traditions are both trying to bring about a their ideal societies on both mages and humans, with the Technocracy using authoritarian forced conformity to eliminate social divisions while the Traditions are trying to be a liberal pluralistic humanist bound version that wants to use diversity as a strength within reason and stamp out anyone that gets too far away from the party line. Meanwhile the Crafts and Disparates don't want what either are selling and are either keeping their heads down as best they can, or organizing as their own mutual alliance as the only way to stay safe (and thus again exploring how to protecting individuality without falling into the statist ideology they're resisting).<br /> <br /> Changeling is literally about nobility and aristocrats trying to reclaim their power over the lower classes in an era where that thinking is outdated, and the dangers of how nostalgia can blind us to all the problems of a fictional idealized past where everything was better (esp. for the Sidhe) that tempts us to try to go back to old ways instead of confronting the new problems ahead of us.<br /> <br /> Stygia is a totalitarian society with forced conscription, slavery, and somehow worse, whee the government uses access to a Wraith's Fetters and Passions to tightly control their deaths all to get Wraiths to give up autonomy for security from the Tempest and Oblivion.<br /> <br /> I can go on if you want me to get into the Revised era games.<br /> <br /> But I think I've made a pretty solid point that there's some heavy real world politics at the core of these games; even the ones where the exploration of those politics is done in fictional group vs. fictional group instead of as direct conflict with in-game representatives of real groups (though good look avoiding that with some of the splats).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That\u2019s just one kind of extreme example, in most cases being ideologically inclusive is way more natural. Just be nice and think of other people\u2019s feelings. </div> </div> </div>Ultimately though, you're just making the case that it's not about being &quot;apolitical&quot; or &quot;light on politics&quot; or whatever. It's avoiding politics the group doesn't like and politics that doesn't upset the group is fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T02:00:37-07:00","id":1533880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1533868#post1533868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let\u2019s say that there is a W:tA game that somebody wants to run and there is a player who is against environmentalism. Not wanting to destroy the planet or anything, just doesn\u2019t believe in global warming, thinks environmental regulations hurt the economy, that sort of stuff. They want to play because they like werewolves and shaman related ideas. It\u2019s certainly possible to include environmental themes without making that person feel attacked, even if it\u2019s just a matter of how everybody acts in towards the person if not the subject matter in game. Maybe the werewolves can fight against a Pentex subsidiary that is causing pollution but also is sacrificing kids from the surrounding neighborhood and the ST can tell an environmental story while giving the anti-environmentalist player something compelling too.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s just one kind of extreme example, in most cases being ideologically inclusive is way more natural. Just be nice and think of other people\u2019s feelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideally even if the player doesn't believe in global warming (or whatever), they'd be willing to accept the basic premise that in this particular game global warming is something that exists and play a character who believes it exists. That's practically the most basic element of roleplaying - playing a character who believes things or does things that you don't or won't. Really, if a player isn't willing to engage with basic ideas or concepts in RPGs because they don't believe in those things, then I'd argue that they're really interested in roleplaying in the first place.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm totally on board with avoiding subjects that make players uncomfortable but if, &quot;global warming exists in this game&quot; is so upsetting for a player that they can't handle it, I'd probably try to play a boardgame or something instead, because trying to roleplay with someone like that sounds like it would be kind of a pain in the ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T04:05:44-07:00","id":1533883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1533868#post1533868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s just one kind of extreme example, in most cases being ideologically inclusive is way more natural. Just be nice and think of other people\u2019s feelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's straightforward enough.<br /> <br /> Other people's feelings including the matter of &quot;a lot of people from traditionally marginalized genders, racial and ethnic groups, and sexual identities take a critical eye to their fiction because things that alternate between erasing and deriding them have a long cultural legacy that pervades a lot of art and rhetoric, in ways that are hard to not notice when they're part of your lived experience and can do anything from making one feel unwelcome to provoking memories of harder forms of those things encountered in real life&quot;.<br /> <br /> People's feelings also including &quot;being proactive about inclusion is an emotionally and psychologically beneficial counterweight to all of that preceding stuff&quot;.<br /> <br /> That being the origin point of a lot of what gets vaguely and euphemistically referred to as politics in RPGs. Like, if there's anything making a strong case for comprehensive regulatory agencies and progressive tax policies to fund them, it must be precious little considering that I never hear about it compared to the other stuff.<br /> <br /> So yes, I think being considerate of other people's feelings is a good starting point.<br /> <br /> That's certainly a big part of how I started off with my position. Something like hearing somebody I regarded as a friend describe how crestfallen she could be trying to read mainstream comic books and feeling like a lot of the art and storylines concerning women were really alienating.<br /> <br /> Some people hear that kind of thing and think &quot;that's sad, and I wish it wasn't so&quot;. Others do and apparently think &quot;I swear to God, if I see so much as one woman holding a milkshake I will lose my fucking mind&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T07:05:16-07:00","id":1533886,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Please refrain from multiple posts in an attempt to get past the automatic moderation tools. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T13:23:16-07:00","id":1534150,"title":"","content":"I can't comment on how the state of super hero orientated comic companies in regards to storytelling as I aged out and on the post on this board I made the comment that it wasn't wokeness or politics that drove me off. I was getting older and wanted more adult orientated fare and found it in Manga with it's many genres, I do hear things from time to time as I will pay some attention to the Batman titles and there was some head turning moments with some changes as such as making Tim Drake gay and I thought when did this happen as he was depicted as straight and was in a long term relationship with Spoiler who was a teenage female.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T16:25:08-07:00","id":1534167,"title":"","content":"While discussing the decision making of comics writers is probably something for another thread, they didn't make Tim Drake gay. They made him bisexual as he's found a former school friend is a lot more to him than a friend. His explicitly experimenting with a same-sex relationship and isn't certain about what it means for him in the long term.<br /> <br /> This is the problem with only taking a peek at something. Tim was always one of my favorite members of the Bat-Fam, and I followed him for awhile even after I stopped buying American superhero comics. Lots of people expected his dating history was a sign of something (even if not explicitly him not being straight) for a long time. If you've been reading his books for years.. him trying dating a guy for a bit feels pretty damned natural whether it sticks or not. He sucks at dating women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T12:24:07-07:00","id":1535521,"title":"","content":"It's interesting as we get older that over time we shift towards a more conservative beliefs because of lifechanging experiences or doing some research on history and acknowledge that perhaps we were mistaken in some of our ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T15:53:22-07:00","id":1535534,"title":"","content":"Well, the fact that people think it's true is an interesting study in human cognitive biases anyway.<br /> <br /> It is, however, not true in the slightest. To the point where it actually used to be the other way around (&quot;getting older makes you more liberal&quot;) during the point where the Silent Generation was the largest group of seniors, and only as the Boomers took over did to flop to the current phrasing. Basically, at best it's a causation vs. correlation error that happens on a generational scale. Older people tend to make up the majority of real power in the government, so their politics tend to dominate an era. Instead of treating each group as a product of their time (and also other demographics), humans tend to then flip causation and correlation and assume that because the old and powerful are of a given political bend, age is the most important factor.<br /> <br /> It's far beyond question across multiple fields that humans &quot;calcify&quot; ideologically with age. The older you get, the more strongly you hold to ideological beliefs (and other forms of belief for that matter). The vast majority of people will hold the same broad ideological beliefs in their 30s as they will in their 70s.<br /> <br /> What tends to change are:<br /> <br /> 1) Historical context. Ideology, policy, and methodology are not the same thing. That is, in forty years what your core beliefs are, are unlikely to change, but you will probably adapt how you feel they should be implemented and advocated for. In the US, most older conservatives are more likely to be open to sensible gun regulations as a way to balance the public good with respect to traditional interpretations of the 2nd Amendment. Where as the &quot;2nd Amendment Absolutist&quot; position (I use quotes because very few people are true 100% no laws on any weapons what-so-ever folks) tends to be more young Boomer and Gen X in popularity (because the 90s esp., and not just in the US, so a lot of really stupid weapon control laws that are obviously more driven by parents worried about their kids watching anime* than any real thoughts about public safety, so people felt the government was overreaching and are inclined to push back). And the younger generations are gong to swing way harder back towards weapon control laws because... well... the last 20 years have not been a great case for lax laws on the subject. Nobody who has a conservative stance on gun policies is going to be advocating for (at least in the US) outlawing guns completely or something, but how guns are being used in society is going to modulate how people think about protecting gun rights and protecting lives at the same time. A lot of political assassinations led to conservative gun control bills, a lot of bad nanny state bullshit led to a lot of dismantling even those measures, and then a lot of mass shootings is driving the need to offer conservative gun safety measures because doing nothing is going to be untenable.<br /> <br /> 2) Trust in the system. This is probably where a lot of the feelings of &quot;you get more conservative as you get older&quot; comes from. Older people tend to trust the system (at least to be the system, even if they don't trust it to be inherently good). Decades of working the system means they see value in institutions, norms, and incremental approaches to advocacy for their policies of choice. Burning the system down because it's flawed doesn't appeal to people that rely on the system to get by (something that is fairly inherent in age). While this plays into the previous point as well, what tends to happen is that older people tend to be more moderate in policy (even if, not in ideology), and protective over gains made rather than pursuing new causes. This is also where there is a stark difference in conservatives and liberals: Conservatives (by nature of being traditionalists in the first place) don't tend to be as big into massive protest movements. Liberals are way more prone to take large collective actions, but the older members of the movement that actually have to make the compromises to further their agenda get labelled as moving to the right instead of being true to the cause.<br /> <br /> 3) The impact of political identity. One of the obfuscating parts of why there's a perception of ideological shift is that political parties themselves are not stable where human ideologies tend to be. There are conservative Democrats in the US who would have been Republicans in the 80s or 90s (many of them were) They didn't get more or less conservative, but the platforms of the major parities shifted and they had to assess which party was actually the party that supported their ideologies. Your average Eisenhower or Nixon Republican has seen their party shift wildly in policies. Some choose to remain Republicans anyway, and some chose not to, but since we tend to use parties as short hand for ideology, it makes it seem like there's all these old conservatives that are actually on board with lots of things we currently associate with liberal policies (which are really neither conservative or liberal, but what parties focus on).<br /> <br /> * - It's actually really funny to look at how the 70s expansion of Hong Kong action movies, and then the 90s spread of anime lead to insane laws that banned items across the Western nations because of the fear that kids would emulate Bruce Lee or ninjas. A Canadian YouTuber I watch occasionally did a great video on how he's more dangerous with a circular saw blade you can legally buy and carry on your person, than he is with a throwing star, but the throwing star is banned to be carried on a person in public. He joked that at least banning nunchucks to spite Bruce Lee prevented a lot of guys hitting themselves in the groin with a questionably practical weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 05-13-2024, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T03:29:34-07:00","id":1535623,"title":"","content":"Well I am conservative and I play various games including rpg. And I can tell myself that it came with the age (being conservative) in my case. I'm watching what's happening in EU very closely and upcoming EU Parliament election is the most important for the continent future in my opinion. We're going straight into chaos, blodshed and war (if the current situation won't change)/ leftist terror of political corectness and crime of thought or we will turn to nationality states again and it might be repeat from 1939.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T11:53:05-07:00","id":1535656,"title":"","content":"Being seen as a conservative or even libertarian seems to be a bad thing in today's polarized climate Werewolf43.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T12:21:19-07:00","id":1535659,"title":"","content":"Keeping distance from the politics and being away from the left/right points of view made me fascist (from the left winged people I know) and traitor from right. I'm avoiding TV, I'm trying to get info from both sides but not often to stay healthy, see points of view from many angles but I always try to think and figure modern problems alone and see the things as I see them not as someone told me - especially polish media, stick to my hobby, to my familly and friend - nowday I have to struggle with him fading away because of the modern world cause it's too much for him, and to my faith - it keeps me running. With the long list of illness and being day by day on 7 different pills that hold me inrelative health that's all I can do to stay myself.<br /> I'm 42 now and I've learned that caring about someone else's opinion that is not important for me and how others see you is the last thing I should do and so I am implementing this idea day after day, often puting a lot of coworkers in consternation. I've learned again that all the mess between left and right side can go along without me so I left this train years ago. The thing is that people from both sides I know tried to draw me in their conflct but for now after I politely explained my point of view I have some peace. Just let them be me.<br /> Biggest concern is that if I am not interested in politics the politicians\u200b will be interested about me sooner or later. But I don't think I'm going to live that long to check it<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T08:41:42-07:00","id":1535733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist?p=1535623#post1535623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">leftist terror of political corectness and crime of thought or we will turn to nationality states again and it might be repeat from 1939.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got to say, leftism has really taken a big hit in the last ninety years. Time was that people were terrified by the idea that the left would confiscate their property and limit their opportunities and nationalise their industry. And now all it can manage is asking people to not use terms evocative of mockery of things like race, gender, sexual identity or disability, and making things into a crime that only gets punished by some people being kind of mean to you on social media* as opposed to, like, prison.<br /> <br /> Would probably be kind of embarrassing for right wing politics to still react to those things as though they're existential threats on the same level as Bolshevik revolution.<br /> <br /> * Alongside the many, many people who will still lionise you for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T13:09:14-07:00","id":1535745,"title":"","content":"I feel like we're falling into the political party vs. political ideology conflation issue.<br /> <br /> Everyone tries to police speech in some fashion. Conservatives have speech they don't like and don't want to see used. Liberals do it as well. From an ideological standpoint... this really isn't a conservatism vs. liberalism issue. Both ideologies agree that there is a line between what should be protected free speech and speech that crosses lines in harmful territory. The default hypothetical of, &quot;It should not be protected speech to yell 'Fire!' in a crowded theater to cause a panic,&quot; is not an ideological wedge. Nobody on either side thinks it should be protected speech for a mob boss to tell an underling to go kill someone. We all acknowledge that is not what &quot;free speech&quot; is meant to protect.<br /> <br /> And when you dig down on where the fights on culture war stuff like where exactly the lines should get drawn in public spaces... it's rarely about political conservatism vs. political liberalism. There's no conservative argument for &quot;slurs are good actually.&quot; But there's a lot of demagoguery to try to strength tribalism instead of weaken it by engaging in fights over what the &quot;correct&quot; way to speak to other people is. Critiques are always stronger from within a shared framework. One of the more successful push backs against political correctness was not right wing pearl clutching... but the people at question just saying, &quot;Stop, it's fine.&quot; In the US, there was this whole push to normalize &quot;African American&quot; as the &quot;politically correct&quot; term for black people... and it failed because most black people are fine with being called black. When black people largely said, &quot;you're not being inclusive by saddling us with a label we don't want,&quot; it worked pretty well to halt the whole terminology thing. It's an argument that works because it comes from within the lefty framework.<br /> <br /> Right-wing talking heads &quot;pushing back&quot; by extolling people for being assholes both doesn't convince lefties that they're taking political correctness to far on a given subject, and it hurts the public perception of normal conservatives that get hit in the crossfire. It depends divides when people opt to do the opposite of their perceived political rivals, rather than what's right by their core values (or the core values were always incompatible anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T12:07:20-07:00","id":1535787,"title":"","content":"If you try to please everyone Werewolf43 and you are doomed to please nobody or trying to appease a small minority that alienates the majority as we seem to see way to frequently..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}